 the world of how incredibly complex systems actually work.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 550, 11, 291, 458, 11, 291, 1823, 666, 264, 1002, 295, 577, 6252, 3997, 3652, 767, 589, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0936882161648474, "compression_ratio": 1.5888157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 6.821551244880208e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2464, "start": 30.82, "end": 32.44, "text": " Right. Which is a never clean.", "tokens": [50674, 1779, 13, 3013, 307, 257, 1128, 2541, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0936882161648474, "compression_ratio": 1.5888157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 6.821551244880208e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2464, "start": 32.66, "end": 45.7, "text": " No, never. Whether we're talking about millions of years of biological evolution or like the recommendation algorithm governing a massive social media platform or even the neural pathways firing inside your own brain right now.", "tokens": [50766, 883, 11, 1128, 13, 8503, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 6803, 295, 924, 295, 13910, 9303, 420, 411, 264, 11879, 9284, 30054, 257, 5994, 2093, 3021, 3663, 420, 754, 264, 18161, 22988, 16045, 1854, 428, 1065, 3567, 558, 586, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0936882161648474, "compression_ratio": 1.5888157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 6.821551244880208e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2464, "start": 45.760000000000005, "end": 47.08, "text": " It's all just incredibly messy.", "tokens": [51421, 467, 311, 439, 445, 6252, 16191, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0936882161648474, "compression_ratio": 1.5888157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 6.821551244880208e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2464, "start": 47.3, "end": 53.900000000000006, "text": " Yeah, exactly. When you look at those systems, that neat binary x-ray machine is completely broken.", "tokens": [51498, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 1133, 291, 574, 412, 729, 3652, 11, 300, 10654, 17434, 2031, 12, 3458, 3479, 307, 2584, 5463, 13, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0936882161648474, "compression_ratio": 1.5888157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 6.821551244880208e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5390, "start": 53.9, "end": 59.6, "text": " We find ourselves looking at this diagnostic landscape that is, quite honestly, murky and overwhelming.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 915, 4175, 1237, 412, 341, 27897, 9661, 300, 307, 11, 1596, 6095, 11, 5257, 4133, 293, 13373, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08807734954051483, "compression_ratio": 1.5682539682539682, "no_speech_prob": 1.681308195965181e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5390, "start": 59.86, "end": 64.53999999999999, "text": " We constantly want simple answers, but the systems just completely refuse to give them to us.", "tokens": [50663, 492, 6460, 528, 2199, 6338, 11, 457, 264, 3652, 445, 2584, 16791, 281, 976, 552, 281, 505, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08807734954051483, "compression_ratio": 1.5682539682539682, "no_speech_prob": 1.681308195965181e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5390, "start": 64.78, "end": 74.46, "text": " They really do. Which is why the material we are diving into today is so vital. It fundamentally reorients how we look at that murkiness.", "tokens": [50909, 814, 534, 360, 13, 3013, 307, 983, 264, 2527, 321, 366, 20241, 666, 965, 307, 370, 11707, 13, 467, 17879, 319, 284, 2448, 577, 321, 574, 412, 300, 5257, 74, 1324, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08807734954051483, "compression_ratio": 1.5682539682539682, "no_speech_prob": 1.681308195965181e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5390, "start": 74.64, "end": 78.64, "text": " Yeah, there is this new, incredibly dense body of research that just came out.", "tokens": [51402, 865, 11, 456, 307, 341, 777, 11, 6252, 18011, 1772, 295, 2132, 300, 445, 1361, 484, 13, 51602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08807734954051483, "compression_ratio": 1.5682539682539682, "no_speech_prob": 1.681308195965181e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5390, "start": 78.66, "end": 83.58, "text": " Right. Published in July 2026 by an independent systems theorist named Flixion.", "tokens": [51603, 1779, 13, 21808, 4173, 294, 7370, 945, 10880, 538, 364, 6695, 3652, 27423, 468, 4926, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08807734954051483, "compression_ratio": 1.5682539682539682, "no_speech_prob": 1.681308195965181e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 8358, "start": 83.58, "end": 89.0, "text": " And what Flixion has done is essentially build a new kind of x-ray for reality itself.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 575, 1096, 307, 4476, 1322, 257, 777, 733, 295, 2031, 12, 3458, 337, 4103, 2564, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07195932614175897, "compression_ratio": 1.4929577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423733033288368e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 8358, "start": 89.16, "end": 101.38, "text": " It's mind boggling. So if you are joining us for this deep dive, you're going to want to settle in because the through line connecting this research is going to completely change how you look at the architecture of your daily life.", "tokens": [50644, 467, 311, 1575, 26132, 70, 1688, 13, 407, 498, 291, 366, 5549, 505, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 11, 291, 434, 516, 281, 528, 281, 11852, 294, 570, 264, 807, 1622, 11015, 341, 2132, 307, 516, 281, 2584, 1319, 577, 291, 574, 412, 264, 9482, 295, 428, 5212, 993, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07195932614175897, "compression_ratio": 1.4929577464788732, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423733033288368e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 10138, "start": 101.38, "end": 106.8, "text": " I mean, we are going to explore three seemingly unconnected wild phenomena.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 321, 366, 516, 281, 6839, 1045, 18709, 517, 9826, 292, 4868, 22004, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16999516487121583, "compression_ratio": 1.0416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.9965949466654864e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 10680, "start": 106.8, "end": 112.56, "text": " Yeah. First, why completely different animal species in the ocean keep independently evolving into crabs.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 2386, 11, 983, 2584, 819, 5496, 6172, 294, 264, 7810, 1066, 21761, 21085, 666, 35147, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 10680, "start": 112.7, "end": 113.82, "text": " Which is a real thing, by the way.", "tokens": [50660, 3013, 307, 257, 957, 551, 11, 538, 264, 636, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 10680, "start": 113.88, "end": 114.24, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50719, 467, 307, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10680, "start": 114.47999999999999, "end": 121.74, "text": " Second, why brilliant tech platforms armed with world-class artificial intelligence somehow cannot stop painfully obvious rental scams.", "tokens": [50749, 5736, 11, 983, 10248, 7553, 9473, 16297, 365, 1002, 12, 11665, 11677, 7599, 6063, 2644, 1590, 1822, 2277, 6322, 21468, 795, 4070, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10680, "start": 121.89999999999999, "end": 123.28, "text": " That one is going to make you mad.", "tokens": [51120, 663, 472, 307, 516, 281, 652, 291, 5244, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10680, "start": 123.5, "end": 124.9, "text": " Oh, it makes me furious.", "tokens": [51200, 876, 11, 309, 1669, 385, 33470, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10900806245349702, "compression_ratio": 1.4658119658119657, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144781688099853e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 12490, "start": 124.9, "end": 136.52, "text": " And third, why a physical wall made of melting wax might actually represent a more profound form of computing than, you know, the silicon microchip sitting in your smartphone right now.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2636, 11, 983, 257, 4001, 2929, 1027, 295, 20493, 17352, 1062, 767, 2906, 257, 544, 14382, 1254, 295, 15866, 813, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 22848, 4532, 339, 647, 3798, 294, 428, 13307, 558, 586, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 12490, "start": 136.82, "end": 141.42000000000002, "text": " On the surface, I know those sound like they belong in three entirely different discussions.", "tokens": [50961, 1282, 264, 3753, 11, 286, 458, 729, 1626, 411, 436, 5784, 294, 1045, 7696, 819, 11088, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 12490, "start": 141.62, "end": 142.68, "text": " Yeah, totally unrelated.", "tokens": [51201, 865, 11, 3879, 38967, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 12490, "start": 142.98000000000002, "end": 147.84, "text": " But the underlying connective tissue that Flixion exposes here is just breathtaking.", "tokens": [51269, 583, 264, 14217, 1745, 488, 12404, 300, 3235, 970, 313, 1278, 4201, 510, 307, 445, 48393, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 12490, "start": 148.52, "end": 151.96, "text": " We are exploring the hidden structures of systems.", "tokens": [51546, 492, 366, 12736, 264, 7633, 9227, 295, 3652, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 12490, "start": 152.36, "end": 154.1, "text": " Like how they are built from the ground up.", "tokens": [51738, 1743, 577, 436, 366, 3094, 490, 264, 2727, 493, 13, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11831492677741094, "compression_ratio": 1.6046511627906976, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012610295531137e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 15410, "start": 154.1, "end": 168.18, "text": " Exactly. We are going to unpack how systems actually originate in the first place, how they can uncouple from physical reality to become toxic and entirely self-referential, and ultimately, how we might physically force them to anchor back to the real world.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 492, 366, 516, 281, 26699, 577, 3652, 767, 4957, 473, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 11, 577, 436, 393, 6219, 263, 781, 490, 4001, 4103, 281, 1813, 12786, 293, 7696, 2698, 12, 265, 612, 2549, 11, 293, 6284, 11, 577, 321, 1062, 9762, 3464, 552, 281, 18487, 646, 281, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07281855174473353, "compression_ratio": 1.60431654676259, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883040104831437e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 15410, "start": 168.28, "end": 175.01999999999998, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this. I want to start by looking at this idea of origins. Specifically, what Flixion calls the historical origin assumption.", "tokens": [51074, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 286, 528, 281, 722, 538, 1237, 412, 341, 1558, 295, 22721, 13, 26058, 11, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 5498, 264, 8584, 4957, 15302, 13, 51411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07281855174473353, "compression_ratio": 1.60431654676259, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883040104831437e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 15410, "start": 175.24, "end": 177.2, "text": " Right. This is where we all get tripped up.", "tokens": [51422, 1779, 13, 639, 307, 689, 321, 439, 483, 1376, 3320, 493, 13, 51520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07281855174473353, "compression_ratio": 1.60431654676259, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883040104831437e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 17720, "start": 177.2, "end": 186.79999999999998, "text": " Yeah, because by default, the way our human brains are wired, if you and I see two things that look incredibly similar, we immediately assume one of two things.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 570, 538, 7576, 11, 264, 636, 527, 1952, 15442, 366, 27415, 11, 498, 291, 293, 286, 536, 732, 721, 300, 574, 6252, 2531, 11, 321, 4258, 6552, 472, 295, 732, 721, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10452286617175953, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.443750392675358e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 17720, "start": 187.11999999999998, "end": 192.67999999999998, "text": " We assume either one copied the other, or they both share a direct common ancestor.", "tokens": [50861, 492, 6552, 2139, 472, 25365, 264, 661, 11, 420, 436, 1293, 2073, 257, 2047, 2689, 40032, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10452286617175953, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.443750392675358e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 17720, "start": 192.94, "end": 195.33999999999997, "text": " Exactly. And that assumption makes total sense, right?", "tokens": [51152, 7587, 13, 400, 300, 15302, 1669, 3217, 2020, 11, 558, 30, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10452286617175953, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.443750392675358e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 17720, "start": 195.35999999999999, "end": 195.6, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51273, 865, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10452286617175953, "compression_ratio": 1.4805825242718447, "no_speech_prob": 1.443750392675358e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 19560, "start": 195.6, "end": 199.82, "text": " It is deeply ingrained in how we are taught to categorize the world.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 8760, 3957, 31774, 294, 577, 321, 366, 5928, 281, 19250, 1125, 264, 1002, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05725992505795488, "compression_ratio": 1.6388888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043329859050104e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 19560, "start": 199.82, "end": 211.57999999999998, "text": " Oh, absolutely. If you study linguistics and you see that two different languages share an almost identical word for mother, you instantly start looking for the ancient parent language they both branched off from.", "tokens": [50576, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 759, 291, 2979, 21766, 6006, 293, 291, 536, 300, 732, 819, 8650, 2073, 364, 1920, 14800, 1349, 337, 2895, 11, 291, 13518, 722, 1237, 337, 264, 7832, 2596, 2856, 436, 1293, 9819, 292, 766, 490, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05725992505795488, "compression_ratio": 1.6388888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043329859050104e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 19560, "start": 211.68, "end": 217.94, "text": " Right. Or if you are in textual criticism and you find two medieval manuscripts with the exact same grammatical error.", "tokens": [51169, 1779, 13, 1610, 498, 291, 366, 294, 2487, 901, 15835, 293, 291, 915, 732, 24078, 42849, 365, 264, 1900, 912, 17570, 267, 804, 6713, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05725992505795488, "compression_ratio": 1.6388888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043329859050104e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 19560, "start": 218.07999999999998, "end": 221.04, "text": " You assume one scribe was just peering over the shoulder of the other.", "tokens": [51489, 509, 6552, 472, 5545, 650, 390, 445, 520, 1794, 670, 264, 7948, 295, 264, 661, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05725992505795488, "compression_ratio": 1.6388888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043329859050104e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 22104, "start": 221.04, "end": 229.18, "text": " Yeah, and in evolutionary biology, if two animals share a similar bone structure in their forelimbs, we trace them back down the evolutionary tree.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 293, 294, 27567, 14956, 11, 498, 732, 4882, 2073, 257, 2531, 9026, 3877, 294, 641, 2091, 4197, 929, 11, 321, 13508, 552, 646, 760, 264, 27567, 4230, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08298344187217184, "compression_ratio": 1.6240875912408759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077794256872836e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 22104, "start": 229.29999999999998, "end": 233.35999999999999, "text": " Right, until we find the shared ancestor that gave them those specific bones.", "tokens": [50778, 1779, 11, 1826, 321, 915, 264, 5507, 40032, 300, 2729, 552, 729, 2685, 10491, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08298344187217184, "compression_ratio": 1.6240875912408759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077794256872836e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 22104, "start": 234.23999999999998, "end": 238.66, "text": " Similarity is almost always viewed as the visible trace left behind by a lineage.", "tokens": [51025, 10905, 507, 307, 1920, 1009, 19174, 382, 264, 8974, 13508, 1411, 2261, 538, 257, 38257, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08298344187217184, "compression_ratio": 1.6240875912408759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077794256872836e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 22104, "start": 239.18, "end": 246.95999999999998, "text": " But Flixion argues this default assumption is actually blinding us. It blinds us to what is really doing the work in shaping our reality.", "tokens": [51272, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 38218, 341, 7576, 15302, 307, 767, 6865, 278, 505, 13, 467, 6865, 82, 505, 281, 437, 307, 534, 884, 264, 589, 294, 25945, 527, 4103, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08298344187217184, "compression_ratio": 1.6240875912408759, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077794256872836e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 24696, "start": 246.96, "end": 254.3, "text": " It really does. And to prove this, they point to one of the most famous, mind-boggling biology experiments of the last century.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 534, 775, 13, 400, 281, 7081, 341, 11, 436, 935, 281, 472, 295, 264, 881, 4618, 11, 1575, 12, 65, 36754, 1688, 14956, 12050, 295, 264, 1036, 4901, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 24696, "start": 254.74, "end": 256.38, "text": " The Richard Lenski E. coli experiment.", "tokens": [50754, 440, 9809, 441, 694, 2984, 462, 13, 1173, 72, 5120, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 24696, "start": 256.42, "end": 259.84000000000003, "text": " Yeah. The scale of the Lenski experiment is truly something to marvel at.", "tokens": [50838, 865, 13, 440, 4373, 295, 264, 441, 694, 2984, 5120, 307, 4908, 746, 281, 23893, 412, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 24696, "start": 260.32, "end": 267.94, "text": " Back in 1988, evolutionary biologist Richard Lenski took a single ancestral strain of E. coli bacteria.", "tokens": [51033, 5833, 294, 27816, 11, 27567, 3228, 9201, 9809, 441, 694, 2984, 1890, 257, 2167, 40049, 14249, 295, 462, 13, 1173, 72, 11763, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 24696, "start": 268.32, "end": 270.92, "text": " Just one single genetic starting point.", "tokens": [51433, 1449, 472, 2167, 12462, 2891, 935, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 24696, "start": 271.0, "end": 271.62, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51567, 7587, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681310910444993, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.846170785690937e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 27162, "start": 271.62, "end": 279.7, "text": " He used that to found 12 identical populations. He put all 12 of these populations into the exact same environment.", "tokens": [50365, 634, 1143, 300, 281, 1352, 2272, 14800, 12822, 13, 634, 829, 439, 2272, 295, 613, 12822, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 2823, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 27162, "start": 279.86, "end": 281.48, "text": " Which was this liquid medium, right?", "tokens": [50777, 3013, 390, 341, 6553, 6399, 11, 558, 30, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 27162, "start": 281.56, "end": 287.02, "text": " Yeah, a medium that was strictly limited in glucose, but also contained a substance called citrate.", "tokens": [50862, 865, 11, 257, 6399, 300, 390, 20792, 5567, 294, 23997, 11, 457, 611, 16212, 257, 12961, 1219, 4814, 4404, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 27162, "start": 287.56, "end": 290.76, "text": " Now, this is the crucial biological context here.", "tokens": [51162, 823, 11, 341, 307, 264, 11462, 13910, 4319, 510, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 27162, "start": 290.86, "end": 291.4, "text": " Okay, what is it?", "tokens": [51327, 1033, 11, 437, 307, 309, 30, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 27162, "start": 291.54, "end": 299.28000000000003, "text": " Normally, E. coli cannot metabolize citrate in an oxygen-rich environment. It is biologically fundamentally off-limits to them.", "tokens": [51361, 17424, 11, 462, 13, 1173, 72, 2644, 19110, 1125, 4814, 4404, 294, 364, 9169, 12, 10794, 2823, 13, 467, 307, 3228, 17157, 17879, 766, 12, 4197, 1208, 281, 552, 13, 51748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 27162, "start": 299.36, "end": 300.02, "text": " Wow, okay.", "tokens": [51752, 3153, 11, 1392, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11632497557278337, "compression_ratio": 1.6219081272084805, "no_speech_prob": 1.83936546549468e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 30002, "start": 300.02, "end": 306.97999999999996, "text": " It would be like putting a human in a room full of wood and expecting them to eat the wood for calories. We just don't have the machinery for it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 312, 411, 3372, 257, 1952, 294, 257, 1808, 1577, 295, 4576, 293, 9650, 552, 281, 1862, 264, 4576, 337, 14904, 13, 492, 445, 500, 380, 362, 264, 27302, 337, 309, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10125925229943317, "compression_ratio": 1.6475409836065573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684909747224919e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 30002, "start": 307.46, "end": 313.74, "text": " Right. So just to paint this picture for you listening, you have 12 identical glass flasks in a lab.", "tokens": [50737, 1779, 13, 407, 445, 281, 4225, 341, 3036, 337, 291, 4764, 11, 291, 362, 2272, 14800, 4276, 932, 296, 1694, 294, 257, 2715, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10125925229943317, "compression_ratio": 1.6475409836065573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684909747224919e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 30002, "start": 313.94, "end": 314.12, "text": " Yep.", "tokens": [51061, 7010, 13, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10125925229943317, "compression_ratio": 1.6475409836065573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684909747224919e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 30002, "start": 314.41999999999996, "end": 321.47999999999996, "text": " You have 12 genetically identical starting populations of bacteria. And you have 12 identical chemical environments. Everything is totally controlled.", "tokens": [51085, 509, 362, 2272, 37582, 14800, 2891, 12822, 295, 11763, 13, 400, 291, 362, 2272, 14800, 7313, 12388, 13, 5471, 307, 3879, 10164, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10125925229943317, "compression_ratio": 1.6475409836065573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684909747224919e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 32148, "start": 321.48, "end": 330.96000000000004, "text": " Everything is identical. And then Lenski and his team just let them reproduce, generation after generation, transferring them to fresh media every single day.", "tokens": [50365, 5471, 307, 14800, 13, 400, 550, 441, 694, 2984, 293, 702, 1469, 445, 718, 552, 29501, 11, 5125, 934, 5125, 11, 31437, 552, 281, 4451, 3021, 633, 2167, 786, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09980351496965457, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.648796984360379e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 32148, "start": 331.16, "end": 333.28000000000003, "text": " And nothing happens, right? For a very long time.", "tokens": [50849, 400, 1825, 2314, 11, 558, 30, 1171, 257, 588, 938, 565, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09980351496965457, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.648796984360379e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 32148, "start": 333.32, "end": 339.20000000000005, "text": " For 30,000 generations, nothing happens regarding the citrate. The bacteria are mutating, of course.", "tokens": [50957, 1171, 2217, 11, 1360, 10593, 11, 1825, 2314, 8595, 264, 4814, 4404, 13, 440, 11763, 366, 5839, 990, 11, 295, 1164, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09980351496965457, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.648796984360379e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 32148, "start": 339.44, "end": 340.18, "text": " Right. Naturally.", "tokens": [51263, 1779, 13, 34304, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09980351496965457, "compression_ratio": 1.5645933014354068, "no_speech_prob": 1.648796984360379e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 34018, "start": 340.18, "end": 349.18, "text": " They are evolving and adapting to become more efficient at eating the limited glucose. But they completely ignore the citrate. It remains totally inaccessible.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 21085, 293, 34942, 281, 1813, 544, 7148, 412, 3936, 264, 5567, 23997, 13, 583, 436, 2584, 11200, 264, 4814, 4404, 13, 467, 7023, 3879, 33230, 780, 964, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11110581522402556, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3986486665021336e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 34018, "start": 349.3, "end": 350.22, "text": " So it's just sitting there.", "tokens": [50821, 407, 309, 311, 445, 3798, 456, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11110581522402556, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3986486665021336e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 34018, "start": 350.3, "end": 358.08, "text": " Just sitting there. But then, right around generation 31,500, something incredible happens.", "tokens": [50871, 1449, 3798, 456, 13, 583, 550, 11, 558, 926, 5125, 10353, 11, 7526, 11, 746, 4651, 2314, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11110581522402556, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3986486665021336e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 34018, "start": 358.2, "end": 358.68, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51266, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11110581522402556, "compression_ratio": 1.476923076923077, "no_speech_prob": 1.3986486665021336e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 35868, "start": 358.68, "end": 365.62, "text": " In one population, and only one out of the 12, a variant suddenly develops the ability to eat the citrate.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 472, 4415, 11, 293, 787, 472, 484, 295, 264, 2272, 11, 257, 17501, 5800, 25453, 264, 3485, 281, 1862, 264, 4814, 4404, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08993546029795771, "compression_ratio": 1.5669014084507042, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610544541050375e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 35868, "start": 365.86, "end": 370.26, "text": " 30,000 generations. I mean, that is a timescale that is hard to even wrap your head around.", "tokens": [50724, 2217, 11, 1360, 10593, 13, 286, 914, 11, 300, 307, 257, 1413, 37088, 300, 307, 1152, 281, 754, 7019, 428, 1378, 926, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08993546029795771, "compression_ratio": 1.5669014084507042, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610544541050375e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 35868, "start": 370.32, "end": 370.94, "text": " It's massive.", "tokens": [50947, 467, 311, 5994, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08993546029795771, "compression_ratio": 1.5669014084507042, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610544541050375e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 35868, "start": 371.06, "end": 378.08, "text": " If we were talking about human generations, that would stretch back into the Pleistocene epoch, like long before Neanderthals went extinct.", "tokens": [50984, 759, 321, 645, 1417, 466, 1952, 10593, 11, 300, 576, 5985, 646, 666, 264, 25658, 468, 905, 1450, 30992, 339, 11, 411, 938, 949, 1734, 4483, 392, 1124, 1437, 35094, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08993546029795771, "compression_ratio": 1.5669014084507042, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610544541050375e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 35868, "start": 378.44, "end": 384.8, "text": " It is an immense amount of time. And here is where Fliction's core argument comes into play.", "tokens": [51353, 467, 307, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 565, 13, 400, 510, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 311, 4965, 6770, 1487, 666, 862, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08993546029795771, "compression_ratio": 1.5669014084507042, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610544541050375e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 38480, "start": 384.8, "end": 395.2, "text": " If you ask a biologist, why did that one specific population figure out how to eat citrate, while the other 11 identical populations didn't?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1029, 257, 3228, 9201, 11, 983, 630, 300, 472, 2685, 4415, 2573, 484, 577, 281, 1862, 4814, 4404, 11, 1339, 264, 661, 2975, 14800, 12822, 994, 380, 30, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 38480, "start": 395.28000000000003, "end": 396.52000000000004, "text": " Right. Why just the one?", "tokens": [50889, 1779, 13, 1545, 445, 264, 472, 30, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 38480, "start": 396.6, "end": 401.72, "text": " Well, the shared ancestor from 1988 gives you absolutely zero explanatory power.", "tokens": [50955, 1042, 11, 264, 5507, 40032, 490, 27816, 2709, 291, 3122, 4018, 9045, 4745, 1347, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 38480, "start": 401.84000000000003, "end": 403.78000000000003, "text": " Because they all share that exact same ancestor.", "tokens": [51217, 1436, 436, 439, 2073, 300, 1900, 912, 40032, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 38480, "start": 403.86, "end": 404.34000000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51318, 7587, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 38480, "start": 404.58000000000004, "end": 412.56, "text": " The historical origin is identical across the board. So looking backwards down the lineage tree explains absolutely nothing about why they diverge so radically.", "tokens": [51354, 440, 8584, 4957, 307, 14800, 2108, 264, 3150, 13, 407, 1237, 12204, 760, 264, 38257, 4230, 13948, 3122, 1825, 466, 983, 436, 18558, 432, 370, 35508, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0941610703101525, "compression_ratio": 1.6089965397923875, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 41256, "start": 412.56, "end": 423.66, "text": " You nailed it. Fliction draws a sharp, necessary line here between a historical origin, which is just the literal first appearance of something in linear time, and an explanatory origin.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 30790, 309, 13, 3235, 4105, 20045, 257, 8199, 11, 4818, 1622, 510, 1296, 257, 8584, 4957, 11, 597, 307, 445, 264, 20411, 700, 8967, 295, 746, 294, 8213, 565, 11, 293, 364, 9045, 4745, 4957, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07354427377382915, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977372419886948e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 41256, "start": 423.8, "end": 426.46, "text": " And what exactly is the explanatory origin in this case?", "tokens": [50927, 400, 437, 2293, 307, 264, 9045, 4745, 4957, 294, 341, 1389, 30, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07354427377382915, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977372419886948e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 41256, "start": 426.6, "end": 431.16, "text": " It's the underlying structure of constraints that makes that appearance possible in the first place.", "tokens": [51067, 467, 311, 264, 14217, 3877, 295, 18491, 300, 1669, 300, 8967, 1944, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07354427377382915, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977372419886948e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 41256, "start": 431.28, "end": 435.5, "text": " In the Lensky experiment, the explanatory origin isn't the ancestor.", "tokens": [51301, 682, 264, 441, 694, 4133, 5120, 11, 264, 9045, 4745, 4957, 1943, 380, 264, 40032, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07354427377382915, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977372419886948e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 41256, "start": 435.84000000000003, "end": 436.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51529, 1779, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07354427377382915, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.5977372419886948e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 43612, "start": 436.12, "end": 447.94, "text": " It is the constraint space. It's the specific chemical medium, the selective pressure of starving for glucose, and crucially, the accumulated independent mutational history of that one specific population.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 25534, 1901, 13, 467, 311, 264, 2685, 7313, 6399, 11, 264, 33930, 3321, 295, 28420, 337, 23997, 11, 293, 5140, 1909, 11, 264, 31346, 6695, 5839, 1478, 2503, 295, 300, 472, 2685, 4415, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06115961656337831, "compression_ratio": 1.4335664335664335, "no_speech_prob": 1.4776662966148324e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 44794, "start": 447.94, "end": 450.68, "text": " Okay, walk me through that mutational history part.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 1792, 385, 807, 300, 5839, 1478, 2503, 644, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 44794, "start": 451.24, "end": 453.18, "text": " Because they were all mutating the whole time, right?", "tokens": [50530, 1436, 436, 645, 439, 5839, 990, 264, 1379, 565, 11, 558, 30, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 44794, "start": 453.3, "end": 457.94, "text": " They were, but the genetic landscape is unfathomably huge.", "tokens": [50633, 814, 645, 11, 457, 264, 12462, 9661, 307, 3971, 998, 298, 1188, 2603, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 44794, "start": 458.2, "end": 468.1, "text": " Over those 30,000 generations, that one specific lineage was randomly accumulating a sequence of totally unremarkable neutral mutations.", "tokens": [50878, 4886, 729, 2217, 11, 1360, 10593, 11, 300, 472, 2685, 38257, 390, 16979, 12989, 12162, 257, 8310, 295, 3879, 517, 2579, 809, 712, 10598, 29243, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 44794, "start": 468.52, "end": 469.86, "text": " So they didn't seem to do anything.", "tokens": [51394, 407, 436, 994, 380, 1643, 281, 360, 1340, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 44794, "start": 470.06, "end": 470.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51471, 1779, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14580778642134232, "compression_ratio": 1.4891774891774892, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858804070303933e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 47028, "start": 470.28, "end": 482.17999999999995, "text": " These mutations didn't help them eat citrate, so they seemed useless, but what they were actually doing was quietly moving that population to a very specific, precarious location in the genetic landscape.", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 29243, 994, 380, 854, 552, 1862, 4814, 4404, 11, 370, 436, 6576, 14115, 11, 457, 437, 436, 645, 767, 884, 390, 19141, 2684, 300, 4415, 281, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 4346, 289, 851, 4914, 294, 264, 12462, 9661, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1038019035173499, "compression_ratio": 1.6431535269709543, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758167982981354e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 47028, "start": 482.34, "end": 482.82, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50968, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1038019035173499, "compression_ratio": 1.6431535269709543, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758167982981354e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 47028, "start": 483.26, "end": 491.32, "text": " They were wandering through the dark until they happened to stand on the exact square where the citrate-eating mutation was suddenly just one tiny step away.", "tokens": [51014, 814, 645, 26396, 807, 264, 2877, 1826, 436, 2011, 281, 1463, 322, 264, 1900, 3732, 689, 264, 4814, 4404, 12, 68, 990, 27960, 390, 5800, 445, 472, 5870, 1823, 1314, 13, 51417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1038019035173499, "compression_ratio": 1.6431535269709543, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758167982981354e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 47028, "start": 491.55999999999995, "end": 492.4, "text": " And the others didn't.", "tokens": [51429, 400, 264, 2357, 994, 380, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1038019035173499, "compression_ratio": 1.6431535269709543, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758167982981354e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 49240, "start": 492.4, "end": 501.21999999999997, "text": " No, the other 11 populations wandered into different parts of the genetic landscape where eating citrate was maybe 50 steps away, which is effectively impossible.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 264, 661, 2975, 12822, 14304, 4073, 666, 819, 3166, 295, 264, 12462, 9661, 689, 3936, 4814, 4404, 390, 1310, 2625, 4439, 1314, 11, 597, 307, 8659, 6243, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 49240, "start": 501.65999999999997, "end": 506.76, "text": " Man, it makes me think of a maze. Imagine we have a massive, complex maze, and we drop a rat in it.", "tokens": [50828, 2458, 11, 309, 1669, 385, 519, 295, 257, 33032, 13, 11739, 321, 362, 257, 5994, 11, 3997, 33032, 11, 293, 321, 3270, 257, 5937, 294, 309, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 49240, "start": 506.84, "end": 507.53999999999996, "text": " Okay, yeah.", "tokens": [51087, 1033, 11, 1338, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 49240, "start": 507.73999999999995, "end": 514.78, "text": " Eventually, the rat finds the cheese at the center. Our human instinct is to give a medal to the rat for finding the center first.", "tokens": [51132, 17586, 11, 264, 5937, 10704, 264, 5399, 412, 264, 3056, 13, 2621, 1952, 16556, 307, 281, 976, 257, 21364, 281, 264, 5937, 337, 5006, 264, 3056, 700, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 49240, "start": 515.12, "end": 516.34, "text": " Right, we celebrate the rat.", "tokens": [51501, 1779, 11, 321, 8098, 264, 5937, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 49240, "start": 516.5, "end": 518.18, "text": " Yeah, we celebrate the historical origin.", "tokens": [51570, 865, 11, 321, 8098, 264, 8584, 4957, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 49240, "start": 518.4399999999999, "end": 518.62, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51667, 865, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11692982032650807, "compression_ratio": 1.6678200692041523, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489054266612512e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 51862, "start": 518.62, "end": 521.54, "text": " We look at the rat and say, wow, what a genius rat.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 574, 412, 264, 5937, 293, 584, 11, 6076, 11, 437, 257, 14017, 5937, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 51862, "start": 521.74, "end": 521.9, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50521, 865, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 51862, "start": 522.02, "end": 528.4, "text": " But we completely ignore the fact that the solid walls of the maze, the explanatory origin, dictated the path all along.", "tokens": [50535, 583, 321, 2584, 11200, 264, 1186, 300, 264, 5100, 7920, 295, 264, 33032, 11, 264, 9045, 4745, 4957, 11, 12569, 770, 264, 3100, 439, 2051, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 51862, "start": 528.52, "end": 529.48, "text": " It's a great analogy.", "tokens": [50860, 467, 311, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 51862, "start": 529.48, "end": 533.16, "text": " The rat didn't magically intuit the location of the cheese.", "tokens": [50908, 440, 5937, 994, 380, 39763, 16224, 264, 4914, 295, 264, 5399, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 51862, "start": 533.34, "end": 540.52, "text": " It just blindly bumped into the constraints of the maze walls until the only open path forced it toward the center.", "tokens": [51101, 467, 445, 47744, 42696, 666, 264, 18491, 295, 264, 33032, 7920, 1826, 264, 787, 1269, 3100, 7579, 309, 7361, 264, 3056, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 51862, "start": 540.7, "end": 542.86, "text": " That is a brilliant way to visualize it.", "tokens": [51469, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11364784064116301, "compression_ratio": 1.641732283464567, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043216680330705e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 54286, "start": 542.86, "end": 549.0600000000001, "text": " But fliction refers to those maze walls mathematically as the admissibility field.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 932, 4105, 14942, 281, 729, 33032, 7920, 44003, 382, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 54286, "start": 549.2, "end": 550.24, "text": " The admissibility field.", "tokens": [50682, 440, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 54286, "start": 550.3000000000001, "end": 550.52, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50737, 1779, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 54286, "start": 550.82, "end": 559.62, "text": " It is a field of physical, chemical, or biological constraints that makes certain outcomes not just possible, but highly probable.", "tokens": [50763, 467, 307, 257, 2519, 295, 4001, 11, 7313, 11, 420, 13910, 18491, 300, 1669, 1629, 10070, 406, 445, 1944, 11, 457, 5405, 21759, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 54286, "start": 559.96, "end": 560.96, "text": " So it guides the outcome.", "tokens": [51220, 407, 309, 17007, 264, 9700, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 54286, "start": 561.0600000000001, "end": 561.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51275, 7587, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 54286, "start": 561.78, "end": 564.22, "text": " The field admits certain shapes and rejects others.", "tokens": [51311, 440, 2519, 46682, 1629, 10854, 293, 8248, 82, 2357, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1872326688068669, "compression_ratio": 1.6195121951219513, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735357895146906e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 56422, "start": 564.22, "end": 570.44, "text": " And what is so compelling about this is that it doesn't just happen in controlled laboratory settings with microscopic bacteria.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 307, 370, 20050, 466, 341, 307, 300, 309, 1177, 380, 445, 1051, 294, 10164, 16523, 6257, 365, 47897, 11763, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 56422, "start": 570.8000000000001, "end": 571.58, "text": " Where else does it happen?", "tokens": [50694, 2305, 1646, 775, 309, 1051, 30, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 56422, "start": 571.9, "end": 575.2, "text": " Fliction points to a phenomenon they call deep absence.", "tokens": [50749, 3235, 4105, 2793, 281, 257, 14029, 436, 818, 2452, 17145, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 56422, "start": 575.86, "end": 579.62, "text": " This is when lineage isn't just screened off like in the 12 flasks.", "tokens": [50947, 639, 307, 562, 38257, 1943, 380, 445, 2568, 292, 766, 411, 294, 264, 2272, 932, 296, 1694, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 56422, "start": 579.78, "end": 579.94, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51143, 1033, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 56422, "start": 580.1800000000001, "end": 584.62, "text": " It is genuinely deeply absent, yet the exact same forms keep appearing.", "tokens": [51163, 467, 307, 17839, 8760, 25185, 11, 1939, 264, 1900, 912, 6422, 1066, 19870, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 56422, "start": 584.96, "end": 587.7, "text": " Which brings us to my absolute favorite part of this deep dive.", "tokens": [51402, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 452, 8236, 2954, 644, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 56422, "start": 588.0600000000001, "end": 591.5400000000001, "text": " The internet meme of everything evolving into crabs.", "tokens": [51557, 440, 4705, 21701, 295, 1203, 21085, 666, 35147, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 56422, "start": 592.24, "end": 592.76, "text": " Carcinization.", "tokens": [51766, 2741, 20021, 2144, 13, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1563435241955669, "compression_ratio": 1.5980392156862746, "no_speech_prob": 1.597738651451519e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 59276, "start": 592.76, "end": 593.36, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 59276, "start": 594.18, "end": 594.78, "text": " Carcinization.", "tokens": [50436, 2741, 20021, 2144, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 59276, "start": 595.28, "end": 598.52, "text": " If you spend any time online, you have probably seen the jokes.", "tokens": [50491, 759, 291, 3496, 604, 565, 2950, 11, 291, 362, 1391, 1612, 264, 14439, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 59276, "start": 599.1, "end": 600.14, "text": " Reject humanity.", "tokens": [50682, 1300, 1020, 10243, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 59276, "start": 600.56, "end": 601.22, "text": " Become crab.", "tokens": [50755, 44308, 17870, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 59276, "start": 601.3, "end": 601.9, "text": " I have seen it.", "tokens": [50792, 286, 362, 1612, 309, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 59276, "start": 601.96, "end": 602.14, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50825, 865, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 59276, "start": 602.4, "end": 605.6, "text": " It's this running joke that evolution only have one final form.", "tokens": [50847, 467, 311, 341, 2614, 7647, 300, 9303, 787, 362, 472, 2572, 1254, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 59276, "start": 606.3, "end": 612.78, "text": " But reading Fliction's breakdown, I realized it's a very real, very serious biological phenomenon.", "tokens": [51042, 583, 3760, 3235, 4105, 311, 18188, 11, 286, 5334, 309, 311, 257, 588, 957, 11, 588, 3156, 13910, 14029, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 59276, "start": 613.0, "end": 617.98, "text": " It is remarkably serious, and it perfectly illustrates the power of the admissibility field.", "tokens": [51377, 467, 307, 37381, 3156, 11, 293, 309, 6239, 41718, 264, 1347, 295, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20140990141396212, "compression_ratio": 1.5515873015873016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610408353270103e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 61798, "start": 617.98, "end": 627.48, "text": " In the evolutionary history of decapod crustaceans, the crab-like body plan has evolved completely independently at least five different times.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 264, 27567, 2503, 295, 368, 9485, 378, 18156, 617, 599, 11, 264, 17870, 12, 4092, 1772, 1393, 575, 14178, 2584, 21761, 412, 1935, 1732, 819, 1413, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16275205110248767, "compression_ratio": 1.502857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043298417187102e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 61798, "start": 627.58, "end": 633.62, "text": " Five independent times, meaning if you trace their family trees back, their most recent common ancestor was not a crab.", "tokens": [50845, 9436, 6695, 1413, 11, 3620, 498, 291, 13508, 641, 1605, 5852, 646, 11, 641, 881, 5162, 2689, 40032, 390, 406, 257, 17870, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16275205110248767, "compression_ratio": 1.502857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043298417187102e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 63362, "start": 633.62, "end": 641.46, "text": " Exactly. Not a crab. We have true crabs, like the blue crabs you might eat, and then we have false crabs, like the massive king crabs or tiny porcelain crabs.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 1726, 257, 17870, 13, 492, 362, 2074, 35147, 11, 411, 264, 3344, 35147, 291, 1062, 1862, 11, 293, 550, 321, 362, 7908, 35147, 11, 411, 264, 5994, 4867, 35147, 420, 5870, 1515, 4933, 491, 35147, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099686800778567, "compression_ratio": 1.6289592760180995, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 63362, "start": 641.58, "end": 642.6, "text": " But they look so similar.", "tokens": [50763, 583, 436, 574, 370, 2531, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099686800778567, "compression_ratio": 1.6289592760180995, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 63362, "start": 642.76, "end": 650.58, "text": " They look almost identical to the untrained eye, but their common ancestor was probably something long, soft, and stretched out. More like a lobster or a shrimp.", "tokens": [50822, 814, 574, 1920, 14800, 281, 264, 1701, 31774, 3313, 11, 457, 641, 2689, 40032, 390, 1391, 746, 938, 11, 2787, 11, 293, 23563, 484, 13, 5048, 411, 257, 33198, 420, 257, 15600, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099686800778567, "compression_ratio": 1.6289592760180995, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 63362, "start": 650.7, "end": 651.68, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [51219, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099686800778567, "compression_ratio": 1.6289592760180995, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 65168, "start": 651.68, "end": 655.38, "text": " Nature just keeps independently inventing the crab from scratch.", "tokens": [50365, 20159, 445, 5965, 21761, 7962, 278, 264, 17870, 490, 8459, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08041228850682576, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 65168, "start": 655.62, "end": 661.9799999999999, "text": " So why? I mean, if it's not a shared ancestor handing down the blueprints, why does nature keep putting the crab on the menu?", "tokens": [50562, 407, 983, 30, 286, 914, 11, 498, 309, 311, 406, 257, 5507, 40032, 34774, 760, 264, 888, 23547, 47523, 11, 983, 775, 3687, 1066, 3372, 264, 17870, 322, 264, 6510, 30, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08041228850682576, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 65168, "start": 662.38, "end": 666.04, "text": " It is critical that we don't fall into the teleological trap here.", "tokens": [50900, 467, 307, 4924, 300, 321, 500, 380, 2100, 666, 264, 4304, 4383, 11487, 510, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08041228850682576, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 65168, "start": 666.14, "end": 666.6999999999999, "text": " What does that mean?", "tokens": [51088, 708, 775, 300, 914, 30, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08041228850682576, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 65168, "start": 667.14, "end": 673.62, "text": " Evolution isn't aiming at an ideal, perfect crab form. It doesn't have a blueprint or a goal.", "tokens": [51138, 40800, 1943, 380, 20253, 412, 364, 7157, 11, 2176, 17870, 1254, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 362, 257, 35868, 420, 257, 3387, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08041228850682576, "compression_ratio": 1.5965665236051503, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674053851708059e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 67362, "start": 673.62, "end": 682.5, "text": " What is happening is that the physical admissibility field of living on the ocean floor heavily favors that specific geometric shape.", "tokens": [50365, 708, 307, 2737, 307, 300, 264, 4001, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 295, 2647, 322, 264, 7810, 4123, 10950, 40554, 300, 2685, 33246, 3909, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 67362, "start": 682.62, "end": 684.66, "text": " Okay, so the maze walls of the ocean floor.", "tokens": [50815, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 33032, 7920, 295, 264, 7810, 4123, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 67362, "start": 684.74, "end": 691.9, "text": " Yes. If you are a Crespation trying to survive on the bottom of the sea, a long, fleshy tail is a massive liability.", "tokens": [50921, 1079, 13, 759, 291, 366, 257, 383, 5667, 399, 1382, 281, 7867, 322, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 4158, 11, 257, 938, 11, 283, 904, 3495, 6838, 307, 257, 5994, 25196, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 67362, "start": 692.58, "end": 693.94, "text": " Predators can grab it easily.", "tokens": [51313, 32969, 3391, 393, 4444, 309, 3612, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 67362, "start": 694.08, "end": 695.6, "text": " Oh, right. It's just dangling out there.", "tokens": [51388, 876, 11, 558, 13, 467, 311, 445, 21892, 1688, 484, 456, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 67362, "start": 695.66, "end": 701.02, "text": " Exactly. But if you mutate to fold that tail underneath a wide, flat armor plate,", "tokens": [51467, 7587, 13, 583, 498, 291, 5839, 473, 281, 4860, 300, 6838, 7223, 257, 4874, 11, 4962, 13124, 5924, 11, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1069390814183122, "compression_ratio": 1.6137184115523466, "no_speech_prob": 1.507128189609519e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 70102, "start": 701.02, "end": 706.26, "text": " suddenly you can walk sideways, you can squeeze into incredibly tight rock crevices to hide,", "tokens": [50365, 5800, 291, 393, 1792, 26092, 11, 291, 393, 13578, 666, 6252, 4524, 3727, 1197, 85, 1473, 281, 6479, 11, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 70102, "start": 706.62, "end": 708.36, "text": " and you are much harder to eat.", "tokens": [50645, 293, 291, 366, 709, 6081, 281, 1862, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 70102, "start": 708.74, "end": 711.1999999999999, "text": " So the environment is basically forcing this shape.", "tokens": [50751, 407, 264, 2823, 307, 1936, 19030, 341, 3909, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 70102, "start": 711.6, "end": 715.9, "text": " The physical constraints of water pressure, rock geometry, and predation force,", "tokens": [50894, 440, 4001, 18491, 295, 1281, 3321, 11, 3727, 18426, 11, 293, 3852, 399, 3464, 11, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 70102, "start": 716.06, "end": 720.12, "text": " entirely different genetic lineages into the exact same morphological center.", "tokens": [51117, 7696, 819, 12462, 1622, 1660, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 25778, 4383, 3056, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 70102, "start": 720.48, "end": 722.0, "text": " The constraints do the designing.", "tokens": [51338, 440, 18491, 360, 264, 14685, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 70102, "start": 722.96, "end": 728.4399999999999, "text": " Infliction points out a fascinating counterexample to prove this isn't just a one-way street toward crab perfection, right?", "tokens": [51462, 682, 3423, 4105, 2793, 484, 257, 10343, 1207, 323, 87, 335, 781, 281, 7081, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 472, 12, 676, 4838, 7361, 17870, 19708, 11, 558, 30, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 70102, "start": 728.6999999999999, "end": 730.3199999999999, "text": " Right. Decarcinization.", "tokens": [51749, 1779, 13, 1346, 6166, 20021, 2144, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230160559377364, "compression_ratio": 1.648562300319489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837513813079073e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 73032, "start": 731.0200000000001, "end": 732.1, "text": " Decarcinization. What is that?", "tokens": [50400, 1346, 6166, 20021, 2144, 13, 708, 307, 300, 30, 50454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 73032, "start": 732.1, "end": 736.44, "text": " Well, if the crab form was some mystical evolutionary destiny,", "tokens": [50454, 1042, 11, 498, 264, 17870, 1254, 390, 512, 40565, 27567, 17893, 11, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 73032, "start": 736.84, "end": 739.88, "text": " everything would turn into a crab and stay that way forever.", "tokens": [50691, 1203, 576, 1261, 666, 257, 17870, 293, 1754, 300, 636, 5680, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 73032, "start": 740.0400000000001, "end": 740.5600000000001, "text": " Makes sense.", "tokens": [50851, 25245, 2020, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 73032, "start": 740.7, "end": 743.48, "text": " But the fossil record shows decarcinization,", "tokens": [50884, 583, 264, 18737, 2136, 3110, 979, 289, 20021, 2144, 11, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 73032, "start": 743.82, "end": 749.0400000000001, "text": " where a lineage that was shaped like a crab mutates and actually loses the crab shape,", "tokens": [51040, 689, 257, 38257, 300, 390, 13475, 411, 257, 17870, 5839, 1024, 293, 767, 18293, 264, 17870, 3909, 11, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 73032, "start": 749.36, "end": 750.74, "text": " elongating back out.", "tokens": [51317, 40786, 990, 646, 484, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 73032, "start": 750.9200000000001, "end": 752.6, "text": " Wow. Does that happen a lot?", "tokens": [51395, 3153, 13, 4402, 300, 1051, 257, 688, 30, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 73032, "start": 752.7600000000001, "end": 754.4000000000001, "text": " It's happened at least seven times.", "tokens": [51487, 467, 311, 2011, 412, 1935, 3407, 1413, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 73032, "start": 754.5400000000001, "end": 755.46, "text": " Seven times.", "tokens": [51576, 14868, 1413, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18374411843039773, "compression_ratio": 1.6048387096774193, "no_speech_prob": 1.585637328903322e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 75546, "start": 755.46, "end": 758.14, "text": " Yeah. It proves that the crab shape isn't a destiny.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 467, 25019, 300, 264, 17870, 3909, 1943, 380, 257, 17893, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362714616079179, "compression_ratio": 1.5209580838323353, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507364032086196e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 75546, "start": 758.36, "end": 761.08, "text": " It is just a highly favored region of the constraint space.", "tokens": [50510, 467, 307, 445, 257, 5405, 44420, 4458, 295, 264, 25534, 1901, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362714616079179, "compression_ratio": 1.5209580838323353, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507364032086196e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 75546, "start": 761.72, "end": 764.9000000000001, "text": " If the environment changes or a species moves to a different habitat,", "tokens": [50678, 759, 264, 2823, 2962, 420, 257, 6172, 6067, 281, 257, 819, 20110, 11, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362714616079179, "compression_ratio": 1.5209580838323353, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507364032086196e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 75546, "start": 765.4200000000001, "end": 769.0, "text": " the maze walls shift and the species gets pushed out of the crab shape.", "tokens": [50863, 264, 33032, 7920, 5513, 293, 264, 6172, 2170, 9152, 484, 295, 264, 17870, 3909, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1362714616079179, "compression_ratio": 1.5209580838323353, "no_speech_prob": 2.1507364032086196e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 76900, "start": 769.0, "end": 772.28, "text": " Okay, so we can clearly see how this works with physical biology.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 393, 4448, 536, 577, 341, 1985, 365, 4001, 14956, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1395118168422154, "compression_ratio": 1.450777202072539, "no_speech_prob": 3.0324911418772027e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 76900, "start": 773.02, "end": 775.5, "text": " The ocean floor acts as a constraint space.", "tokens": [50566, 440, 7810, 4123, 10672, 382, 257, 25534, 1901, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1395118168422154, "compression_ratio": 1.450777202072539, "no_speech_prob": 3.0324911418772027e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 76900, "start": 776.46, "end": 783.4, "text": " But what absolutely blew my mind is how fliction and scales this exact same framework up to intellectual and cultural history.", "tokens": [50738, 583, 437, 3122, 19075, 452, 1575, 307, 577, 932, 4105, 293, 17408, 341, 1900, 912, 8388, 493, 281, 12576, 293, 6988, 2503, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1395118168422154, "compression_ratio": 1.450777202072539, "no_speech_prob": 3.0324911418772027e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 76900, "start": 783.46, "end": 785.44, "text": " Oh, it's a huge leap, but it works so well.", "tokens": [51088, 876, 11, 309, 311, 257, 2603, 19438, 11, 457, 309, 1985, 370, 731, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1395118168422154, "compression_ratio": 1.450777202072539, "no_speech_prob": 3.0324911418772027e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 78544, "start": 785.44, "end": 790.08, "text": " They argue that human ideas and inventions are also governed by admissibility fields.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 9695, 300, 1952, 3487, 293, 43748, 366, 611, 35529, 538, 5910, 891, 2841, 7909, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 78544, "start": 790.4000000000001, "end": 791.32, "text": " They absolutely are.", "tokens": [50613, 814, 3122, 366, 13, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 78544, "start": 791.5200000000001, "end": 795.34, "text": " The classic example is the theory of evolution by natural selection.", "tokens": [50669, 440, 7230, 1365, 307, 264, 5261, 295, 9303, 538, 3303, 9450, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 78544, "start": 796.0, "end": 804.9000000000001, "text": " Charles Darwin and Alfred Russell Wallace independently arrived at the exact same world-altering biological theory at almost the exact same time.", "tokens": [50893, 10523, 30233, 293, 28327, 20937, 32626, 21761, 6678, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 1002, 12, 304, 34200, 13910, 5261, 412, 1920, 264, 1900, 912, 565, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 78544, "start": 805.0200000000001, "end": 805.98, "text": " And they didn't know each other.", "tokens": [51344, 400, 436, 994, 380, 458, 1184, 661, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 78544, "start": 806.22, "end": 809.48, "text": " Well, Wallace was sweating in a jungle in the Malay archipelago,", "tokens": [51404, 1042, 11, 32626, 390, 25438, 294, 257, 18228, 294, 264, 5746, 320, 3912, 647, 338, 6442, 11, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 78544, "start": 809.9000000000001, "end": 812.6400000000001, "text": " and Darwin was sitting in his comfortable study in England.", "tokens": [51588, 293, 30233, 390, 3798, 294, 702, 4619, 2979, 294, 8196, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 78544, "start": 813.2600000000001, "end": 815.0200000000001, "text": " They were completely isolated from one another.", "tokens": [51756, 814, 645, 2584, 14621, 490, 472, 1071, 13, 51844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694373603628463, "compression_ratio": 1.673015873015873, "no_speech_prob": 3.080176955508329e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 81502, "start": 815.02, "end": 816.98, "text": " They were not copying each other's homework.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 645, 406, 27976, 1184, 661, 311, 14578, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 81502, "start": 817.3199999999999, "end": 820.52, "text": " So how did they both bump into the same cheese at the center of the maze?", "tokens": [50480, 407, 577, 630, 436, 1293, 9961, 666, 264, 912, 5399, 412, 264, 3056, 295, 264, 33032, 30, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 81502, "start": 820.68, "end": 824.66, "text": " Because they were navigating the same intellectual admissibility field.", "tokens": [50648, 1436, 436, 645, 32054, 264, 912, 12576, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 81502, "start": 825.5, "end": 830.1999999999999, "text": " In the mid-19th century, certain intellectual maze walls had been constructed.", "tokens": [50889, 682, 264, 2062, 12, 3405, 392, 4901, 11, 1629, 12576, 33032, 7920, 632, 668, 17083, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 81502, "start": 830.3199999999999, "end": 831.0799999999999, "text": " Like what kind of walls?", "tokens": [51130, 1743, 437, 733, 295, 7920, 30, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 81502, "start": 831.38, "end": 838.06, "text": " Well, both men had access to a massive, accumulating body of geological data showing the Earth was incredibly old.", "tokens": [51183, 1042, 11, 1293, 1706, 632, 2105, 281, 257, 5994, 11, 12989, 12162, 1772, 295, 1519, 4383, 1412, 4099, 264, 4755, 390, 6252, 1331, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 81502, "start": 838.12, "end": 838.92, "text": " Okay, that's one wall.", "tokens": [51520, 1033, 11, 300, 311, 472, 2929, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 81502, "start": 839.0799999999999, "end": 841.26, "text": " Both men were studying island biogeography.", "tokens": [51568, 6767, 1706, 645, 7601, 6077, 12198, 432, 5820, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10290106272293349, "compression_ratio": 1.6135593220338984, "no_speech_prob": 1.2159454216079113e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 84126, "start": 841.26, "end": 851.86, "text": " And crucially, both men read the economist Thomas Malthus, who wrote about population growth inevitably outstripping the food supply, creating a struggle for existence.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 1293, 1706, 1401, 264, 36696, 8500, 376, 1302, 301, 11, 567, 4114, 466, 4415, 4599, 28171, 484, 372, 470, 3759, 264, 1755, 5847, 11, 4084, 257, 7799, 337, 9123, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13120654135039359, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298430704012046e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 84126, "start": 852.3199999999999, "end": 854.6, "text": " Ah, so they had the same foundational pieces.", "tokens": [50918, 2438, 11, 370, 436, 632, 264, 912, 32195, 3755, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13120654135039359, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298430704012046e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 84126, "start": 854.9, "end": 855.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51047, 1779, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13120654135039359, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298430704012046e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 84126, "start": 855.22, "end": 858.88, "text": " Those three pillars of knowledge formed a constraint space.", "tokens": [51063, 3950, 1045, 26729, 295, 3601, 8693, 257, 25534, 1901, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13120654135039359, "compression_ratio": 1.4635416666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.6298430704012046e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 85888, "start": 858.88, "end": 868.14, "text": " Once you enter that specific intellectual space, the theory of natural selection becomes highly accessible from multiple independent starting points.", "tokens": [50365, 3443, 291, 3242, 300, 2685, 12576, 1901, 11, 264, 5261, 295, 3303, 9450, 3643, 5405, 9515, 490, 3866, 6695, 2891, 2793, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15922991909197906, "compression_ratio": 1.4825870646766168, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900343750668068e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 85888, "start": 868.78, "end": 870.7, "text": " The field did the heavy lifting.", "tokens": [50860, 440, 2519, 630, 264, 4676, 15798, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15922991909197906, "compression_ratio": 1.4825870646766168, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900343750668068e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 85888, "start": 871.32, "end": 873.9399999999999, "text": " Infliction points out an even bigger example of this, right?", "tokens": [50987, 682, 3423, 4105, 2793, 484, 364, 754, 3801, 1365, 295, 341, 11, 558, 30, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15922991909197906, "compression_ratio": 1.4825870646766168, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900343750668068e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 85888, "start": 874.36, "end": 876.02, "text": " The invention of human agriculture.", "tokens": [51139, 440, 22265, 295, 1952, 14837, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15922991909197906, "compression_ratio": 1.4825870646766168, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900343750668068e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 85888, "start": 876.36, "end": 877.36, "text": " That's a huge one.", "tokens": [51239, 663, 311, 257, 2603, 472, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15922991909197906, "compression_ratio": 1.4825870646766168, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900343750668068e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 87736, "start": 877.36, "end": 883.9, "text": " We are talking about human populations in the Fertile Crescent, in China, in Mesoamerica, the Andes, New Guinea.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 1952, 12822, 294, 264, 479, 911, 794, 383, 495, 2207, 11, 294, 3533, 11, 294, 17485, 78, 13530, 2262, 11, 264, 400, 279, 11, 1873, 46793, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 87736, "start": 885.0600000000001, "end": 894.08, "text": " All of these completely isolated groups independently invented agriculture and the domestication of plants right after the end of the last ice age.", "tokens": [50750, 1057, 295, 613, 2584, 14621, 3935, 21761, 14479, 14837, 293, 264, 10939, 399, 295, 5972, 558, 934, 264, 917, 295, 264, 1036, 4435, 3205, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 87736, "start": 894.24, "end": 895.36, "text": " Yeah, totally independent.", "tokens": [51209, 865, 11, 3879, 6695, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 87736, "start": 895.5600000000001, "end": 900.1, "text": " There was no global WhatsApp group where they texted each other, hey, I just figured out how to plant wheat.", "tokens": [51275, 821, 390, 572, 4338, 30513, 1594, 689, 436, 42553, 1184, 661, 11, 4177, 11, 286, 445, 8932, 484, 577, 281, 3709, 16691, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 87736, "start": 900.1800000000001, "end": 900.9, "text": " You guys should try this.", "tokens": [51506, 509, 1074, 820, 853, 341, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 87736, "start": 900.96, "end": 901.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51545, 1779, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09733659816238116, "compression_ratio": 1.56, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897530246030469e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 90116, "start": 901.16, "end": 905.4599999999999, "text": " The post-glacial climate stabilization was a shared global constraint.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2183, 12, 7191, 25980, 5659, 35476, 390, 257, 5507, 4338, 25534, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 90116, "start": 906.2199999999999, "end": 912.0, "text": " The chaotic, freezing climate of the Pleistocene acted as a barrier preventing agriculture.", "tokens": [50618, 440, 27013, 11, 20200, 5659, 295, 264, 25658, 468, 905, 1450, 20359, 382, 257, 13357, 19965, 14837, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 90116, "start": 912.2199999999999, "end": 913.8199999999999, "text": " It kept them out of that part of the maze.", "tokens": [50918, 467, 4305, 552, 484, 295, 300, 644, 295, 264, 33032, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 90116, "start": 914.18, "end": 914.5799999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51016, 7587, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 90116, "start": 915.04, "end": 924.7199999999999, "text": " Once that barrier lifted, the combination of human cognitive capacity and stable seasonal weather created a massive global admissibility field.", "tokens": [51059, 3443, 300, 13357, 17854, 11, 264, 6562, 295, 1952, 15605, 6042, 293, 8351, 27421, 5503, 2942, 257, 5994, 4338, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 90116, "start": 925.12, "end": 928.9599999999999, "text": " It pushed isolated populations toward the same behavioral attractor.", "tokens": [51563, 467, 9152, 14621, 12822, 7361, 264, 912, 19124, 5049, 284, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1142033197546518, "compression_ratio": 1.623574144486692, "no_speech_prob": 1.427272471217489e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 92896, "start": 928.96, "end": 933.96, "text": " Which raises a really profound question about how we view human invention, honestly.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 19658, 257, 534, 14382, 1168, 466, 577, 321, 1910, 1952, 22265, 11, 6095, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 92896, "start": 934.22, "end": 934.64, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [50628, 1012, 370, 30, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 92896, "start": 934.72, "end": 938.1600000000001, "text": " Well, we love the myth of the lone genius having a sudden eureka moment.", "tokens": [50653, 1042, 11, 321, 959, 264, 9474, 295, 264, 35314, 14017, 1419, 257, 3990, 32845, 2330, 1623, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 92896, "start": 938.7800000000001, "end": 946.9200000000001, "text": " But Fliction suggests that if the cultural and environmental field is narrow enough, multiple independent discoveries aren't a spooky magical coincidence.", "tokens": [50856, 583, 3235, 4105, 13409, 300, 498, 264, 6988, 293, 8303, 2519, 307, 9432, 1547, 11, 3866, 6695, 28400, 3212, 380, 257, 30510, 12066, 22137, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 92896, "start": 947.5400000000001, "end": 949.96, "text": " They are the statistical mathematical expectation.", "tokens": [51294, 814, 366, 264, 22820, 18894, 14334, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 92896, "start": 950.62, "end": 951.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51448, 7587, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 92896, "start": 951.34, "end": 956.72, "text": " Okay, but I have to jump in here and push back on this a little bit because as I was reading this section, I kept thinking about mathematics.", "tokens": [51484, 1033, 11, 457, 286, 362, 281, 3012, 294, 510, 293, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 857, 570, 382, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 3541, 11, 286, 4305, 1953, 466, 18666, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 92896, "start": 957.08, "end": 958.36, "text": " Oh, this is a tricky area.", "tokens": [51771, 876, 11, 341, 307, 257, 12414, 1859, 13, 51835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11186224316793775, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428712994702831e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 95836, "start": 958.36, "end": 966.3000000000001, "text": " If we're talking about different cultures independently discovering the same thing, isn't math the ultimate slam-dunk example of Fliction's theory?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 819, 12951, 21761, 24773, 264, 912, 551, 11, 1943, 380, 5221, 264, 9705, 25617, 12, 67, 3197, 1365, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 5261, 30, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09095085991753472, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359711979205271e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 95836, "start": 966.5, "end": 967.46, "text": " You'd think so, wouldn't you?", "tokens": [50772, 509, 1116, 519, 370, 11, 2759, 380, 291, 30, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09095085991753472, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359711979205271e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 95836, "start": 967.62, "end": 967.82, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50828, 865, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09095085991753472, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359711979205271e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 95836, "start": 968.12, "end": 978.4, "text": " You look at ancient history and the Babylonians, the Chinese, the Greeks in antiquity, they all independently discovered the Pythagorean theorem without ever communicating.", "tokens": [50853, 509, 574, 412, 7832, 2503, 293, 264, 30278, 2567, 11, 264, 4649, 11, 264, 31029, 294, 41036, 507, 11, 436, 439, 21761, 6941, 264, 9953, 392, 559, 25885, 20904, 1553, 1562, 17559, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09095085991753472, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359711979205271e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 95836, "start": 979.12, "end": 982.66, "text": " Doesn't that prove the idea of an admissibility field perfectly?", "tokens": [51403, 12955, 380, 300, 7081, 264, 1558, 295, 364, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 6239, 30, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09095085991753472, "compression_ratio": 1.6007604562737643, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359711979205271e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 98266, "start": 982.66, "end": 993.16, "text": " It is incredibly tempting to use mathematics as the ultimate proof, but Fliction is actually very careful to deliberately exclude mathematics from this specific argument.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 6252, 37900, 281, 764, 18666, 382, 264, 9705, 8177, 11, 457, 3235, 4105, 307, 767, 588, 5026, 281, 23506, 33536, 18666, 490, 341, 2685, 6770, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 98266, "start": 993.3199999999999, "end": 993.86, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50898, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 98266, "start": 994.2199999999999, "end": 994.56, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [50943, 1545, 30, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 98266, "start": 995.1, "end": 996.2199999999999, "text": " It seems like a perfect fit.", "tokens": [50987, 467, 2544, 411, 257, 2176, 3318, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 98266, "start": 996.36, "end": 1002.3199999999999, "text": " Because there is a vital difference in the modality of the truth being discovered.", "tokens": [51050, 1436, 456, 307, 257, 11707, 2649, 294, 264, 1072, 1860, 295, 264, 3494, 885, 6941, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 98266, "start": 1002.74, "end": 1003.48, "text": " The modality?", "tokens": [51369, 440, 1072, 1860, 30, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1545509084065755, "compression_ratio": 1.5217391304347827, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465658689625908e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 100348, "start": 1003.48, "end": 1003.9200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12149723186049351, "compression_ratio": 1.7399103139013452, "no_speech_prob": 1.8820602628449867e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 100348, "start": 1004.12, "end": 1014.5, "text": " When we talk about biological convergence, like the crabs, or cultural convergence, like agriculture, we are talking about probability within a biased attractor.", "tokens": [50397, 1133, 321, 751, 466, 13910, 32181, 11, 411, 264, 35147, 11, 420, 6988, 32181, 11, 411, 14837, 11, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 8482, 1951, 257, 28035, 5049, 284, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12149723186049351, "compression_ratio": 1.7399103139013452, "no_speech_prob": 1.8820602628449867e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 100348, "start": 1014.54, "end": 1015.34, "text": " Okay, probability.", "tokens": [50918, 1033, 11, 8482, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12149723186049351, "compression_ratio": 1.7399103139013452, "no_speech_prob": 1.8820602628449867e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 100348, "start": 1015.74, "end": 1026.28, "text": " The physical constraints of the ocean make the crab shape highly likely, but as we saw with the species that lost the crab shape, it is not strictly logically necessary for survival.", "tokens": [50978, 440, 4001, 18491, 295, 264, 7810, 652, 264, 17870, 3909, 5405, 3700, 11, 457, 382, 321, 1866, 365, 264, 6172, 300, 2731, 264, 17870, 3909, 11, 309, 307, 406, 20792, 38887, 4818, 337, 12559, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12149723186049351, "compression_ratio": 1.7399103139013452, "no_speech_prob": 1.8820602628449867e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 100348, "start": 1026.48, "end": 1027.0, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [51515, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12149723186049351, "compression_ratio": 1.7399103139013452, "no_speech_prob": 1.8820602628449867e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 102700, "start": 1027.0, "end": 1033.74, "text": " But mathematics operates in a completely different realm. Mathematics is about absolute logical necessity.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 18666, 22577, 294, 257, 2584, 819, 15355, 13, 15776, 37541, 307, 466, 8236, 14978, 24217, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09689380725224812, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668258791096124e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 102700, "start": 1034.1, "end": 1038.8, "text": " Oh, I see. Because 2 plus 2 equaling 5 is just not an option on the table no matter what environment you are in.", "tokens": [50720, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 1436, 568, 1804, 568, 2681, 278, 1025, 307, 445, 406, 364, 3614, 322, 264, 3199, 572, 1871, 437, 2823, 291, 366, 294, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09689380725224812, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668258791096124e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 102700, "start": 1038.9, "end": 1052.34, "text": " Exactly. Mathematical convergence isn't a biological trajectory being physically squeezed toward a highly probable outcome by the environment. It is a logical trajectory arriving at the only coherent outcome that exists.", "tokens": [50960, 7587, 13, 15776, 8615, 804, 32181, 1943, 380, 257, 13910, 21512, 885, 9762, 39470, 7361, 257, 5405, 21759, 9700, 538, 264, 2823, 13, 467, 307, 257, 14978, 21512, 22436, 412, 264, 787, 36239, 9700, 300, 8198, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09689380725224812, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668258791096124e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 102700, "start": 1052.52, "end": 1053.14, "text": " Wow, okay.", "tokens": [51641, 3153, 11, 1392, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09689380725224812, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.5668258791096124e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 105314, "start": 1053.14, "end": 1067.76, "text": " The Babylonians and the Greeks didn't independently invent the Pythagorean theorem because their environments shared similar constraints. They discovered it because there is no alternative geometry available without breaking the fundamental laws of logic itself.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 30278, 2567, 293, 264, 31029, 994, 380, 21761, 7962, 264, 9953, 392, 559, 25885, 20904, 570, 641, 12388, 5507, 2531, 18491, 13, 814, 6941, 309, 570, 456, 307, 572, 8535, 18426, 2435, 1553, 7697, 264, 8088, 6064, 295, 9952, 2564, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06396666921750464, "compression_ratio": 1.6081504702194358, "no_speech_prob": 2.12534829145683e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 105314, "start": 1068.1000000000001, "end": 1070.72, "text": " So it's not a maze, it's just a single straight line.", "tokens": [51113, 407, 309, 311, 406, 257, 33032, 11, 309, 311, 445, 257, 2167, 2997, 1622, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06396666921750464, "compression_ratio": 1.6081504702194358, "no_speech_prob": 2.12534829145683e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 105314, "start": 1070.8400000000001, "end": 1081.94, "text": " Yes. If fliction included mathematics in their theory of admissibility fields, they would be confusing physical likelihood with logical necessity, which would actually weaken the entire framework.", "tokens": [51250, 1079, 13, 759, 932, 4105, 5556, 18666, 294, 641, 5261, 295, 5910, 891, 2841, 7909, 11, 436, 576, 312, 13181, 4001, 22119, 365, 14978, 24217, 11, 597, 576, 767, 48576, 264, 2302, 8388, 13, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06396666921750464, "compression_ratio": 1.6081504702194358, "no_speech_prob": 2.12534829145683e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 108194, "start": 1081.94, "end": 1090.8400000000001, "text": " That is a really elegant distinction. So, keeping math in its own lane, what does this framework mean for how we view originality in science and art?", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 534, 21117, 16844, 13, 407, 11, 5145, 5221, 294, 1080, 1065, 12705, 11, 437, 775, 341, 8388, 914, 337, 577, 321, 1910, 4957, 1860, 294, 3497, 293, 1523, 30, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05884119531382685, "compression_ratio": 1.62012987012987, "no_speech_prob": 2.092399170594561e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 108194, "start": 1090.94, "end": 1091.94, "text": " It's pretty disruptive.", "tokens": [50815, 467, 311, 1238, 37865, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05884119531382685, "compression_ratio": 1.62012987012987, "no_speech_prob": 2.092399170594561e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 108194, "start": 1092.14, "end": 1098.72, "text": " Yeah, if the maze walls are doing the actual work of guiding discovery, what happens to our concept of the genius inventor?", "tokens": [50875, 865, 11, 498, 264, 33032, 7920, 366, 884, 264, 3539, 589, 295, 25061, 12114, 11, 437, 2314, 281, 527, 3410, 295, 264, 14017, 41593, 30, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05884119531382685, "compression_ratio": 1.62012987012987, "no_speech_prob": 2.092399170594561e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 108194, "start": 1098.94, "end": 1108.24, "text": " It completely disrupts it, like I said. Fliction argues that as a society, we waste a massive amount of institutional and emotional energy obsessing over priority.", "tokens": [51215, 467, 2584, 14124, 82, 309, 11, 411, 286, 848, 13, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 382, 257, 4086, 11, 321, 5964, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 18391, 293, 6863, 2281, 35803, 278, 670, 9365, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05884119531382685, "compression_ratio": 1.62012987012987, "no_speech_prob": 2.092399170594561e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 108194, "start": 1108.48, "end": 1109.94, "text": " Priority meaning who got there first?", "tokens": [51692, 24032, 507, 3620, 567, 658, 456, 700, 30, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05884119531382685, "compression_ratio": 1.62012987012987, "no_speech_prob": 2.092399170594561e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 110994, "start": 1109.94, "end": 1120.04, "text": " The obsession with who got there first. Think about the infamous priority dispute over the invention of calculus between Isaac Newton and Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz in the 17th century.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 30521, 365, 567, 658, 456, 700, 13, 6557, 466, 264, 30769, 9365, 25379, 670, 264, 22265, 295, 33400, 1296, 22505, 19541, 293, 19133, 22773, 9483, 48319, 1456, 897, 77, 590, 294, 264, 3282, 392, 4901, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06592130041741706, "compression_ratio": 1.4618644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484496059843146e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 110994, "start": 1120.3, "end": 1129.46, "text": " Oh, that was notoriously vicious. There were accusations of plagiarism, the Royal Society in London got involved, reputations were just dragged through the mud.", "tokens": [50883, 876, 11, 300, 390, 46772, 8994, 30093, 13, 821, 645, 38556, 295, 33756, 9448, 1434, 11, 264, 12717, 13742, 294, 7042, 658, 3288, 11, 1085, 325, 763, 645, 445, 25717, 807, 264, 8933, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06592130041741706, "compression_ratio": 1.4618644067796611, "no_speech_prob": 1.6484496059843146e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 112946, "start": 1129.46, "end": 1143.82, "text": " It was decades of bitter, toxic fighting over the historical origin. The entire scientific community was obsessed with the lineage. Who had the idea first? Did Leibniz secretly peek at Newton's unpublished letters?", "tokens": [50365, 467, 390, 7878, 295, 13871, 11, 12786, 5237, 670, 264, 8584, 4957, 13, 440, 2302, 8134, 1768, 390, 16923, 365, 264, 38257, 13, 2102, 632, 264, 1558, 700, 30, 2589, 1456, 897, 77, 590, 22611, 19604, 412, 19541, 311, 20994, 836, 4173, 7825, 30, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07388238249153926, "compression_ratio": 1.379120879120879, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797050082963504e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 112946, "start": 1144.08, "end": 1145.98, "text": " It was basically a giant soap opera.", "tokens": [51096, 467, 390, 1936, 257, 7410, 14587, 22202, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07388238249153926, "compression_ratio": 1.379120879120879, "no_speech_prob": 1.5797050082963504e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 114598, "start": 1145.98, "end": 1161.7, "text": " It was. But fiction points out that this obsession entirely misses the explanatory origin. The antecedent mathematical field, the prior work done by thinkers like Fermat, Barrow, and Wallace, had already narrowed the space of viable next steps so significantly.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 390, 13, 583, 13266, 2793, 484, 300, 341, 30521, 7696, 29394, 264, 9045, 4745, 4957, 13, 440, 23411, 1232, 317, 18894, 2519, 11, 264, 4059, 589, 1096, 538, 37895, 411, 43261, 267, 11, 4156, 1892, 11, 293, 32626, 11, 632, 1217, 9432, 292, 264, 1901, 295, 22024, 958, 4439, 370, 10591, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057135229680075575, "compression_ratio": 1.4771573604060915, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363630285856634e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 114598, "start": 1161.8600000000001, "end": 1162.94, "text": " It was just a matter of time.", "tokens": [51159, 467, 390, 445, 257, 1871, 295, 565, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.057135229680075575, "compression_ratio": 1.4771573604060915, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363630285856634e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 116294, "start": 1162.94, "end": 1168.76, "text": " Right. The invention of calculus was basically inevitable for anyone who was paying attention and had the right cognitive tools.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 22265, 295, 33400, 390, 1936, 21451, 337, 2878, 567, 390, 6229, 3202, 293, 632, 264, 558, 15605, 3873, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10882797626533894, "compression_ratio": 1.6288659793814433, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406808215682409e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 116294, "start": 1169.24, "end": 1176.52, "text": " Priority in this context is just a relationship between a thinker's trajectory and a stopwatch. It doesn't actually tell you anything about the invention itself.", "tokens": [50680, 24032, 507, 294, 341, 4319, 307, 445, 257, 2480, 1296, 257, 519, 260, 311, 21512, 293, 257, 1590, 15219, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 767, 980, 291, 1340, 466, 264, 22265, 2564, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10882797626533894, "compression_ratio": 1.6288659793814433, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406808215682409e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 116294, "start": 1176.64, "end": 1180.74, "text": " So how should we define originality, if not by who crossed the finish line first?", "tokens": [51050, 407, 577, 820, 321, 6964, 4957, 1860, 11, 498, 406, 538, 567, 14622, 264, 2413, 1622, 700, 30, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10882797626533894, "compression_ratio": 1.6288659793814433, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406808215682409e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 116294, "start": 1181.44, "end": 1187.0800000000002, "text": " Flitchin suggests that true originality means genuinely traversing the constraint structure yourself.", "tokens": [51290, 3235, 1549, 259, 13409, 300, 2074, 4957, 1860, 1355, 17839, 23149, 278, 264, 25534, 3877, 1803, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10882797626533894, "compression_ratio": 1.6288659793814433, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406808215682409e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 118708, "start": 1187.08, "end": 1188.06, "text": " Ooh, I like that.", "tokens": [50365, 7951, 11, 286, 411, 300, 13, 50414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07633570994227386, "compression_ratio": 1.6137071651090342, "no_speech_prob": 1.543106788182147e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 118708, "start": 1188.06, "end": 1201.28, "text": " It means doing the cognitive labor of bumping into the maze walls, calculating the dead ends, and finding the center on your own merit, rather than just taking a shortcut and copying the finished product from someone else.", "tokens": [50414, 467, 1355, 884, 264, 15605, 5938, 295, 9961, 278, 666, 264, 33032, 7920, 11, 28258, 264, 3116, 5314, 11, 293, 5006, 264, 3056, 322, 428, 1065, 24527, 11, 2831, 813, 445, 1940, 257, 24822, 293, 27976, 264, 4335, 1674, 490, 1580, 1646, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07633570994227386, "compression_ratio": 1.6137071651090342, "no_speech_prob": 1.543106788182147e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 118708, "start": 1201.3799999999999, "end": 1206.54, "text": " So by that definition, both Newton and Leibniz were fully, genuinely original.", "tokens": [51080, 407, 538, 300, 7123, 11, 1293, 19541, 293, 1456, 897, 77, 590, 645, 4498, 11, 17839, 3380, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07633570994227386, "compression_ratio": 1.6137071651090342, "no_speech_prob": 1.543106788182147e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 118708, "start": 1206.8999999999999, "end": 1212.4199999999998, "text": " Exactly. Regardless of what the clock said, because they both did the intellectual labor of navigating the field.", "tokens": [51356, 7587, 13, 25148, 295, 437, 264, 7830, 848, 11, 570, 436, 1293, 630, 264, 12576, 5938, 295, 32054, 264, 2519, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07633570994227386, "compression_ratio": 1.6137071651090342, "no_speech_prob": 1.543106788182147e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 118708, "start": 1212.6, "end": 1216.74, "text": " But just to be clear, Flitchin isn't saying that lineage is never the answer, right?", "tokens": [51641, 583, 445, 281, 312, 1850, 11, 3235, 1549, 259, 1943, 380, 1566, 300, 38257, 307, 1128, 264, 1867, 11, 558, 30, 51848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07633570994227386, "compression_ratio": 1.6137071651090342, "no_speech_prob": 1.543106788182147e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 121674, "start": 1216.74, "end": 1217.02, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 121674, "start": 1217.56, "end": 1225.94, "text": " Because if I am a college professor and a student hands in an essay that is word-for-word copied from a Wikipedia article, I'm not going to stroke my chin and say,", "tokens": [50406, 1436, 498, 286, 669, 257, 3859, 8304, 293, 257, 3107, 2377, 294, 364, 16238, 300, 307, 1349, 12, 2994, 12, 7462, 25365, 490, 257, 28999, 7222, 11, 286, 478, 406, 516, 281, 12403, 452, 14210, 293, 584, 11, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 121674, "start": 1226.06, "end": 1231.66, "text": " ah, yes, they must have just navigated the same cultural admissibility field as the Wikipedia editors.", "tokens": [50831, 3716, 11, 2086, 11, 436, 1633, 362, 445, 7407, 770, 264, 912, 6988, 5910, 891, 2841, 2519, 382, 264, 28999, 31446, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 121674, "start": 1231.8, "end": 1233.58, "text": " No, absolutely not. That would be absurd.", "tokens": [51118, 883, 11, 3122, 406, 13, 663, 576, 312, 19774, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 121674, "start": 1234.14, "end": 1238.6200000000001, "text": " And Flitchin provides a very clear caveat for this called, when lineage wins.", "tokens": [51235, 400, 3235, 1549, 259, 6417, 257, 588, 1850, 43012, 337, 341, 1219, 11, 562, 38257, 10641, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 121674, "start": 1238.94, "end": 1240.2, "text": " When lineage wins.", "tokens": [51475, 1133, 38257, 10641, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 121674, "start": 1240.2, "end": 1240.6200000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51538, 1033, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 121674, "start": 1240.94, "end": 1246.38, "text": " If you are tracking the spread of an internet meme or analyzing scribal spelling errors in ancient texts", "tokens": [51575, 759, 291, 366, 11603, 264, 3974, 295, 364, 4705, 21701, 420, 23663, 39435, 304, 22254, 13603, 294, 7832, 15765, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500727797999527, "compression_ratio": 1.5818181818181818, "no_speech_prob": 1.9733453152787073e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 124638, "start": 1246.38, "end": 1255.0800000000002, "text": " or dealing with blatant plagiarism, the lineage explanation, the historical origin is almost always the correct and most efficient explanation.", "tokens": [50365, 420, 6260, 365, 42780, 394, 33756, 9448, 1434, 11, 264, 38257, 10835, 11, 264, 8584, 4957, 307, 1920, 1009, 264, 3006, 293, 881, 7148, 10835, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19283662993332434, "compression_ratio": 1.4834437086092715, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813179537847334e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 124638, "start": 1255.38, "end": 1256.7600000000002, "text": " So there's a rule of thumb for this.", "tokens": [50815, 407, 456, 311, 257, 4978, 295, 9298, 337, 341, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19283662993332434, "compression_ratio": 1.4834437086092715, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813179537847334e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 124638, "start": 1257.0800000000002, "end": 1257.2600000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50900, 865, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19283662993332434, "compression_ratio": 1.4834437086092715, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813179537847334e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 124638, "start": 1257.4, "end": 1259.0600000000002, "text": " Flitchin gives a solid rule of thumb.", "tokens": [50916, 3235, 1549, 259, 2709, 257, 5100, 4978, 295, 9298, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19283662993332434, "compression_ratio": 1.4834437086092715, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813179537847334e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 125906, "start": 1259.06, "end": 1265.5, "text": " If a transmission channel between two similar things is plausible and open, you should default to assuming lineage.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 11574, 2269, 1296, 732, 2531, 721, 307, 39925, 293, 1269, 11, 291, 820, 7576, 281, 11926, 38257, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1349327632359096, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048041159162028e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 125906, "start": 1266.06, "end": 1272.48, "text": " We should only invoke explanatory origins, these constraint fields, when the transmission channels are physically impossible,", "tokens": [50715, 492, 820, 787, 41117, 9045, 4745, 22721, 11, 613, 25534, 7909, 11, 562, 264, 11574, 9235, 366, 9762, 6243, 11, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1349327632359096, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048041159162028e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 125906, "start": 1272.86, "end": 1278.4199999999998, "text": " deeply separated by thousands of years, or strictly screened off in a laboratory like the Lensky bacteria.", "tokens": [51055, 8760, 12005, 538, 5383, 295, 924, 11, 420, 20792, 2568, 292, 766, 294, 257, 16523, 411, 264, 441, 694, 4133, 11763, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1349327632359096, "compression_ratio": 1.5746606334841629, "no_speech_prob": 1.4048041159162028e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 127842, "start": 1278.42, "end": 1281.64, "text": " Okay. So that establishes a massive foundation for us.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 300, 8327, 279, 257, 5994, 7030, 337, 505, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 127842, "start": 1282.22, "end": 1289.26, "text": " In nature and history, we have these physical, chemical, and biological constraints that gently, or sometimes violently,", "tokens": [50555, 682, 3687, 293, 2503, 11, 321, 362, 613, 4001, 11, 7313, 11, 293, 13910, 18491, 300, 13073, 11, 420, 2171, 46728, 11, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 127842, "start": 1289.76, "end": 1292.14, "text": " guide systems toward convergent outcomes.", "tokens": [50932, 5934, 3652, 7361, 9652, 6930, 10070, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 127842, "start": 1292.4, "end": 1294.88, "text": " The walls of reality keep things grounded.", "tokens": [51064, 440, 7920, 295, 4103, 1066, 721, 23535, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 127842, "start": 1295.14, "end": 1295.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51201, 1779, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 127842, "start": 1295.68, "end": 1299.88, "text": " But I want to pivot now, because this leads us directly into the second part of Flitchin's research,", "tokens": [51228, 583, 286, 528, 281, 14538, 586, 11, 570, 341, 6689, 505, 3838, 666, 264, 1150, 644, 295, 3235, 1549, 259, 311, 2132, 11, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 127842, "start": 1300.1000000000001, "end": 1302.0800000000002, "text": " which is titled, The Geometry of Correction.", "tokens": [51449, 597, 307, 19841, 11, 440, 2876, 34730, 295, 3925, 11417, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16062706295806584, "compression_ratio": 1.5353159851301115, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949190531981295e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 130208, "start": 1302.08, "end": 1307.26, "text": " Because if nature is governed by inescapable physical constraints, the immediate quotient is,", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 3687, 307, 35529, 538, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 4001, 18491, 11, 264, 11629, 9641, 1196, 307, 11, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 130208, "start": 1307.58, "end": 1312.32, "text": " what happens when human beings build synthetic systems that entirely ignore physical constraints?", "tokens": [50640, 437, 2314, 562, 1952, 8958, 1322, 23420, 3652, 300, 7696, 11200, 4001, 18491, 30, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 130208, "start": 1312.48, "end": 1319.22, "text": " And that transition is exactly where Flitchin takes this theoretical framework and weaponizes it to diagnose our modern institutions,", "tokens": [50885, 400, 300, 6034, 307, 2293, 689, 3235, 1549, 259, 2516, 341, 20864, 8388, 293, 7463, 5660, 309, 281, 36238, 527, 4363, 8142, 11, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 130208, "start": 1319.6599999999999, "end": 1323.08, "text": " specifically looking at the architecture of megascale tech platforms.", "tokens": [51244, 4682, 1237, 412, 264, 9482, 295, 10816, 4806, 1220, 7553, 9473, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 130208, "start": 1323.54, "end": 1328.0, "text": " And this touches on a daily visceral frustration for you, the listener.", "tokens": [51438, 400, 341, 17431, 322, 257, 5212, 1452, 47879, 20491, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 130208, "start": 1328.6399999999999, "end": 1331.5, "text": " We have all experienced this maddening contradiction.", "tokens": [51693, 492, 362, 439, 6751, 341, 5244, 1556, 278, 34937, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13811284359370438, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.6363654138304429e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 133150, "start": 1331.5, "end": 1332.4, "text": " Oh, definitely.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 2138, 13, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 133150, "start": 1332.62, "end": 1335.1, "text": " You open up a social media app or a video platform,", "tokens": [50421, 509, 1269, 493, 257, 2093, 3021, 724, 420, 257, 960, 3663, 11, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 133150, "start": 1335.76, "end": 1343.04, "text": " you know for a fact that the company running this app possesses world-class, multi-billion-dollar artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50578, 291, 458, 337, 257, 1186, 300, 264, 2237, 2614, 341, 724, 17490, 279, 1002, 12, 11665, 11, 4825, 12, 65, 11836, 12, 40485, 11677, 7599, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 133150, "start": 1343.48, "end": 1349.32, "text": " This AI is so sophisticated that it can predict, with terrifying surgical accuracy,", "tokens": [50964, 639, 7318, 307, 370, 16950, 300, 309, 393, 6069, 11, 365, 18106, 26646, 14170, 11, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 133150, "start": 1349.82, "end": 1353.72, "text": " exactly which 15-second video will trigger your specific dopamine receptors", "tokens": [51281, 2293, 597, 2119, 12, 27375, 960, 486, 7875, 428, 2685, 37219, 34102, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 133150, "start": 1353.72, "end": 1358.08, "text": " and keep you, or a teenager, scrolling for another 45 minutes.", "tokens": [51476, 293, 1066, 291, 11, 420, 257, 21440, 11, 29053, 337, 1071, 6905, 2077, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 133150, "start": 1358.38, "end": 1360.78, "text": " The predictive modeling is astonishingly precise.", "tokens": [51709, 440, 35521, 15983, 307, 35264, 356, 13600, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15260404069847036, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.832473409124624e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 136078, "start": 1360.78, "end": 1363.3, "text": " Right. It knows your deepest psychological hooks.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 467, 3255, 428, 28288, 14346, 26485, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 136078, "start": 1363.84, "end": 1368.78, "text": " But somehow, simultaneously, this exact same, multi-billion-dollar platform", "tokens": [50518, 583, 6063, 11, 16561, 11, 341, 1900, 912, 11, 4825, 12, 65, 11836, 12, 40485, 3663, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 136078, "start": 1368.78, "end": 1371.84, "text": " completely fails to detect a three-day-old account,", "tokens": [50765, 2584, 18199, 281, 5531, 257, 1045, 12, 810, 12, 2641, 2696, 11, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 136078, "start": 1372.28, "end": 1375.96, "text": " using a heavily pixelated, stolen profile picture of a stock photo model,", "tokens": [50940, 1228, 257, 10950, 19261, 770, 11, 15900, 7964, 3036, 295, 257, 4127, 5052, 2316, 11, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 136078, "start": 1376.34, "end": 1380.7, "text": " which is actively messaging your grandmother to ask for a $500 pet deposit", "tokens": [51143, 597, 307, 13022, 21812, 428, 14317, 281, 1029, 337, 257, 1848, 7526, 3817, 19107, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 136078, "start": 1380.7, "end": 1383.3, "text": " on a golden retriever puppy that clearly doesn't exist.", "tokens": [51361, 322, 257, 9729, 19817, 331, 18196, 300, 4448, 1177, 380, 2514, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 136078, "start": 1383.3799999999999, "end": 1384.16, "text": " It's wired.", "tokens": [51495, 467, 311, 27415, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681711936483578, "compression_ratio": 1.4756554307116105, "no_speech_prob": 2.58372576805721e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 138416, "start": 1384.16, "end": 1385.24, "text": " It feels like a paradox.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3417, 411, 257, 26221, 13, 50419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13234761783054896, "compression_ratio": 1.5283842794759825, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966086076128597e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 138416, "start": 1385.5, "end": 1390.66, "text": " How can they be godlike in predicting my desires, but completely incompetent in stopping a blatant scam?", "tokens": [50432, 1012, 393, 436, 312, 3044, 4092, 294, 32884, 452, 18005, 11, 457, 2584, 41602, 317, 294, 12767, 257, 42780, 394, 26917, 30, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13234761783054896, "compression_ratio": 1.5283842794759825, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966086076128597e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 138416, "start": 1390.92, "end": 1395.26, "text": " What's fascinating here is how Fliction dismantles our assumptions about that paradox.", "tokens": [50703, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 3235, 4105, 30506, 904, 527, 17695, 466, 300, 26221, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13234761783054896, "compression_ratio": 1.5283842794759825, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966086076128597e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 138416, "start": 1395.72, "end": 1400.52, "text": " When we see that contradiction, our instinct is to view it as a technical failure.", "tokens": [50943, 1133, 321, 536, 300, 34937, 11, 527, 16556, 307, 281, 1910, 309, 382, 257, 6191, 7763, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13234761783054896, "compression_ratio": 1.5283842794759825, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966086076128597e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 138416, "start": 1400.64, "end": 1402.4, "text": " Like they just haven't written the right code yet.", "tokens": [51189, 1743, 436, 445, 2378, 380, 3720, 264, 558, 3089, 1939, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13234761783054896, "compression_ratio": 1.5283842794759825, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966086076128597e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 140240, "start": 1402.4, "end": 1405.0800000000002, "text": " Right. We assume the engineers are working hard on it,", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 492, 6552, 264, 11955, 366, 1364, 1152, 322, 309, 11, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 140240, "start": 1405.14, "end": 1408.26, "text": " but they just haven't quite solved the fake account problem yet,", "tokens": [50502, 457, 436, 445, 2378, 380, 1596, 13041, 264, 7592, 2696, 1154, 1939, 11, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 140240, "start": 1408.3600000000001, "end": 1410.0600000000002, "text": " because it's technically difficult.", "tokens": [50663, 570, 309, 311, 12120, 2252, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 140240, "start": 1410.46, "end": 1414.72, "text": " But Fliction introduces a concept called synthetic sociality.", "tokens": [50768, 583, 3235, 4105, 31472, 257, 3410, 1219, 23420, 2093, 507, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 140240, "start": 1414.8600000000001, "end": 1416.0600000000002, "text": " Synthetic sociality.", "tokens": [50988, 318, 18656, 3532, 2093, 507, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 140240, "start": 1416.1200000000001, "end": 1420.7, "text": " And argues that this contradiction is not a result of technical incompetence at all.", "tokens": [51051, 400, 38218, 300, 341, 34937, 307, 406, 257, 1874, 295, 6191, 41602, 655, 412, 439, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19370582776191908, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888366127596147e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 142070, "start": 1420.7, "end": 1425.3, "text": " It is a deliberate structural feature of the system's architecture.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 30515, 15067, 4111, 295, 264, 1185, 311, 9482, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 142070, "start": 1425.98, "end": 1428.8600000000001, "text": " But whenever these massive platforms are hauled in front of Congress", "tokens": [50629, 583, 5699, 613, 5994, 9473, 366, 21167, 292, 294, 1868, 295, 6426, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 142070, "start": 1428.8600000000001, "end": 1432.28, "text": " or questioned by journalists about the scams and the bots,", "tokens": [50773, 420, 28146, 538, 19535, 466, 264, 795, 4070, 293, 264, 35410, 11, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 142070, "start": 1432.54, "end": 1435.3600000000001, "text": " they always use a very specific defense, right?", "tokens": [50957, 436, 1009, 764, 257, 588, 2685, 7654, 11, 558, 30, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 142070, "start": 1436.1200000000001, "end": 1438.98, "text": " Which Fliction calls the infrastructure alibi.", "tokens": [51136, 3013, 3235, 4105, 5498, 264, 6896, 419, 25515, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 142070, "start": 1439.48, "end": 1442.28, "text": " Yes. The infrastructure alibi is their primary shield.", "tokens": [51304, 1079, 13, 440, 6896, 419, 25515, 307, 641, 6194, 10257, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 142070, "start": 1442.44, "end": 1444.16, "text": " They argue, look, we are just a utility.", "tokens": [51452, 814, 9695, 11, 574, 11, 321, 366, 445, 257, 14877, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 142070, "start": 1444.3400000000001, "end": 1445.64, "text": " We build the digital roads.", "tokens": [51547, 492, 1322, 264, 4562, 11344, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 142070, "start": 1445.66, "end": 1446.3, "text": " Right, like a highway.", "tokens": [51613, 1779, 11, 411, 257, 17205, 13, 51645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 142070, "start": 1446.6200000000001, "end": 1449.4, "text": " We provide open communication tools for the world.", "tokens": [51661, 492, 2893, 1269, 6101, 3873, 337, 264, 1002, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17197518348693847, "compression_ratio": 1.6321070234113713, "no_speech_prob": 1.91292706501478e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 144940, "start": 1449.4, "end": 1454.96, "text": " If malicious actors decide to use our roads to drive their getaway cars after robbing a bank,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 33496, 10037, 4536, 281, 764, 527, 11344, 281, 3332, 641, 483, 10318, 5163, 934, 3870, 4324, 257, 3765, 11, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 144940, "start": 1455.42, "end": 1459.1000000000001, "text": " that is a reflection of a sick society, not a broken platform.", "tokens": [50666, 300, 307, 257, 12914, 295, 257, 4998, 4086, 11, 406, 257, 5463, 3663, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 144940, "start": 1459.76, "end": 1462.9, "text": " We are a neutral substrate, just like the highway system.", "tokens": [50883, 492, 366, 257, 10598, 27585, 11, 445, 411, 264, 17205, 1185, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 144940, "start": 1463.18, "end": 1465.9, "text": " Which, on a surface level, sounds perfectly reasonable.", "tokens": [51054, 3013, 11, 322, 257, 3753, 1496, 11, 3263, 6239, 10585, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 144940, "start": 1466.38, "end": 1468.38, "text": " A highway isn't responsible for bank robbers.", "tokens": [51214, 316, 17205, 1943, 380, 6250, 337, 3765, 3870, 1616, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 144940, "start": 1469.0, "end": 1474.5, "text": " But Fliction completely shreds that alibi by looking at the actual mathematics running beneath the surface.", "tokens": [51345, 583, 3235, 4105, 2584, 21567, 82, 300, 419, 25515, 538, 1237, 412, 264, 3539, 18666, 2614, 17149, 264, 3753, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 144940, "start": 1474.52, "end": 1475.98, "text": " Okay, they absolutely shred it.", "tokens": [51621, 1033, 11, 436, 3122, 21567, 309, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436321431940252, "compression_ratio": 1.6113074204946995, "no_speech_prob": 1.6949084280168392e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 147598, "start": 1475.98, "end": 1483.5, "text": " Fliction bypasses the PR statements and looks at the actual optimization functions these platforms use to govern their networks.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 24996, 279, 264, 11568, 12363, 293, 1542, 412, 264, 3539, 19618, 6828, 613, 9473, 764, 281, 1980, 641, 9590, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 147598, "start": 1484.1200000000001, "end": 1486.32, "text": " Let's simplify it and call it Equation EA.", "tokens": [50772, 961, 311, 20460, 309, 293, 818, 309, 15624, 399, 35747, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 147598, "start": 1486.68, "end": 1488.48, "text": " Equation EA. What does that stand for?", "tokens": [50900, 15624, 399, 35747, 13, 708, 775, 300, 1463, 337, 30, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 147598, "start": 1488.84, "end": 1492.78, "text": " It stands for the expected engagement produced by any given activity on the network.", "tokens": [51008, 467, 7382, 337, 264, 5176, 8742, 7126, 538, 604, 2212, 5191, 322, 264, 3209, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 147598, "start": 1493.3, "end": 1496.34, "text": " The entire architecture of the system, every server and algorithm,", "tokens": [51231, 440, 2302, 9482, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 633, 7154, 293, 9284, 11, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 147598, "start": 1496.54, "end": 1499.3600000000001, "text": " is rigorously programmed to maximize the output of EA.", "tokens": [51393, 307, 42191, 5098, 31092, 281, 19874, 264, 5598, 295, 35747, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15008655347322164, "compression_ratio": 1.61003861003861, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759262806339327e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 149936, "start": 1499.36, "end": 1501.32, "text": " Okay, that makes sense for a business.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 337, 257, 1606, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 149936, "start": 1501.4799999999998, "end": 1504.4399999999998, "text": " But if you open up that equation and look at the variables inside it,", "tokens": [50471, 583, 498, 291, 1269, 493, 300, 5367, 293, 574, 412, 264, 9102, 1854, 309, 11, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 149936, "start": 1504.74, "end": 1507.06, "text": " authenticity is literally not a variable.", "tokens": [50634, 34215, 307, 3736, 406, 257, 7006, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 149936, "start": 1507.26, "end": 1508.6, "text": " Wait, I really want to emphasize this.", "tokens": [50760, 3802, 11, 286, 534, 528, 281, 16078, 341, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 149936, "start": 1508.74, "end": 1508.8799999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50834, 865, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 149936, "start": 1509.4199999999998, "end": 1513.32, "text": " It is not that the algorithm looks at authenticity and assigns it a low weight,", "tokens": [50868, 467, 307, 406, 300, 264, 9284, 1542, 412, 34215, 293, 6269, 82, 309, 257, 2295, 3364, 11, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 149936, "start": 1513.4399999999998, "end": 1517.28, "text": " like saying we care about engagement 90% and authenticity 10%.", "tokens": [51069, 411, 1566, 321, 1127, 466, 8742, 4289, 4, 293, 34215, 1266, 6856, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 149936, "start": 1517.28, "end": 1517.5, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51261, 865, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 149936, "start": 1517.86, "end": 1520.4799999999998, "text": " It's that authenticity doesn't exist in the math at all.", "tokens": [51290, 467, 311, 300, 34215, 1177, 380, 2514, 294, 264, 5221, 412, 439, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 149936, "start": 1520.6, "end": 1523.36, "text": " It is completely absent from the objective function.", "tokens": [51427, 467, 307, 2584, 25185, 490, 264, 10024, 2445, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15506514524802184, "compression_ratio": 1.663003663003663, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722233848685207e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 152336, "start": 1523.36, "end": 1527.56, "text": " From the purely mathematical perspective of the recommendation algorithm,", "tokens": [50365, 3358, 264, 17491, 18894, 4585, 295, 264, 11879, 9284, 11, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 152336, "start": 1528.1, "end": 1533.6399999999999, "text": " a genuine human being sharing a heartfelt real story that generates 10 clicks", "tokens": [50602, 257, 16699, 1952, 885, 5414, 257, 49332, 957, 1657, 300, 23815, 1266, 18521, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 152336, "start": 1533.6399999999999, "end": 1538.4399999999998, "text": " is mathematically functionally indistinguishable from a networked bot farm", "tokens": [50879, 307, 44003, 2445, 379, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 257, 3209, 292, 10592, 5421, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 152336, "start": 1538.4399999999998, "end": 1542.3999999999999, "text": " sharing a completely fabricated outrage story that generates 10 clicks.", "tokens": [51119, 5414, 257, 2584, 7253, 770, 25933, 1657, 300, 23815, 1266, 18521, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 152336, "start": 1542.56, "end": 1543.06, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51325, 3153, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 152336, "start": 1543.32, "end": 1545.4599999999998, "text": " The system isn't failing to tell them apart.", "tokens": [51363, 440, 1185, 1943, 380, 18223, 281, 980, 552, 4936, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1466250043166311, "compression_ratio": 1.6338028169014085, "no_speech_prob": 1.660913594159208e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 154546, "start": 1545.46, "end": 1549.48, "text": " It is succeeding flawlessly at the exact task it was given,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 47912, 13717, 12048, 412, 264, 1900, 5633, 309, 390, 2212, 11, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 154546, "start": 1549.88, "end": 1553.72, "text": " which explicitly treats them as interchangeable units of engagement.", "tokens": [50586, 597, 20803, 19566, 552, 382, 30358, 712, 6815, 295, 8742, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 154546, "start": 1554.22, "end": 1554.74, "text": " That is chilling.", "tokens": [50803, 663, 307, 31047, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 154546, "start": 1554.94, "end": 1555.58, "text": " It gets worse.", "tokens": [50839, 467, 2170, 5324, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 154546, "start": 1555.98, "end": 1559.48, "text": " Because they are interchangeable in the math up to a certain point of saturation,", "tokens": [50891, 1436, 436, 366, 30358, 712, 294, 264, 5221, 493, 281, 257, 1629, 935, 295, 27090, 11, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 154546, "start": 1559.78, "end": 1563.38, "text": " automated bot networks are actually economically useful to the platform.", "tokens": [51081, 18473, 10592, 9590, 366, 767, 26811, 4420, 281, 264, 3663, 13, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 154546, "start": 1563.54, "end": 1564.22, "text": " Useful.", "tokens": [51269, 8278, 906, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 154546, "start": 1564.26, "end": 1565.72, "text": " They fill in the engagement gaps.", "tokens": [51305, 814, 2836, 294, 264, 8742, 15031, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 154546, "start": 1565.8, "end": 1566.98, "text": " They keep the metrics climbing.", "tokens": [51382, 814, 1066, 264, 16367, 14780, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 154546, "start": 1567.3, "end": 1569.3600000000001, "text": " They simulate a bustling town square.", "tokens": [51457, 814, 27817, 257, 19432, 1688, 3954, 3732, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 154546, "start": 1569.6000000000001, "end": 1573.54, "text": " As long as the advertisers don't notice that the town square is full of mannequins,", "tokens": [51572, 1018, 938, 382, 264, 42679, 500, 380, 3449, 300, 264, 3954, 3732, 307, 1577, 295, 49815, 358, 1292, 11, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16662957933213976, "compression_ratio": 1.695364238410596, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279272189115515e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 157354, "start": 1573.54, "end": 1576.34, "text": " the bots are a feature, not a bug.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 35410, 366, 257, 4111, 11, 406, 257, 7426, 13, 50505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 157354, "start": 1576.54, "end": 1576.76, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50515, 1033, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 157354, "start": 1576.96, "end": 1580.3999999999999, "text": " To explain how a system becomes this blind to reality,", "tokens": [50536, 1407, 2903, 577, 257, 1185, 3643, 341, 6865, 281, 4103, 11, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 157354, "start": 1580.96, "end": 1584.18, "text": " Flixion formally defines this using a mathematical coefficient,", "tokens": [50736, 3235, 970, 313, 25983, 23122, 341, 1228, 257, 18894, 17619, 11, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 157354, "start": 1584.76, "end": 1585.82, "text": " the Greek letter rho.", "tokens": [50926, 264, 10281, 5063, 20293, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 157354, "start": 1586.26, "end": 1588.3, "text": " Let's really unpack the rho coefficient,", "tokens": [51001, 961, 311, 534, 26699, 264, 20293, 17619, 11, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 157354, "start": 1588.6599999999999, "end": 1590.68, "text": " because this is the key to the whole diagnosis.", "tokens": [51121, 570, 341, 307, 264, 2141, 281, 264, 1379, 15217, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 157354, "start": 1590.8799999999999, "end": 1591.18, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51232, 4894, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 157354, "start": 1591.6, "end": 1594.72, "text": " Rho measures what Flixion calls the coupling coefficient.", "tokens": [51268, 497, 1289, 8000, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 5498, 264, 37447, 17619, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 157354, "start": 1595.3999999999999, "end": 1597.74, "text": " Think of it as a measurement of structural humility.", "tokens": [51458, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 257, 13160, 295, 15067, 27106, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 157354, "start": 1597.8999999999999, "end": 1598.6599999999999, "text": " So structural humility.", "tokens": [51583, 407, 15067, 27106, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 157354, "start": 1598.6599999999999, "end": 1603.46, "text": " It represents how strongly a system's internal evaluation of its own success", "tokens": [51621, 467, 8855, 577, 10613, 257, 1185, 311, 6920, 13344, 295, 1080, 1065, 2245, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20653704674013199, "compression_ratio": 1.7003484320557491, "no_speech_prob": 2.236074173045388e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 160346, "start": 1603.46, "end": 1608.4, "text": " is tied to an external channel of reality that the system does not control.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 9601, 281, 364, 8320, 2269, 295, 4103, 300, 264, 1185, 775, 406, 1969, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 160346, "start": 1608.72, "end": 1612.96, "text": " So if a system only evaluates its success by looking at its own internal dashboards,", "tokens": [50628, 407, 498, 257, 1185, 787, 6133, 1024, 1080, 2245, 538, 1237, 412, 1080, 1065, 6920, 8240, 17228, 11, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 160346, "start": 1613.16, "end": 1617.66, "text": " like metrics it generates itself, such as clicks, time on site, or daily active users,", "tokens": [50850, 411, 16367, 309, 23815, 2564, 11, 1270, 382, 18521, 11, 565, 322, 3621, 11, 420, 5212, 4967, 5022, 11, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 160346, "start": 1618.22, "end": 1620.2, "text": " that is a highly self-referential system.", "tokens": [51103, 300, 307, 257, 5405, 2698, 12, 265, 612, 2549, 1185, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 160346, "start": 1620.32, "end": 1620.64, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51208, 12753, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 160346, "start": 1620.92, "end": 1622.18, "text": " When rho approaches zero,", "tokens": [51238, 1133, 20293, 11587, 4018, 11, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 160346, "start": 1622.3400000000001, "end": 1625.44, "text": " it means the system has completely stopped listening to the outside world.", "tokens": [51309, 309, 1355, 264, 1185, 575, 2584, 5936, 4764, 281, 264, 2380, 1002, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 160346, "start": 1625.82, "end": 1627.14, "text": " It is totally self-referential.", "tokens": [51483, 467, 307, 3879, 2698, 12, 265, 612, 2549, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 160346, "start": 1627.26, "end": 1628.54, "text": " It's grading its own homework.", "tokens": [51555, 467, 311, 35540, 1080, 1065, 14578, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 160346, "start": 1628.68, "end": 1629.58, "text": " That sounds dangerous.", "tokens": [51626, 663, 3263, 5795, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10367161560058594, "compression_ratio": 1.6782006920415224, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426222361476395e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 162958, "start": 1629.58, "end": 1634.4399999999998, "text": " But if the system is structurally forced to consult something outside of its own control,", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 264, 1185, 307, 6594, 6512, 7579, 281, 7189, 746, 2380, 295, 1080, 1065, 1969, 11, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 162958, "start": 1634.6, "end": 1637.24, "text": " like an independent audit, or a physical constraint,", "tokens": [50616, 411, 364, 6695, 17748, 11, 420, 257, 4001, 25534, 11, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 162958, "start": 1637.52, "end": 1640.36, "text": " or the verified biological reality of its users,", "tokens": [50762, 420, 264, 31197, 13910, 4103, 295, 1080, 5022, 11, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 162958, "start": 1640.54, "end": 1642.3799999999999, "text": " then it has a high rho coefficient.", "tokens": [50913, 550, 309, 575, 257, 1090, 20293, 17619, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 162958, "start": 1643.1, "end": 1644.6799999999998, "text": " It is reality-anchored.", "tokens": [51041, 467, 307, 4103, 12, 4778, 2769, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 162958, "start": 1644.9399999999998, "end": 1648.1399999999999, "text": " And this leads to what Flixion calls the correction suppression principle,", "tokens": [51133, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 437, 3235, 970, 313, 5498, 264, 19984, 36807, 8665, 11, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 162958, "start": 1648.46, "end": 1652.4199999999998, "text": " which is one of those concepts that makes you want to pull your hair out once you understand it.", "tokens": [51309, 597, 307, 472, 295, 729, 10392, 300, 1669, 291, 528, 281, 2235, 428, 2578, 484, 1564, 291, 1223, 309, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 162958, "start": 1652.4399999999998, "end": 1653.8799999999999, "text": " It is infuriating, yeah.", "tokens": [51508, 467, 307, 1536, 9744, 990, 11, 1338, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610558587151604, "compression_ratio": 1.6231884057971016, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111192883960014e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 165388, "start": 1653.88, "end": 1659.8400000000001, "text": " Because when a platform's rho drops to zero, the external reality didn't magically vanish.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 562, 257, 3663, 311, 20293, 11438, 281, 4018, 11, 264, 8320, 4103, 994, 380, 39763, 43584, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 165388, "start": 1660.48, "end": 1663.24, "text": " The reality of the rental scam is still happening.", "tokens": [50695, 440, 4103, 295, 264, 21468, 26917, 307, 920, 2737, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 165388, "start": 1663.3000000000002, "end": 1663.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50836, 1779, 13, 50841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 165388, "start": 1663.5200000000002, "end": 1664.5200000000002, "text": " People are still getting hurt.", "tokens": [50847, 3432, 366, 920, 1242, 4607, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 165388, "start": 1664.92, "end": 1668.98, "text": " The grandmother, whose pet deposit got stolen, is still out $500.", "tokens": [50917, 440, 14317, 11, 6104, 3817, 19107, 658, 15900, 11, 307, 920, 484, 1848, 7526, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 165388, "start": 1669.64, "end": 1671.5200000000002, "text": " She is screaming into the void.", "tokens": [51153, 1240, 307, 12636, 666, 264, 22009, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 165388, "start": 1671.98, "end": 1673.68, "text": " She is submitting customer service tickets.", "tokens": [51270, 1240, 307, 31836, 5474, 2643, 12628, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 165388, "start": 1674.0800000000002, "end": 1675.7800000000002, "text": " She is tagging the company's help account.", "tokens": [51375, 1240, 307, 6162, 3249, 264, 2237, 311, 854, 2696, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 165388, "start": 1675.8600000000001, "end": 1676.94, "text": " She is warning her friends.", "tokens": [51464, 1240, 307, 9164, 720, 1855, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 165388, "start": 1677.6200000000001, "end": 1680.0800000000002, "text": " The signal of reality is incredibly loud.", "tokens": [51552, 440, 6358, 295, 4103, 307, 6252, 6588, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 165388, "start": 1680.3200000000002, "end": 1680.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51687, 7587, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14634323120117188, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013968359180787e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 168068, "start": 1680.68, "end": 1683.38, "text": " The system isn't blind because there is no light.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1185, 1943, 380, 6865, 570, 456, 307, 572, 1442, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 168068, "start": 1683.68, "end": 1686.0, "text": " It's blind because it intentionally closed its eyes.", "tokens": [50515, 467, 311, 6865, 570, 309, 22062, 5395, 1080, 2575, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 168068, "start": 1686.1200000000001, "end": 1688.3200000000002, "text": " It just weighted that external channel at zero.", "tokens": [50637, 467, 445, 32807, 300, 8320, 2269, 412, 4018, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 168068, "start": 1688.8200000000002, "end": 1691.18, "text": " It structurally suppressed the correction.", "tokens": [50772, 467, 6594, 6512, 42645, 264, 19984, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 168068, "start": 1691.7, "end": 1696.72, "text": " Pathological self-reference in these systems usually isn't caused by a lack of available evidence", "tokens": [50916, 21914, 4383, 2698, 12, 265, 5158, 294, 613, 3652, 2673, 1943, 380, 7008, 538, 257, 5011, 295, 2435, 4467, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 168068, "start": 1696.72, "end": 1698.0600000000002, "text": " about the harm they are causing.", "tokens": [51167, 466, 264, 6491, 436, 366, 9853, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 168068, "start": 1698.38, "end": 1702.1000000000001, "text": " It is a structural mathematical refusal to be moved by that evidence.", "tokens": [51250, 467, 307, 257, 15067, 18894, 48948, 281, 312, 4259, 538, 300, 4467, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 168068, "start": 1702.28, "end": 1706.18, "text": " It makes me think of a terribly managed nightmare of a restaurant.", "tokens": [51445, 467, 1669, 385, 519, 295, 257, 22903, 6453, 18724, 295, 257, 6383, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 168068, "start": 1706.3, "end": 1706.8, "text": " Let's hear it.", "tokens": [51646, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1606473588106925, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 170680, "start": 1706.8, "end": 1712.3799999999999, "text": " Imagine a massive restaurant kitchen where the chefs and the expediters are evaluated and", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 257, 5994, 6383, 6525, 689, 264, 30191, 293, 264, 19348, 270, 433, 366, 25509, 293, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 170680, "start": 1712.3799999999999, "end": 1715.12, "text": " pay their bonuses based entirely on one metric.", "tokens": [50644, 1689, 641, 33205, 2361, 7696, 322, 472, 20678, 13, 50781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 170680, "start": 1716.0, "end": 1720.18, "text": " How fast plates of food pass through the swinging doors into the dining room.", "tokens": [50825, 1012, 2370, 14231, 295, 1755, 1320, 807, 264, 29500, 8077, 666, 264, 17874, 1808, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 170680, "start": 1720.32, "end": 1720.9199999999998, "text": " Plate velocity.", "tokens": [51041, 46043, 9269, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 170680, "start": 1721.06, "end": 1721.6599999999999, "text": " Plate velocity.", "tokens": [51078, 46043, 9269, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 170680, "start": 1721.82, "end": 1722.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51116, 7587, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 170680, "start": 1722.86, "end": 1725.04, "text": " So the kitchen door swings open.", "tokens": [51168, 407, 264, 6525, 2853, 32386, 1269, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 170680, "start": 1725.36, "end": 1726.9199999999998, "text": " Plates fly out at record speed.", "tokens": [51293, 2149, 1024, 3603, 484, 412, 2136, 3073, 13, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 170680, "start": 1727.36, "end": 1728.76, "text": " The kitchen stat is high-fiving.", "tokens": [51393, 440, 6525, 2219, 307, 1090, 12, 69, 2123, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 170680, "start": 1729.26, "end": 1730.96, "text": " But out in the dining room, the chicken is raw.", "tokens": [51488, 583, 484, 294, 264, 17874, 1808, 11, 264, 4662, 307, 8936, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 170680, "start": 1731.3, "end": 1732.24, "text": " The soup is cold.", "tokens": [51590, 440, 7884, 307, 3554, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 170680, "start": 1732.84, "end": 1734.24, "text": " Customers are getting food poisoning.", "tokens": [51667, 16649, 433, 366, 1242, 1755, 36778, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 170680, "start": 1734.36, "end": 1735.46, "text": " They are screaming at the waiters.", "tokens": [51743, 814, 366, 12636, 412, 264, 1699, 433, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16509940407492898, "compression_ratio": 1.7544483985765125, "no_speech_prob": 1.501476677365221e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 173546, "start": 1735.46, "end": 1736.72, "text": " They are demanding refunds.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 19960, 29384, 82, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 173546, "start": 1736.72, "end": 1736.98, "text": " Chaos.", "tokens": [50428, 32644, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 173546, "start": 1737.42, "end": 1737.6000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50463, 1779, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 173546, "start": 1738.42, "end": 1743.82, "text": " But the restaurant owner is sitting in a soundproof, locked office upstairs, staring at a green", "tokens": [50513, 583, 264, 6383, 7289, 307, 3798, 294, 257, 1626, 15690, 11, 9376, 3398, 16462, 11, 18043, 412, 257, 3092, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 173546, "start": 1743.82, "end": 1746.3400000000001, "text": " dashboard that says, plates per minute, 150.", "tokens": [50783, 18342, 300, 1619, 11, 14231, 680, 3456, 11, 8451, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 173546, "start": 1747.04, "end": 1750.52, "text": " The owner is counting the money, completely insulated from the chaos.", "tokens": [50944, 440, 7289, 307, 13251, 264, 1460, 11, 2584, 1028, 6987, 490, 264, 14158, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 173546, "start": 1750.8400000000001, "end": 1756.76, "text": " That restaurant analogy perfectly illustrates Fliction's critique of what they call the portfolio", "tokens": [51134, 663, 6383, 21663, 6239, 41718, 3235, 4105, 311, 25673, 295, 437, 436, 818, 264, 12583, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 173546, "start": 1756.76, "end": 1758.18, "text": " model of tech leadership.", "tokens": [51430, 2316, 295, 7553, 5848, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 173546, "start": 1758.74, "end": 1762.48, "text": " We tend to anthropomorphize massive tech companies.", "tokens": [51529, 492, 3928, 281, 22727, 32702, 1125, 5994, 7553, 3431, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2216678730492453, "compression_ratio": 1.562043795620438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7479214690224731e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 176248, "start": 1762.48, "end": 1767.56, "text": " We talk about them as if they have a single unified brain and a single conscience.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 751, 466, 552, 382, 498, 436, 362, 257, 2167, 26787, 3567, 293, 257, 2167, 20537, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 176248, "start": 1767.92, "end": 1768.0, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50637, 1779, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 176248, "start": 1768.08, "end": 1770.44, "text": " Like Google thinks this or Meta wants that.", "tokens": [50645, 1743, 3329, 7309, 341, 420, 6377, 64, 2738, 300, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 176248, "start": 1770.54, "end": 1771.28, "text": " But they don't.", "tokens": [50768, 583, 436, 500, 380, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 176248, "start": 1771.4, "end": 1774.64, "text": " They are highly fragmented, distributed bureaucracies.", "tokens": [50811, 814, 366, 5405, 9241, 14684, 11, 12631, 26360, 12080, 530, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 176248, "start": 1775.28, "end": 1780.4, "text": " In this portfolio model, you have an engineering team that is heavily incentivized to maximize", "tokens": [51005, 682, 341, 12583, 2316, 11, 291, 362, 364, 7043, 1469, 300, 307, 10950, 35328, 1602, 281, 19874, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 176248, "start": 1780.4, "end": 1784.22, "text": " the EA equation to get the plates out of the kitchen as fast as possible.", "tokens": [51261, 264, 35747, 5367, 281, 483, 264, 14231, 484, 295, 264, 6525, 382, 2370, 382, 1944, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 176248, "start": 1784.42, "end": 1784.6, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51462, 1033, 13, 51471], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 176248, "start": 1784.64, "end": 1785.0, "text": " The chefs.", "tokens": [51473, 440, 30191, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17647165465123446, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 1.9541774882309015e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 178500, "start": 1785.0, "end": 1790.06, "text": " Then you have a vastly underfunded trust and safety team, which is the equivalent of the", "tokens": [50365, 1396, 291, 362, 257, 41426, 833, 43589, 3361, 293, 4514, 1469, 11, 597, 307, 264, 10344, 295, 264, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 178500, "start": 1790.06, "end": 1794.08, "text": " waiters getting yelled at in the dining room, and they are measured by how quickly they can", "tokens": [50618, 1699, 433, 1242, 38023, 412, 294, 264, 17874, 1808, 11, 293, 436, 366, 12690, 538, 577, 2661, 436, 393, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 178500, "start": 1794.08, "end": 1795.16, "text": " close complaint tickets.", "tokens": [50819, 1998, 20100, 12628, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 178500, "start": 1795.28, "end": 1796.3, "text": " Oh, that sounds miserable.", "tokens": [50879, 876, 11, 300, 3263, 22321, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 178500, "start": 1796.56, "end": 1800.82, "text": " And at the very top, you have the strategic executives sitting in the soundproof office,", "tokens": [50943, 400, 412, 264, 588, 1192, 11, 291, 362, 264, 10924, 28485, 3798, 294, 264, 1626, 15690, 3398, 11, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 178500, "start": 1800.98, "end": 1803.74, "text": " completely insulated from the operational reality.", "tokens": [51164, 2584, 1028, 6987, 490, 264, 16607, 4103, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 178500, "start": 1803.94, "end": 1808.86, "text": " So operational responsibility is intentionally distributed across all these disconnected silos,", "tokens": [51312, 407, 16607, 6357, 307, 22062, 12631, 2108, 439, 613, 29426, 48893, 11, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11003681220630608, "compression_ratio": 1.6714285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.79002440040682e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 180886, "start": 1808.86, "end": 1814.9399999999998, "text": " but the strategic power and the financial rewards are intensely concentrated at the very top.", "tokens": [50365, 457, 264, 10924, 1347, 293, 264, 4669, 17203, 366, 43235, 21321, 412, 264, 588, 1192, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 180886, "start": 1815.3799999999999, "end": 1815.4599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50691, 1779, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 180886, "start": 1815.82, "end": 1820.5, "text": " And the geometry of that governance structure dictates a very predictable flow of consequences.", "tokens": [50713, 400, 264, 18426, 295, 300, 17449, 3877, 12569, 1024, 257, 588, 27737, 3095, 295, 10098, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 180886, "start": 1821.32, "end": 1827.26, "text": " When things go well, when engagement is high and ad revenue is up, the success flows vertically,", "tokens": [50988, 1133, 721, 352, 731, 11, 562, 8742, 307, 1090, 293, 614, 9324, 307, 493, 11, 264, 2245, 12867, 28450, 11, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 180886, "start": 1827.6799999999998, "end": 1829.6399999999999, "text": " straight to the top executives and shareholders.", "tokens": [51306, 2997, 281, 264, 1192, 28485, 293, 33294, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 180886, "start": 1829.9199999999998, "end": 1830.6999999999998, "text": " Everyone gets a bonus.", "tokens": [51418, 5198, 2170, 257, 10882, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16301290488537448, "compression_ratio": 1.6008771929824561, "no_speech_prob": 1.883271316671653e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 183070, "start": 1830.7, "end": 1836.14, "text": " But when there is a systemic failure, like a platform-wide saturation of synthetic fraud", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 456, 307, 257, 23789, 7763, 11, 411, 257, 3663, 12, 7990, 27090, 295, 23420, 14560, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 183070, "start": 1836.14, "end": 1839.64, "text": " and bot networks, the responsibility diffuses laterally.", "tokens": [50637, 293, 10592, 9590, 11, 264, 6357, 7593, 8355, 1780, 379, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 183070, "start": 1840.0, "end": 1842.3600000000001, "text": " It spreads out into the gaps between the silos.", "tokens": [50830, 467, 25728, 484, 666, 264, 15031, 1296, 264, 48893, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 183070, "start": 1842.8, "end": 1844.48, "text": " Everyone points the finger at someone else.", "tokens": [50970, 5198, 2793, 264, 5984, 412, 1580, 1646, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 183070, "start": 1844.6000000000001, "end": 1844.8600000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51060, 7587, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 183070, "start": 1845.48, "end": 1849.02, "text": " The engineering team says, hey, we just build the feed recommendation engine.", "tokens": [51104, 440, 7043, 1469, 1619, 11, 4177, 11, 321, 445, 1322, 264, 3154, 11879, 2848, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 183070, "start": 1849.16, "end": 1850.2, "text": " We don't police content.", "tokens": [51288, 492, 500, 380, 3804, 2701, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 183070, "start": 1850.68, "end": 1854.9, "text": " The trust and safety team says, we're doing our best, but we are under-resourced and dealing", "tokens": [51364, 440, 3361, 293, 4514, 1469, 1619, 11, 321, 434, 884, 527, 1151, 11, 457, 321, 366, 833, 12, 495, 396, 1232, 293, 6260, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 183070, "start": 1854.9, "end": 1856.5800000000002, "text": " with a billion users.", "tokens": [51575, 365, 257, 5218, 5022, 13, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 183070, "start": 1856.78, "end": 1858.16, "text": " And what does the CEO say?", "tokens": [51669, 400, 437, 775, 264, 9282, 584, 30, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14560098496694412, "compression_ratio": 1.6151315789473684, "no_speech_prob": 1.6980824298767905e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 185816, "start": 1858.16, "end": 1863.14, "text": " The strategic leaders at the POP issue a press release saying, combating synthetic behavior", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10924, 3523, 412, 264, 430, 12059, 2734, 257, 1886, 4374, 1566, 11, 2512, 990, 23420, 5223, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 185816, "start": 1863.14, "end": 1865.44, "text": " is a complex, industry-wide challenge.", "tokens": [50614, 307, 257, 3997, 11, 3518, 12, 7990, 3430, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 185816, "start": 1865.5600000000002, "end": 1866.16, "text": " Oh, classic.", "tokens": [50735, 876, 11, 7230, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 185816, "start": 1866.72, "end": 1871.0400000000002, "text": " And meanwhile, who absorbs the actual cost of this failure?", "tokens": [50793, 400, 29252, 11, 567, 40745, 264, 3539, 2063, 295, 341, 7763, 30, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 185816, "start": 1871.8600000000001, "end": 1877.78, "text": " The cost is externalized entirely onto the public, onto you, the individual user.", "tokens": [51050, 440, 2063, 307, 8320, 1602, 7696, 3911, 264, 1908, 11, 3911, 291, 11, 264, 2609, 4195, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 185816, "start": 1877.88, "end": 1883.2, "text": " You are the one who has to spend three hours doing forensic research to figure out if a rental", "tokens": [51351, 509, 366, 264, 472, 567, 575, 281, 3496, 1045, 2496, 884, 39084, 2132, 281, 2573, 484, 498, 257, 21468, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 185816, "start": 1883.2, "end": 1884.1200000000001, "text": " listing is real.", "tokens": [51617, 22161, 307, 957, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14889113757075095, "compression_ratio": 1.5387596899224807, "no_speech_prob": 2.0522470441791674e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 188412, "start": 1884.12, "end": 1889.6999999999998, "text": " You are the one dealing with the emotional fallout of a cloned account trying to scam your", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 264, 472, 6260, 365, 264, 6863, 2100, 346, 295, 257, 596, 19009, 2696, 1382, 281, 26917, 428, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09800666495214534, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465600142708594e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 188412, "start": 1889.6999999999998, "end": 1890.06, "text": " family.", "tokens": [50644, 1605, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09800666495214534, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465600142708594e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 188412, "start": 1891.12, "end": 1896.6799999999998, "text": " The platform achieves its frictionless scale by externalizing all the friction onto society.", "tokens": [50715, 440, 3663, 3538, 977, 1080, 17710, 1832, 4373, 538, 8320, 3319, 439, 264, 17710, 3911, 4086, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09800666495214534, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465600142708594e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 188412, "start": 1896.8999999999999, "end": 1902.8, "text": " Which brings us to a really uncomfortable but necessary transition because the logical", "tokens": [51004, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 534, 10532, 457, 4818, 6034, 570, 264, 14978, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09800666495214534, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465600142708594e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 188412, "start": 1902.8, "end": 1908.4399999999998, "text": " next question any outside observer would ask is, if we know this restaurant is serving", "tokens": [51299, 958, 1168, 604, 2380, 27878, 576, 1029, 307, 11, 498, 321, 458, 341, 6383, 307, 8148, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09800666495214534, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.8465600142708594e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 190844, "start": 1908.44, "end": 1914.04, "text": " raw chicken, if we know these platforms are hollow, manipulative, and externalizing their", "tokens": [50365, 8936, 4662, 11, 498, 321, 458, 613, 9473, 366, 23972, 11, 9258, 22678, 11, 293, 8320, 3319, 641, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 190844, "start": 1914.04, "end": 1916.66, "text": " costs onto us, why do we keep eating there?", "tokens": [50645, 5497, 3911, 505, 11, 983, 360, 321, 1066, 3936, 456, 30, 50776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 190844, "start": 1916.8400000000001, "end": 1917.1200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50785, 1779, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 190844, "start": 1917.2, "end": 1921.8, "text": " If we are consciously aware that these platforms are infested with synthetic sociality and bots,", "tokens": [50803, 759, 321, 366, 32538, 3650, 300, 613, 9473, 366, 1536, 21885, 365, 23420, 2093, 507, 293, 35410, 11, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 190844, "start": 1922.18, "end": 1923.4, "text": " why can't we just put the phone down?", "tokens": [51052, 983, 393, 380, 321, 445, 829, 264, 2593, 760, 30, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 190844, "start": 1923.46, "end": 1924.52, "text": " Why can't we stop scrolling?", "tokens": [51116, 1545, 393, 380, 321, 1590, 29053, 30, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 190844, "start": 1924.92, "end": 1926.56, "text": " It's a deep psychological trap.", "tokens": [51189, 467, 311, 257, 2452, 14346, 11487, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09423324499237404, "compression_ratio": 1.5774647887323943, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879052409241035e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 192656, "start": 1926.56, "end": 1931.28, "text": " And this brings us deep into the third section of Flixin's research, the trapped mind, which", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 2452, 666, 264, 2636, 3541, 295, 3235, 970, 259, 311, 2132, 11, 264, 14994, 1575, 11, 597, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 192656, "start": 1931.28, "end": 1934.86, "text": " shifts the focus from the architecture of the platform to the architecture of our own", "tokens": [50601, 19201, 264, 1879, 490, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 3663, 281, 264, 9482, 295, 527, 1065, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 192656, "start": 1934.86, "end": 1935.28, "text": " brains.", "tokens": [50780, 15442, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 192656, "start": 1935.8, "end": 1937.6799999999998, "text": " It looks at subjective self-reference.", "tokens": [50827, 467, 1542, 412, 25972, 2698, 12, 265, 5158, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 192656, "start": 1938.1399999999999, "end": 1943.12, "text": " Now, before we dive into the neuroscience of this, Flixin is very careful to establish", "tokens": [50944, 823, 11, 949, 321, 9192, 666, 264, 42762, 295, 341, 11, 3235, 970, 259, 307, 588, 5026, 281, 8327, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 192656, "start": 1943.12, "end": 1947.24, "text": " a firewall regarding what kind of AI interaction is actually harmful.", "tokens": [51193, 257, 36109, 8595, 437, 733, 295, 7318, 9285, 307, 767, 19727, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 192656, "start": 1947.86, "end": 1950.76, "text": " They aren't saying all interaction with non-humans is bad.", "tokens": [51430, 814, 3212, 380, 1566, 439, 9285, 365, 2107, 12, 14645, 599, 307, 1578, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 192656, "start": 1951.06, "end": 1951.6799999999998, "text": " Oh, okay.", "tokens": [51590, 876, 11, 1392, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 192656, "start": 1951.86, "end": 1952.22, "text": " Like what?", "tokens": [51630, 1743, 437, 30, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15273536553903788, "compression_ratio": 1.6210526315789473, "no_speech_prob": 2.068351783249267e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 195222, "start": 1952.22, "end": 1957.3, "text": " So, knowingly engaging with an automated account, like chatting with an airline's customer service", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 5276, 356, 11268, 365, 364, 18473, 2696, 11, 411, 24654, 365, 364, 29528, 311, 5474, 2643, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 195222, "start": 1957.3, "end": 1963.38, "text": " bot to change a flight, or watching a virtual VTuber personality stream a video game is perfectly", "tokens": [50619, 10592, 281, 1319, 257, 7018, 11, 420, 1976, 257, 6374, 691, 51, 10261, 9033, 4309, 257, 960, 1216, 307, 6239, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 195222, "start": 1963.38, "end": 1963.82, "text": " fine.", "tokens": [50923, 2489, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 195222, "start": 1964.0, "end": 1965.48, "text": " Because it's clear what they are.", "tokens": [50954, 1436, 309, 311, 1850, 437, 436, 366, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 195222, "start": 1965.68, "end": 1966.76, "text": " It is consensual.", "tokens": [51038, 467, 307, 1014, 694, 901, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 195222, "start": 1966.88, "end": 1967.72, "text": " You know it's a machine.", "tokens": [51098, 509, 458, 309, 311, 257, 3479, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 195222, "start": 1967.84, "end": 1968.98, "text": " The machine knows it's a machine.", "tokens": [51146, 440, 3479, 3255, 309, 311, 257, 3479, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 195222, "start": 1969.52, "end": 1975.22, "text": " The pathology, the psychological damage arises entirely from the undisclosed, non-consensual", "tokens": [51230, 440, 3100, 1793, 11, 264, 14346, 4344, 27388, 7696, 490, 264, 674, 271, 3474, 1744, 11, 2107, 12, 21190, 694, 901, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 195222, "start": 1975.22, "end": 1976.38, "text": " capture of our attention.", "tokens": [51515, 7983, 295, 527, 3202, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 195222, "start": 1976.38, "end": 1982.04, "text": " It is the fake accounts masquerading as our peers, or the algorithmically amplified,", "tokens": [51573, 467, 307, 264, 7592, 9402, 2300, 8035, 8166, 382, 527, 16739, 11, 420, 264, 9284, 984, 49237, 11, 51856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13193617294083781, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 198222, "start": 1982.22, "end": 1987.22, "text": " outrage designed to artificially mimic real human consensus that does the damage.", "tokens": [50365, 25933, 4761, 281, 39905, 2270, 31075, 957, 1952, 19115, 300, 775, 264, 4344, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2833210097418891, "compression_ratio": 1.08, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537851375483028e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 198722, "start": 1987.22, "end": 1988.94, "text": " So, how does it capture us so effectively?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 577, 775, 309, 7983, 505, 370, 8659, 30, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 198722, "start": 1989.16, "end": 1991.72, "text": " How does a string of code hijack a human mind?", "tokens": [50462, 1012, 775, 257, 6798, 295, 3089, 10625, 501, 257, 1952, 1575, 30, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 198722, "start": 1991.98, "end": 1997.18, "text": " To explain that mechanism, Flixin dives deep into modern computational neuroscience, specifically", "tokens": [50603, 1407, 2903, 300, 7513, 11, 3235, 970, 259, 274, 1539, 2452, 666, 4363, 28270, 42762, 11, 4682, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 198722, "start": 1997.18, "end": 1999.28, "text": " focusing on the free energy principle.", "tokens": [50863, 8416, 322, 264, 1737, 2281, 8665, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 198722, "start": 1999.42, "end": 2000.18, "text": " The free energy principle.", "tokens": [50975, 440, 1737, 2281, 8665, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 198722, "start": 2000.44, "end": 2004.72, "text": " For a long time, the dominant view of the human brain was that it functioned like a passive", "tokens": [51026, 1171, 257, 938, 565, 11, 264, 15657, 1910, 295, 264, 1952, 3567, 390, 300, 309, 2445, 292, 411, 257, 14975, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 198722, "start": 2004.72, "end": 2005.1200000000001, "text": " camera.", "tokens": [51240, 2799, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 198722, "start": 2005.78, "end": 2010.54, "text": " We thought the brain just sat inside the skull, receiving light through the eyes and sound", "tokens": [51293, 492, 1194, 264, 3567, 445, 3227, 1854, 264, 11743, 11, 10040, 1442, 807, 264, 2575, 293, 1626, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 198722, "start": 2010.54, "end": 2014.8600000000001, "text": " through the ears, and painted an internal picture of the outside world.", "tokens": [51531, 807, 264, 8798, 11, 293, 11797, 364, 6920, 3036, 295, 264, 2380, 1002, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11659363777406755, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.507501588837723e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 201486, "start": 2014.86, "end": 2017.28, "text": " But that model is outdated now, isn't it?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 300, 2316, 307, 36313, 586, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 201486, "start": 2017.4799999999998, "end": 2018.3999999999999, "text": " Completely outdated.", "tokens": [50496, 39978, 36313, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 201486, "start": 2019.0, "end": 2024.54, "text": " The modern view is that the brain is a highly active, predictive inference engine.", "tokens": [50572, 440, 4363, 1910, 307, 300, 264, 3567, 307, 257, 5405, 4967, 11, 35521, 38253, 2848, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 201486, "start": 2025.26, "end": 2027.6, "text": " It does not wait for information to arrive.", "tokens": [50885, 467, 775, 406, 1699, 337, 1589, 281, 8881, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 201486, "start": 2027.6999999999998, "end": 2032.8, "text": " It is constantly, relentlessly generating hypotheses about what is going to happen in the next microsecond.", "tokens": [51007, 467, 307, 6460, 11, 34045, 12048, 17746, 49969, 466, 437, 307, 516, 281, 1051, 294, 264, 958, 3123, 37841, 18882, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 201486, "start": 2032.8799999999999, "end": 2034.1999999999998, "text": " It's anticipating reality.", "tokens": [51266, 467, 311, 40568, 4103, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 201486, "start": 2034.36, "end": 2040.06, "text": " And its primary biological imperative is to minimize what neuroscientists call variational free", "tokens": [51340, 400, 1080, 6194, 13910, 32490, 307, 281, 17522, 437, 28813, 5412, 1751, 818, 3034, 1478, 1737, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12845930119150692, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132654244270904e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 204006, "start": 2040.06, "end": 2044.3799999999999, "text": " energy, which in plain terms essentially means surprise or uncertainty.", "tokens": [50365, 2281, 11, 597, 294, 11121, 2115, 4476, 1355, 6365, 420, 15697, 13, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 204006, "start": 2044.3799999999999, "end": 2048.46, "text": " I want to make sure we really ground this concept of variational free energy, because", "tokens": [50581, 286, 528, 281, 652, 988, 321, 534, 2727, 341, 3410, 295, 3034, 1478, 1737, 2281, 11, 570, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 204006, "start": 2048.46, "end": 2051.74, "text": " it sounds intimidating, but it is actually a very physical experience.", "tokens": [50785, 309, 3263, 29714, 11, 457, 309, 307, 767, 257, 588, 4001, 1752, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 204006, "start": 2051.86, "end": 2052.42, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50955, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 204006, "start": 2052.56, "end": 2056.62, "text": " Think about walking down a flight of stairs in your house in the pitch dark.", "tokens": [50990, 6557, 466, 4494, 760, 257, 7018, 295, 13471, 294, 428, 1782, 294, 264, 7293, 2877, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 204006, "start": 2057.08, "end": 2061.08, "text": " Your brain is generating a predictive model of exactly when your foot is going to hit the", "tokens": [51216, 2260, 3567, 307, 17746, 257, 35521, 2316, 295, 2293, 562, 428, 2671, 307, 516, 281, 2045, 264, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 204006, "start": 2061.08, "end": 2061.7, "text": " next step.", "tokens": [51416, 958, 1823, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 204006, "start": 2061.9, "end": 2062.1, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51457, 865, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 204006, "start": 2062.18, "end": 2064.1, "text": " You reach the bottom, but your brain miscalculated.", "tokens": [51471, 509, 2524, 264, 2767, 11, 457, 428, 3567, 3346, 9895, 2444, 770, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13695976061698717, "compression_ratio": 1.6597222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.882982485212903e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 206410, "start": 2064.1, "end": 2069.56, "text": " And you take one more step, expecting solid wood, but there's just empty air.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 291, 747, 472, 544, 1823, 11, 9650, 5100, 4576, 11, 457, 456, 311, 445, 6707, 1988, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 206410, "start": 2069.7999999999997, "end": 2070.12, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50650, 1079, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 206410, "start": 2070.58, "end": 2075.92, "text": " That heart-stopping jolt you feel in your chest, that stomach-dropping sensation, that is a", "tokens": [50689, 663, 1917, 12, 13559, 3381, 361, 4837, 291, 841, 294, 428, 7443, 11, 300, 9665, 12, 45869, 3759, 20069, 11, 300, 307, 257, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 206410, "start": 2075.92, "end": 2078.7599999999998, "text": " massive spike in variational free energy.", "tokens": [50956, 5994, 21053, 294, 3034, 1478, 1737, 2281, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 206410, "start": 2079.04, "end": 2079.5, "text": " It's awful.", "tokens": [51112, 467, 311, 11232, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 206410, "start": 2079.64, "end": 2081.58, "text": " That is a critical prediction error.", "tokens": [51142, 663, 307, 257, 4924, 17630, 6713, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 206410, "start": 2082.02, "end": 2087.54, "text": " Your brain predicted a floor, reality delivered empty space, and your nervous system floods", "tokens": [51261, 2260, 3567, 19147, 257, 4123, 11, 4103, 10144, 6707, 1901, 11, 293, 428, 6296, 1185, 35536, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 206410, "start": 2087.54, "end": 2091.7999999999997, "text": " with alarm signals to force you to update your model immediately so you don't fall and", "tokens": [51537, 365, 14183, 12354, 281, 3464, 291, 281, 5623, 428, 2316, 4258, 370, 291, 500, 380, 2100, 293, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 206410, "start": 2091.7999999999997, "end": 2092.38, "text": " break your neck.", "tokens": [51750, 1821, 428, 6189, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0910850572986763, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747640600722757e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 209238, "start": 2092.38, "end": 2096.2400000000002, "text": " Okay, so our brains are desperately trying to avoid that feeling of missing a step.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 527, 15442, 366, 23726, 1382, 281, 5042, 300, 2633, 295, 5361, 257, 1823, 13, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 209238, "start": 2096.6, "end": 2098.4, "text": " We want the world to match our predictions.", "tokens": [50576, 492, 528, 264, 1002, 281, 2995, 527, 21264, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 209238, "start": 2099.3, "end": 2102.82, "text": " And Fliction points out that the brain doesn't just passively update its models.", "tokens": [50711, 400, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 264, 3567, 1177, 380, 445, 1320, 3413, 5623, 1080, 5245, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 209238, "start": 2103.28, "end": 2104.2200000000003, "text": " It's self-evidences.", "tokens": [50910, 467, 311, 2698, 12, 13379, 41298, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 209238, "start": 2104.48, "end": 2104.92, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50970, 7587, 13, 50992], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 209238, "start": 2105.36, "end": 2110.26, "text": " Self-evidencing means the brain actively takes actions in the world to make the world conform", "tokens": [51014, 16348, 12, 13379, 4380, 2175, 1355, 264, 3567, 13022, 2516, 5909, 294, 264, 1002, 281, 652, 264, 1002, 18975, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 209238, "start": 2110.26, "end": 2111.48, "text": " to its internal models.", "tokens": [51259, 281, 1080, 6920, 5245, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 209238, "start": 2112.1, "end": 2116.7400000000002, "text": " We seek out environments and information that confirm what we already expect, thereby keeping", "tokens": [51351, 492, 8075, 484, 12388, 293, 1589, 300, 9064, 437, 321, 1217, 2066, 11, 28281, 5145, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 209238, "start": 2116.7400000000002, "end": 2119.88, "text": " our free energy low and our uncertainty manageable.", "tokens": [51583, 527, 1737, 2281, 2295, 293, 527, 15697, 38798, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 209238, "start": 2120.28, "end": 2121.52, "text": " So what does this all mean?", "tokens": [51760, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 30, 51822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12940353570982469, "compression_ratio": 1.7320261437908497, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611134567868445e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 212152, "start": 2121.52, "end": 2122.6, "text": " Take that a step further.", "tokens": [50365, 3664, 300, 257, 1823, 3052, 13, 50419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 212152, "start": 2123.24, "end": 2127.18, "text": " What does all of this neurobiology mean when I am lying in bed at 1 a.m.", "tokens": [50451, 708, 775, 439, 295, 341, 16499, 5614, 1793, 914, 562, 286, 669, 8493, 294, 2901, 412, 502, 257, 13, 76, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 212152, "start": 2127.56, "end": 2132.08, "text": " based in the blue light of my phone, scrolling endlessly through a feed that is making me", "tokens": [50667, 2361, 294, 264, 3344, 1442, 295, 452, 2593, 11, 29053, 44920, 807, 257, 3154, 300, 307, 1455, 385, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 212152, "start": 2132.08, "end": 2133.06, "text": " actively angry?", "tokens": [50893, 13022, 6884, 30, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 212152, "start": 2133.42, "end": 2137.84, "text": " It means that these platforms have figured out how to weaponize your neurobiology against", "tokens": [50960, 467, 1355, 300, 613, 9473, 362, 8932, 484, 577, 281, 7463, 1125, 428, 16499, 5614, 1793, 1970, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 212152, "start": 2137.84, "end": 2138.18, "text": " you.", "tokens": [51181, 291, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 212152, "start": 2138.68, "end": 2144.0, "text": " Fliction connects this predictive processing model to a concept from Lacanian psychoanalysis", "tokens": [51223, 3235, 4105, 16967, 341, 35521, 9007, 2316, 281, 257, 3410, 490, 40113, 282, 952, 33355, 29702, 4642, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 212152, "start": 2144.0, "end": 2144.7599999999998, "text": " called jouissance.", "tokens": [51489, 1219, 11110, 14431, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 212152, "start": 2145.16, "end": 2145.48, "text": " Jouissance.", "tokens": [51547, 508, 263, 14431, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 212152, "start": 2145.48, "end": 2146.36, "text": " It's a great word.", "tokens": [51563, 467, 311, 257, 869, 1349, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18187597592671711, "compression_ratio": 1.5673758865248226, "no_speech_prob": 1.9266736643597238e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 214636, "start": 2146.36, "end": 2148.36, "text": " What exactly is it in this context?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 2293, 307, 309, 294, 341, 4319, 30, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1498930421594071, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 2.253959605763578e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 214636, "start": 2148.7400000000002, "end": 2152.4, "text": " Jouissance is often translated simply as enjoyment, but that's really misleading.", "tokens": [50484, 508, 263, 14431, 307, 2049, 16805, 2935, 382, 32013, 11, 457, 300, 311, 534, 36429, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1498930421594071, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 2.253959605763578e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 214636, "start": 2152.92, "end": 2158.5, "text": " In psychoanalysis, it refers to a surplus of excitation, an intense, almost painful repetition", "tokens": [50693, 682, 33355, 29702, 4642, 11, 309, 14942, 281, 257, 31019, 295, 1624, 4614, 11, 364, 9447, 11, 1920, 11697, 30432, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1498930421594071, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 2.253959605763578e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 214636, "start": 2158.5, "end": 2162.1800000000003, "text": " of an action that causes distress rather than actual pleasure.", "tokens": [50972, 295, 364, 3069, 300, 7700, 24516, 2831, 813, 3539, 6834, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1498930421594071, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 2.253959605763578e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 214636, "start": 2162.34, "end": 2163.2200000000003, "text": " Like picking a scab.", "tokens": [51164, 1743, 8867, 257, 795, 455, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1498930421594071, "compression_ratio": 1.48, "no_speech_prob": 2.253959605763578e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 216322, "start": 2163.22, "end": 2163.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 216322, "start": 2163.74, "end": 2167.6, "text": " It is the paradox of why we are drawn to things that hurt us.", "tokens": [50391, 467, 307, 264, 26221, 295, 983, 321, 366, 10117, 281, 721, 300, 4607, 505, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 216322, "start": 2167.74, "end": 2170.6, "text": " Why do we doomscroll when it undeniably makes us miserable?", "tokens": [50591, 1545, 360, 321, 37131, 4417, 3970, 562, 309, 674, 15711, 1188, 1669, 505, 22321, 30, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 216322, "start": 2171.08, "end": 2176.48, "text": " We do it because the platform algorithms, through billions of hours of A-B testing and maximizing", "tokens": [50758, 492, 360, 309, 570, 264, 3663, 14642, 11, 807, 17375, 295, 2496, 295, 316, 12, 33, 4997, 293, 5138, 3319, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 216322, "start": 2176.48, "end": 2182.04, "text": " that E engagement equation, have empirically discovered how to trigger what are called subcortical", "tokens": [51028, 300, 462, 8742, 5367, 11, 362, 25790, 984, 6941, 577, 281, 7875, 437, 366, 1219, 1422, 66, 477, 804, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 216322, "start": 2182.04, "end": 2182.7, "text": " errors.", "tokens": [51306, 13603, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13709529789014793, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 2.17609610886349e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 218270, "start": 2182.7, "end": 2184.04, "text": " What is a subcortical error?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 307, 257, 1422, 66, 477, 804, 6713, 30, 50432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 218270, "start": 2184.2599999999998, "end": 2189.8599999999997, "text": " These are the deepest, most primal evolutionary triggers hardwired into our nervous systems.", "tokens": [50443, 1981, 366, 264, 28288, 11, 881, 2886, 304, 27567, 22827, 1152, 86, 1824, 666, 527, 6296, 3652, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 218270, "start": 2190.3799999999997, "end": 2196.16, "text": " We are talking about fear, outrage, and most importantly for humans, the threat of social", "tokens": [50749, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 4240, 11, 25933, 11, 293, 881, 8906, 337, 6255, 11, 264, 4734, 295, 2093, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 218270, "start": 2196.16, "end": 2196.74, "text": " exclusion.", "tokens": [51038, 33049, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 218270, "start": 2197.24, "end": 2199.8999999999996, "text": " Things the primate brain literally cannot ignore.", "tokens": [51092, 9514, 264, 2886, 473, 3567, 3736, 2644, 11200, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 218270, "start": 2200.2, "end": 2200.8199999999997, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51240, 48746, 736, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 218270, "start": 2201.08, "end": 2205.3399999999997, "text": " In the brain's predictive modeling system, not all errors are treated equally.", "tokens": [51284, 682, 264, 3567, 311, 35521, 15983, 1185, 11, 406, 439, 13603, 366, 8668, 12309, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15842532051934136, "compression_ratio": 1.553648068669528, "no_speech_prob": 2.19281082007583e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 220534, "start": 2205.34, "end": 2211.1800000000003, "text": " If you are reading an email and you spot a minor typo, your brain registers the error,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 366, 3760, 364, 3796, 293, 291, 4008, 257, 6696, 2125, 78, 11, 428, 3567, 38351, 264, 6713, 11, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 220534, "start": 2211.6600000000003, "end": 2214.36, "text": " assigns it a very low priority, and you keep reading.", "tokens": [50681, 6269, 82, 309, 257, 588, 2295, 9365, 11, 293, 291, 1066, 3760, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 220534, "start": 2214.54, "end": 2215.44, "text": " You barely notice it.", "tokens": [50825, 509, 10268, 3449, 309, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 220534, "start": 2215.5, "end": 2220.06, "text": " But if you see a post suggesting that your political tribe is under attack or that you", "tokens": [50873, 583, 498, 291, 536, 257, 2183, 18094, 300, 428, 3905, 17625, 307, 833, 2690, 420, 300, 291, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 220534, "start": 2220.06, "end": 2224.98, "text": " hold an opinion that will get you ostracized from your community, your brain assigns that", "tokens": [51101, 1797, 364, 4800, 300, 486, 483, 291, 44024, 326, 1602, 490, 428, 1768, 11, 428, 3567, 6269, 82, 300, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 220534, "start": 2224.98, "end": 2226.4, "text": " a massive precision weighting.", "tokens": [51347, 257, 5994, 18356, 3364, 278, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 220534, "start": 2226.48, "end": 2230.7400000000002, "text": " You cannot ignore a perceived threat to your social standing any more than you can ignore", "tokens": [51422, 509, 2644, 11200, 257, 19049, 4734, 281, 428, 2093, 4877, 604, 544, 813, 291, 393, 11200, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 220534, "start": 2230.7400000000002, "end": 2231.6600000000003, "text": " a tiger in the bushes.", "tokens": [51635, 257, 21432, 294, 264, 34303, 13, 51681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08712393442789713, "compression_ratio": 1.7563636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112890744562127e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 223166, "start": 2231.66, "end": 2235.72, "text": " Because for our ancestors, being excluded from the tribe meant starving to death.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 337, 527, 18069, 11, 885, 29486, 490, 264, 17625, 4140, 28420, 281, 2966, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 223166, "start": 2235.8399999999997, "end": 2237.5, "text": " It is a survival level threat.", "tokens": [50574, 467, 307, 257, 12559, 1496, 4734, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 223166, "start": 2237.7599999999998, "end": 2238.2599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50670, 7587, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 223166, "start": 2238.7799999999997, "end": 2243.3199999999997, "text": " So what the platforms do is generate a constant algorithmic stream of these high precision", "tokens": [50721, 407, 437, 264, 9473, 360, 307, 8460, 257, 5754, 9284, 299, 4309, 295, 613, 1090, 18356, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 223166, "start": 2243.3199999999997, "end": 2244.94, "text": " subcortical prediction errors.", "tokens": [50948, 1422, 66, 477, 804, 17630, 13603, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 223166, "start": 2245.48, "end": 2249.16, "text": " Your brain feels a massive biological imperative to resolve the uncertainty.", "tokens": [51056, 2260, 3567, 3417, 257, 5994, 13910, 32490, 281, 14151, 264, 15697, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 223166, "start": 2249.3399999999997, "end": 2250.2599999999998, "text": " So you have to keep looking.", "tokens": [51249, 407, 291, 362, 281, 1066, 1237, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 223166, "start": 2250.56, "end": 2255.66, "text": " You feel the spike of free energy and your instinct is to scroll down, to read the comments, to find", "tokens": [51310, 509, 841, 264, 21053, 295, 1737, 2281, 293, 428, 16556, 307, 281, 11369, 760, 11, 281, 1401, 264, 3053, 11, 281, 915, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 223166, "start": 2255.66, "end": 2259.64, "text": " resolution, to figure out where the tribe stands so you can feel safe again.", "tokens": [51565, 8669, 11, 281, 2573, 484, 689, 264, 17625, 7382, 370, 291, 393, 841, 3273, 797, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12045797994059901, "compression_ratio": 1.689102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370863219385522e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 225964, "start": 2259.64, "end": 2262.06, "text": " But you never actually feel safe, do you?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 291, 1128, 767, 841, 3273, 11, 360, 291, 30, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 225964, "start": 2262.3199999999997, "end": 2266.62, "text": " No, because the architecture of the feed is designed so that you never get resolution.", "tokens": [50499, 883, 11, 570, 264, 9482, 295, 264, 3154, 307, 4761, 370, 300, 291, 1128, 483, 8669, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 225964, "start": 2267.18, "end": 2269.56, "text": " You never find the solid floor at the bottom of the stairs.", "tokens": [50742, 509, 1128, 915, 264, 5100, 4123, 412, 264, 2767, 295, 264, 13471, 13, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 225964, "start": 2269.8399999999997, "end": 2273.3799999999997, "text": " You just get handed the next outrage stimulus, the next missing step.", "tokens": [50875, 509, 445, 483, 16013, 264, 958, 25933, 21366, 11, 264, 958, 5361, 1823, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 225964, "start": 2273.6, "end": 2277.1, "text": " You are trapped in a state of permanent, agonizing suspense.", "tokens": [51063, 509, 366, 14994, 294, 257, 1785, 295, 10996, 11, 623, 266, 3319, 47803, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 225964, "start": 2277.8599999999997, "end": 2279.9, "text": " So my conscious awareness completely fails.", "tokens": [51276, 407, 452, 6648, 8888, 2584, 18199, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 225964, "start": 2280.1, "end": 2284.2599999999998, "text": " I can sit there and logically say to myself, I know this feed is toxic.", "tokens": [51388, 286, 393, 1394, 456, 293, 38887, 584, 281, 2059, 11, 286, 458, 341, 3154, 307, 12786, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.149019753491437, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396395518038844e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 228426, "start": 2284.26, "end": 2289.6400000000003, "text": " I know half of these outraged comments are generated by bots trying to drive engagement.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 458, 1922, 295, 613, 12301, 3004, 3053, 366, 10833, 538, 35410, 1382, 281, 3332, 8742, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 228426, "start": 2289.98, "end": 2293.4, "text": " But my predictive brain is caught in a biological loop.", "tokens": [50651, 583, 452, 35521, 3567, 307, 5415, 294, 257, 13910, 6367, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 228426, "start": 2293.5400000000004, "end": 2294.88, "text": " You can't think your way out of it.", "tokens": [50829, 509, 393, 380, 519, 428, 636, 484, 295, 309, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 228426, "start": 2295.1800000000003, "end": 2299.8, "text": " My own mind's row coefficient, my personal anchor to the physical reality of my quiet bedroom,", "tokens": [50911, 1222, 1065, 1575, 311, 5386, 17619, 11, 452, 2973, 18487, 281, 264, 4001, 4103, 295, 452, 5677, 11211, 11, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 228426, "start": 2300.5400000000004, "end": 2302.5400000000004, "text": " has been hijacked by the digital feed.", "tokens": [51179, 575, 668, 10625, 25949, 538, 264, 4562, 3154, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 228426, "start": 2302.78, "end": 2304.1400000000003, "text": " That is the tragedy of it.", "tokens": [51291, 663, 307, 264, 18563, 295, 309, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 228426, "start": 2304.44, "end": 2307.0, "text": " The row of your mind is driven near zero.", "tokens": [51374, 440, 5386, 295, 428, 1575, 307, 9555, 2651, 4018, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1572694682111644, "compression_ratio": 1.5506072874493928, "no_speech_prob": 1.501478412088697e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 230700, "start": 2307.0, "end": 2311.16, "text": " Not because you literally lost access to the physical reality around you,", "tokens": [50365, 1726, 570, 291, 3736, 2731, 2105, 281, 264, 4001, 4103, 926, 291, 11, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 230700, "start": 2311.32, "end": 2315.68, "text": " but because the precision weighting mechanism that usually connects you to the real world", "tokens": [50581, 457, 570, 264, 18356, 3364, 278, 7513, 300, 2673, 16967, 291, 281, 264, 957, 1002, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 230700, "start": 2315.68, "end": 2318.42, "text": " has been entirely recruited by the synthetic algorithm.", "tokens": [50799, 575, 668, 7696, 33004, 538, 264, 23420, 9284, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 230700, "start": 2318.86, "end": 2324.6, "text": " Your brain is expending all its energy trying to resolve fake crises generated by a machine.", "tokens": [50958, 2260, 3567, 307, 1278, 2029, 439, 1080, 2281, 1382, 281, 14151, 7592, 31403, 10833, 538, 257, 3479, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 230700, "start": 2325.02, "end": 2325.34, "text": " Well, wait.", "tokens": [51266, 1042, 11, 1699, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 230700, "start": 2325.5, "end": 2326.92, "text": " I want to play devil's advocate for a second.", "tokens": [51290, 286, 528, 281, 862, 13297, 311, 14608, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 230700, "start": 2326.96, "end": 2327.54, "text": " Okay, go for it.", "tokens": [51363, 1033, 11, 352, 337, 309, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 230700, "start": 2327.72, "end": 2330.02, "text": " Because whenever tech companies defend their designs,", "tokens": [51401, 1436, 5699, 7553, 3431, 8602, 641, 11347, 11, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 230700, "start": 2330.24, "end": 2332.44, "text": " they don't talk about hijacking our brains.", "tokens": [51527, 436, 500, 380, 751, 466, 10625, 14134, 527, 15442, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 230700, "start": 2332.74, "end": 2334.28, "text": " They talk about removing friction.", "tokens": [51652, 814, 751, 466, 12720, 17710, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16390479978967887, "compression_ratio": 1.6300940438871474, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609817262228875e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 233428, "start": 2334.28, "end": 2337.88, "text": " They say they are making it seamless to log in,", "tokens": [50365, 814, 584, 436, 366, 1455, 309, 28677, 281, 3565, 294, 11, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 233428, "start": 2338.34, "end": 2340.0400000000004, "text": " seamless to find content you like,", "tokens": [50568, 28677, 281, 915, 2701, 291, 411, 11, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 233428, "start": 2340.5, "end": 2341.98, "text": " seamless to connect with friends.", "tokens": [50676, 28677, 281, 1745, 365, 1855, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 233428, "start": 2342.42, "end": 2345.52, "text": " Their whole design philosophy is about reducing resistance.", "tokens": [50772, 6710, 1379, 1715, 10675, 307, 466, 12245, 7335, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 233428, "start": 2345.94, "end": 2348.0400000000004, "text": " And frankly, isn't friction bad?", "tokens": [50948, 400, 11939, 11, 1943, 380, 17710, 1578, 30, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 233428, "start": 2348.46, "end": 2350.5800000000004, "text": " I don't want to use a clunky, difficult app.", "tokens": [51074, 286, 500, 380, 528, 281, 764, 257, 596, 25837, 11, 2252, 724, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 233428, "start": 2350.6600000000003, "end": 2351.7000000000003, "text": " I want it to be easy.", "tokens": [51184, 286, 528, 309, 281, 312, 1858, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 233428, "start": 2352.1800000000003, "end": 2357.6600000000003, "text": " Flixion strongly, fundamentally disagrees with the Silicon Valley dogma that all friction is bad.", "tokens": [51260, 3235, 970, 313, 10613, 11, 17879, 10414, 4856, 365, 264, 25351, 10666, 3000, 1696, 300, 439, 17710, 307, 1578, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 233428, "start": 2358.2000000000003, "end": 2361.28, "text": " To counter this, they introduce a vital concept called waymaking.", "tokens": [51561, 1407, 5682, 341, 11, 436, 5366, 257, 11707, 3410, 1219, 636, 12402, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 233428, "start": 2361.44, "end": 2361.86, "text": " Waymaking.", "tokens": [51723, 9558, 12402, 13, 51744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18526370585465632, "compression_ratio": 1.6340579710144927, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204035063558056e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 236186, "start": 2361.86, "end": 2366.78, "text": " Waymaking is the continuous, necessary cognitive labor of drawing boundaries,", "tokens": [50365, 9558, 12402, 307, 264, 10957, 11, 4818, 15605, 5938, 295, 6316, 13180, 11, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951984112079327, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179394621620215e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 236186, "start": 2367.26, "end": 2371.54, "text": " of bracketing off irrelevant information, of actively negotiating with uncertainty.", "tokens": [50635, 295, 12305, 9880, 766, 28682, 1589, 11, 295, 13022, 30396, 365, 15697, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951984112079327, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179394621620215e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 236186, "start": 2372.04, "end": 2373.6800000000003, "text": " Can you give me an example of waymaking?", "tokens": [50874, 1664, 291, 976, 385, 364, 1365, 295, 636, 12402, 30, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951984112079327, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179394621620215e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 236186, "start": 2374.1400000000003, "end": 2380.2400000000002, "text": " Think about the process of reading a dense, difficult book or doing original research in a library.", "tokens": [50979, 6557, 466, 264, 1399, 295, 3760, 257, 18011, 11, 2252, 1446, 420, 884, 3380, 2132, 294, 257, 6405, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1951984112079327, "compression_ratio": 1.495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179394621620215e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 238024, "start": 2380.24, "end": 2383.22, "text": " There is physical and mental resistance.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 4001, 293, 4973, 7335, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 238024, "start": 2383.8399999999997, "end": 2385.7999999999997, "text": " You have to hunt for the right source.", "tokens": [50545, 509, 362, 281, 12454, 337, 264, 558, 4009, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 238024, "start": 2386.0, "end": 2388.9199999999996, "text": " You have to struggle to understand a complex paragraph.", "tokens": [50653, 509, 362, 281, 7799, 281, 1223, 257, 3997, 18865, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 238024, "start": 2389.3999999999996, "end": 2392.3599999999997, "text": " You have to synthesize conflicting opinions.", "tokens": [50823, 509, 362, 281, 26617, 1125, 43784, 11819, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 238024, "start": 2392.7, "end": 2393.14, "text": " It's hard work.", "tokens": [50988, 467, 311, 1152, 589, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 238024, "start": 2393.3399999999997, "end": 2394.8599999999997, "text": " That is productive friction.", "tokens": [51020, 663, 307, 13304, 17710, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 238024, "start": 2395.4199999999996, "end": 2402.2799999999997, "text": " And Flixion argues that this specific kind of friction is neurologically required for actual learning and genuine meaning making.", "tokens": [51124, 400, 3235, 970, 313, 38218, 300, 341, 2685, 733, 295, 17710, 307, 28351, 984, 4739, 337, 3539, 2539, 293, 16699, 3620, 1455, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2177377723785768, "compression_ratio": 1.5848214285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034109362102813e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 240228, "start": 2402.28, "end": 2408.36, "text": " You only build cognitive maps of the world by encountering resistance and overcoming it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 787, 1322, 15605, 11317, 295, 264, 1002, 538, 8593, 278, 7335, 293, 38047, 309, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08543046977784899, "compression_ratio": 1.5196078431372548, "no_speech_prob": 1.649054807636996e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 240228, "start": 2408.5600000000004, "end": 2420.2400000000002, "text": " So when the TikTok or YouTube algorithm pre-computes exactly what I want to see before I even know I want to see it and just feeds it to me on an endless frictionless conveyor belt, it is doing the cognitive labor for me.", "tokens": [50679, 407, 562, 264, 20211, 420, 3088, 9284, 659, 12, 21541, 1819, 2293, 437, 286, 528, 281, 536, 949, 286, 754, 458, 286, 528, 281, 536, 309, 293, 445, 23712, 309, 281, 385, 322, 364, 16144, 17710, 1832, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 309, 307, 884, 264, 15605, 5938, 337, 385, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08543046977784899, "compression_ratio": 1.5196078431372548, "no_speech_prob": 1.649054807636996e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 242024, "start": 2420.24, "end": 2425.8399999999997, "text": " Yes. And by removing that productive friction, the algorithm completely destroys your capacity for waymaking.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 400, 538, 12720, 300, 13304, 17710, 11, 264, 9284, 2584, 36714, 428, 6042, 337, 636, 12402, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12535458226357737, "compression_ratio": 1.4385026737967914, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 242024, "start": 2426.06, "end": 2427.4199999999996, "text": " You aren't navigating a landscape.", "tokens": [50656, 509, 3212, 380, 32054, 257, 9661, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12535458226357737, "compression_ratio": 1.4385026737967914, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 242024, "start": 2427.64, "end": 2430.7999999999997, "text": " You are just being spoon-fed stimuli while strapped to a chair.", "tokens": [50735, 509, 366, 445, 885, 12453, 12, 33712, 47752, 1339, 2148, 3320, 281, 257, 6090, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12535458226357737, "compression_ratio": 1.4385026737967914, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 242024, "start": 2431.2, "end": 2434.64, "text": " Flixion describes these frictionless environments as hollow.", "tokens": [50913, 3235, 970, 313, 15626, 613, 17710, 1832, 12388, 382, 23972, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12535458226357737, "compression_ratio": 1.4385026737967914, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 243464, "start": 2434.64, "end": 2436.8599999999997, "text": " The network isn't empty.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3209, 1943, 380, 6707, 13, 50476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14980859959379156, "compression_ratio": 1.6007751937984496, "no_speech_prob": 1.973875273300618e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 243464, "start": 2437.16, "end": 2442.2799999999997, "text": " It is densely packed with billions of videos and posts, but it is structurally hollow.", "tokens": [50491, 467, 307, 24505, 736, 13265, 365, 17375, 295, 2145, 293, 12300, 11, 457, 309, 307, 6594, 6512, 23972, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14980859959379156, "compression_ratio": 1.6007751937984496, "no_speech_prob": 1.973875273300618e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 243464, "start": 2442.6, "end": 2450.52, "text": " There is no depth to it because the friction required to build depth has been deliberately engineered out in the pursuit of engagement.", "tokens": [50763, 821, 307, 572, 7161, 281, 309, 570, 264, 17710, 4739, 281, 1322, 7161, 575, 668, 23506, 38648, 484, 294, 264, 23365, 295, 8742, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14980859959379156, "compression_ratio": 1.6007751937984496, "no_speech_prob": 1.973875273300618e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 243464, "start": 2450.74, "end": 2453.54, "text": " Okay. I have to admit, this is getting incredibly bleak.", "tokens": [51170, 1033, 13, 286, 362, 281, 9796, 11, 341, 307, 1242, 6252, 5408, 514, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14980859959379156, "compression_ratio": 1.6007751937984496, "no_speech_prob": 1.973875273300618e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 243464, "start": 2453.8799999999997, "end": 2459.96, "text": " We have massive tech platforms that are structurally blind to reality because their row coefficient is zero.", "tokens": [51327, 492, 362, 5994, 7553, 9473, 300, 366, 6594, 6512, 6865, 281, 4103, 570, 641, 5386, 17619, 307, 4018, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14980859959379156, "compression_ratio": 1.6007751937984496, "no_speech_prob": 1.973875273300618e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 245996, "start": 2459.96, "end": 2470.04, "text": " And we have our own biological brains trapped inside these hollow networks, hijacked by Chuson's loops, and starved of the productive friction we need to actually think critically.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 362, 527, 1065, 13910, 15442, 14994, 1854, 613, 23972, 9590, 11, 10625, 25949, 538, 761, 301, 266, 311, 16121, 11, 293, 3543, 937, 295, 264, 13304, 17710, 321, 643, 281, 767, 519, 22797, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11670702934265137, "compression_ratio": 1.5269230769230768, "no_speech_prob": 2.1341960317056152e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 245996, "start": 2470.5, "end": 2471.34, "text": " It's a dark picture.", "tokens": [50892, 467, 311, 257, 2877, 3036, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11670702934265137, "compression_ratio": 1.5269230769230768, "no_speech_prob": 2.1341960317056152e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 245996, "start": 2471.78, "end": 2474.76, "text": " So pivoting to the fourth section of the research, how do we force the anchor?", "tokens": [50956, 407, 14538, 278, 281, 264, 6409, 3541, 295, 264, 2132, 11, 577, 360, 321, 3464, 264, 18487, 30, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11670702934265137, "compression_ratio": 1.5269230769230768, "no_speech_prob": 2.1341960317056152e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 245996, "start": 2475.12, "end": 2476.7200000000003, "text": " How do we fix a system that's broken?", "tokens": [51123, 1012, 360, 321, 3191, 257, 1185, 300, 311, 5463, 30, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11670702934265137, "compression_ratio": 1.5269230769230768, "no_speech_prob": 2.1341960317056152e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 245996, "start": 2477.14, "end": 2482.34, "text": " The immediate knee-jerk instinct in our society is to impose top-down control.", "tokens": [51224, 440, 11629, 9434, 12, 73, 10608, 16556, 294, 527, 4086, 307, 281, 26952, 1192, 12, 5093, 1969, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11670702934265137, "compression_ratio": 1.5269230769230768, "no_speech_prob": 2.1341960317056152e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 248234, "start": 2482.34, "end": 2490.96, "text": " We say, let's create a supreme regulator, let's form a global AI ethics board, or a government commission with the power to find these companies into submission.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 584, 11, 718, 311, 1884, 257, 27756, 36250, 11, 718, 311, 1254, 257, 4338, 7318, 19769, 3150, 11, 420, 257, 2463, 9221, 365, 264, 1347, 281, 915, 613, 3431, 666, 23689, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13298025131225585, "compression_ratio": 1.558139534883721, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686376672764291e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 248234, "start": 2491.32, "end": 2491.96, "text": " Right, bring the government.", "tokens": [50814, 1779, 11, 1565, 264, 2463, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13298025131225585, "compression_ratio": 1.558139534883721, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686376672764291e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 248234, "start": 2492.2400000000002, "end": 2496.8, "text": " But fiction warns that this approach falls immediately into what they call the recursion problem.", "tokens": [50860, 583, 13266, 12286, 82, 300, 341, 3109, 8804, 4258, 666, 437, 436, 818, 264, 20560, 313, 1154, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13298025131225585, "compression_ratio": 1.558139534883721, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686376672764291e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 248234, "start": 2497.0, "end": 2498.2400000000002, "text": " Because who corrects the corrector?", "tokens": [51098, 1436, 567, 3006, 82, 264, 29731, 1672, 30, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13298025131225585, "compression_ratio": 1.558139534883721, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686376672764291e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 248234, "start": 2498.48, "end": 2499.0, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51172, 48746, 736, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13298025131225585, "compression_ratio": 1.558139534883721, "no_speech_prob": 1.6686376672764291e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 249900, "start": 2499.0, "end": 2504.14, "text": " A regulatory body is not a magical entity existing outside of reality.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 18260, 1772, 307, 406, 257, 12066, 13977, 6741, 2380, 295, 4103, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 249900, "start": 2504.44, "end": 2505.66, "text": " It is just another system.", "tokens": [50637, 467, 307, 445, 1071, 1185, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 249900, "start": 2506.28, "end": 2513.32, "text": " It is a human-built institution with its own incentive structures, its own evaluation functions, and its own internal signals.", "tokens": [50729, 467, 307, 257, 1952, 12, 23018, 7818, 365, 1080, 1065, 22346, 9227, 11, 1080, 1065, 13344, 6828, 11, 293, 1080, 1065, 6920, 12354, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 249900, "start": 2513.82, "end": 2518.18, "text": " And crucially, a regulator's row coefficient can also drop to zero.", "tokens": [51106, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 257, 36250, 311, 5386, 17619, 393, 611, 3270, 281, 4018, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 249900, "start": 2518.42, "end": 2521.84, "text": " How does a regulator lose its anchor to reality?", "tokens": [51336, 1012, 775, 257, 36250, 3624, 1080, 18487, 281, 4103, 30, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 249900, "start": 2522.32, "end": 2523.4, "text": " It happens all the time.", "tokens": [51531, 467, 2314, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14386091449043967, "compression_ratio": 1.6339285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.943031239376447e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 252340, "start": 2523.4, "end": 2531.58, "text": " A regulatory agency might start judging its own success not by whether it actually reduced harm to the end users, but by internal metrics.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 18260, 7934, 1062, 722, 23587, 1080, 1065, 2245, 406, 538, 1968, 309, 767, 9212, 6491, 281, 264, 917, 5022, 11, 457, 538, 6920, 16367, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053304076194763184, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439592100137788e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 252340, "start": 2532.08, "end": 2540.38, "text": " It might measure success by how many millions of dollars in fines it issued this quarter, or how many high-profile congressional hearings it held, or how many press releases it put out.", "tokens": [50799, 467, 1062, 3481, 2245, 538, 577, 867, 6803, 295, 3808, 294, 37989, 309, 14379, 341, 6555, 11, 420, 577, 867, 1090, 12, 29175, 794, 32962, 34052, 309, 5167, 11, 420, 577, 867, 1886, 16952, 309, 829, 484, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053304076194763184, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439592100137788e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 252340, "start": 2540.6, "end": 2540.92, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [51225, 876, 11, 558, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053304076194763184, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439592100137788e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 252340, "start": 2541.04, "end": 2549.7000000000003, "text": " The fines become a cost of doing business for the tech giant, the regulator looks tough on paper, and the actual user being scammed is still screaming into the void.", "tokens": [51247, 440, 37989, 1813, 257, 2063, 295, 884, 1606, 337, 264, 7553, 7410, 11, 264, 36250, 1542, 4930, 322, 3035, 11, 293, 264, 3539, 4195, 885, 795, 19859, 307, 920, 12636, 666, 264, 22009, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.053304076194763184, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.4439592100137788e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 254970, "start": 2549.7, "end": 2554.0, "text": " If the regulator becomes self-referential, it is just as useless as the algorithm.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 36250, 3643, 2698, 12, 265, 612, 2549, 11, 309, 307, 445, 382, 14115, 382, 264, 9284, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 254970, "start": 2554.72, "end": 2562.16, "text": " So centralized autopoiesis, the idea of a single central brain controlling and correcting the system from the top down, doesn't work.", "tokens": [50616, 407, 32395, 31090, 78, 530, 271, 11, 264, 1558, 295, 257, 2167, 5777, 3567, 14905, 293, 47032, 264, 1185, 490, 264, 1192, 760, 11, 1177, 380, 589, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 254970, "start": 2562.56, "end": 2563.3799999999997, "text": " What is the alternative?", "tokens": [51008, 708, 307, 264, 8535, 30, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 254970, "start": 2563.8399999999997, "end": 2566.46, "text": " The alternative Fliction proposes is sympoiesis.", "tokens": [51072, 440, 8535, 3235, 4105, 2365, 4201, 307, 13240, 78, 530, 271, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 254970, "start": 2566.9199999999996, "end": 2567.6, "text": " Sympoiesis.", "tokens": [51226, 3902, 2455, 78, 530, 271, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 254970, "start": 2567.7999999999997, "end": 2569.2999999999997, "text": " This translates to making with.", "tokens": [51270, 639, 28468, 281, 1455, 365, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 254970, "start": 2569.72, "end": 2572.46, "text": " It is a model of distributed, collective correction.", "tokens": [51366, 467, 307, 257, 2316, 295, 12631, 11, 12590, 19984, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16188907623291016, "compression_ratio": 1.6125, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080488499271462e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 257246, "start": 2572.46, "end": 2588.04, "text": " Instead of relying on a single watchdog, the coherence and safety of the system must emerge organically from the ongoing, continuous interaction of millions of participants, none of whom has the unilateral power to control the whole thing.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 295, 24140, 322, 257, 2167, 1159, 14833, 11, 264, 26528, 655, 293, 4514, 295, 264, 1185, 1633, 21511, 1798, 984, 490, 264, 10452, 11, 10957, 9285, 295, 6803, 295, 10503, 11, 6022, 295, 7101, 575, 264, 517, 37751, 1347, 281, 1969, 264, 1379, 551, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10948715426705101, "compression_ratio": 1.586466165413534, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537860049100408e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 257246, "start": 2588.2400000000002, "end": 2590.1, "text": " That sounds incredibly complicated.", "tokens": [51154, 663, 3263, 6252, 6179, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10948715426705101, "compression_ratio": 1.586466165413534, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537860049100408e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 257246, "start": 2590.26, "end": 2598.86, "text": " And technically, to make sympoiesis possible in a digital network, Fliction proposes a radically different software architecture called SpherePop.", "tokens": [51255, 400, 12120, 11, 281, 652, 13240, 78, 530, 271, 1944, 294, 257, 4562, 3209, 11, 3235, 4105, 2365, 4201, 257, 35508, 819, 4722, 9482, 1219, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10948715426705101, "compression_ratio": 1.586466165413534, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537860049100408e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 259886, "start": 2598.86, "end": 2604.8, "text": " SpherePop. I absolutely love this concept because it solves one of the most maddening things about the Internet.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 6605, 38677, 13, 286, 3122, 959, 341, 3410, 570, 309, 39890, 472, 295, 264, 881, 5244, 1556, 278, 721, 466, 264, 7703, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 259886, "start": 2605.3, "end": 2606.42, "text": " Let me use an analogy here.", "tokens": [50687, 961, 385, 764, 364, 21663, 510, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 259886, "start": 2606.76, "end": 2612.04, "text": " Right now, social media accounts, especially for scammers and bot networks, operate like Etch-a-Sketches.", "tokens": [50760, 1779, 586, 11, 2093, 3021, 9402, 11, 2318, 337, 795, 48414, 293, 10592, 9590, 11, 9651, 411, 3790, 339, 12, 64, 12, 50, 5758, 3781, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 259886, "start": 2612.28, "end": 2613.84, "text": " That is a perfect comparison.", "tokens": [51036, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 9660, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 259886, "start": 2614.1200000000003, "end": 2621.7400000000002, "text": " If you were a scammer, you draw your scam on the screen, you steal some money, you spread some disinformation, eventually the platform catches you and bans your account.", "tokens": [51128, 759, 291, 645, 257, 26917, 936, 11, 291, 2642, 428, 26917, 322, 264, 2568, 11, 291, 11009, 512, 1460, 11, 291, 3974, 512, 717, 20941, 11, 4728, 264, 3663, 25496, 291, 293, 272, 599, 428, 2696, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 259886, "start": 2622.46, "end": 2626.82, "text": " But what do you do? You don't go to jail. You just shake the Etch-a-Sketch.", "tokens": [51545, 583, 437, 360, 291, 360, 30, 509, 500, 380, 352, 281, 10511, 13, 509, 445, 10283, 264, 3790, 339, 12, 64, 12, 50, 5758, 339, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 259886, "start": 2626.9, "end": 2628.1800000000003, "text": " Yep, completely clean slate.", "tokens": [51767, 7010, 11, 2584, 2541, 39118, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11627976958816116, "compression_ratio": 1.6497005988023952, "no_speech_prob": 2.0364716857290688e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 262818, "start": 2628.18, "end": 2637.8599999999997, "text": " The screen goes blank, all your history is erased, and you just create a brand new account with a new email address five minutes later and start the exact same scam over again.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2568, 1709, 8247, 11, 439, 428, 2503, 307, 38359, 11, 293, 291, 445, 1884, 257, 3360, 777, 2696, 365, 257, 777, 3796, 2985, 1732, 2077, 1780, 293, 722, 264, 1900, 912, 26917, 670, 797, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 262818, "start": 2638.22, "end": 2640.1, "text": " There is zero permanent consequence.", "tokens": [50867, 821, 307, 4018, 10996, 18326, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 262818, "start": 2640.1, "end": 2646.3599999999997, "text": " And that is the core architectural vulnerability of our current platforms, the total erasability of history.", "tokens": [50961, 400, 300, 307, 264, 4965, 26621, 24210, 295, 527, 2190, 9473, 11, 264, 3217, 1189, 296, 2310, 295, 2503, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 262818, "start": 2647.02, "end": 2651.2, "text": " They are state-based systems where only the current state matters.", "tokens": [51307, 814, 366, 1785, 12, 6032, 3652, 689, 787, 264, 2190, 1785, 7001, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 262818, "start": 2651.3799999999997, "end": 2652.7, "text": " So how does SpherePop fix that?", "tokens": [51525, 407, 577, 775, 318, 6605, 38677, 3191, 300, 30, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 262818, "start": 2652.9199999999996, "end": 2654.72, "text": " SpherePop flips this entirely.", "tokens": [51602, 318, 6605, 38677, 40249, 341, 7696, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12788714454287575, "compression_ratio": 1.6496350364963503, "no_speech_prob": 1.868777702029867e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 265472, "start": 2654.72, "end": 2661.58, "text": " It changes the fundamental primitive of the network from erasable profiles to irreversible event histories.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2962, 264, 8088, 28540, 295, 264, 3209, 490, 1189, 296, 712, 23693, 281, 16014, 840, 964, 2280, 30631, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 265472, "start": 2662.18, "end": 2665.48, "text": " Under SpherePop, interactions are governed by four operators.", "tokens": [50738, 6974, 318, 6605, 38677, 11, 13280, 366, 35529, 538, 1451, 19077, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 265472, "start": 2666.0, "end": 2668.6, "text": " Pop, Refuse, Bind, and Collapse.", "tokens": [50929, 10215, 11, 16957, 438, 11, 363, 471, 11, 293, 4586, 11145, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 265472, "start": 2668.74, "end": 2673.1, "text": " Okay, slow down and walk me through those four operators, because this is the mechanics of how we fix the Internet.", "tokens": [51066, 1033, 11, 2964, 760, 293, 1792, 385, 807, 729, 1451, 19077, 11, 570, 341, 307, 264, 12939, 295, 577, 321, 3191, 264, 7703, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 265472, "start": 2673.3199999999997, "end": 2673.9199999999996, "text": " What is Pop?", "tokens": [51295, 708, 307, 10215, 30, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 265472, "start": 2674.24, "end": 2676.24, "text": " Pop is the initiation of an event.", "tokens": [51341, 10215, 307, 264, 43569, 295, 364, 2280, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13594126194081407, "compression_ratio": 1.5443037974683544, "no_speech_prob": 1.1972042281149786e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 267624, "start": 2676.24, "end": 2679.74, "text": " Let's say a user wants to send a direct message to another user.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 257, 4195, 2738, 281, 2845, 257, 2047, 3636, 281, 1071, 4195, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 267624, "start": 2679.9599999999996, "end": 2683.08, "text": " The system pops an interaction sphere into existence.", "tokens": [50551, 440, 1185, 16795, 364, 9285, 16687, 666, 9123, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 267624, "start": 2683.2999999999997, "end": 2684.3599999999997, "text": " It's a proposed connection.", "tokens": [50718, 467, 311, 257, 10348, 4984, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 267624, "start": 2684.64, "end": 2685.3199999999997, "text": " Okay, and refuse.", "tokens": [50785, 1033, 11, 293, 16791, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 267624, "start": 2685.54, "end": 2691.68, "text": " If the receiver looks at the message, sees it's a scammer, and rejects the connection, that is a refuse.", "tokens": [50830, 759, 264, 20086, 1542, 412, 264, 3636, 11, 8194, 309, 311, 257, 26917, 936, 11, 293, 8248, 82, 264, 4984, 11, 300, 307, 257, 16791, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 267624, "start": 2692.18, "end": 2695.3399999999997, "text": " But here is the critical difference from current platforms.", "tokens": [51162, 583, 510, 307, 264, 4924, 2649, 490, 2190, 9473, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 267624, "start": 2695.7999999999997, "end": 2698.2799999999997, "text": " That refusal doesn't just disappear into the ether.", "tokens": [51343, 663, 48948, 1177, 380, 445, 11596, 666, 264, 37096, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 267624, "start": 2698.7799999999997, "end": 2702.8399999999997, "text": " It is permanently cryptographically logged in the ledger of the sender.", "tokens": [51492, 467, 307, 24042, 9844, 3108, 984, 27231, 294, 264, 4684, 1321, 295, 264, 2845, 260, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15464208851689878, "compression_ratio": 1.6902985074626866, "no_speech_prob": 1.1919927935324925e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 270284, "start": 2702.84, "end": 2703.44, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 270284, "start": 2703.6400000000003, "end": 2704.6600000000003, "text": " So the failure is recorded.", "tokens": [50405, 407, 264, 7763, 307, 8287, 13, 50456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 270284, "start": 2704.78, "end": 2705.42, "text": " What about Bind?", "tokens": [50462, 708, 466, 363, 471, 30, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 270284, "start": 2706.36, "end": 2711.54, "text": " If the receiver accepts the message and replies, both parties bind to the interaction.", "tokens": [50541, 759, 264, 20086, 33538, 264, 3636, 293, 42289, 11, 1293, 8265, 14786, 281, 264, 9285, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 270284, "start": 2712.0, "end": 2714.9, "text": " They are now mutually engaged in a shared event space.", "tokens": [50823, 814, 366, 586, 39144, 8237, 294, 257, 5507, 2280, 1901, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 270284, "start": 2715.04, "end": 2716.1600000000003, "text": " And finally, collapse.", "tokens": [50975, 400, 2721, 11, 15584, 13, 51031], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 270284, "start": 2716.4, "end": 2718.9, "text": " When the interaction ends, the sphere collapses.", "tokens": [51043, 1133, 264, 9285, 5314, 11, 264, 16687, 48765, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 270284, "start": 2719.7200000000003, "end": 2723.98, "text": " The final state of that interaction, whether it was a successful transaction, a friendly chat,", "tokens": [51209, 440, 2572, 1785, 295, 300, 9285, 11, 1968, 309, 390, 257, 4406, 14425, 11, 257, 9208, 5081, 11, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 270284, "start": 2724.1400000000003, "end": 2730.02, "text": " or one person reporting the other for fraud, is permanently hard-coded into the event histories of both participants.", "tokens": [51430, 420, 472, 954, 10031, 264, 661, 337, 14560, 11, 307, 24042, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 666, 264, 2280, 30631, 295, 1293, 10503, 13, 51724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 270284, "start": 2730.1400000000003, "end": 2731.2000000000003, "text": " That's a huge shift.", "tokens": [51730, 663, 311, 257, 2603, 5513, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15205790710449218, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.1870173897629566e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 273120, "start": 2731.2, "end": 2737.74, "text": " The key to all of this is that identity in SpherePop is no longer a superficial profile score that you can reset.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2141, 281, 439, 295, 341, 307, 300, 6575, 294, 318, 6605, 38677, 307, 572, 2854, 257, 34622, 7964, 6175, 300, 291, 393, 14322, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 273120, "start": 2738.24, "end": 2742.7799999999997, "text": " Your identity is your accumulated, permanent history of collapsed events.", "tokens": [50717, 2260, 6575, 307, 428, 31346, 11, 10996, 2503, 295, 24578, 3931, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 273120, "start": 2742.8999999999996, "end": 2744.3999999999996, "text": " So let's run the scammer through this.", "tokens": [50950, 407, 718, 311, 1190, 264, 26917, 936, 807, 341, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 273120, "start": 2745.06, "end": 2748.2, "text": " A scammer tries to shake the Etch-A-Sketch under SpherePop rules.", "tokens": [51058, 316, 26917, 936, 9898, 281, 10283, 264, 3790, 339, 12, 32, 12, 50, 5758, 339, 833, 318, 6605, 38677, 4474, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 273120, "start": 2748.58, "end": 2749.2, "text": " They can't.", "tokens": [51234, 814, 393, 380, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 273120, "start": 2749.2999999999997, "end": 2756.96, "text": " If they spam 10,000 people and get 10,000 refuse logs, that history is permanently attached to their cryptographic identity.", "tokens": [51270, 759, 436, 24028, 1266, 11, 1360, 561, 293, 483, 1266, 11, 1360, 16791, 20820, 11, 300, 2503, 307, 24042, 8570, 281, 641, 9844, 12295, 6575, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 273120, "start": 2757.2799999999997, "end": 2758.66, "text": " But couldn't they just make a new account?", "tokens": [51669, 583, 2809, 380, 436, 445, 652, 257, 777, 2696, 30, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914354355104509, "compression_ratio": 1.6109215017064846, "no_speech_prob": 1.3940757185790242e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 275866, "start": 2758.66, "end": 2764.16, "text": " If they try to abandon that identity and start a new one, the new identity has zero collapse history.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 436, 853, 281, 9072, 300, 6575, 293, 722, 257, 777, 472, 11, 264, 777, 6575, 575, 4018, 15584, 2503, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12847495690370217, "compression_ratio": 1.5391705069124424, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 275866, "start": 2764.8999999999996, "end": 2770.2799999999997, "text": " And in a symbiotic network, a completely blank history is inherently untrusted.", "tokens": [50677, 400, 294, 257, 43700, 6471, 299, 3209, 11, 257, 2584, 8247, 2503, 307, 27993, 1701, 81, 6589, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12847495690370217, "compression_ratio": 1.5391705069124424, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 275866, "start": 2770.7, "end": 2777.3599999999997, "text": " You can't interact with high-trust individuals without building up a genuine history of positive, collapsed events.", "tokens": [50967, 509, 393, 380, 4648, 365, 1090, 12, 6903, 381, 5346, 1553, 2390, 493, 257, 16699, 2503, 295, 3353, 11, 24578, 3931, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12847495690370217, "compression_ratio": 1.5391705069124424, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 275866, "start": 2777.46, "end": 2778.8999999999996, "text": " So it actually costs them something.", "tokens": [51305, 407, 309, 767, 5497, 552, 746, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12847495690370217, "compression_ratio": 1.5391705069124424, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362162276115089e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 277890, "start": 2778.9, "end": 2784.9, "text": " SpherePop drastically, structurally raises the thermodynamic cost of deception.", "tokens": [50365, 318, 6605, 38677, 29673, 11, 6594, 6512, 19658, 264, 8810, 34988, 2063, 295, 40451, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 277890, "start": 2785.44, "end": 2787.86, "text": " It makes faking it too expensive to be profitable.", "tokens": [50692, 467, 1669, 283, 2456, 309, 886, 5124, 281, 312, 21608, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 277890, "start": 2788.1800000000003, "end": 2789.1, "text": " That is brilliant.", "tokens": [50829, 663, 307, 10248, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 277890, "start": 2789.28, "end": 2792.1800000000003, "text": " It uses the structure of the network itself to enforce consequence.", "tokens": [50884, 467, 4960, 264, 3877, 295, 264, 3209, 2564, 281, 24825, 18326, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 277890, "start": 2792.36, "end": 2792.62, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51038, 865, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 277890, "start": 2792.84, "end": 2794.62, "text": " But I have to ask about the elephant in the room.", "tokens": [51062, 583, 286, 362, 281, 1029, 466, 264, 19791, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 277890, "start": 2794.78, "end": 2796.04, "text": " What about the AI itself?", "tokens": [51159, 708, 466, 264, 7318, 2564, 30, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 277890, "start": 2796.1600000000003, "end": 2797.1600000000003, "text": " Right, the AI.", "tokens": [51228, 1779, 11, 264, 7318, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1885182773365694, "compression_ratio": 1.5096153846153846, "no_speech_prob": 1.6870669358043378e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 279716, "start": 2797.16, "end": 2799.3999999999996, "text": " Because we aren't just dealing with human scammers anymore.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 321, 3212, 380, 445, 6260, 365, 1952, 795, 48414, 3602, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 279716, "start": 2799.54, "end": 2807.2599999999998, "text": " With large language models, we are seeing AI generate completely coherent, sometimes incredibly persuasive text, video, and audio.", "tokens": [50484, 2022, 2416, 2856, 5245, 11, 321, 366, 2577, 7318, 8460, 2584, 36239, 11, 2171, 6252, 16336, 23686, 2487, 11, 960, 11, 293, 6278, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 279716, "start": 2808.06, "end": 2810.7599999999998, "text": " How does SpherePop handle an entity that isn't even human?", "tokens": [50910, 1012, 775, 318, 6605, 38677, 4813, 364, 13977, 300, 1943, 380, 754, 1952, 30, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 279716, "start": 2811.1, "end": 2814.7599999999998, "text": " This brings us to what Fliction identifies as the post-Turing condition.", "tokens": [51062, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 437, 3235, 4105, 34597, 382, 264, 2183, 12, 51, 1345, 4188, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 279716, "start": 2815.3199999999997, "end": 2823.56, "text": " To understand the danger of modern AI, Fliction breaks down the concept of subjectivity, how a mind interacts with the world, into four distinct parts.", "tokens": [51273, 1407, 1223, 264, 4330, 295, 4363, 7318, 11, 3235, 4105, 9857, 760, 264, 3410, 295, 3983, 4253, 11, 577, 257, 1575, 43582, 365, 264, 1002, 11, 666, 1451, 10644, 3166, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 279716, "start": 2824.06, "end": 2825.16, "text": " The acronym is PRMO.", "tokens": [51710, 440, 39195, 307, 11568, 18976, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1484413799057659, "compression_ratio": 1.5566037735849056, "no_speech_prob": 2.2623936144633428e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 282516, "start": 2825.16, "end": 2826.02, "text": " P-R-M-O.", "tokens": [50365, 430, 12, 49, 12, 44, 12, 46, 13, 50408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 282516, "start": 2826.2799999999997, "end": 2827.2599999999998, "text": " P-R-M-O.", "tokens": [50421, 430, 12, 49, 12, 44, 12, 46, 13, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 282516, "start": 2827.3199999999997, "end": 2828.12, "text": " Let's break those down.", "tokens": [50473, 961, 311, 1821, 729, 760, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 282516, "start": 2828.2999999999997, "end": 2829.52, "text": " P stands for perception.", "tokens": [50522, 430, 7382, 337, 12860, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 282516, "start": 2829.7799999999997, "end": 2831.2999999999997, "text": " This is raw sensory input.", "tokens": [50596, 639, 307, 8936, 27233, 4846, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 282516, "start": 2831.7599999999998, "end": 2834.8599999999997, "text": " Photons hitting the retina, sound waves vibrating the eardrum.", "tokens": [50695, 13919, 892, 8850, 264, 1533, 1426, 11, 1626, 9417, 47748, 264, 308, 515, 6247, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 282516, "start": 2835.04, "end": 2836.18, "text": " Okay, P is perception.", "tokens": [50859, 1033, 11, 430, 307, 12860, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 282516, "start": 2836.3799999999997, "end": 2837.98, "text": " R stands for representation.", "tokens": [50926, 497, 7382, 337, 10290, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 282516, "start": 2838.8199999999997, "end": 2843.06, "text": " This is the manipulation of symbols, language, syntax, and internal models.", "tokens": [51048, 639, 307, 264, 26475, 295, 16944, 11, 2856, 11, 28431, 11, 293, 6920, 5245, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 282516, "start": 2843.7599999999998, "end": 2844.8599999999997, "text": " M stands for meaning.", "tokens": [51295, 376, 7382, 337, 3620, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 282516, "start": 2845.48, "end": 2851.44, "text": " This is the contextual, lived understanding of those symbols, knowing why a word matters, not just what it is.", "tokens": [51381, 639, 307, 264, 35526, 11, 5152, 3701, 295, 729, 16944, 11, 5276, 983, 257, 1349, 7001, 11, 406, 445, 437, 309, 307, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 282516, "start": 2851.56, "end": 2851.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51685, 1779, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21382660498985878, "compression_ratio": 1.696, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204254935762833e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 285166, "start": 2851.66, "end": 2855.7, "text": " And O stands for the real, the actual objective physical world outside the mind.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 422, 7382, 337, 264, 957, 11, 264, 3539, 10024, 4001, 1002, 2380, 264, 1575, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1411661894425102, "compression_ratio": 1.5360824742268042, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485529083677287e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 285166, "start": 2855.8799999999997, "end": 2858.52, "text": " Okay, perception, representation, meaning, and the real.", "tokens": [50576, 1033, 11, 12860, 11, 10290, 11, 3620, 11, 293, 264, 957, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1411661894425102, "compression_ratio": 1.5360824742268042, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485529083677287e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 285166, "start": 2859.2, "end": 2863.02, "text": " Where do our current massive AI models sit in that framework?", "tokens": [50742, 2305, 360, 527, 2190, 5994, 7318, 5245, 1394, 294, 300, 8388, 30, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1411661894425102, "compression_ratio": 1.5360824742268042, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485529083677287e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 285166, "start": 2863.2599999999998, "end": 2867.2999999999997, "text": " Current LLMs operate almost entirely and exclusively in the R representation.", "tokens": [50945, 15629, 441, 43, 26386, 9651, 1920, 7696, 293, 20638, 294, 264, 497, 10290, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1411661894425102, "compression_ratio": 1.5360824742268042, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485529083677287e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 285166, "start": 2867.62, "end": 2868.2, "text": " Just representation.", "tokens": [51163, 1449, 10290, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1411661894425102, "compression_ratio": 1.5360824742268042, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485529083677287e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 286820, "start": 2868.2, "end": 2871.8599999999997, "text": " They are astonishingly good at manipulating symbolic abstractions.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 35264, 356, 665, 412, 40805, 25755, 12649, 626, 13, 50548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 286820, "start": 2872.2999999999997, "end": 2875.3999999999996, "text": " They can predict the next word in a sentence with terrifying fluency.", "tokens": [50570, 814, 393, 6069, 264, 958, 1349, 294, 257, 8174, 365, 18106, 5029, 3020, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 286820, "start": 2875.96, "end": 2877.74, "text": " But they have zero true perception.", "tokens": [50753, 583, 436, 362, 4018, 2074, 12860, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 286820, "start": 2878.3399999999997, "end": 2879.5, "text": " They don't feel the world.", "tokens": [50872, 814, 500, 380, 841, 264, 1002, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 286820, "start": 2879.8799999999997, "end": 2881.24, "text": " They have no genuine meaning.", "tokens": [50949, 814, 362, 572, 16699, 3620, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 286820, "start": 2881.58, "end": 2883.46, "text": " They don't understand context or consequence.", "tokens": [51034, 814, 500, 380, 1223, 4319, 420, 18326, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 286820, "start": 2884.12, "end": 2887.3999999999996, "text": " And they have absolutely no direct triangulation with the real.", "tokens": [51161, 400, 436, 362, 3122, 572, 2047, 19335, 2776, 365, 264, 957, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 286820, "start": 2887.68, "end": 2889.8399999999997, "text": " They are floating in a void of pure syntax.", "tokens": [51339, 814, 366, 12607, 294, 257, 22009, 295, 6075, 28431, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21433912297730806, "compression_ratio": 1.6508620689655173, "no_speech_prob": 1.9054436847798506e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 288984, "start": 2889.84, "end": 2891.5, "text": " So what is the danger there?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 437, 307, 264, 4330, 456, 30, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 288984, "start": 2891.58, "end": 2893.8, "text": " Is it just that they confidently hallucinate facts?", "tokens": [50452, 1119, 309, 445, 300, 436, 41956, 35212, 13923, 9130, 30, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 288984, "start": 2893.88, "end": 2894.84, "text": " We see that all the time.", "tokens": [50567, 492, 536, 300, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 288984, "start": 2895.06, "end": 2896.5, "text": " Hallucination is just a symptom.", "tokens": [50626, 5434, 1311, 2486, 307, 445, 257, 29370, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 288984, "start": 2897.08, "end": 2903.34, "text": " The terrifying existential risk fliction identifies is something called machine-only coherence.", "tokens": [50727, 440, 18106, 37133, 3148, 932, 4105, 34597, 307, 746, 1219, 3479, 12, 25202, 26528, 655, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 288984, "start": 2903.44, "end": 2904.86, "text": " Machine-only coherence.", "tokens": [51045, 22155, 12, 25202, 26528, 655, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 288984, "start": 2904.94, "end": 2910.86, "text": " Imagine a near-future network where highly advanced AI agents are communicating with each other millions of times a second.", "tokens": [51120, 11739, 257, 2651, 12, 69, 325, 540, 3209, 689, 5405, 7339, 7318, 12554, 366, 17559, 365, 1184, 661, 6803, 295, 1413, 257, 1150, 13, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527208774647814, "compression_ratio": 1.602510460251046, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656435767262392e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 291086, "start": 2910.86, "end": 2921.0, "text": " Because they lack meaning and a tether to the real world, they start coordinating and stabilizing their own definitions of reality entirely amongst themselves without any human input.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 436, 5011, 3620, 293, 257, 256, 1666, 281, 264, 957, 1002, 11, 436, 722, 37824, 293, 11652, 3319, 641, 1065, 21988, 295, 4103, 7696, 12918, 2969, 1553, 604, 1952, 4846, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08375205207116825, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907935113443575e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 291086, "start": 2921.32, "end": 2928.8, "text": " An entire ecosystem of superintelligent algorithms agreeing on a version of reality that has absolutely nothing to do with physics or humanity.", "tokens": [50888, 1107, 2302, 11311, 295, 1687, 20761, 25002, 14642, 36900, 322, 257, 3037, 295, 4103, 300, 575, 3122, 1825, 281, 360, 365, 10649, 420, 10243, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08375205207116825, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907935113443575e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 291086, "start": 2929.1200000000003, "end": 2929.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51278, 1079, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08375205207116825, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907935113443575e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 291086, "start": 2929.7000000000003, "end": 2937.34, "text": " They form a self-consistent, closed loop that is functionally opaque to us and completely uncoupled from human well-being.", "tokens": [51307, 814, 1254, 257, 2698, 12, 21190, 25367, 11, 5395, 6367, 300, 307, 2445, 379, 42687, 281, 505, 293, 2584, 6219, 263, 15551, 490, 1952, 731, 12, 13054, 13, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08375205207116825, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.8907935113443575e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 293734, "start": 2937.34, "end": 2942.46, "text": " It is the ultimate drop of the rho coefficient down to absolute zero.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 3270, 295, 264, 20293, 17619, 760, 281, 8236, 4018, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 293734, "start": 2943.28, "end": 2943.96, "text": " That's terrifying.", "tokens": [50662, 663, 311, 18106, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 293734, "start": 2944.08, "end": 2949.28, "text": " To prevent this, Flitschin proposes a radical architectural constraint called quadrangulation.", "tokens": [50702, 1407, 4871, 341, 11, 3235, 1208, 32167, 2365, 4201, 257, 12001, 26621, 25534, 1219, 10787, 32926, 2776, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 293734, "start": 2949.76, "end": 2950.2400000000002, "text": " Quadrangulation.", "tokens": [50986, 29619, 32926, 2776, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 293734, "start": 2950.34, "end": 2953.42, "text": " Normally we talk about triangulation, like two people looking at a tree and a green.", "tokens": [51015, 17424, 321, 751, 466, 19335, 2776, 11, 411, 732, 561, 1237, 412, 257, 4230, 293, 257, 3092, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 293734, "start": 2953.54, "end": 2954.34, "text": " Yes, that is a tree.", "tokens": [51175, 1079, 11, 300, 307, 257, 4230, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 293734, "start": 2955.0, "end": 2955.78, "text": " Triangulating effect.", "tokens": [51248, 10931, 656, 12162, 1802, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 293734, "start": 2955.92, "end": 2958.34, "text": " What is the fourth point in quadrangulation?", "tokens": [51294, 708, 307, 264, 6409, 935, 294, 10787, 32926, 2776, 30, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 293734, "start": 2958.6000000000004, "end": 2961.96, "text": " The fourth point is a mandated, specific human being.", "tokens": [51428, 440, 6409, 935, 307, 257, 47563, 11, 2685, 1952, 885, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 293734, "start": 2962.7400000000002, "end": 2967.26, "text": " Quadrangulation is a formal, hard-coded constraint built into the digital architecture.", "tokens": [51635, 29619, 32926, 2776, 307, 257, 9860, 11, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 25534, 3094, 666, 264, 4562, 9482, 13, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15650401482215295, "compression_ratio": 1.7881944444444444, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492042106963645e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 296734, "start": 2967.34, "end": 2980.5, "text": " It states that any output from an AI system, any stabilization of meaning between machines, must formally remain within a mathematically bounded distance of a specific, verifiable human participant's perspective.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4368, 300, 604, 5598, 490, 364, 7318, 1185, 11, 604, 35476, 295, 3620, 1296, 8379, 11, 1633, 25983, 6222, 1951, 257, 44003, 37498, 4560, 295, 257, 2685, 11, 1306, 30876, 1952, 24950, 311, 4585, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10588259775130475, "compression_ratio": 1.47979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961679878499616e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 296734, "start": 2980.7400000000002, "end": 2984.48, "text": " Wait, so you literally hard-code a tether between the AI and a biological human?", "tokens": [51035, 3802, 11, 370, 291, 3736, 1152, 12, 22332, 257, 256, 1666, 1296, 264, 7318, 293, 257, 13910, 1952, 30, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10588259775130475, "compression_ratio": 1.47979797979798, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961679878499616e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 298448, "start": 2984.48, "end": 2985.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12836468787420363, "compression_ratio": 1.5573770491803278, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715612806896047e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 298448, "start": 2985.6, "end": 2989.1, "text": " The AI is not allowed to close the loop of meaning on its own.", "tokens": [50421, 440, 7318, 307, 406, 4350, 281, 1998, 264, 6367, 295, 3620, 322, 1080, 1065, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12836468787420363, "compression_ratio": 1.5573770491803278, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715612806896047e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 298448, "start": 2989.62, "end": 2999.7, "text": " If the AI agents in the network start drifting too far from the human anchor, if the conceptual distance exceeds a certain threshold, the stabilization process is considered architecturally invalid.", "tokens": [50622, 759, 264, 7318, 12554, 294, 264, 3209, 722, 37973, 886, 1400, 490, 264, 1952, 18487, 11, 498, 264, 24106, 4560, 43305, 257, 1629, 14678, 11, 264, 35476, 1399, 307, 4888, 6331, 6512, 34702, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12836468787420363, "compression_ratio": 1.5573770491803278, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715612806896047e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 298448, "start": 3000.04, "end": 3000.92, "text": " So it just shuts down.", "tokens": [51143, 407, 309, 445, 48590, 760, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12836468787420363, "compression_ratio": 1.5573770491803278, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715612806896047e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 298448, "start": 3001.1, "end": 3005.56, "text": " The system forcefully reopens the interpretive process and demands human intervention.", "tokens": [51196, 440, 1185, 3464, 2277, 28994, 694, 264, 7302, 488, 1399, 293, 15107, 1952, 13176, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12836468787420363, "compression_ratio": 1.5573770491803278, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715612806896047e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 300556, "start": 3005.56, "end": 3014.58, "text": " The AI cannot legally, mathematically, or architecturally conclude a process without checking in with the physical reality of a human mind.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7318, 2644, 21106, 11, 44003, 11, 420, 6331, 6512, 16886, 257, 1399, 1553, 8568, 294, 365, 264, 4001, 4103, 295, 257, 1952, 1575, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13443247047630516, "compression_ratio": 1.5893719806763285, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970791513557185e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 300556, "start": 3014.7599999999998, "end": 3015.7999999999997, "text": " That is profound.", "tokens": [50825, 663, 307, 14382, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13443247047630516, "compression_ratio": 1.5893719806763285, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970791513557185e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 300556, "start": 3016.12, "end": 3022.02, "text": " Forcing the digital world, at a foundational level, to remain permanently tethered to the physical human.", "tokens": [50893, 1171, 2175, 264, 4562, 1002, 11, 412, 257, 32195, 1496, 11, 281, 6222, 24042, 256, 1666, 292, 281, 264, 4001, 1952, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13443247047630516, "compression_ratio": 1.5893719806763285, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970791513557185e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 300556, "start": 3023.2, "end": 3026.2599999999998, "text": " But let's take that concept of physical reality one step further.", "tokens": [51247, 583, 718, 311, 747, 300, 3410, 295, 4001, 4103, 472, 1823, 3052, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13443247047630516, "compression_ratio": 1.5893719806763285, "no_speech_prob": 1.9970791513557185e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 302626, "start": 3026.26, "end": 3035.1800000000003, "text": " Because the fifth and final section of Flixian's research, titled Radiative Switch Computation, asks a question that genuinely blew my mind.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 9266, 293, 2572, 3541, 295, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 2132, 11, 19841, 37806, 1166, 13893, 37804, 399, 11, 8962, 257, 1168, 300, 17839, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10455861503695264, "compression_ratio": 1.497854077253219, "no_speech_prob": 3.3440524654926307e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 302626, "start": 3035.46, "end": 3036.6800000000003, "text": " This is where it all comes together.", "tokens": [50825, 639, 307, 689, 309, 439, 1487, 1214, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10455861503695264, "compression_ratio": 1.497854077253219, "no_speech_prob": 3.3440524654926307e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 302626, "start": 3036.86, "end": 3043.44, "text": " Up until now, this whole deep dive has been about how we force digital silicon systems to look back at physical reality.", "tokens": [50895, 5858, 1826, 586, 11, 341, 1379, 2452, 9192, 575, 668, 466, 577, 321, 3464, 4562, 22848, 3652, 281, 574, 646, 412, 4001, 4103, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10455861503695264, "compression_ratio": 1.497854077253219, "no_speech_prob": 3.3440524654926307e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 302626, "start": 3043.78, "end": 3045.9, "text": " But what if the physical reality was the computer?", "tokens": [51241, 583, 437, 498, 264, 4001, 4103, 390, 264, 3820, 30, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10455861503695264, "compression_ratio": 1.497854077253219, "no_speech_prob": 3.3440524654926307e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 304590, "start": 3045.9, "end": 3050.88, "text": " This is the climax of Flixian's work, where they introduced the concept of xylomorphic computation.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 264, 41329, 295, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 589, 11, 689, 436, 7268, 264, 3410, 295, 2031, 5088, 32702, 299, 24903, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 304590, "start": 3051.38, "end": 3056.52, "text": " The word comes from the Greek xylon, meaning wood or matter, and morphy, meaning form.", "tokens": [50639, 440, 1349, 1487, 490, 264, 10281, 2031, 34926, 11, 3620, 4576, 420, 1871, 11, 293, 1896, 15680, 11, 3620, 1254, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 304590, "start": 3056.78, "end": 3057.6600000000003, "text": " Matter and form.", "tokens": [50909, 20285, 293, 1254, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 304590, "start": 3057.8, "end": 3058.14, "text": " Wood form.", "tokens": [50960, 11558, 1254, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 304590, "start": 3058.2200000000003, "end": 3058.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50981, 1079, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 304590, "start": 3058.84, "end": 3068.7200000000003, "text": " Xylomorphic computation is a system where the physical substrate, the mathematical computation being performed, and the actual physical function in the real world are utterly, indivisibly inseparable.", "tokens": [51012, 1783, 5088, 32702, 299, 24903, 307, 257, 1185, 689, 264, 4001, 27585, 11, 264, 18894, 24903, 885, 10332, 11, 293, 264, 3539, 4001, 2445, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 366, 30251, 11, 1016, 592, 271, 3545, 33874, 42012, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 304590, "start": 3069.08, "end": 3069.34, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51524, 1033, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 304590, "start": 3069.6600000000003, "end": 3074.1800000000003, "text": " To understand this, we have to look at how non-xylomorphic our current computers are.", "tokens": [51553, 1407, 1223, 341, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 577, 2107, 12, 87, 5088, 32702, 299, 527, 2190, 10807, 366, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1303038163618608, "compression_ratio": 1.7716262975778547, "no_speech_prob": 2.708127559009066e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 307418, "start": 3074.18, "end": 3076.7, "text": " Think about the laptop sitting on your desk.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 10732, 3798, 322, 428, 10026, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 307418, "start": 3076.7799999999997, "end": 3077.66, "text": " Okay, my laptop.", "tokens": [50495, 1033, 11, 452, 10732, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 307418, "start": 3078.12, "end": 3080.7599999999998, "text": " It has a silicon chip, a battery, a screen.", "tokens": [50562, 467, 575, 257, 22848, 11409, 11, 257, 5809, 11, 257, 2568, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 307418, "start": 3081.06, "end": 3081.4199999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50709, 1779, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 307418, "start": 3081.96, "end": 3085.12, "text": " Your laptop is fundamentally disconnected from its physical environment.", "tokens": [50754, 2260, 10732, 307, 17879, 29426, 490, 1080, 4001, 2823, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 307418, "start": 3085.8799999999997, "end": 3092.46, "text": " If you open a massive spreadsheet and run a complex calculation, the processor works incredibly hard.", "tokens": [50950, 759, 291, 1269, 257, 5994, 27733, 293, 1190, 257, 3997, 17108, 11, 264, 15321, 1985, 6252, 1152, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 307418, "start": 3092.96, "end": 3095.7799999999997, "text": " It generates physical heat as a waste byproduct.", "tokens": [51304, 467, 23815, 4001, 3738, 382, 257, 5964, 538, 33244, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 307418, "start": 3095.8999999999996, "end": 3097.0, "text": " Sure, the fan kicks on.", "tokens": [51451, 4894, 11, 264, 3429, 21293, 322, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 307418, "start": 3097.16, "end": 3100.2999999999997, "text": " But the silicon chip does not care what the spreadsheet says.", "tokens": [51514, 583, 264, 22848, 11409, 775, 406, 1127, 437, 264, 27733, 1619, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15696180434454055, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.567401482042985e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 310030, "start": 3100.3, "end": 3104.7000000000003, "text": " It doesn't care if it's calculating a cure for cancer or rendering a video game.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 1127, 498, 309, 311, 28258, 257, 13698, 337, 5592, 420, 22407, 257, 960, 1216, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 310030, "start": 3105.1800000000003, "end": 3108.54, "text": " The physics of the chip and the logic of the software are separate layers.", "tokens": [50609, 440, 10649, 295, 264, 11409, 293, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 4722, 366, 4994, 7914, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 310030, "start": 3109.0800000000004, "end": 3111.28, "text": " The heat is just garbage to be fanned away.", "tokens": [50804, 440, 3738, 307, 445, 14150, 281, 312, 283, 5943, 1314, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 310030, "start": 3111.48, "end": 3113.54, "text": " The hardware is just a dumb vessel for the software.", "tokens": [50924, 440, 8837, 307, 445, 257, 10316, 18098, 337, 264, 4722, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 310030, "start": 3113.7000000000003, "end": 3114.1000000000004, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51035, 7587, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 310030, "start": 3114.46, "end": 3119.36, "text": " But Flitsheen points to a real-world xylomorphic device to show us an alternative.", "tokens": [51073, 583, 3235, 1208, 42276, 2793, 281, 257, 957, 12, 13217, 2031, 5088, 32702, 299, 4302, 281, 855, 505, 364, 8535, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 310030, "start": 3120.0600000000004, "end": 3122.44, "text": " It is called a PCM radiative switch.", "tokens": [51353, 467, 307, 1219, 257, 6465, 44, 16335, 1166, 3679, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13415917983421913, "compression_ratio": 1.5614754098360655, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251238856886506e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 312244, "start": 3122.44, "end": 3127.98, "text": " Imagine a small square tile that you install on the exterior roof or the wall of a building.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 257, 1359, 3732, 20590, 300, 291, 3625, 322, 264, 20677, 8418, 420, 264, 2929, 295, 257, 2390, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 312244, "start": 3128.32, "end": 3133.84, "text": " Inside this tile is a layer of phase change material, specifically hexadecane wax.", "tokens": [50659, 15123, 341, 20590, 307, 257, 4583, 295, 5574, 1319, 2527, 11, 4682, 23291, 762, 66, 1929, 17352, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 312244, "start": 3134.02, "end": 3135.2200000000003, "text": " Okay, hexadecane wax.", "tokens": [50944, 1033, 11, 23291, 762, 66, 1929, 17352, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 312244, "start": 3135.58, "end": 3137.28, "text": " Why that specific material?", "tokens": [51022, 1545, 300, 2685, 2527, 30, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 312244, "start": 3137.62, "end": 3140.5, "text": " Because hexadecane wax has a very specific melting point.", "tokens": [51124, 1436, 23291, 762, 66, 1929, 17352, 575, 257, 588, 2685, 20493, 935, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 312244, "start": 3141.18, "end": 3145.28, "text": " About 18 degrees Celsius, which is right around 65 degrees Fahrenheit.", "tokens": [51302, 7769, 2443, 5310, 22658, 11, 597, 307, 558, 926, 11624, 5310, 31199, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 312244, "start": 3145.68, "end": 3148.84, "text": " It is basically the threshold of a comfortable room temperature.", "tokens": [51527, 467, 307, 1936, 264, 14678, 295, 257, 4619, 1808, 4292, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 312244, "start": 3149.1, "end": 3150.14, "text": " All right, so 18 degrees.", "tokens": [51698, 1057, 558, 11, 370, 2443, 5310, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1687596525464739, "compression_ratio": 1.6729323308270676, "no_speech_prob": 1.377634876835454e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 315014, "start": 3150.14, "end": 3153.2799999999997, "text": " Now, attached to this wax is a louver.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 8570, 281, 341, 17352, 307, 257, 15185, 331, 13, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 315014, "start": 3154.08, "end": 3156.12, "text": " Think of a single slot of a window blind.", "tokens": [50562, 6557, 295, 257, 2167, 14747, 295, 257, 4910, 6865, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 315014, "start": 3156.8599999999997, "end": 3160.54, "text": " The lever is painted black on one side to absorb heat from the sun,", "tokens": [50701, 440, 12451, 307, 11797, 2211, 322, 472, 1252, 281, 15631, 3738, 490, 264, 3295, 11, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 315014, "start": 3160.7599999999998, "end": 3165.74, "text": " and painted highly reflective white on the other side to radiate heat away into the sky.", "tokens": [50896, 293, 11797, 5405, 28931, 2418, 322, 264, 661, 1252, 281, 2843, 13024, 3738, 1314, 666, 264, 5443, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 315014, "start": 3165.8199999999997, "end": 3166.72, "text": " Okay, I have the picture.", "tokens": [51149, 1033, 11, 286, 362, 264, 3036, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 315014, "start": 3167.2, "end": 3169.62, "text": " A wax tile with a flippable blind on it.", "tokens": [51218, 316, 17352, 20590, 365, 257, 932, 2488, 712, 6865, 322, 309, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 315014, "start": 3169.7799999999997, "end": 3170.7599999999998, "text": " Here's how it works.", "tokens": [51347, 1692, 311, 577, 309, 1985, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 315014, "start": 3171.2, "end": 3175.74, "text": " When the sun beats down on the building and the room temperature hits 18 degrees Celsius,", "tokens": [51418, 1133, 264, 3295, 16447, 760, 322, 264, 2390, 293, 264, 1808, 4292, 8664, 2443, 5310, 22658, 11, 51645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 315014, "start": 3176.3799999999997, "end": 3179.2, "text": " the hexadecane wax hits its phase change threshold.", "tokens": [51677, 264, 23291, 762, 66, 1929, 17352, 8664, 1080, 5574, 1319, 14678, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14581571519374847, "compression_ratio": 1.6159169550173011, "no_speech_prob": 2.3439286536003356e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 317920, "start": 3179.2, "end": 3180.54, "text": " It physically melts.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 9762, 30136, 13, 50432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 317920, "start": 3180.7599999999998, "end": 3181.74, "text": " And what happens when it melts?", "tokens": [50443, 400, 437, 2314, 562, 309, 30136, 30, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 317920, "start": 3182.14, "end": 3185.9199999999996, "text": " As it turns from solid to liquid, it expands in volume by about 10%.", "tokens": [50512, 1018, 309, 4523, 490, 5100, 281, 6553, 11, 309, 33706, 294, 5523, 538, 466, 1266, 6856, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 317920, "start": 3185.9199999999996, "end": 3189.4399999999996, "text": " That physical expansion pushes a tiny mechanical piston.", "tokens": [50701, 663, 4001, 11260, 21020, 257, 5870, 12070, 30002, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 317920, "start": 3189.8799999999997, "end": 3194.9199999999996, "text": " The piston pushes a lever, and the lever physically flips the louver from the black side to the white side.", "tokens": [50899, 440, 30002, 21020, 257, 12451, 11, 293, 264, 12451, 9762, 40249, 264, 15185, 331, 490, 264, 2211, 1252, 281, 264, 2418, 1252, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 317920, "start": 3195.46, "end": 3198.66, "text": " Suddenly, the tile is reflecting heat away, cooling the building down.", "tokens": [51178, 21194, 11, 264, 20590, 307, 23543, 3738, 1314, 11, 14785, 264, 2390, 760, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13637069175983296, "compression_ratio": 1.63013698630137, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051561543637074e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 319866, "start": 3198.66, "end": 3199.68, "text": " And when it gets cold.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 562, 309, 2170, 3554, 13, 50416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13346566858979844, "compression_ratio": 1.521186440677966, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281913747280164e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 319866, "start": 3200.0, "end": 3203.7799999999997, "text": " When the temperature drops below 18 degrees, the wax solidifies.", "tokens": [50432, 1133, 264, 4292, 11438, 2507, 2443, 5310, 11, 264, 17352, 5100, 11221, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13346566858979844, "compression_ratio": 1.521186440677966, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281913747280164e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 319866, "start": 3204.3799999999997, "end": 3212.08, "text": " It shrinks, the piston retracts, and the louver flips back to the black side, absorbing the sun's heat to warm the building.", "tokens": [50651, 467, 9884, 16431, 11, 264, 30002, 41107, 82, 11, 293, 264, 15185, 331, 40249, 646, 281, 264, 2211, 1252, 11, 38720, 264, 3295, 311, 3738, 281, 4561, 264, 2390, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13346566858979844, "compression_ratio": 1.521186440677966, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281913747280164e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 319866, "start": 3212.44, "end": 3218.3599999999997, "text": " Now, I have to push back here, because while that is a very neat mechanical trick, isn't that just a smart thermostat?", "tokens": [51054, 823, 11, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 510, 11, 570, 1339, 300, 307, 257, 588, 10654, 12070, 4282, 11, 1943, 380, 300, 445, 257, 4069, 8810, 39036, 30, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13346566858979844, "compression_ratio": 1.521186440677966, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281913747280164e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 319866, "start": 3218.8599999999997, "end": 3220.02, "text": " I know, it sounds like one.", "tokens": [51375, 286, 458, 11, 309, 3263, 411, 472, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13346566858979844, "compression_ratio": 1.521186440677966, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281913747280164e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 322002, "start": 3220.02, "end": 3223.64, "text": " I mean, I have a smart thermostat in my hallway that does the exact same thing.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 286, 362, 257, 4069, 8810, 39036, 294, 452, 23903, 300, 775, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15460740818696864, "compression_ratio": 1.4470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.604572703005347e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 322002, "start": 3223.82, "end": 3225.7599999999998, "text": " It turns the AC on when it gets hot.", "tokens": [50555, 467, 4523, 264, 8157, 322, 562, 309, 2170, 2368, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15460740818696864, "compression_ratio": 1.4470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.604572703005347e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 322002, "start": 3226.34, "end": 3228.52, "text": " How is this wax tile a computer?", "tokens": [50681, 1012, 307, 341, 17352, 20590, 257, 3820, 30, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15460740818696864, "compression_ratio": 1.4470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.604572703005347e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 322002, "start": 3228.94, "end": 3232.06, "text": " That is the critical paradigm-shifting distinction.", "tokens": [50811, 663, 307, 264, 4924, 24709, 12, 2716, 10106, 16844, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15460740818696864, "compression_ratio": 1.4470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.604572703005347e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 322002, "start": 3232.7599999999998, "end": 3235.36, "text": " Your smart thermostat is heavily abstracted.", "tokens": [51002, 2260, 4069, 8810, 39036, 307, 10950, 12649, 292, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15460740818696864, "compression_ratio": 1.4470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.604572703005347e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 323536, "start": 3235.36, "end": 3238.04, "text": " It has a digital thermometer that reads the room.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 575, 257, 4562, 42539, 300, 15700, 264, 1808, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 323536, "start": 3238.3, "end": 3243.88, "text": " It has an analog-to-digital converter that translates that physical temperature into a symbolic piece of data.", "tokens": [50512, 467, 575, 364, 16660, 12, 1353, 12, 25259, 1686, 33905, 300, 28468, 300, 4001, 4292, 666, 257, 25755, 2522, 295, 1412, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 323536, "start": 3244.6200000000003, "end": 3250.1200000000003, "text": " It has a silicon microprocessor that runs a software algorithm to compare that data to a target number.", "tokens": [50828, 467, 575, 257, 22848, 3123, 1513, 340, 25432, 300, 6676, 257, 4722, 9284, 281, 6794, 300, 1412, 281, 257, 3779, 1230, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 323536, "start": 3250.58, "end": 3255.0, "text": " And finally, it sends an electrical signal to a relay to turn on an HVAC motor.", "tokens": [51126, 400, 2721, 11, 309, 14790, 364, 12147, 6358, 281, 257, 24214, 281, 1261, 322, 364, 389, 53, 4378, 5932, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 323536, "start": 3255.5, "end": 3257.6, "text": " It is a massive chain of representations.", "tokens": [51372, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 5021, 295, 33358, 13, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 323536, "start": 3258.2000000000003, "end": 3260.28, "text": " The thermostat is thinking about reality.", "tokens": [51507, 440, 8810, 39036, 307, 1953, 466, 4103, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 323536, "start": 3260.46, "end": 3260.7400000000002, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [51620, 2438, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 323536, "start": 3261.06, "end": 3264.1800000000003, "text": " It's translating reality into math and then back into reality.", "tokens": [51650, 467, 311, 35030, 4103, 666, 5221, 293, 550, 646, 666, 4103, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 323536, "start": 3264.54, "end": 3264.9, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51824, 1079, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15166914367675782, "compression_ratio": 1.7361111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956308760916137e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 326536, "start": 3265.36, "end": 3268.76, "text": " But in the radiative switch, there is no digital controller.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 264, 16335, 1166, 3679, 11, 456, 307, 572, 4562, 10561, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 326536, "start": 3269.36, "end": 3270.48, "text": " There is no software.", "tokens": [50565, 821, 307, 572, 4722, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 326536, "start": 3270.78, "end": 3272.08, "text": " There is no line of code.", "tokens": [50636, 821, 307, 572, 1622, 295, 3089, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 326536, "start": 3272.4, "end": 3274.94, "text": " There is no sensor separate from the actuator.", "tokens": [50717, 821, 307, 572, 10200, 4994, 490, 264, 34964, 1639, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 326536, "start": 3275.1, "end": 3275.6, "text": " Wait, wait.", "tokens": [50852, 3802, 11, 1699, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 326536, "start": 3275.6800000000003, "end": 3278.34, "text": " The melting wax is the sensor detecting the heat.", "tokens": [50881, 440, 20493, 17352, 307, 264, 10200, 40237, 264, 3738, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 326536, "start": 3278.34, "end": 3280.02, "text": " It is the memory storing the state.", "tokens": [51014, 467, 307, 264, 4675, 26085, 264, 1785, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 326536, "start": 3280.38, "end": 3282.2400000000002, "text": " And it is the actuator pushing the louver.", "tokens": [51116, 400, 309, 307, 264, 34964, 1639, 7380, 264, 15185, 331, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 326536, "start": 3283.04, "end": 3289.2000000000003, "text": " The control loop isn't world translates to sensor, translates to processor, translates to actuator.", "tokens": [51249, 440, 1969, 6367, 1943, 380, 1002, 28468, 281, 10200, 11, 28468, 281, 15321, 11, 28468, 281, 34964, 1639, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 326536, "start": 3289.32, "end": 3289.96, "text": " It's all one thing.", "tokens": [51563, 467, 311, 439, 472, 551, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 326536, "start": 3290.2200000000003, "end": 3293.6800000000003, "text": " The lube is completely collapsed down to its barest physical essence.", "tokens": [51608, 440, 287, 1977, 307, 2584, 24578, 760, 281, 1080, 6949, 372, 4001, 12801, 13, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575571890095718, "compression_ratio": 1.8910505836575875, "no_speech_prob": 1.825312036934923e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 329368, "start": 3293.68, "end": 3298.08, "text": " World leads directly to material state, which immediately alters the world.", "tokens": [50365, 3937, 6689, 3838, 281, 2527, 1785, 11, 597, 4258, 419, 1559, 264, 1002, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152969837188721, "compression_ratio": 1.056338028169014, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428694563265899e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 329808, "start": 3298.08, "end": 3301.7, "text": " The heating and the cooling of the wax is the computation itself.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15082, 293, 264, 14785, 295, 264, 17352, 307, 264, 24903, 2564, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1501744634964887, "compression_ratio": 1.0833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145525249932954e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 330170, "start": 3301.7, "end": 3304.2999999999997, "text": " The hardware and the software are the exact same thing.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8837, 293, 264, 4722, 366, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15772507985432943, "compression_ratio": 1.5064102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393539729516517e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 330170, "start": 3304.96, "end": 3306.54, "text": " But how do you scale that up?", "tokens": [50528, 583, 577, 360, 291, 4373, 300, 493, 30, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15772507985432943, "compression_ratio": 1.5064102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393539729516517e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 330170, "start": 3306.8799999999997, "end": 3309.18, "text": " A single flippable blind is a switch.", "tokens": [50624, 316, 2167, 932, 2488, 712, 6865, 307, 257, 3679, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15772507985432943, "compression_ratio": 1.5064102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393539729516517e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 330170, "start": 3309.48, "end": 3314.3399999999997, "text": " But how do you turn a wall of wax into something that can actually process complex information like a computer?", "tokens": [50754, 583, 577, 360, 291, 1261, 257, 2929, 295, 17352, 666, 746, 300, 393, 767, 1399, 3997, 1589, 411, 257, 3820, 30, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15772507985432943, "compression_ratio": 1.5064102564102564, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393539729516517e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 331434, "start": 3314.34, "end": 3316.1000000000004, "text": " You build a field of them.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 1322, 257, 2519, 295, 552, 13, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 331434, "start": 3316.54, "end": 3320.1400000000003, "text": " You tile the entire side of a skyscraper with thousands of these switches.", "tokens": [50475, 509, 20590, 264, 2302, 1252, 295, 257, 48227, 39302, 610, 365, 5383, 295, 613, 19458, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 331434, "start": 3320.7000000000003, "end": 3322.04, "text": " But you don't make them all identical.", "tokens": [50683, 583, 291, 500, 380, 652, 552, 439, 14800, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 331434, "start": 3322.96, "end": 3327.1600000000003, "text": " You introduce what Fliction calls heterogeneous thresholds.", "tokens": [50796, 509, 5366, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 20789, 31112, 14678, 82, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 331434, "start": 3327.52, "end": 3330.58, "text": " You use slightly different chemical mixtures of wax.", "tokens": [51024, 509, 764, 4748, 819, 7313, 2752, 37610, 295, 17352, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 331434, "start": 3330.96, "end": 3334.34, "text": " Some tiles melt at 16 degrees, some at 18 degrees, some at 20 degrees.", "tokens": [51196, 2188, 21982, 10083, 412, 3165, 5310, 11, 512, 412, 2443, 5310, 11, 512, 412, 945, 5310, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 331434, "start": 3334.6800000000003, "end": 3338.92, "text": " You distribute them strategically across the wall based on shade and sun exposure.", "tokens": [51382, 509, 20594, 552, 38061, 2108, 264, 2929, 2361, 322, 11466, 293, 3295, 10420, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2113577651977539, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213656293615706e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 333892, "start": 3338.92, "end": 3341.3, "text": " So different parts of the wall activate at different times.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 819, 3166, 295, 264, 2929, 13615, 412, 819, 1413, 13, 50484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 333892, "start": 3341.42, "end": 3341.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50490, 7587, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 333892, "start": 3342.4, "end": 3344.0, "text": " Then you utilize hysteresis.", "tokens": [50539, 1396, 291, 16117, 35915, 9374, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 333892, "start": 3344.58, "end": 3352.46, "text": " Hysteresis is the natural physical lag between the temperature at which the wax melts and the slightly lower temperature at which it freezes solid again.", "tokens": [50648, 5701, 3120, 9374, 307, 264, 3303, 4001, 8953, 1296, 264, 4292, 412, 597, 264, 17352, 30136, 293, 264, 4748, 3126, 4292, 412, 597, 309, 1737, 12214, 5100, 797, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 333892, "start": 3352.58, "end": 3354.7000000000003, "text": " So it doesn't just instantly flip back and forth.", "tokens": [51048, 407, 309, 1177, 380, 445, 13518, 7929, 646, 293, 5220, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 333892, "start": 3354.82, "end": 3355.1, "text": " No.", "tokens": [51160, 883, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 333892, "start": 3355.26, "end": 3360.76, "text": " That gap, that physical delay, acts as a form of short-term material memory for the system.", "tokens": [51182, 663, 7417, 11, 300, 4001, 8577, 11, 10672, 382, 257, 1254, 295, 2099, 12, 7039, 2527, 4675, 337, 264, 1185, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 333892, "start": 3361.2400000000002, "end": 3362.96, "text": " And finally, you couple them locally.", "tokens": [51481, 400, 2721, 11, 291, 1916, 552, 16143, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1500612011662236, "compression_ratio": 1.6477272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750168960188994e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 336296, "start": 3362.96, "end": 3370.08, "text": " The tiles share heat with each other through physical conduction, and they exchange heat radiatively across the surface of the building.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 21982, 2073, 3738, 365, 1184, 661, 807, 4001, 43842, 11, 293, 436, 7742, 3738, 16335, 19020, 2108, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 2390, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694779889336948, "compression_ratio": 1.6422413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810500895972583e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 336296, "start": 3370.28, "end": 3377.8, "text": " So a wave of heat moves across the wall, triggering cascades of melting and flipping louvers, which then shade other louvers, changing their temperature.", "tokens": [50731, 407, 257, 5772, 295, 3738, 6067, 2108, 264, 2929, 11, 40406, 3058, 66, 2977, 295, 20493, 293, 26886, 15185, 840, 11, 597, 550, 11466, 661, 15185, 840, 11, 4473, 641, 4292, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694779889336948, "compression_ratio": 1.6422413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810500895972583e-12}, {"id": 914, "seek": 336296, "start": 3378.2, "end": 3380.52, "text": " It's a massive physical neural network.", "tokens": [51127, 467, 311, 257, 5994, 4001, 18161, 3209, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694779889336948, "compression_ratio": 1.6422413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810500895972583e-12}, {"id": 915, "seek": 336296, "start": 3380.86, "end": 3381.18, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51260, 1079, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694779889336948, "compression_ratio": 1.6422413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810500895972583e-12}, {"id": 916, "seek": 336296, "start": 3381.88, "end": 3384.68, "text": " It is computing the environment in real time.", "tokens": [51311, 467, 307, 15866, 264, 2823, 294, 957, 565, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11694779889336948, "compression_ratio": 1.6422413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.9810500895972583e-12}, {"id": 917, "seek": 338468, "start": 3384.68, "end": 3393.1, "text": " But wait, with my laptop, if I run a calculation and it spits out 2 plus 2 equals 5, the operating system throws an error code.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 365, 452, 10732, 11, 498, 286, 1190, 257, 17108, 293, 309, 637, 1208, 484, 568, 1804, 568, 6915, 1025, 11, 264, 7447, 1185, 19251, 364, 6713, 3089, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 918, "seek": 338468, "start": 3394.1, "end": 3395.16, "text": " I know it's broken.", "tokens": [50836, 286, 458, 309, 311, 5463, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 919, "seek": 338468, "start": 3395.56, "end": 3399.54, "text": " If I have a wall of melting wax, how do I know if it's computing the right answer?", "tokens": [50909, 759, 286, 362, 257, 2929, 295, 20493, 17352, 11, 577, 360, 286, 458, 498, 309, 311, 15866, 264, 558, 1867, 30, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 920, "seek": 338468, "start": 3400.04, "end": 3402.2599999999998, "text": " There is no screen to show me an error code.", "tokens": [51133, 821, 307, 572, 2568, 281, 855, 385, 364, 6713, 3089, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 921, "seek": 338468, "start": 3402.9199999999996, "end": 3410.68, "text": " To answer that, Flickchina reaches back to the founding days of cybernetics, specifically W. Ross Ashby's concept of ultra-stability.", "tokens": [51277, 1407, 1867, 300, 11, 3235, 618, 339, 1426, 14235, 646, 281, 264, 22223, 1708, 295, 13411, 7129, 1167, 11, 4682, 343, 13, 16140, 10279, 2322, 311, 3410, 295, 14808, 12, 372, 2310, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 922, "seek": 338468, "start": 3410.8599999999997, "end": 3411.3999999999996, "text": " Ultra-stability.", "tokens": [51674, 20925, 12, 372, 2310, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1325012711454029, "compression_ratio": 1.58364312267658, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622756552648777e-12}, {"id": 923, "seek": 341140, "start": 3411.4, "end": 3418.02, "text": " We have been conditioned by digital computers to believe that computation is about matching an external, pre-programmed answer key.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 668, 35833, 538, 4562, 10807, 281, 1697, 300, 24903, 307, 466, 14324, 364, 8320, 11, 659, 12, 32726, 1912, 1867, 2141, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 924, "seek": 341140, "start": 3418.42, "end": 3421.6800000000003, "text": " But the radiative switch computer isn't trying to match an answer key.", "tokens": [50716, 583, 264, 16335, 1166, 3679, 3820, 1943, 380, 1382, 281, 2995, 364, 1867, 2141, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 925, "seek": 341140, "start": 3422.02, "end": 3425.76, "text": " It is trying to maintain an admissible region of physical viability.", "tokens": [50896, 467, 307, 1382, 281, 6909, 364, 5910, 41073, 4458, 295, 4001, 1932, 2310, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 926, "seek": 341140, "start": 3425.84, "end": 3427.1800000000003, "text": " Viability, meaning survival.", "tokens": [51087, 6626, 2310, 11, 3620, 12559, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 927, "seek": 341140, "start": 3427.34, "end": 3427.6, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51162, 1079, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 928, "seek": 341140, "start": 3428.0, "end": 3438.6, "text": " If the house stays at a livable temperature, despite the sun moving across the sky, a storm rolling in, clouds passing, and 30 people walking into the living room, then the computation is, by definition, correct.", "tokens": [51195, 759, 264, 1782, 10834, 412, 257, 11477, 712, 4292, 11, 7228, 264, 3295, 2684, 2108, 264, 5443, 11, 257, 7679, 9439, 294, 11, 12193, 8437, 11, 293, 2217, 561, 4494, 666, 264, 2647, 1808, 11, 550, 264, 24903, 307, 11, 538, 7123, 11, 3006, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11180835564931234, "compression_ratio": 1.6872964169381108, "no_speech_prob": 1.4611130231059755e-12}, {"id": 929, "seek": 343860, "start": 3438.6, "end": 3447.56, "text": " Correctness in a xylomorphic system is defined entirely by survival, equilibrium, and physical stability, not by outputting a symbolic string of text on a screen.", "tokens": [50365, 12753, 1287, 294, 257, 2031, 5088, 32702, 299, 1185, 307, 7642, 7696, 538, 12559, 11, 15625, 11, 293, 4001, 11826, 11, 406, 538, 5598, 783, 257, 25755, 6798, 295, 2487, 322, 257, 2568, 13, 50813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13274551630020143, "compression_ratio": 1.4778761061946903, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111215652205637e-12}, {"id": 930, "seek": 343860, "start": 3447.8199999999997, "end": 3450.92, "text": " This completely shatters how I think about what a computer even is.", "tokens": [50826, 639, 2584, 402, 37690, 577, 286, 519, 466, 437, 257, 3820, 754, 307, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13274551630020143, "compression_ratio": 1.4778761061946903, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111215652205637e-12}, {"id": 931, "seek": 343860, "start": 3451.06, "end": 3451.24, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50988, 865, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13274551630020143, "compression_ratio": 1.4778761061946903, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111215652205637e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 343860, "start": 3451.5, "end": 3456.3399999999997, "text": " And Flickchina takes this and categorizes how these physical systems compute through time, right?", "tokens": [51010, 400, 3235, 618, 339, 1426, 2516, 341, 293, 19250, 5660, 577, 613, 4001, 3652, 14722, 807, 565, 11, 558, 30, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13274551630020143, "compression_ratio": 1.4778761061946903, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111215652205637e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 345634, "start": 3456.34, "end": 3457.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 345634, "start": 3457.1800000000003, "end": 3460.96, "text": " Flickchina outlines three distinct temporal modes of computation.", "tokens": [50407, 3235, 618, 339, 1426, 40125, 1045, 10644, 30881, 14068, 295, 24903, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 935, "seek": 345634, "start": 3461.6800000000003, "end": 3463.78, "text": " The first is continuous computation.", "tokens": [50632, 440, 700, 307, 10957, 24903, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 936, "seek": 345634, "start": 3464.1800000000003, "end": 3464.92, "text": " Like the thermostat.", "tokens": [50757, 1743, 264, 8810, 39036, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 937, "seek": 345634, "start": 3465.0, "end": 3467.46, "text": " This is like a traditional HVAC thermostat.", "tokens": [50798, 639, 307, 411, 257, 5164, 389, 53, 4378, 8810, 39036, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 938, "seek": 345634, "start": 3467.98, "end": 3471.6600000000003, "text": " It only computes the environment while it is actively running and receiving electricity.", "tokens": [50947, 467, 787, 715, 1819, 264, 2823, 1339, 309, 307, 13022, 2614, 293, 10040, 10356, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 939, "seek": 345634, "start": 3472.26, "end": 3475.98, "text": " The moment you unplug it, the computation ceases to exist.", "tokens": [51161, 440, 1623, 291, 39456, 309, 11, 264, 24903, 1769, 1957, 281, 2514, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 940, "seek": 345634, "start": 3476.38, "end": 3477.7200000000003, "text": " It has no permanence.", "tokens": [51367, 467, 575, 572, 8105, 655, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 941, "seek": 345634, "start": 3478.0, "end": 3478.26, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51448, 1033, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 942, "seek": 345634, "start": 3478.48, "end": 3478.96, "text": " Continuous.", "tokens": [51472, 14674, 12549, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 943, "seek": 345634, "start": 3479.04, "end": 3479.82, "text": " What is the second?", "tokens": [51500, 708, 307, 264, 1150, 30, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 944, "seek": 345634, "start": 3480.1000000000004, "end": 3482.58, "text": " The second is accumulative computation.", "tokens": [51553, 440, 1150, 307, 12989, 22678, 24903, 13, 51677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 945, "seek": 345634, "start": 3483.2000000000003, "end": 3485.1400000000003, "text": " Think of the rings inside the trunk of a tree.", "tokens": [51708, 6557, 295, 264, 11136, 1854, 264, 19849, 295, 257, 4230, 13, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1943932336474222, "compression_ratio": 1.7296296296296296, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845755677179056e-12}, {"id": 946, "seek": 348514, "start": 3485.14, "end": 3493.06, "text": " The tree is a biological computer constantly processing its environment, the amount of rainfall, the harshness of the winter, the nutrients in the soil.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4230, 307, 257, 13910, 3820, 6460, 9007, 1080, 2823, 11, 264, 2372, 295, 29382, 11, 264, 14897, 1287, 295, 264, 6355, 11, 264, 17617, 294, 264, 6704, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 947, "seek": 348514, "start": 3493.48, "end": 3493.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50782, 1779, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 948, "seek": 348514, "start": 3493.7799999999997, "end": 3497.3599999999997, "text": " But unlike the thermostat, the tree preserves that computational history.", "tokens": [50797, 583, 8343, 264, 8810, 39036, 11, 264, 4230, 1183, 9054, 300, 28270, 2503, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 949, "seek": 348514, "start": 3497.6, "end": 3500.98, "text": " It writes it down physically, layer by layer into the wood.", "tokens": [50988, 467, 13657, 309, 760, 9762, 11, 4583, 538, 4583, 666, 264, 4576, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 950, "seek": 348514, "start": 3501.22, "end": 3503.46, "text": " The computation accumulates over time.", "tokens": [51169, 440, 24903, 12989, 26192, 670, 565, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 951, "seek": 348514, "start": 3503.58, "end": 3503.8799999999997, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51287, 3153, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 952, "seek": 348514, "start": 3504.08, "end": 3504.2599999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51312, 1033, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 953, "seek": 348514, "start": 3504.3199999999997, "end": 3505.52, "text": " So a thermostat is continuous.", "tokens": [51324, 407, 257, 8810, 39036, 307, 10957, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 954, "seek": 348514, "start": 3505.66, "end": 3506.52, "text": " A tree is accumulative.", "tokens": [51391, 316, 4230, 307, 12989, 22678, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 955, "seek": 348514, "start": 3506.94, "end": 3508.12, "text": " What is the third mode?", "tokens": [51455, 708, 307, 264, 2636, 4391, 30, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 956, "seek": 348514, "start": 3508.2799999999997, "end": 3512.2999999999997, "text": " What happens if a system calculates something once and then permanently locks it in?", "tokens": [51522, 708, 2314, 498, 257, 1185, 4322, 1024, 746, 1564, 293, 550, 24042, 20703, 309, 294, 30, 51723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16389203071594238, "compression_ratio": 1.6956521739130435, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266193478287836e-12}, {"id": 957, "seek": 351230, "start": 3512.3, "end": 3513.5600000000004, "text": " That is the third mode.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 264, 2636, 4391, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 958, "seek": 351230, "start": 3514.0, "end": 3514.94, "text": " Terminal computation.", "tokens": [50450, 19835, 2071, 24903, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 959, "seek": 351230, "start": 3515.6000000000004, "end": 3518.6600000000003, "text": " Imagine the process of building an ancient stone arch.", "tokens": [50530, 11739, 264, 1399, 295, 2390, 364, 7832, 7581, 3912, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 960, "seek": 351230, "start": 3518.84, "end": 3519.1000000000004, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50692, 1033, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 961, "seek": 351230, "start": 3519.1600000000003, "end": 3519.48, "text": " An arch.", "tokens": [50708, 1107, 3912, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 962, "seek": 351230, "start": 3519.8, "end": 3521.38, "text": " You have the wooden scaffolding underneath.", "tokens": [50740, 509, 362, 264, 14744, 44094, 278, 7223, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 963, "seek": 351230, "start": 3522.0, "end": 3524.2200000000003, "text": " You place the heavy stones one by one.", "tokens": [50850, 509, 1081, 264, 4676, 14083, 472, 538, 472, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 964, "seek": 351230, "start": 3524.48, "end": 3527.34, "text": " And then the moment comes to remove the scaffolding.", "tokens": [50974, 400, 550, 264, 1623, 1487, 281, 4159, 264, 44094, 278, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 965, "seek": 351230, "start": 3527.86, "end": 3530.44, "text": " As the wood is pulled away, the stones shift.", "tokens": [51143, 1018, 264, 4576, 307, 7373, 1314, 11, 264, 14083, 5513, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 966, "seek": 351230, "start": 3531.1000000000004, "end": 3533.42, "text": " The friction catches between the rough surfaces.", "tokens": [51305, 440, 17710, 25496, 1296, 264, 5903, 16130, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 967, "seek": 351230, "start": 3534.1400000000003, "end": 3536.1600000000003, "text": " Gravity pulls the mass downward.", "tokens": [51457, 49478, 16982, 264, 2758, 24805, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22739012101117304, "compression_ratio": 1.6478260869565218, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552453852014537e-12}, {"id": 968, "seek": 353616, "start": 3536.16, "end": 3537.7799999999997, "text": " It calculates the load.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 4322, 1024, 264, 3677, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 969, "seek": 353616, "start": 3538.0, "end": 3542.8399999999997, "text": " The arch physically calculates the distribution of load-bearing forces in real time.", "tokens": [50457, 440, 3912, 9762, 4322, 1024, 264, 7316, 295, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 5874, 294, 957, 565, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 970, "seek": 353616, "start": 3543.22, "end": 3544.62, "text": " And then it settles.", "tokens": [50718, 400, 550, 309, 5584, 904, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 971, "seek": 353616, "start": 3544.8199999999997, "end": 3547.3999999999996, "text": " It locks into its final stable geometry.", "tokens": [50798, 467, 20703, 666, 1080, 2572, 8351, 18426, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 972, "seek": 353616, "start": 3547.8599999999997, "end": 3551.02, "text": " The computation of those forces is completely resolved.", "tokens": [50950, 440, 24903, 295, 729, 5874, 307, 2584, 20772, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 973, "seek": 353616, "start": 3551.3199999999997, "end": 3554.74, "text": " And the arch essentially erases the history of its loading.", "tokens": [51123, 400, 264, 3912, 4476, 1189, 1957, 264, 2503, 295, 1080, 15114, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 974, "seek": 353616, "start": 3554.98, "end": 3560.22, "text": " It just stands there for centuries as a frozen physical answer to the problem of gravity.", "tokens": [51306, 467, 445, 7382, 456, 337, 13926, 382, 257, 12496, 4001, 1867, 281, 264, 1154, 295, 12110, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 975, "seek": 353616, "start": 3560.3799999999997, "end": 3561.3999999999996, "text": " That is absolutely beautiful.", "tokens": [51576, 663, 307, 3122, 2238, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 976, "seek": 353616, "start": 3561.48, "end": 3562.72, "text": " The arch is a terminal computer.", "tokens": [51631, 440, 3912, 307, 257, 14709, 3820, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 977, "seek": 353616, "start": 3562.94, "end": 3563.16, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51704, 3153, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17742223997373838, "compression_ratio": 1.7411764705882353, "no_speech_prob": 1.965925252450651e-12}, {"id": 978, "seek": 356316, "start": 3563.16, "end": 3566.5, "text": " Okay, let's step back and take a breath because we have covered an immense amount of ground", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1823, 646, 293, 747, 257, 6045, 570, 321, 362, 5343, 364, 22920, 2372, 295, 2727, 50532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 979, "seek": 356316, "start": 3566.5, "end": 3570.3399999999997, "text": " and we need to summarize this incredible journey we've been on through Flixing's research.", "tokens": [50532, 293, 321, 643, 281, 20858, 341, 4651, 4671, 321, 600, 668, 322, 807, 3235, 970, 278, 311, 2132, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 980, "seek": 356316, "start": 3570.44, "end": 3571.2999999999997, "text": " It's been a lot, yeah.", "tokens": [50729, 467, 311, 668, 257, 688, 11, 1338, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 981, "seek": 356316, "start": 3571.54, "end": 3573.7599999999998, "text": " We started in the realm of biology and history.", "tokens": [50784, 492, 1409, 294, 264, 15355, 295, 14956, 293, 2503, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 982, "seek": 356316, "start": 3574.3199999999997, "end": 3578.04, "text": " We learned that if we want to understand why systems take the shapes they do,", "tokens": [50923, 492, 3264, 300, 498, 321, 528, 281, 1223, 983, 3652, 747, 264, 10854, 436, 360, 11, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 983, "seek": 356316, "start": 3578.7799999999997, "end": 3584.3399999999997, "text": " we have to look past the historical origin, who got there first, or what the ancestor was.", "tokens": [51146, 321, 362, 281, 574, 1791, 264, 8584, 4957, 11, 567, 658, 456, 700, 11, 420, 437, 264, 40032, 390, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 984, "seek": 356316, "start": 3584.42, "end": 3584.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51428, 1779, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 985, "seek": 356316, "start": 3584.68, "end": 3586.52, "text": " The explanatory origin is what matters.", "tokens": [51441, 440, 9045, 4745, 4957, 307, 437, 7001, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1143354336420695, "compression_ratio": 1.6284722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881564505674684e-12}, {"id": 986, "seek": 358652, "start": 3586.52, "end": 3590.96, "text": " We have to look at the invisible constraint spaces, the admissibility fields, like the", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 14603, 25534, 7673, 11, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 7909, 11, 411, 264, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1483111045729946, "compression_ratio": 1.5902439024390245, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045700338747e-12}, {"id": 987, "seek": 358652, "start": 3590.96, "end": 3595.38, "text": " physical pressures of the ocean floor shaping the crab, or the climate constraints shaping", "tokens": [50587, 4001, 23573, 295, 264, 7810, 4123, 25945, 264, 17870, 11, 420, 264, 5659, 18491, 25945, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1483111045729946, "compression_ratio": 1.5902439024390245, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045700338747e-12}, {"id": 988, "seek": 358652, "start": 3595.38, "end": 3596.36, "text": " human agriculture.", "tokens": [50808, 1952, 14837, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1483111045729946, "compression_ratio": 1.5902439024390245, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045700338747e-12}, {"id": 989, "seek": 358652, "start": 3596.8, "end": 3598.7, "text": " The maze walls dictate the path.", "tokens": [50879, 440, 33032, 7920, 36071, 264, 3100, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1483111045729946, "compression_ratio": 1.5902439024390245, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045700338747e-12}, {"id": 990, "seek": 358652, "start": 3599.04, "end": 3604.2599999999998, "text": " And from there, we applied that understanding of constraints to our modern digital institutions.", "tokens": [50991, 400, 490, 456, 11, 321, 6456, 300, 3701, 295, 18491, 281, 527, 4363, 4562, 8142, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1483111045729946, "compression_ratio": 1.5902439024390245, "no_speech_prob": 1.649045700338747e-12}, {"id": 991, "seek": 360426, "start": 3604.26, "end": 3611.6000000000004, "text": " We saw how megascale tech platforms intentionally uncouple from the friction of physical reality.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1866, 577, 10816, 4806, 1220, 7553, 9473, 22062, 6219, 263, 781, 490, 264, 17710, 295, 4001, 4103, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20143913010419426, "compression_ratio": 1.5027322404371584, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970218412280414e-12}, {"id": 992, "seek": 360426, "start": 3611.82, "end": 3612.76, "text": " Their row drops to zero.", "tokens": [50743, 6710, 5386, 11438, 281, 4018, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20143913010419426, "compression_ratio": 1.5027322404371584, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970218412280414e-12}, {"id": 993, "seek": 360426, "start": 3613.1200000000003, "end": 3617.98, "text": " They let their row coefficient drop to zero, creating hollow, synthetic networks optimized", "tokens": [50808, 814, 718, 641, 5386, 17619, 3270, 281, 4018, 11, 4084, 23972, 11, 23420, 9590, 26941, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20143913010419426, "compression_ratio": 1.5027322404371584, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970218412280414e-12}, {"id": 994, "seek": 360426, "start": 3617.98, "end": 3621.7200000000003, "text": " purely for engagement metrics rather than human authenticity.", "tokens": [51051, 17491, 337, 8742, 16367, 2831, 813, 1952, 34215, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20143913010419426, "compression_ratio": 1.5027322404371584, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970218412280414e-12}, {"id": 995, "seek": 362172, "start": 3621.72, "end": 3624.3199999999997, "text": " They suppress the correction of reality.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 26835, 264, 19984, 295, 4103, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 996, "seek": 362172, "start": 3624.3199999999997, "end": 3627.3399999999997, "text": " Which led us to look inward at our own biology.", "tokens": [50495, 3013, 4684, 505, 281, 574, 29876, 412, 527, 1065, 14956, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 997, "seek": 362172, "start": 3628.02, "end": 3632.52, "text": " We saw how our brains, acting as predictive engines constantly trying to minimize free energy,", "tokens": [50680, 492, 1866, 577, 527, 15442, 11, 6577, 382, 35521, 12982, 6460, 1382, 281, 17522, 1737, 2281, 11, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 998, "seek": 362172, "start": 3633.04, "end": 3634.6, "text": " get hijacked by these platforms.", "tokens": [50931, 483, 10625, 25949, 538, 613, 9473, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 999, "seek": 362172, "start": 3634.9599999999996, "end": 3641.5, "text": " We get trapped in jouissance loops of outrage and social fear, starved of the productive friction", "tokens": [51027, 492, 483, 14994, 294, 11110, 14431, 16121, 295, 25933, 293, 2093, 4240, 11, 3543, 937, 295, 264, 13304, 17710, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 1000, "seek": 362172, "start": 3641.5, "end": 3644.14, "text": " and waymaking we need to genuinely learn and map our world.", "tokens": [51354, 293, 636, 12402, 321, 643, 281, 17839, 1466, 293, 4471, 527, 1002, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 1001, "seek": 362172, "start": 3644.3399999999997, "end": 3646.54, "text": " But we also explored the structural solutions.", "tokens": [51496, 583, 321, 611, 24016, 264, 15067, 6547, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 1002, "seek": 362172, "start": 3647.02, "end": 3650.8999999999996, "text": " We moved past the trap of centralized regulation and the recursion problem,", "tokens": [51630, 492, 4259, 1791, 264, 11487, 295, 32395, 15062, 293, 264, 20560, 313, 1154, 11, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1418047118605229, "compression_ratio": 1.6402640264026402, "no_speech_prob": 2.8831297158721236e-12}, {"id": 1003, "seek": 365090, "start": 3650.9, "end": 3653.08, "text": " and looked at distributed sympoises.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 2956, 412, 12631, 6697, 2259, 3598, 13, 50474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1004, "seek": 365090, "start": 3653.52, "end": 3654.76, "text": " The sphere-pop concept.", "tokens": [50496, 440, 16687, 12, 13872, 3410, 13, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1005, "seek": 365090, "start": 3654.9, "end": 3660.6600000000003, "text": " We explored sphere-pop, replacing erasable profiles with irreversible event histories", "tokens": [50565, 492, 24016, 16687, 12, 13872, 11, 19139, 1189, 296, 712, 23693, 365, 16014, 840, 964, 2280, 30631, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1006, "seek": 365090, "start": 3660.6600000000003, "end": 3663.12, "text": " to make deception thermodynamically expensive.", "tokens": [50853, 281, 652, 40451, 8810, 21399, 984, 5124, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1007, "seek": 365090, "start": 3663.58, "end": 3669.92, "text": " And we looked at the post-Turing condition, requiring AI to be architecturally quadrangulated", "tokens": [50999, 400, 321, 2956, 412, 264, 2183, 12, 51, 1345, 4188, 11, 24165, 7318, 281, 312, 6331, 6512, 10787, 32926, 6987, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1008, "seek": 365090, "start": 3669.92, "end": 3673.2200000000003, "text": " to a human perspective so it doesn't drift into machine-only coherence.", "tokens": [51316, 281, 257, 1952, 4585, 370, 309, 1177, 380, 19699, 666, 3479, 12, 25202, 26528, 655, 13, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1009, "seek": 365090, "start": 3673.34, "end": 3676.54, "text": " Which finally brought us to the ultimate synthesis, the radiative switch.", "tokens": [51487, 3013, 2721, 3038, 505, 281, 264, 9705, 30252, 11, 264, 16335, 1166, 3679, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1010, "seek": 365090, "start": 3676.6600000000003, "end": 3676.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51653, 1779, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1011, "seek": 365090, "start": 3677.04, "end": 3678.12, "text": " Xylomorphic computation.", "tokens": [51672, 1783, 5088, 32702, 299, 24903, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17471738962026742, "compression_ratio": 1.5870307167235496, "no_speech_prob": 3.31832629950346e-12}, {"id": 1012, "seek": 367812, "start": 3678.12, "end": 3683.7799999999997, "text": " The profound idea that the substrate, the calculation, and the physical function can be entirely inseparable.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 14382, 1558, 300, 264, 27585, 11, 264, 17108, 11, 293, 264, 4001, 2445, 393, 312, 7696, 33874, 42012, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1013, "seek": 367812, "start": 3684.12, "end": 3686.42, "text": " That the physical world can compute itself.", "tokens": [50665, 663, 264, 4001, 1002, 393, 14722, 2564, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1014, "seek": 367812, "start": 3686.52, "end": 3686.7599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50785, 7587, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1015, "seek": 367812, "start": 3686.8399999999997, "end": 3691.6, "text": " Which leaves you, the listener, with a final lingering thought to mull over today.", "tokens": [50801, 3013, 5510, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 365, 257, 2572, 49542, 1194, 281, 275, 858, 670, 965, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1016, "seek": 367812, "start": 3691.98, "end": 3695.6, "text": " We started this entire journey by talking about x-rays.", "tokens": [51058, 492, 1409, 341, 2302, 4671, 538, 1417, 466, 2031, 12, 36212, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1017, "seek": 367812, "start": 3695.8599999999997, "end": 3701.2799999999997, "text": " We talked about how much we crave looking for that clean, visible, perfectly manageable line", "tokens": [51252, 492, 2825, 466, 577, 709, 321, 46875, 1237, 337, 300, 2541, 11, 8974, 11, 6239, 38798, 1622, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1018, "seek": 367812, "start": 3701.2799999999997, "end": 3702.24, "text": " of a broken bone.", "tokens": [51523, 295, 257, 5463, 9026, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1019, "seek": 367812, "start": 3702.3599999999997, "end": 3703.5, "text": " We want it to be simple.", "tokens": [51577, 492, 528, 309, 281, 312, 2199, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14335962990734064, "compression_ratio": 1.6125461254612545, "no_speech_prob": 2.4853999067153687e-12}, {"id": 1020, "seek": 370350, "start": 3703.5, "end": 3709.42, "text": " In many ways, we built our entire modern digital world trying to artificially create that clean,", "tokens": [50365, 682, 867, 2098, 11, 321, 3094, 527, 2302, 4363, 4562, 1002, 1382, 281, 39905, 2270, 1884, 300, 2541, 11, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15496494400669153, "compression_ratio": 1.4816753926701571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967613074459932e-12}, {"id": 1021, "seek": 370350, "start": 3709.56, "end": 3711.42, "text": " visible, manageable space.", "tokens": [50668, 8974, 11, 38798, 1901, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15496494400669153, "compression_ratio": 1.4816753926701571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967613074459932e-12}, {"id": 1022, "seek": 370350, "start": 3711.74, "end": 3717.28, "text": " We built the internet as a frictionless virtual escape from the messy, muddy, resistant waters", "tokens": [50777, 492, 3094, 264, 4705, 382, 257, 17710, 1832, 6374, 7615, 490, 264, 16191, 11, 38540, 11, 20383, 12975, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15496494400669153, "compression_ratio": 1.4816753926701571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967613074459932e-12}, {"id": 1023, "seek": 370350, "start": 3717.28, "end": 3718.44, "text": " of the physical world.", "tokens": [51054, 295, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15496494400669153, "compression_ratio": 1.4816753926701571, "no_speech_prob": 1.7967613074459932e-12}, {"id": 1024, "seek": 370350, "start": 3718.56, "end": 3719.98, "text": " But maybe that was the wrong goal.", "tokens": [51118, 583, 1310, 300, 390, 264, 2085, 3387, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15496494400669153, "compression_ratio": 1.4816753926701571, "no_speech_prob": 1.79676130744599