_speech_prob": 6.162779162856291e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2934, "start": 39.8, "end": 46.8, "text": " And right in the middle of a critical explanation, they threw up a chart where the X and Y axes were clearly swapped.", "tokens": [50888, 400, 558, 294, 264, 2808, 295, 257, 4924, 10835, 11, 436, 11918, 493, 257, 6927, 689, 264, 1783, 293, 398, 35387, 645, 4448, 50011, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1022940677145253, "compression_ratio": 1.5866666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 6.162779162856291e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2934, "start": 46.94, "end": 52.14, "text": " Oh, man. That is brutal. It completely shatters the illusion of authority when that happens.", "tokens": [51245, 876, 11, 587, 13, 663, 307, 17878, 13, 467, 2584, 402, 37690, 264, 18854, 295, 8281, 562, 300, 2314, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1022940677145253, "compression_ratio": 1.5866666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 6.162779162856291e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2934, "start": 52.4, "end": 57.620000000000005, "text": " It really does. But you know what really struck me was the creator's solution to it. They couldn't just like fix it.", "tokens": [51518, 467, 534, 775, 13, 583, 291, 458, 437, 534, 13159, 385, 390, 264, 14181, 311, 3827, 281, 309, 13, 814, 2809, 380, 445, 411, 3191, 309, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1022940677145253, "compression_ratio": 1.5866666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 6.162779162856291e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 5762, "start": 57.62, "end": 59.379999999999995, "text": " Right. Because it is already out there.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 1436, 309, 307, 1217, 484, 456, 13, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321879900418795, "compression_ratio": 1.4023668639053255, "no_speech_prob": 1.617157796562907e-12}, {"id": 12, "seek": 5762, "start": 59.44, "end": 67.64, "text": " Exactly. Instead, there was a pinned comment at a very top of the comment section saying, you know, hey, guys, at 42.15, the axes are swapped. Sorry about that.", "tokens": [50456, 7587, 13, 7156, 11, 456, 390, 257, 33802, 2871, 412, 257, 588, 1192, 295, 264, 2871, 3541, 1566, 11, 291, 458, 11, 4177, 11, 1074, 11, 412, 14034, 13, 5211, 11, 264, 35387, 366, 50011, 13, 4919, 466, 300, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321879900418795, "compression_ratio": 1.4023668639053255, "no_speech_prob": 1.617157796562907e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5762, "start": 67.88, "end": 70.46, "text": " Yep. The classic pinned comment fix.", "tokens": [50878, 7010, 13, 440, 7230, 33802, 2871, 3191, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321879900418795, "compression_ratio": 1.4023668639053255, "no_speech_prob": 1.617157796562907e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 7046, "start": 70.46, "end": 82.25999999999999, "text": " And I realized right then that in modern digital media, despite living in an era of supposedly infinite mutability, that mistake is effectively carved in stone.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 286, 5334, 558, 550, 300, 294, 4363, 4562, 3021, 11, 7228, 2647, 294, 364, 4249, 295, 20581, 13785, 5839, 2310, 11, 300, 6146, 307, 8659, 28613, 294, 7581, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07475913138616652, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 7046, "start": 82.52, "end": 83.22, "text": " It is frozen.", "tokens": [50968, 467, 307, 12496, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07475913138616652, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 7046, "start": 83.63999999999999, "end": 96.24, "text": " It is. We are looking at a publishing landscape that is just trapped in amber. We treat code and text as things we can patch. But complex media is suddenly treated like wet concrete that is completely set.", "tokens": [51024, 467, 307, 13, 492, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 17832, 9661, 300, 307, 445, 14994, 294, 48304, 13, 492, 2387, 3089, 293, 2487, 382, 721, 321, 393, 9972, 13, 583, 3997, 3021, 307, 5800, 8668, 411, 6630, 9859, 300, 307, 2584, 992, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07475913138616652, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493961586481419e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 9624, "start": 96.24, "end": 104.19999999999999, "text": " We have built these incredibly sophisticated delivery pipelines. But fundamentally, the objects we are delivering are frozen artifacts. Right.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 3094, 613, 6252, 16950, 8982, 40168, 13, 583, 17879, 11, 264, 6565, 321, 366, 14666, 366, 12496, 24617, 13, 1779, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603031199029152, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694502567189847e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 9624, "start": 104.41999999999999, "end": 110.97999999999999, "text": " We have inherited this bizarre mental model where the final presentation of an idea is treated as the idea itself.", "tokens": [50774, 492, 362, 27091, 341, 18265, 4973, 2316, 689, 264, 2572, 5860, 295, 364, 1558, 307, 8668, 382, 264, 1558, 2564, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603031199029152, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694502567189847e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 9624, "start": 111.24, "end": 115.0, "text": " And that actually brings us perfectly to the core theme for today's deep dive.", "tokens": [51115, 400, 300, 767, 5607, 505, 6239, 281, 264, 4965, 6314, 337, 965, 311, 2452, 9192, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603031199029152, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694502567189847e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 9624, "start": 115.14, "end": 121.08, "text": " We're going to be looking at the hidden, frankly, broken architecture of how we consume information and learn complex systems.", "tokens": [51310, 492, 434, 516, 281, 312, 1237, 412, 264, 7633, 11, 11939, 11, 5463, 9482, 295, 577, 321, 14732, 1589, 293, 1466, 3997, 3652, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10603031199029152, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.2694502567189847e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 12108, "start": 121.08, "end": 122.6, "text": " It is a massive problem.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 1154, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12469580679228812, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524389479636973e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 12108, "start": 122.92, "end": 135.6, "text": " It really is. And to you, the listener, have you ever felt that frustration, like the permanence of a mistake in a video or maybe using a clone software tool that looks perfect, but fundamentally feels wrong the second you actually try to use it?", "tokens": [50457, 467, 534, 307, 13, 400, 281, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 362, 291, 1562, 2762, 300, 20491, 11, 411, 264, 8105, 655, 295, 257, 6146, 294, 257, 960, 420, 1310, 1228, 257, 26506, 4722, 2290, 300, 1542, 2176, 11, 457, 17879, 3417, 2085, 264, 1150, 291, 767, 853, 281, 764, 309, 30, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12469580679228812, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524389479636973e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 12108, "start": 135.72, "end": 137.6, "text": " I think everyone has run into that at some point.", "tokens": [51097, 286, 519, 1518, 575, 1190, 666, 300, 412, 512, 935, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12469580679228812, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524389479636973e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 12108, "start": 137.7, "end": 138.07999999999998, "text": " For sure.", "tokens": [51196, 1171, 988, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12469580679228812, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524389479636973e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 12108, "start": 139.07999999999998, "end": 146.24, "text": " So today we are exploring a revolutionary concept designed to fix this exact issue.", "tokens": [51265, 407, 965, 321, 366, 12736, 257, 22687, 3410, 4761, 281, 3191, 341, 1900, 2734, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12469580679228812, "compression_ratio": 1.571969696969697, "no_speech_prob": 2.0524389479636973e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 14624, "start": 146.24, "end": 159.86, "text": " We are talking about fundamentally tearing apart the absolute truth of a piece of information, what we will call the canonical source, and completely separating that from its visual presentation or the rendering.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 17879, 29401, 4936, 264, 8236, 3494, 295, 257, 2522, 295, 1589, 11, 437, 321, 486, 818, 264, 46491, 4009, 11, 293, 2584, 29279, 300, 490, 1080, 5056, 5860, 420, 264, 22407, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07981636986803653, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830495109907862e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 14624, "start": 160.08, "end": 164.34, "text": " And, you know, the shift in thinking required here really cannot be overstated.", "tokens": [51057, 400, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 5513, 294, 1953, 4739, 510, 534, 2644, 312, 48834, 770, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07981636986803653, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830495109907862e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 14624, "start": 164.42000000000002, "end": 165.28, "text": " No, it is huge.", "tokens": [51274, 883, 11, 309, 307, 2603, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07981636986803653, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830495109907862e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 16528, "start": 165.28, "end": 176.44, "text": " We are moving from a paradigm where the presentation is synonymous with the truth to a world where the presentation is nothing more than a disposable, temporary view compiled from the truth.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 2684, 490, 257, 24709, 689, 264, 5860, 307, 5451, 18092, 365, 264, 3494, 281, 257, 1002, 689, 264, 5860, 307, 1825, 544, 813, 257, 41578, 11, 13413, 1910, 36548, 490, 264, 3494, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09793987391907492, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074987699120745e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 16528, "start": 176.56, "end": 178.12, "text": " I love that. The temporary view.", "tokens": [50929, 286, 959, 300, 13, 440, 13413, 1910, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09793987391907492, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074987699120745e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 16528, "start": 178.4, "end": 187.26, "text": " It is the difference between handing someone a baked cake versus handing them the recipe, the raw ingredients, and like a molecular breakdown of how they interact.", "tokens": [51021, 467, 307, 264, 2649, 1296, 34774, 1580, 257, 19453, 5908, 5717, 34774, 552, 264, 6782, 11, 264, 8936, 6952, 11, 293, 411, 257, 19046, 18188, 295, 577, 436, 4648, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09793987391907492, "compression_ratio": 1.6973684210526316, "no_speech_prob": 1.5074987699120745e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 18726, "start": 187.26, "end": 195.23999999999998, "text": " That is a great analogy. And I was reading two wildly different sources over the weekend that surprisingly tackled this exact same philosophical problem.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 400, 286, 390, 3760, 732, 34731, 819, 7139, 670, 264, 6711, 300, 17600, 9426, 1493, 341, 1900, 912, 25066, 1154, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12823698692715046, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485577872775049e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 18726, "start": 195.44, "end": 197.73999999999998, "text": " But from completely opposite ends of the spectrum, right?", "tokens": [50774, 583, 490, 2584, 6182, 5314, 295, 264, 11143, 11, 558, 30, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12823698692715046, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485577872775049e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 18726, "start": 198.0, "end": 206.62, "text": " Exactly. The first is a highly technical design specification document. It is called Buffer World, Technical Specification V 0.2.", "tokens": [50902, 7587, 13, 440, 700, 307, 257, 5405, 6191, 1715, 31256, 4166, 13, 467, 307, 1219, 20254, 260, 3937, 11, 35512, 20484, 3774, 691, 1958, 13, 17, 13, 51333], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12823698692715046, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485577872775049e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 18726, "start": 206.88, "end": 208.39999999999998, "text": " A fascinating document.", "tokens": [51346, 316, 10343, 4166, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12823698692715046, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485577872775049e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 18726, "start": 208.56, "end": 212.57999999999998, "text": " It really is. It outlines the architecture for a 3D spatial video game.", "tokens": [51430, 467, 534, 307, 13, 467, 40125, 264, 9482, 337, 257, 805, 35, 23598, 960, 1216, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12823698692715046, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485577872775049e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 21258, "start": 212.58, "end": 220.70000000000002, "text": " But it is not just a game. It is built specifically to teach the notoriously complex keyboard motions of the VimText editor.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 307, 406, 445, 257, 1216, 13, 467, 307, 3094, 4682, 281, 2924, 264, 46772, 8994, 3997, 10186, 27500, 295, 264, 691, 332, 50198, 9839, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08991159573949949, "compression_ratio": 1.5267175572519085, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 21258, "start": 220.88000000000002, "end": 227.0, "text": " Which, just on its own, is a fascinating translation of a purely textual interface into a 3D spatial environment.", "tokens": [50780, 3013, 11, 445, 322, 1080, 1065, 11, 307, 257, 10343, 12853, 295, 257, 17491, 2487, 901, 9226, 666, 257, 805, 35, 23598, 2823, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08991159573949949, "compression_ratio": 1.5267175572519085, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 21258, "start": 227.26000000000002, "end": 233.58, "text": " Totally. But then the second source we have zooms this concept out to encompass, well, all of human knowledge.", "tokens": [51099, 22837, 13, 583, 550, 264, 1150, 4009, 321, 362, 5721, 4785, 341, 3410, 484, 281, 28268, 11, 731, 11, 439, 295, 1952, 3601, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08991159573949949, "compression_ratio": 1.5267175572519085, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 21258, "start": 233.66000000000003, "end": 234.66000000000003, "text": " Just a small leap.", "tokens": [51419, 1449, 257, 1359, 19438, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08991159573949949, "compression_ratio": 1.5267175572519085, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 21258, "start": 234.74, "end": 236.16000000000003, "text": " Right. Just a casual expansion.", "tokens": [51473, 1779, 13, 1449, 257, 13052, 11260, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08991159573949949, "compression_ratio": 1.5267175572519085, "no_speech_prob": 1.890634567305871e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 23616, "start": 236.16, "end": 244.96, "text": " It is a theoretical essay published in July 2026 titled, Plenum Hub slash Polluxan, toward a source-first publishing substrate.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 20864, 16238, 6572, 294, 7370, 945, 10880, 19841, 11, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 17330, 31304, 2449, 282, 11, 7361, 257, 4009, 12, 29581, 17832, 27585, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 23616, "start": 245.06, "end": 247.06, "text": " By an independent researcher known as Flixim.", "tokens": [50810, 3146, 364, 6695, 21751, 2570, 382, 3235, 970, 332, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 23616, "start": 247.24, "end": 247.98, "text": " Yes, Flixim.", "tokens": [50919, 1079, 11, 3235, 970, 332, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 23616, "start": 248.28, "end": 252.16, "text": " And they are proposing a radical re-architecting of literally all digital media.", "tokens": [50971, 400, 436, 366, 29939, 257, 12001, 319, 12, 1178, 5739, 278, 295, 3736, 439, 4562, 3021, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 23616, "start": 252.26, "end": 253.4, "text": " It is incredibly ambitious.", "tokens": [51170, 467, 307, 6252, 20239, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 23616, "start": 254.0, "end": 258.15999999999997, "text": " So our mission for this deep dive is to synthesize these two documents for you.", "tokens": [51257, 407, 527, 4447, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 307, 281, 26617, 1125, 613, 732, 8512, 337, 291, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1521477018083845, "compression_ratio": 1.4763779527559056, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 25816, "start": 258.16, "end": 271.40000000000003, "text": " We want to unpack how treating the source and the rendering as two entirely different things gives you unprecedented, absolute power over how you learn, read, and interact with the digital world.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 528, 281, 26699, 577, 15083, 264, 4009, 293, 264, 22407, 382, 732, 7696, 819, 721, 2709, 291, 21555, 11, 8236, 1347, 670, 577, 291, 1466, 11, 1401, 11, 293, 4648, 365, 264, 4562, 1002, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330654492942236, "compression_ratio": 1.5943775100401607, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837663432978876e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 25816, "start": 271.68, "end": 273.38000000000005, "text": " It changes everything about media consumption.", "tokens": [51041, 467, 2962, 1203, 466, 3021, 12126, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330654492942236, "compression_ratio": 1.5943775100401607, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837663432978876e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 25816, "start": 274.1, "end": 275.34000000000003, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [51162, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330654492942236, "compression_ratio": 1.5943775100401607, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837663432978876e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 25816, "start": 275.40000000000003, "end": 277.04, "text": " I want to start with the root of the disease.", "tokens": [51227, 286, 528, 281, 722, 365, 264, 5593, 295, 264, 4752, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330654492942236, "compression_ratio": 1.5943775100401607, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837663432978876e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 25816, "start": 277.3, "end": 282.62, "text": " In the Plenum Hub essay, Flixian diagnoses something called the conflation problem.", "tokens": [51322, 682, 264, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 16238, 11, 3235, 970, 952, 7234, 4201, 746, 1219, 264, 1497, 24278, 1154, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1330654492942236, "compression_ratio": 1.5943775100401607, "no_speech_prob": 1.4837663432978876e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 28262, "start": 282.62, "end": 290.08, "text": " Right. And the genius of Flixian's diagnosis here is pointing out something so ubiquitous that we have gone completely blind to it.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 400, 264, 14017, 295, 3235, 970, 952, 311, 15217, 510, 307, 12166, 484, 746, 370, 43868, 39831, 300, 321, 362, 2780, 2584, 6865, 281, 309, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 28262, "start": 290.12, "end": 291.68, "text": " It is just water to a fish at this point.", "tokens": [50740, 467, 307, 445, 1281, 281, 257, 3506, 412, 341, 935, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 28262, "start": 291.78000000000003, "end": 294.6, "text": " Exactly. Think about traditional video-based publishing.", "tokens": [50823, 7587, 13, 6557, 466, 5164, 960, 12, 6032, 17832, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 28262, "start": 295.14, "end": 299.84000000000003, "text": " A platform like YouTube structurally conflates the source of a work with its rendering.", "tokens": [50991, 316, 3663, 411, 3088, 6594, 6512, 1497, 75, 1024, 264, 4009, 295, 257, 589, 365, 1080, 22407, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 28262, "start": 300.02, "end": 301.44, "text": " They're completely mashed together.", "tokens": [51235, 814, 434, 2584, 38964, 1214, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 28262, "start": 301.58, "end": 308.4, "text": " The video file you stream is simultaneously the intellectual argument being made and the literal recording of that argument.", "tokens": [51313, 440, 960, 3991, 291, 4309, 307, 16561, 264, 12576, 6770, 885, 1027, 293, 264, 20411, 6613, 295, 300, 6770, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 28262, "start": 308.6, "end": 312.5, "text": " They are smashed together at a molecular level. It goes back to your cake analogy.", "tokens": [51664, 814, 366, 33269, 1214, 412, 257, 19046, 1496, 13, 467, 1709, 646, 281, 428, 5908, 21663, 13, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08058275604248047, "compression_ratio": 1.6529411764705881, "no_speech_prob": 2.370967354739517e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 31262, "start": 313.02, "end": 315.46, "text": " Once it is baked, I cannot extract the eggs.", "tokens": [50385, 3443, 309, 307, 19453, 11, 286, 2644, 8947, 264, 6466, 13, 50507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 31262, "start": 315.58, "end": 316.84000000000003, "text": " Nope. They are in there for good.", "tokens": [50513, 12172, 13, 814, 366, 294, 456, 337, 665, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 31262, "start": 317.2, "end": 323.8, "text": " I cannot unbake the video to reduce the sugar or, you know, fix that swapped axis on the chart.", "tokens": [50594, 286, 2644, 517, 65, 619, 264, 960, 281, 5407, 264, 5076, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 3191, 300, 50011, 10298, 322, 264, 6927, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 31262, "start": 324.0, "end": 330.28000000000003, "text": " That analogy holds up perfectly because there is no accessible version-controlled object underneath the video.", "tokens": [50934, 663, 21663, 9190, 493, 6239, 570, 456, 307, 572, 9515, 3037, 12, 49344, 2657, 7223, 264, 960, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 31262, "start": 330.42, "end": 332.32, "text": " Right. It is just the video.", "tokens": [51255, 1779, 13, 467, 307, 445, 264, 960, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 31262, "start": 332.32, "end": 340.6, "text": " If a researcher wants to analyze the core claims of a video essay, they are forced to watch pixels change color and listen to an audio waveform.", "tokens": [51350, 759, 257, 21751, 2738, 281, 12477, 264, 4965, 9441, 295, 257, 960, 16238, 11, 436, 366, 7579, 281, 1159, 18668, 1319, 2017, 293, 2140, 281, 364, 6278, 36512, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11656380543666603, "compression_ratio": 1.6392857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.466482100684341e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 34060, "start": 340.6, "end": 342.70000000000005, "text": " Which is crazy when you think about it.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 3219, 562, 291, 519, 466, 309, 13, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14105182583049192, "compression_ratio": 1.2974683544303798, "no_speech_prob": 1.790017461512916e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 34060, "start": 342.70000000000005, "end": 347.82000000000005, "text": " It is. They cannot query the underlying logic. The MP4 file is a master copy.", "tokens": [50470, 467, 307, 13, 814, 2644, 14581, 264, 14217, 9952, 13, 440, 14146, 19, 3991, 307, 257, 4505, 5055, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14105182583049192, "compression_ratio": 1.2974683544303798, "no_speech_prob": 1.790017461512916e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 34060, "start": 348.08000000000004, "end": 351.26000000000005, "text": " But I keep asking myself, why did we build our systems this way?", "tokens": [50739, 583, 286, 1066, 3365, 2059, 11, 983, 630, 321, 1322, 527, 3652, 341, 636, 30, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14105182583049192, "compression_ratio": 1.2974683544303798, "no_speech_prob": 1.790017461512916e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 34060, "start": 351.42, "end": 352.3, "text": " It is a good question.", "tokens": [50906, 467, 307, 257, 665, 1168, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14105182583049192, "compression_ratio": 1.2974683544303798, "no_speech_prob": 1.790017461512916e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 35230, "start": 352.3, "end": 361.7, "text": " Like, if I am a software developer writing in C++ our time, I write human-readable source code and then I compile it into a binary executable for the computer to run.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 669, 257, 4722, 10754, 3579, 294, 383, 25472, 527, 565, 11, 286, 2464, 1952, 12, 2538, 712, 4009, 3089, 293, 550, 286, 31413, 309, 666, 257, 17434, 7568, 712, 337, 264, 3820, 281, 1190, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959613213172326, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 1.561057273030686e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 35230, "start": 361.82, "end": 363.34000000000003, "text": " Right. The computer reads the binary.", "tokens": [50841, 1779, 13, 440, 3820, 15700, 264, 17434, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959613213172326, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 1.561057273030686e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 35230, "start": 363.56, "end": 364.82, "text": " But I never edit the binary.", "tokens": [50928, 583, 286, 1128, 8129, 264, 17434, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959613213172326, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 1.561057273030686e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 35230, "start": 365.28000000000003, "end": 368.58000000000004, "text": " If there is a bug, I edit the source code and recompile it.", "tokens": [51014, 759, 456, 307, 257, 7426, 11, 286, 8129, 264, 4009, 3089, 293, 48000, 794, 309, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959613213172326, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 1.561057273030686e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 35230, "start": 368.98, "end": 371.02, "text": " Why didn't digital media adopt that model?", "tokens": [51199, 1545, 994, 380, 4562, 3021, 6878, 300, 2316, 30, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959613213172326, "compression_ratio": 1.6076555023923444, "no_speech_prob": 1.561057273030686e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 37102, "start": 371.02, "end": 374.08, "text": " Honestly, it comes down to historical hangovers.", "tokens": [50365, 12348, 11, 309, 1487, 760, 281, 8584, 3967, 25348, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 37102, "start": 374.28, "end": 375.12, "text": " Historical hangovers.", "tokens": [50528, 46124, 3967, 25348, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 37102, "start": 375.15999999999997, "end": 382.29999999999995, "text": " Yeah. The printing press said our mental models for centuries. A physical book had to conflate the source and the rendering.", "tokens": [50572, 865, 13, 440, 14699, 1886, 848, 527, 4973, 5245, 337, 13926, 13, 316, 4001, 1446, 632, 281, 1497, 17593, 264, 4009, 293, 264, 22407, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 37102, "start": 382.52, "end": 384.26, "text": " Well, sure. Because it is ink on paper.", "tokens": [50940, 1042, 11, 988, 13, 1436, 309, 307, 11276, 322, 3035, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 37102, "start": 384.56, "end": 394.46, "text": " There was simply no practical way to distribute the semantic structural argument of a novel or a textbook separately from its typeset ink and paper form.", "tokens": [51042, 821, 390, 2935, 572, 8496, 636, 281, 20594, 264, 47982, 15067, 6770, 295, 257, 7613, 420, 257, 25591, 14759, 490, 1080, 3467, 302, 11276, 293, 3035, 1254, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 37102, "start": 394.76, "end": 397.91999999999996, "text": " The physical page was the only available delivery mechanism.", "tokens": [51552, 440, 4001, 3028, 390, 264, 787, 2435, 8982, 7513, 13, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14771893445183248, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.6817119528542146e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 39792, "start": 397.92, "end": 405.08000000000004, "text": " Exactly. So, when we moved to digital video platforms, we didn't reinvent the wheel. We just digitized the printing press.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 407, 11, 562, 321, 4259, 281, 4562, 960, 9473, 11, 321, 994, 380, 33477, 264, 5589, 13, 492, 445, 14293, 1602, 264, 14699, 1886, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 39792, "start": 405.18, "end": 407.32, "text": " We brought our old baggage into the new medium.", "tokens": [50728, 492, 3038, 527, 1331, 41567, 666, 264, 777, 6399, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 39792, "start": 407.44, "end": 412.68, "text": " We inherited the fusion of content and presentation by default rather than by necessity.", "tokens": [50841, 492, 27091, 264, 23100, 295, 2701, 293, 5860, 538, 7576, 2831, 813, 538, 24217, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 39792, "start": 412.94, "end": 416.6, "text": " So, we treated digital video the exact same way we treated a printed book.", "tokens": [51116, 407, 11, 321, 8668, 4562, 960, 264, 1900, 912, 636, 321, 8668, 257, 13567, 1446, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 39792, "start": 416.70000000000005, "end": 417.22, "text": " Pretty much.", "tokens": [51304, 10693, 709, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 39792, "start": 417.46000000000004, "end": 425.90000000000003, "text": " And because of that, you know, intellectual laziness, we ended up with all these downstream pathologies that Fliction outlines in the essay.", "tokens": [51342, 400, 570, 295, 300, 11, 291, 458, 11, 12576, 19320, 1324, 11, 321, 4590, 493, 365, 439, 613, 30621, 3100, 6204, 300, 3235, 4105, 40125, 294, 264, 16238, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12388159935934502, "compression_ratio": 1.6655290102389078, "no_speech_prob": 1.825306399083626e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 42590, "start": 425.9, "end": 429.08, "text": " Okay. Let's dig into those, starting with uncorrectability.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 2528, 666, 729, 11, 2891, 365, 6219, 284, 2554, 2310, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 42590, "start": 429.65999999999997, "end": 434.34, "text": " Uncorrectability is definitely the most obvious pain point, as you noted with your chert example earlier.", "tokens": [50553, 1156, 19558, 2554, 2310, 307, 2138, 264, 881, 6322, 1822, 935, 11, 382, 291, 12964, 365, 428, 417, 911, 1365, 3071, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 42590, "start": 434.5, "end": 434.9, "text": " It is infuriating.", "tokens": [50795, 467, 307, 1536, 9744, 990, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 42590, "start": 435.7, "end": 441.2, "text": " If you make a factual error in a traditional video, you face an absurd logistical nightmare.", "tokens": [50855, 759, 291, 652, 257, 48029, 6713, 294, 257, 5164, 960, 11, 291, 1851, 364, 19774, 3565, 42686, 18724, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 42590, "start": 441.59999999999997, "end": 443.44, "text": " You cannot simply patch the error.", "tokens": [51150, 509, 2644, 2935, 9972, 264, 6713, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 42590, "start": 443.5, "end": 444.9, "text": " No. You have to nuke the whole thing.", "tokens": [51245, 883, 13, 509, 362, 281, 3822, 330, 264, 1379, 551, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223361522593397, "compression_ratio": 1.5486725663716814, "no_speech_prob": 1.839361996047728e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 44490, "start": 444.9, "end": 455.08, "text": " You have to take down the entire artifact, pull up your editing software, re-render the massive file, and upload a completely new artifact.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 281, 747, 760, 264, 2302, 34806, 11, 2235, 493, 428, 10000, 4722, 11, 319, 12, 13292, 264, 5994, 3991, 11, 293, 6580, 257, 2584, 777, 34806, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635754768294517, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754417727666727e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 44490, "start": 455.4, "end": 463.46, "text": " And furthermore, all the old incorrect copies will persist in edge caches, user downloads, and unauthorized reposts forever.", "tokens": [50890, 400, 3052, 3138, 11, 439, 264, 1331, 18424, 14341, 486, 13233, 294, 4691, 269, 13272, 11, 4195, 36553, 11, 293, 517, 34224, 1602, 1085, 555, 82, 5680, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635754768294517, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754417727666727e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 44490, "start": 463.7, "end": 467.38, "text": " Exactly. And for the creator, you lose all your engagement metrics.", "tokens": [51305, 7587, 13, 400, 337, 264, 14181, 11, 291, 3624, 439, 428, 8742, 16367, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635754768294517, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754417727666727e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 44490, "start": 467.52, "end": 471.9, "text": " Oh, all the incoming links break, all the embedded players across the internet go dark.", "tokens": [51496, 876, 11, 439, 264, 22341, 6123, 1821, 11, 439, 264, 16741, 4150, 2108, 264, 4705, 352, 2877, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07635754768294517, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.7754417727666727e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 47190, "start": 471.9, "end": 475.88, "text": " It financially disincentivizes creators from ever correcting the record.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 20469, 717, 259, 2207, 592, 5660, 16039, 490, 1562, 47032, 264, 2136, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 47190, "start": 475.97999999999996, "end": 477.94, "text": " They literally lose money if they fix a mistake.", "tokens": [50569, 814, 3736, 3624, 1460, 498, 436, 3191, 257, 6146, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 47190, "start": 478.14, "end": 480.64, "text": " So they just leave the pinned comment and move on.", "tokens": [50677, 407, 436, 445, 1856, 264, 33802, 2871, 293, 1286, 322, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 47190, "start": 480.67999999999995, "end": 481.09999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50804, 7587, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 47190, "start": 481.38, "end": 482.94, "text": " Okay. What is the next pathology?", "tokens": [50839, 1033, 13, 708, 307, 264, 958, 3100, 1793, 30, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 47190, "start": 483.23999999999995, "end": 485.14, "text": " The next one is forced linearity.", "tokens": [50932, 440, 958, 472, 307, 7579, 8213, 507, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 47190, "start": 485.62, "end": 491.76, "text": " A video is time-locked. It plays from beginning to end at a pace dictated entirely by the creator, not the reader.", "tokens": [51051, 316, 960, 307, 565, 12, 4102, 292, 13, 467, 5749, 490, 2863, 281, 917, 412, 257, 11638, 12569, 770, 7696, 538, 264, 14181, 11, 406, 264, 15149, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 47190, "start": 491.91999999999996, "end": 493.44, "text": " Right. You are strapped in for the ride.", "tokens": [51366, 1779, 13, 509, 366, 2148, 3320, 294, 337, 264, 5077, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 47190, "start": 493.56, "end": 498.32, "text": " And to maintain that narrative momentum, complex caveats are inevitably cut.", "tokens": [51448, 400, 281, 6909, 300, 9977, 11244, 11, 3997, 11730, 1720, 366, 28171, 1723, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 47190, "start": 498.38, "end": 499.94, "text": " Because they slow things down.", "tokens": [51689, 1436, 436, 2964, 721, 760, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253485361735026, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423653886529777e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 49994, "start": 499.94, "end": 507.76, "text": " Tangents, towner examples, and methodological doubts, which, you know, in theoretical work, often carry the highest density of actual information.", "tokens": [50365, 22063, 791, 11, 3954, 260, 5110, 11, 293, 3170, 4383, 22618, 11, 597, 11, 291, 458, 11, 294, 20864, 589, 11, 2049, 3985, 264, 6343, 10305, 295, 3539, 1589, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 49994, "start": 507.98, "end": 508.62, "text": " Right. The nuance.", "tokens": [50767, 1779, 13, 440, 42625, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 49994, "start": 508.94, "end": 510.78, "text": " That nuance is systematically pruned.", "tokens": [50815, 663, 42625, 307, 39531, 582, 43703, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 49994, "start": 511.48, "end": 519.1, "text": " The creator is forced to construct a singular, closure-seeking narrative flow, even when the topic demands branching exploration.", "tokens": [50942, 440, 14181, 307, 7579, 281, 7690, 257, 20010, 11, 24653, 12, 405, 38437, 9977, 3095, 11, 754, 562, 264, 4829, 15107, 9819, 278, 16197, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 49994, "start": 519.36, "end": 520.68, "text": " I feel that one intensely.", "tokens": [51336, 286, 841, 300, 472, 43235, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 49994, "start": 520.92, "end": 521.12, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51414, 865, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 49994, "start": 521.46, "end": 525.32, "text": " You are forced to choose between accuracy and audience retention.", "tokens": [51441, 509, 366, 7579, 281, 2826, 1296, 14170, 293, 4034, 22871, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 49994, "start": 525.62, "end": 527.48, "text": " It is a terrible choice to have to make.", "tokens": [51649, 467, 307, 257, 6237, 3922, 281, 362, 281, 652, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09719089039585047, "compression_ratio": 1.6143344709897611, "no_speech_prob": 1.5489077034858134e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 52748, "start": 527.48, "end": 534.86, "text": " If you pause to explain a crucial but dry statistical caveat, the algorithm punishes you because viewers click away.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 10465, 281, 2903, 257, 11462, 457, 4016, 22820, 43012, 11, 264, 9284, 9842, 279, 291, 570, 8499, 2052, 1314, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 52748, "start": 534.96, "end": 535.98, "text": " So you just smooth it over.", "tokens": [50739, 407, 291, 445, 5508, 309, 670, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 52748, "start": 536.22, "end": 539.48, "text": " You sand down the edges of reality to fit it into a cinematic timeline.", "tokens": [50802, 509, 4932, 760, 264, 8819, 295, 4103, 281, 3318, 309, 666, 257, 32250, 12933, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 52748, "start": 539.6800000000001, "end": 543.48, "text": " Which directly causes the third pathology, the complete loss of provenance.", "tokens": [50975, 3013, 3838, 7700, 264, 2636, 3100, 1793, 11, 264, 3566, 4470, 295, 12785, 719, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 52748, "start": 543.54, "end": 544.62, "text": " Okay. Provenance.", "tokens": [51168, 1033, 13, 1705, 553, 719, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 52748, "start": 544.6800000000001, "end": 544.9, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51225, 865, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 52748, "start": 545.24, "end": 550.72, "text": " Meaning the trackable history of where a piece of information came from and how it evolved over time.", "tokens": [51253, 19948, 264, 2837, 712, 2503, 295, 689, 257, 2522, 295, 1589, 1361, 490, 293, 577, 309, 14178, 670, 565, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09970334432657482, "compression_ratio": 1.5597014925373134, "no_speech_prob": 1.4384646902440568e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 55072, "start": 550.72, "end": 556.52, "text": " Precisely. Consider two versions of a recorded lecture uploaded to a platform, maybe a year apart.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 17416, 732, 9606, 295, 257, 8287, 7991, 17135, 281, 257, 3663, 11, 1310, 257, 1064, 4936, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 55072, "start": 556.6800000000001, "end": 556.9200000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50663, 1033, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 55072, "start": 557.28, "end": 560.46, "text": " The platform treats them as entirely alien, unrelated artifacts.", "tokens": [50693, 440, 3663, 19566, 552, 382, 7696, 12319, 11, 38967, 24617, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 55072, "start": 561.12, "end": 564.44, "text": " There is no automated diff command to show you what the professor changed.", "tokens": [50885, 821, 307, 572, 18473, 7593, 5622, 281, 855, 291, 437, 264, 8304, 3105, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 55072, "start": 564.5400000000001, "end": 565.6600000000001, "text": " There are no track changes.", "tokens": [51056, 821, 366, 572, 2837, 2962, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 55072, "start": 565.96, "end": 568.94, "text": " There is no errata sheet embedded in the file.", "tokens": [51127, 821, 307, 572, 45267, 3274, 8193, 16741, 294, 264, 3991, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 55072, "start": 569.3000000000001, "end": 571.48, "text": " If you want to know how the professor's thoughts evolved,", "tokens": [51294, 759, 291, 528, 281, 458, 577, 264, 8304, 311, 4598, 14178, 11, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010083240011465, "compression_ratio": 1.632034632034632, "no_speech_prob": 2.2539387890818663e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 57148, "start": 571.48, "end": 578.14, "text": " you literally have to open two browser windows and manually cross-reference the audio, second by second.", "tokens": [50365, 291, 3736, 362, 281, 1269, 732, 11185, 9309, 293, 16945, 3278, 12, 265, 5158, 264, 6278, 11, 1150, 538, 1150, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 57148, "start": 578.2, "end": 579.82, "text": " Which nobody's going to do.", "tokens": [50701, 3013, 5079, 311, 516, 281, 360, 13, 50782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 57148, "start": 579.9, "end": 581.94, "text": " The system itself is entirely amnesic.", "tokens": [50786, 440, 1185, 2564, 307, 7696, 669, 4081, 299, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 57148, "start": 582.12, "end": 584.72, "text": " It has absolute no memory of how things came to be.", "tokens": [50897, 467, 575, 8236, 572, 4675, 295, 577, 721, 1361, 281, 312, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 57148, "start": 585.0, "end": 588.6800000000001, "text": " Which leads to the final and, frankly, I think the most dangerous pathology.", "tokens": [51041, 3013, 6689, 281, 264, 2572, 293, 11, 11939, 11, 286, 519, 264, 881, 5795, 3100, 1793, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 57148, "start": 589.84, "end": 591.66, "text": " The asymmetry of authority.", "tokens": [51283, 440, 37277, 9889, 295, 8281, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 57148, "start": 592.32, "end": 596.3000000000001, "text": " I see this happening constantly in political and scientific discourse online.", "tokens": [51407, 286, 536, 341, 2737, 6460, 294, 3905, 293, 8134, 23938, 2950, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1801857566833496, "compression_ratio": 1.5797665369649805, "no_speech_prob": 1.882977714723344e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 59630, "start": 596.3, "end": 597.26, "text": " Oh, it is everywhere.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 309, 307, 5315, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 59630, "start": 597.9799999999999, "end": 603.14, "text": " And this happens because the medium itself actively resists any kind of rebuttal in kind.", "tokens": [50449, 400, 341, 2314, 570, 264, 6399, 2564, 13022, 725, 1751, 604, 733, 295, 319, 5955, 32831, 294, 733, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 59630, "start": 603.56, "end": 604.16, "text": " What do you mean by that?", "tokens": [50728, 708, 360, 291, 914, 538, 300, 30, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 59630, "start": 604.4399999999999, "end": 608.88, "text": " When a claim is presented in a highly polished, heavily edited video format,", "tokens": [50772, 1133, 257, 3932, 307, 8212, 294, 257, 5405, 29079, 11, 10950, 23016, 960, 7877, 11, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 59630, "start": 609.18, "end": 611.4399999999999, "text": " it acquires an artificial authority.", "tokens": [51009, 309, 6667, 3145, 364, 11677, 8281, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 59630, "start": 611.68, "end": 613.18, "text": " Because it looks expensive and professional.", "tokens": [51134, 1436, 309, 1542, 5124, 293, 4843, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 59630, "start": 613.4599999999999, "end": 613.7199999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51223, 1779, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 59630, "start": 614.12, "end": 617.9799999999999, "text": " The viewer cannot pause the video and interrogate the data feeding the charts.", "tokens": [51256, 440, 16767, 2644, 10465, 264, 960, 293, 24871, 473, 264, 1412, 12919, 264, 17767, 13, 51449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 59630, "start": 618.24, "end": 620.26, "text": " They cannot query the underlying assumptions.", "tokens": [51462, 814, 2644, 14581, 264, 14217, 17695, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 59630, "start": 620.5999999999999, "end": 621.9399999999999, "text": " You just have to take their word for it.", "tokens": [51580, 509, 445, 362, 281, 747, 641, 1349, 337, 309, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 59630, "start": 621.9399999999999, "end": 626.24, "text": " The format renders the claims effectively unfalsifiable in the moment of consumption.", "tokens": [51647, 440, 7877, 6125, 433, 264, 9441, 8659, 3971, 1124, 30876, 294, 264, 1623, 295, 12126, 13, 51862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15504804298059263, "compression_ratio": 1.6716867469879517, "no_speech_prob": 1.9508784778604626e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 62630, "start": 626.8399999999999, "end": 627.76, "text": " It is a monolith.", "tokens": [50392, 467, 307, 257, 1108, 29131, 13, 50438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 62630, "start": 628.3399999999999, "end": 628.4399999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50467, 865, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 62630, "start": 628.76, "end": 634.8399999999999, "text": " If someone spends $50,000 making a slick documentary full of terrible science, right,", "tokens": [50488, 759, 1580, 25620, 1848, 2803, 11, 1360, 1455, 257, 37406, 15674, 1577, 295, 6237, 3497, 11, 558, 11, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 62630, "start": 635.1999999999999, "end": 640.8599999999999, "text": " and a brilliant postdoc writes a plain text blog post completely debunking it,", "tokens": [50810, 293, 257, 10248, 2183, 39966, 13657, 257, 11121, 2487, 6968, 2183, 2584, 3001, 3197, 278, 309, 11, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 62630, "start": 641.62, "end": 645.4799999999999, "text": " the human brain naturally grants more weight to the documentary.", "tokens": [51131, 264, 1952, 3567, 8195, 16101, 544, 3364, 281, 264, 15674, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 62630, "start": 645.8399999999999, "end": 649.0999999999999, "text": " We are wired to trust the high production value.", "tokens": [51342, 492, 366, 27415, 281, 3361, 264, 1090, 4265, 2158, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 62630, "start": 649.0999999999999, "end": 652.7199999999999, "text": " The presentation layer completely hijacks our critical thinking.", "tokens": [51505, 440, 5860, 4583, 2584, 10625, 7424, 527, 4924, 1953, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2093375735812717, "compression_ratio": 1.555084745762712, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610535867432995e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 65272, "start": 653.2, "end": 656.64, "text": " At that postdoc, they can't inject their rebuttal into the documentary.", "tokens": [50389, 1711, 300, 2183, 39966, 11, 436, 393, 380, 10711, 641, 319, 5955, 32831, 666, 264, 15674, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 65272, "start": 657.14, "end": 658.58, "text": " They are locked out of the rendering.", "tokens": [50586, 814, 366, 9376, 484, 295, 264, 22407, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 65272, "start": 658.8000000000001, "end": 661.9200000000001, "text": " The conflation of source and rendering is exactly what locks them out.", "tokens": [50669, 440, 1497, 24278, 295, 4009, 293, 22407, 307, 2293, 437, 20703, 552, 484, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 65272, "start": 662.2, "end": 668.0600000000001, "text": " As long as the MP4 is the master copy, the viewer is entirely at the mercy of the creator's editorial choices.", "tokens": [50839, 1018, 938, 382, 264, 14146, 19, 307, 264, 4505, 5055, 11, 264, 16767, 307, 7696, 412, 264, 13174, 295, 264, 14181, 311, 33412, 7994, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 65272, "start": 668.3000000000001, "end": 668.52, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51144, 1033, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 65272, "start": 668.64, "end": 672.1, "text": " So the disease is the conflation of the source and the presentation.", "tokens": [51161, 407, 264, 4752, 307, 264, 1497, 24278, 295, 264, 4009, 293, 264, 5860, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 65272, "start": 672.5, "end": 673.86, "text": " How do we actually cure it?", "tokens": [51354, 1012, 360, 321, 767, 13698, 309, 30, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 65272, "start": 673.94, "end": 675.0600000000001, "text": " That is the big question.", "tokens": [51426, 663, 307, 264, 955, 1168, 13, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1549527967298353, "compression_ratio": 1.6867469879518073, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858796480888726e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 67506, "start": 675.06, "end": 681.0, "text": " How do we build a system that separates the C++ source code from the compiled binary in media?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 360, 321, 1322, 257, 1185, 300, 34149, 264, 383, 25472, 4009, 3089, 490, 264, 36548, 17434, 294, 3021, 30, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 67506, "start": 681.8199999999999, "end": 686.8599999999999, "text": " To understand the mechanics of this, let's pivot to the first source, the buffer world specification.", "tokens": [50703, 1407, 1223, 264, 12939, 295, 341, 11, 718, 311, 14538, 281, 264, 700, 4009, 11, 264, 21762, 1002, 31256, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 67506, "start": 687.06, "end": 688.0, "text": " Yes, buffer world.", "tokens": [50965, 1079, 11, 21762, 1002, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 67506, "start": 688.18, "end": 692.76, "text": " Because they are attempting to do exactly this, but in the highly specific context of a video game.", "tokens": [51021, 1436, 436, 366, 22001, 281, 360, 2293, 341, 11, 457, 294, 264, 5405, 2685, 4319, 295, 257, 960, 1216, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 67506, "start": 693.02, "end": 699.7199999999999, "text": " Buffer world is perhaps the most extreme, pedantic case study of decoupling source and presentation imaginable.", "tokens": [51263, 20254, 260, 1002, 307, 4317, 264, 881, 8084, 11, 5670, 7128, 1389, 2979, 295, 979, 263, 11970, 4009, 293, 5860, 23427, 712, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 67506, "start": 699.8399999999999, "end": 701.18, "text": " Extreme is a good word for it.", "tokens": [51604, 39525, 307, 257, 665, 1349, 337, 309, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10748884894631126, "compression_ratio": 1.6415770609318996, "no_speech_prob": 1.861034113273541e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 70118, "start": 701.18, "end": 704.14, "text": " The concept is a 3D spatial puzzle game.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3410, 307, 257, 805, 35, 23598, 12805, 1216, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 70118, "start": 704.52, "end": 707.4399999999999, "text": " You move around a 3D environment, manipulating objects.", "tokens": [50532, 509, 1286, 926, 257, 805, 35, 2823, 11, 40805, 6565, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 70118, "start": 707.66, "end": 710.54, "text": " But the entire engine is designed to teach Vim.", "tokens": [50689, 583, 264, 2302, 2848, 307, 4761, 281, 2924, 691, 332, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 70118, "start": 710.88, "end": 711.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50850, 1033, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 70118, "start": 711.2399999999999, "end": 720.0999999999999, "text": " And for those who might not spend their days in terminal windows, Vim is a highly complex, incredibly powerful text editor used primarily by programmers.", "tokens": [50868, 400, 337, 729, 567, 1062, 406, 3496, 641, 1708, 294, 14709, 9309, 11, 691, 332, 307, 257, 5405, 3997, 11, 6252, 4005, 2487, 9839, 1143, 10029, 538, 41504, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 70118, "start": 720.4799999999999, "end": 722.9799999999999, "text": " It is infamous for its steep learning curve.", "tokens": [51330, 467, 307, 30769, 337, 1080, 16841, 2539, 7605, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 70118, "start": 723.04, "end": 723.2199999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51458, 1779, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 70118, "start": 723.26, "end": 729.14, "text": " The old joke is that the number one most Googled programming question is just, how do I exit Vim?", "tokens": [51469, 440, 1331, 7647, 307, 300, 264, 1230, 472, 881, 45005, 1493, 9410, 1168, 307, 445, 11, 577, 360, 286, 11043, 691, 332, 30, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 70118, "start": 729.14, "end": 730.26, "text": " It is entirely modal.", "tokens": [51763, 467, 307, 7696, 39745, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12206001912266755, "compression_ratio": 1.5404530744336569, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234807552126251e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 73118, "start": 731.18, "end": 732.26, "text": " You aren't just typing.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 3212, 380, 445, 18444, 13, 50419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11755671446350799, "compression_ratio": 1.502008032128514, "no_speech_prob": 1.9891297810270547e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 73118, "start": 732.52, "end": 738.3, "text": " You are issuing commands that combine operators and motions to manipulate text at blazing speeds.", "tokens": [50432, 509, 366, 43214, 16901, 300, 10432, 19077, 293, 27500, 281, 20459, 2487, 412, 16379, 8781, 16411, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11755671446350799, "compression_ratio": 1.502008032128514, "no_speech_prob": 1.9891297810270547e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 73118, "start": 738.4599999999999, "end": 740.18, "text": " It's like playing a piano almost.", "tokens": [50729, 467, 311, 411, 2433, 257, 9211, 1920, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11755671446350799, "compression_ratio": 1.502008032128514, "no_speech_prob": 1.9891297810270547e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 73118, "start": 740.18, "end": 744.9599999999999, "text": " Building a 3D game to teach this muscle memory is a brilliant pedagogical concept.", "tokens": [50815, 18974, 257, 805, 35, 1216, 281, 2924, 341, 8679, 4675, 307, 257, 10248, 5670, 31599, 804, 3410, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11755671446350799, "compression_ratio": 1.502008032128514, "no_speech_prob": 1.9891297810270547e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 73118, "start": 745.42, "end": 752.5799999999999, "text": " However, the creators of buffer world established a non-negotiable architectural rule before they wrote a single line of graphics code.", "tokens": [51077, 2908, 11, 264, 16039, 295, 21762, 1002, 7545, 257, 2107, 12, 28561, 8206, 712, 26621, 4978, 949, 436, 4114, 257, 2167, 1622, 295, 11837, 3089, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11755671446350799, "compression_ratio": 1.502008032128514, "no_speech_prob": 1.9891297810270547e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 75258, "start": 752.58, "end": 754.96, "text": " And they call it their phase zero correctness bar.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 818, 309, 641, 5574, 4018, 3006, 1287, 2159, 13, 50484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14112741030179538, "compression_ratio": 1.4508670520231215, "no_speech_prob": 2.3993133868582817e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 75258, "start": 754.96, "end": 766.6600000000001, "text": " The specification dictates that the input parser, so the actual core logic engine that takes a user's keystrokes and figures out what they mean in the context of Vim, must be built headless.", "tokens": [50484, 440, 31256, 12569, 1024, 300, 264, 4846, 21156, 260, 11, 370, 264, 3539, 4965, 9952, 2848, 300, 2516, 257, 4195, 311, 2141, 27616, 5993, 293, 9624, 484, 437, 436, 914, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 691, 332, 11, 1633, 312, 3094, 1378, 1832, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14112741030179538, "compression_ratio": 1.4508670520231215, "no_speech_prob": 2.3993133868582817e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 75258, "start": 767.2, "end": 767.72, "text": " Headless.", "tokens": [51096, 11398, 1832, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14112741030179538, "compression_ratio": 1.4508670520231215, "no_speech_prob": 2.3993133868582817e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 76772, "start": 767.72, "end": 773.6, "text": " Now, I know what that means in server architecture, but what does a headless parser mean for a 3D video game?", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 286, 458, 437, 300, 1355, 294, 7154, 9482, 11, 457, 437, 775, 257, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 914, 337, 257, 805, 35, 960, 1216, 30, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11463572762229225, "compression_ratio": 1.3769633507853403, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468336668991947e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 76772, "start": 773.72, "end": 779.1, "text": " Well, in traditional game development, the player's input is often tightly coupled to the visual representation.", "tokens": [50665, 1042, 11, 294, 5164, 1216, 3250, 11, 264, 4256, 311, 4846, 307, 2049, 21952, 29482, 281, 264, 5056, 10290, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11463572762229225, "compression_ratio": 1.3769633507853403, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468336668991947e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 76772, "start": 779.5600000000001, "end": 781.12, "text": " Like in Unity or Unreal Engine.", "tokens": [50957, 1743, 294, 27913, 420, 34464, 7659, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11463572762229225, "compression_ratio": 1.3769633507853403, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468336668991947e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 76772, "start": 781.34, "end": 781.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51046, 7587, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11463572762229225, "compression_ratio": 1.3769633507853403, "no_speech_prob": 1.8468336668991947e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 78178, "start": 781.78, "end": 788.04, "text": " Pressing the W key might directly apply a physical force to the 3D character model, pushing it forward.", "tokens": [50365, 6776, 278, 264, 343, 2141, 1062, 3838, 3079, 257, 4001, 3464, 281, 264, 805, 35, 2517, 2316, 11, 7380, 309, 2128, 13, 50678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10569477081298828, "compression_ratio": 1.4791666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918399411118944e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 78178, "start": 788.56, "end": 792.66, "text": " The physics engine, the rendering, and the input are all talking to each other constantly.", "tokens": [50704, 440, 10649, 2848, 11, 264, 22407, 11, 293, 264, 4846, 366, 439, 1417, 281, 1184, 661, 6460, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10569477081298828, "compression_ratio": 1.4791666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918399411118944e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 78178, "start": 792.76, "end": 793.98, "text": " They are all tangled up.", "tokens": [50914, 814, 366, 439, 47192, 493, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10569477081298828, "compression_ratio": 1.4791666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918399411118944e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 78178, "start": 794.12, "end": 797.42, "text": " Headless, in the buffer world spec, mandates the exact opposite.", "tokens": [50982, 11398, 1832, 11, 294, 264, 21762, 1002, 1608, 11, 48662, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10569477081298828, "compression_ratio": 1.4791666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5918399411118944e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 79742, "start": 797.42, "end": 806.54, "text": " It means the core logic of parsing Vim commands and updating the text buffer must be implemented, compiled, and exhaustively unit tested in an absolute void.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1355, 264, 4965, 9952, 295, 21156, 278, 691, 332, 16901, 293, 25113, 264, 2487, 21762, 1633, 312, 12270, 11, 36548, 11, 293, 14687, 3413, 4985, 8246, 294, 364, 8236, 22009, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 79742, "start": 806.66, "end": 808.02, "text": " Zero rendering dependencies.", "tokens": [50827, 17182, 22407, 36606, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 79742, "start": 808.24, "end": 808.4799999999999, "text": " None.", "tokens": [50906, 14492, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 79742, "start": 808.7199999999999, "end": 812.38, "text": " No graphics libraries, no lighting engines, no 3D coordinate math.", "tokens": [50930, 883, 11837, 15148, 11, 572, 9577, 12982, 11, 572, 805, 35, 15670, 5221, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 79742, "start": 812.9399999999999, "end": 814.3, "text": " Pure abstract logic.", "tokens": [51141, 29474, 12649, 9952, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 79742, "start": 814.4, "end": 819.5, "text": " So you have this invisible brain sitting in the dark, perfectly simulating a text file, and taking keystrokes.", "tokens": [51214, 407, 291, 362, 341, 14603, 3567, 3798, 294, 264, 2877, 11, 6239, 1034, 12162, 257, 2487, 3991, 11, 293, 1940, 2141, 27616, 5993, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 79742, "start": 819.8, "end": 824.9, "text": " And only after that brain is flawless do you attach a 3D world to it.", "tokens": [51484, 400, 787, 934, 300, 3567, 307, 45693, 360, 291, 5085, 257, 805, 35, 1002, 281, 309, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12249036805819621, "compression_ratio": 1.5841924398625429, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011292548219092e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 82490, "start": 824.9, "end": 827.92, "text": " This is codified as the fidelity principle.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 17656, 2587, 382, 264, 46404, 8665, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 82490, "start": 828.4, "end": 833.3, "text": " The specification enforces a strict, immutable, one-way flow of data.", "tokens": [50540, 440, 31256, 25495, 887, 257, 10910, 11, 3397, 32148, 11, 472, 12, 676, 3095, 295, 1412, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 82490, "start": 833.5, "end": 834.0, "text": " One way.", "tokens": [50795, 1485, 636, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 82490, "start": 834.4399999999999, "end": 835.4599999999999, "text": " Okay, walk me through that.", "tokens": [50842, 1033, 11, 1792, 385, 807, 300, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 82490, "start": 835.86, "end": 837.04, "text": " The user presses a key.", "tokens": [50913, 440, 4195, 40892, 257, 2141, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 82490, "start": 837.68, "end": 839.86, "text": " The input parser interprets it.", "tokens": [51004, 440, 4846, 21156, 260, 17489, 1373, 309, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 82490, "start": 840.16, "end": 845.3199999999999, "text": " The parser updates the abstract buffer model, which is the hidden, headless state.", "tokens": [51128, 440, 21156, 260, 9205, 264, 12649, 21762, 2316, 11, 597, 307, 264, 7633, 11, 1378, 1832, 1785, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 82490, "start": 845.4399999999999, "end": 845.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51392, 1779, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 82490, "start": 845.9, "end": 851.12, "text": " Finally, the renderer takes a read-only snapshot of that state and updates the 3D visuals.", "tokens": [51415, 6288, 11, 264, 15529, 260, 2516, 257, 1401, 12, 25202, 30163, 295, 300, 1785, 293, 9205, 264, 805, 35, 26035, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 82490, "start": 851.54, "end": 854.68, "text": " Data never flows backward from the renderer to the parser.", "tokens": [51697, 11888, 1128, 12867, 23897, 490, 264, 15529, 260, 281, 264, 21156, 260, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17909031822567895, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691664105923266e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 85468, "start": 854.68, "end": 857.28, "text": " But wait, wouldn't that make game development incredibly tedious?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 2759, 380, 300, 652, 1216, 3250, 6252, 38284, 30, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 85468, "start": 857.4599999999999, "end": 858.62, "text": " Oh, extremely tedious.", "tokens": [50504, 876, 11, 4664, 38284, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 85468, "start": 858.7199999999999, "end": 865.6999999999999, "text": " Let's say a developer makes really cool jump animation, but they realize it takes slightly longer to animate than the headless parser expects.", "tokens": [50567, 961, 311, 584, 257, 10754, 1669, 534, 1627, 3012, 9603, 11, 457, 436, 4325, 309, 2516, 4748, 2854, 281, 36439, 813, 264, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 33280, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 85468, "start": 865.92, "end": 867.2399999999999, "text": " Right, a timing mismatch.", "tokens": [50927, 1779, 11, 257, 10822, 23220, 852, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 85468, "start": 867.42, "end": 875.0999999999999, "text": " The natural instinct in game design is to just tweak the parser logic, maybe add a few frames of delay so the animation looks smooth and the game feels better.", "tokens": [51002, 440, 3303, 16556, 294, 1216, 1715, 307, 281, 445, 29879, 264, 21156, 260, 9952, 11, 1310, 909, 257, 1326, 12083, 295, 8577, 370, 264, 9603, 1542, 5508, 293, 264, 1216, 3417, 1101, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 85468, "start": 875.2399999999999, "end": 880.64, "text": " If a developer submitted code doing that to Buffer Worlds, the pull request would be rejected instantly.", "tokens": [51393, 759, 257, 10754, 14405, 3089, 884, 300, 281, 20254, 260, 43003, 11, 264, 2235, 5308, 576, 312, 15749, 13518, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 85468, "start": 881.0, "end": 882.38, "text": " Instantly rejected, wow.", "tokens": [51681, 2730, 3627, 15749, 11, 6076, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09396547032153513, "compression_ratio": 1.6882716049382716, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077921108527017e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 88238, "start": 882.38, "end": 889.14, "text": " If a visual interaction conflicts with actual, real-world VIM behavior, VIM behavior wins unconditionally.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 5056, 9285, 19807, 365, 3539, 11, 957, 12, 13217, 691, 6324, 5223, 11, 691, 6324, 5223, 10641, 34959, 15899, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518884508797292, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.8894167914257354e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 88238, "start": 889.62, "end": 891.46, "text": " It is like a puppeteer in a puppet.", "tokens": [50727, 467, 307, 411, 257, 17014, 3498, 260, 294, 257, 32107, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518884508797292, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.8894167914257354e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 88238, "start": 891.7, "end": 893.46, "text": " That is a great way to look at it.", "tokens": [50831, 663, 307, 257, 869, 636, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518884508797292, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.8894167914257354e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 88238, "start": 893.6, "end": 897.0, "text": " The headless parser is the puppeteer, sitting in the dark above the stage.", "tokens": [50926, 440, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 307, 264, 17014, 3498, 260, 11, 3798, 294, 264, 2877, 3673, 264, 3233, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518884508797292, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.8894167914257354e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 88238, "start": 897.48, "end": 900.58, "text": " The 3D game is just a puppet made of glowing polygons.", "tokens": [51120, 440, 805, 35, 1216, 307, 445, 257, 32107, 1027, 295, 27064, 6754, 70, 892, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1518884508797292, "compression_ratio": 1.5743589743589743, "no_speech_prob": 1.8894167914257354e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 90058, "start": 900.58, "end": 906.1800000000001, "text": " If the puppet ever tries to pull its own strings, the system fundamentally breaks.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 32107, 1562, 9898, 281, 2235, 1080, 1065, 13985, 11, 264, 1185, 17879, 9857, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 90058, "start": 906.5600000000001, "end": 908.96, "text": " The rendering layer can only consume the truth.", "tokens": [50664, 440, 22407, 4583, 393, 787, 14732, 264, 3494, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 90058, "start": 909.1600000000001, "end": 910.1800000000001, "text": " It can never dictate it.", "tokens": [50794, 467, 393, 1128, 36071, 309, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 90058, "start": 910.46, "end": 910.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50859, 7587, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 90058, "start": 911.4200000000001, "end": 915.62, "text": " But I have to ask, does this dogmatic strictness make the game worse?", "tokens": [50907, 583, 286, 362, 281, 1029, 11, 775, 341, 3000, 25915, 10910, 1287, 652, 264, 1216, 5324, 30, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 90058, "start": 916.3000000000001, "end": 919.4200000000001, "text": " Does it sacrifice fun at the altar of accuracy?", "tokens": [51151, 4402, 309, 11521, 1019, 412, 264, 31435, 295, 14170, 30, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 90058, "start": 920.08, "end": 921.08, "text": " Well, it depends on the goal.", "tokens": [51340, 1042, 11, 309, 5946, 322, 264, 3387, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18423564093453543, "compression_ratio": 1.4786729857819905, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179329569489866e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 92108, "start": 921.08, "end": 928.0400000000001, "text": " If the goal is just to make a fun arcade game loosely inspired by text editing, then yes, this strictness ruins it.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 3387, 307, 445, 281, 652, 257, 1019, 25664, 1216, 37966, 7547, 538, 2487, 10000, 11, 550, 2086, 11, 341, 10910, 1287, 24747, 309, 13, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09703741754804339, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.6168963954191207e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 92108, "start": 928.1600000000001, "end": 928.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50719, 1779, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09703741754804339, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.6168963954191207e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 92108, "start": 928.58, "end": 931.32, "text": " But the goal of Buffer World is educational transfer.", "tokens": [50740, 583, 264, 3387, 295, 20254, 260, 3937, 307, 10189, 5003, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09703741754804339, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.6168963954191207e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 92108, "start": 931.84, "end": 938.84, "text": " If the game bends the rules of VIM to make an animation look cooler, the player's muscle memory adapts to the bent rule.", "tokens": [50903, 759, 264, 1216, 42990, 264, 4474, 295, 691, 6324, 281, 652, 364, 9603, 574, 15566, 11, 264, 4256, 311, 8679, 4675, 23169, 1373, 281, 264, 14075, 4978, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09703741754804339, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.6168963954191207e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 92108, "start": 939.1, "end": 939.74, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51266, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09703741754804339, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.6168963954191207e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 93974, "start": 939.74, "end": 944.54, "text": " When they eventually go to work and open real VIM on a server, their muscle memory will betray them.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 436, 4728, 352, 281, 589, 293, 1269, 957, 691, 6324, 322, 257, 7154, 11, 641, 8679, 4675, 486, 15560, 552, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 93974, "start": 944.72, "end": 945.96, "text": " Because they learned a lie.", "tokens": [50614, 1436, 436, 3264, 257, 4544, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 93974, "start": 946.36, "end": 946.8, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50696, 7587, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 93974, "start": 947.3, "end": 956.44, "text": " By enforcing this one-way data flow, the game guarantees that the canonical source, the absolute unforgiving reality of VIM mechanics, remains pure.", "tokens": [50743, 3146, 25495, 2175, 341, 472, 12, 676, 1412, 3095, 11, 264, 1216, 32567, 300, 264, 46491, 4009, 11, 264, 8236, 31411, 15441, 4103, 295, 691, 6324, 12939, 11, 7023, 6075, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 93974, "start": 956.98, "end": 961.12, "text": " The 3D world is just a disposable visualization of that truth.", "tokens": [51227, 440, 805, 35, 1002, 307, 445, 257, 41578, 25801, 295, 300, 3494, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 93974, "start": 961.28, "end": 963.28, "text": " Here is where it gets really interesting, though.", "tokens": [51442, 1692, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 11, 1673, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 93974, "start": 963.6, "end": 969.04, "text": " Because the truth of VIM is not a clean, elegant set of mathematical axioms.", "tokens": [51558, 1436, 264, 3494, 295, 691, 6324, 307, 406, 257, 2541, 11, 21117, 992, 295, 18894, 6360, 72, 4785, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 93974, "start": 969.04, "end": 969.66, "text": " Not at all.", "tokens": [51830, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11418106479029502, "compression_ratio": 1.5895765472312704, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983050386664255e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 96974, "start": 969.74, "end": 977.08, "text": " It is a messy, deeply human artifact, full of bizarre exceptions, historical quirks, and highly pedantic rules.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 16191, 11, 8760, 1952, 34806, 11, 1577, 295, 18265, 22847, 11, 8584, 35645, 1694, 11, 293, 5405, 5670, 7128, 4474, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 96974, "start": 977.22, "end": 979.02, "text": " Decades of accumulated quirks.", "tokens": [50739, 12427, 2977, 295, 31346, 35645, 1694, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 96974, "start": 979.1800000000001, "end": 987.48, "text": " To understand why the headless parser has to be so heavily fortified against the rendering layer, we have to look at the granular mechanics Buffer World is forced to replicate.", "tokens": [50837, 1407, 1223, 983, 264, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 575, 281, 312, 370, 10950, 5009, 2587, 1970, 264, 22407, 4583, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 264, 39962, 12939, 20254, 260, 3937, 307, 7579, 281, 25356, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 96974, "start": 987.48, "end": 993.14, "text": " The specification spends pages detailing the exact behaviors that most VIM clones get wrong.", "tokens": [51252, 440, 31256, 25620, 7183, 42459, 264, 1900, 15501, 300, 881, 691, 6324, 43803, 483, 2085, 13, 51535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 96974, "start": 993.66, "end": 994.92, "text": " Let's look at count multiplication.", "tokens": [51561, 961, 311, 574, 412, 1207, 27290, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 96974, "start": 995.0600000000001, "end": 995.66, "text": " Okay, let's do it.", "tokens": [51631, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 360, 309, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 96974, "start": 995.88, "end": 999.04, "text": " In VIM, a user can prefix commands with numbers to repeat them.", "tokens": [51672, 682, 691, 6324, 11, 257, 4195, 393, 46969, 16901, 365, 3547, 281, 7149, 552, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10884508490562439, "compression_ratio": 1.589820359281437, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 99904, "start": 999.04, "end": 1005.48, "text": " Right, if I wanted to delete three words, I could type D for delete, three for the count, and W for word, D3W.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 498, 286, 1415, 281, 12097, 1045, 2283, 11, 286, 727, 2010, 413, 337, 12097, 11, 1045, 337, 264, 1207, 11, 293, 343, 337, 1349, 11, 413, 18, 54, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374130884806316, "compression_ratio": 1.445945945945946, "no_speech_prob": 2.5742921249544137e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 99904, "start": 1005.6999999999999, "end": 1007.7199999999999, "text": " But you can also prefix the operator itself.", "tokens": [50698, 583, 291, 393, 611, 46969, 264, 12973, 2564, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374130884806316, "compression_ratio": 1.445945945945946, "no_speech_prob": 2.5742921249544137e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 99904, "start": 1007.88, "end": 1011.54, "text": " You could type 3DW, which means three times delete a word.", "tokens": [50807, 509, 727, 2010, 805, 35, 54, 11, 597, 1355, 1045, 1413, 12097, 257, 1349, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12374130884806316, "compression_ratio": 1.445945945945946, "no_speech_prob": 2.5742921249544137e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 101154, "start": 1011.54, "end": 1014.62, "text": " Okay, so the number can go before the action or before the target.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 1230, 393, 352, 949, 264, 3069, 420, 949, 264, 3779, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24582578697983098, "compression_ratio": 1.2347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 3.2667991575752175e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 101154, "start": 1014.88, "end": 1015.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50532, 1779, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24582578697983098, "compression_ratio": 1.2347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 3.2667991575752175e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 101154, "start": 1015.5, "end": 1016.4399999999999, "text": " Or you can do both.", "tokens": [50563, 1610, 291, 393, 360, 1293, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24582578697983098, "compression_ratio": 1.2347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 3.2667991575752175e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 101154, "start": 1016.54, "end": 1018.68, "text": " You can type 3D2W.", "tokens": [50615, 509, 393, 2010, 805, 35, 17, 54, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24582578697983098, "compression_ratio": 1.2347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 3.2667991575752175e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 101154, "start": 1018.88, "end": 1021.0999999999999, "text": " Three times delete two words.", "tokens": [50732, 6244, 1413, 12097, 732, 2283, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24582578697983098, "compression_ratio": 1.2347826086956522, "no_speech_prob": 3.2667991575752175e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 102110, "start": 1021.1, "end": 1024.52, "text": " So mathematically, that is deleting six words.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 44003, 11, 300, 307, 48946, 2309, 2283, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13563919067382812, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 2.8942692426731087e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 102110, "start": 1024.52, "end": 1031.06, "text": " Yes, but the parser cannot just trigger the delete animation three times in a row, each deleting two words.", "tokens": [50536, 1079, 11, 457, 264, 21156, 260, 2644, 445, 7875, 264, 12097, 9603, 1045, 1413, 294, 257, 5386, 11, 1184, 48946, 732, 2283, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13563919067382812, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 2.8942692426731087e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 102110, "start": 1031.22, "end": 1031.6200000000001, "text": " Why not?", "tokens": [50871, 1545, 406, 30, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13563919067382812, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 2.8942692426731087e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 102110, "start": 1031.74, "end": 1039.22, "text": " The specification requires the parser to construct an abstract syntax tree that mathematically resolves the user's intent before execution.", "tokens": [50897, 440, 31256, 7029, 264, 21156, 260, 281, 7690, 364, 12649, 28431, 4230, 300, 44003, 7923, 977, 264, 4195, 311, 8446, 949, 15058, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13563919067382812, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 2.8942692426731087e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 102110, "start": 1039.56, "end": 1040.04, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51288, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13563919067382812, "compression_ratio": 1.5544554455445545, "no_speech_prob": 2.8942692426731087e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 104004, "start": 1040.04, "end": 1048.92, "text": " Typing 3D2W must resolve internally to the exact same canonical command object as D6W or 6DW.", "tokens": [50365, 5569, 3381, 805, 35, 17, 54, 1633, 14151, 19501, 281, 264, 1900, 912, 46491, 5622, 2657, 382, 413, 21, 54, 420, 1386, 35, 54, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1112067652683632, "compression_ratio": 1.6062992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773154708754398e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 104004, "start": 1049.52, "end": 1055.02, "text": " The headless state must multiply the counts and present a unified delete six word state to the renderer.", "tokens": [50839, 440, 1378, 1832, 1785, 1633, 12972, 264, 14893, 293, 1974, 257, 26787, 12097, 2309, 1349, 1785, 281, 264, 15529, 260, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1112067652683632, "compression_ratio": 1.6062992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773154708754398e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 104004, "start": 1055.1, "end": 1062.48, "text": " Because if the renderer just watched the keystrokes and blindly played an animation, it wouldn't actually understand the logical structure of the edit.", "tokens": [51118, 1436, 498, 264, 15529, 260, 445, 6337, 264, 2141, 27616, 5993, 293, 47744, 3737, 364, 9603, 11, 309, 2759, 380, 767, 1223, 264, 14978, 3877, 295, 264, 8129, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1112067652683632, "compression_ratio": 1.6062992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773154708754398e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 104004, "start": 1062.62, "end": 1063.96, "text": " It would just be parroting inputs.", "tokens": [51494, 467, 576, 445, 312, 42462, 278, 15743, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1112067652683632, "compression_ratio": 1.6062992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773154708754398e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 104004, "start": 1064.1, "end": 1064.92, "text": " It would be faking it.", "tokens": [51568, 467, 576, 312, 283, 2456, 309, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1112067652683632, "compression_ratio": 1.6062992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.3773154708754398e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 106492, "start": 1064.92, "end": 1065.96, "text": " What about the cursor?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 466, 264, 28169, 30, 50417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 106492, "start": 1066.7, "end": 1070.2, "text": " The spec seems obsessed with exactly where the cursor lands after an operation.", "tokens": [50454, 440, 1608, 2544, 16923, 365, 2293, 689, 264, 28169, 5949, 934, 364, 6916, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 106492, "start": 1070.5, "end": 1075.3200000000002, "text": " Cursor invariants are the Achilles heel of almost every piece of software that tries to emulate Vim.", "tokens": [50644, 383, 2156, 284, 33270, 1719, 366, 264, 15847, 14835, 9430, 295, 1920, 633, 2522, 295, 4722, 300, 9898, 281, 45497, 691, 332, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 106492, "start": 1075.48, "end": 1076.88, "text": " Why is that so hard to get right?", "tokens": [50893, 1545, 307, 300, 370, 1152, 281, 483, 558, 30, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 106492, "start": 1077.24, "end": 1085.0800000000002, "text": " Developers often get the text modification right, like the correct words disappear from the screen, but they leave the cursor in the wrong column.", "tokens": [50981, 11442, 433, 2049, 483, 264, 2487, 26747, 558, 11, 411, 264, 3006, 2283, 11596, 490, 264, 2568, 11, 457, 436, 1856, 264, 28169, 294, 264, 2085, 7738, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 106492, "start": 1085.42, "end": 1086.44, "text": " I know exactly what you mean.", "tokens": [51390, 286, 458, 2293, 437, 291, 914, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 106492, "start": 1087.02, "end": 1093.8600000000001, "text": " I have tried browser extensions that claim to give you Vim key bindings, and they constantly leave my cursor one space off.", "tokens": [51470, 286, 362, 3031, 11185, 25129, 300, 3932, 281, 976, 291, 691, 332, 2141, 14786, 1109, 11, 293, 436, 6460, 1856, 452, 28169, 472, 1901, 766, 13, 51812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11195506900548935, "compression_ratio": 1.713375796178344, "no_speech_prob": 2.280487647679519e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 109386, "start": 1093.86, "end": 1095.1399999999999, "text": " It is so jarring.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 370, 361, 18285, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 109386, "start": 1095.24, "end": 1096.1799999999998, "text": " It drives me insane.", "tokens": [50434, 467, 11754, 385, 10838, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 109386, "start": 1096.3, "end": 1098.0, "text": " It feels like wearing someone else's glasses.", "tokens": [50487, 467, 3417, 411, 4769, 1580, 1646, 311, 10812, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 109386, "start": 1098.34, "end": 1102.52, "text": " That uncanny valley feeling is exactly what Buffer World has to avoid.", "tokens": [50589, 663, 6219, 11612, 17636, 2633, 307, 2293, 437, 20254, 260, 3937, 575, 281, 5042, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 109386, "start": 1102.9599999999998, "end": 1106.3799999999999, "text": " A perfect example is the behavior when leaving insert mode.", "tokens": [50820, 316, 2176, 1365, 307, 264, 5223, 562, 5012, 8969, 4391, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 109386, "start": 1106.62, "end": 1106.8999999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51003, 1033, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 109386, "start": 1107.1799999999998, "end": 1112.5, "text": " In Vim, when you are typing naturally, your cursor represents where the next character will appear.", "tokens": [51031, 682, 691, 332, 11, 562, 291, 366, 18444, 8195, 11, 428, 28169, 8855, 689, 264, 958, 2517, 486, 4204, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 109386, "start": 1113.0, "end": 1116.6799999999998, "text": " It is technically positioned one column past the last character you typed.", "tokens": [51322, 467, 307, 12120, 24889, 472, 7738, 1791, 264, 1036, 2517, 291, 33941, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 109386, "start": 1116.82, "end": 1118.82, "text": " Sure, just like any normal word processor.", "tokens": [51513, 4894, 11, 445, 411, 604, 2710, 1349, 15321, 13, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12207474275068804, "compression_ratio": 1.579136690647482, "no_speech_prob": 3.396682241030291e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 111882, "start": 1118.82, "end": 1124.98, "text": " But when you press the escape key to return to normal command mode, the cursor does not stay in that empty space.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 291, 1886, 264, 7615, 2141, 281, 2736, 281, 2710, 5622, 4391, 11, 264, 28169, 775, 406, 1754, 294, 300, 6707, 1901, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 111882, "start": 1125.1799999999998, "end": 1125.4199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50683, 1779, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 111882, "start": 1125.6599999999999, "end": 1131.78, "text": " It visibly steps backward, one column to the left, resting directly on top of the last character you typed.", "tokens": [50707, 467, 1452, 3545, 4439, 23897, 11, 472, 7738, 281, 264, 1411, 11, 21221, 3838, 322, 1192, 295, 264, 1036, 2517, 291, 33941, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 111882, "start": 1132.02, "end": 1134.6799999999998, "text": " My muscle memory completely expects that jump backward.", "tokens": [51025, 1222, 8679, 4675, 2584, 33280, 300, 3012, 23897, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 111882, "start": 1135.1399999999999, "end": 1139.96, "text": " If I hit escape and the cursor just sits there in the void, I immediately assume the program is frozen.", "tokens": [51181, 759, 286, 2045, 7615, 293, 264, 28169, 445, 12696, 456, 294, 264, 22009, 11, 286, 4258, 6552, 264, 1461, 307, 12496, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 111882, "start": 1140.36, "end": 1143.74, "text": " That backward step is a documented mandatory feature.", "tokens": [51442, 663, 23897, 1823, 307, 257, 23007, 22173, 4111, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 111882, "start": 1144.06, "end": 1145.22, "text": " It is an invariant.", "tokens": [51627, 467, 307, 364, 33270, 394, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 111882, "start": 1145.6599999999999, "end": 1146.9399999999998, "text": " Buffer World has to nail that.", "tokens": [51707, 20254, 260, 3937, 575, 281, 10173, 300, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10212530971558625, "compression_ratio": 1.6655405405405406, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485440179099143e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 114694, "start": 1146.94, "end": 1150.06, "text": " The headless parser must enforce this rigorously.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 1633, 24825, 341, 42191, 5098, 13, 50521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 114694, "start": 1150.68, "end": 1156.3, "text": " When the state transitions from insert to normal, the parser must update the coordinate state of the cursor,", "tokens": [50552, 1133, 264, 1785, 23767, 490, 8969, 281, 2710, 11, 264, 21156, 260, 1633, 5623, 264, 15670, 1785, 295, 264, 28169, 11, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 114694, "start": 1156.72, "end": 1161.74, "text": " and the 3D renderer simply observes that change and moves the player's avatar backward.", "tokens": [50854, 293, 264, 805, 35, 15529, 260, 2935, 3181, 9054, 300, 1319, 293, 6067, 264, 4256, 311, 36205, 23897, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 114694, "start": 1162.2, "end": 1164.76, "text": " So the engine has to handle movement logic perfectly.", "tokens": [51128, 407, 264, 2848, 575, 281, 4813, 3963, 9952, 6239, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 114694, "start": 1165.22, "end": 1170.7, "text": " But the spec also talks about the difference between exclusive, inclusive, and line-wise motions.", "tokens": [51279, 583, 264, 1608, 611, 6686, 466, 264, 2649, 1296, 13005, 11, 13429, 11, 293, 1622, 12, 3711, 27500, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 114694, "start": 1170.8600000000001, "end": 1171.14, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51561, 1079, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1293675104777018, "compression_ratio": 1.6055776892430278, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552867374714729e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 117114, "start": 1171.14, "end": 1178.0, "text": " This feels like the kind of logic that would cause absolute chaos if the 3D graphics engine tried to handle it ad hoc.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 3417, 411, 264, 733, 295, 9952, 300, 576, 3082, 8236, 14158, 498, 264, 805, 35, 11837, 2848, 3031, 281, 4813, 309, 614, 16708, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 117114, "start": 1178.4, "end": 1179.16, "text": " It would be a nightmare.", "tokens": [50728, 467, 576, 312, 257, 18724, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 117114, "start": 1179.5600000000002, "end": 1180.72, "text": " Let's define them quickly.", "tokens": [50786, 961, 311, 6964, 552, 2661, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 117114, "start": 1181.1200000000001, "end": 1185.7, "text": " An exclusive motion, like W for moving to the next word, moves the cursor.", "tokens": [50864, 1107, 13005, 5394, 11, 411, 343, 337, 2684, 281, 264, 958, 1349, 11, 6067, 264, 28169, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 117114, "start": 1186.0800000000002, "end": 1191.14, "text": " But if you combine it with a delete operator, it does not delete the character the cursor lands on.", "tokens": [51112, 583, 498, 291, 10432, 309, 365, 257, 12097, 12973, 11, 309, 775, 406, 12097, 264, 2517, 264, 28169, 5949, 322, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 117114, "start": 1191.16, "end": 1192.3200000000002, "text": " It stalks just before it.", "tokens": [51366, 467, 21789, 82, 445, 949, 309, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 117114, "start": 1192.5, "end": 1192.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51433, 1779, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1113922119140625, "compression_ratio": 1.5365853658536586, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674024578249401e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 119274, "start": 1192.74, "end": 1198.74, "text": " An inclusive motion, like E for moving to the end of a word, does include the landing character in the operation.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 13429, 5394, 11, 411, 462, 337, 2684, 281, 264, 917, 295, 257, 1349, 11, 775, 4090, 264, 11202, 2517, 294, 264, 6916, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 119274, "start": 1199.04, "end": 1203.6200000000001, "text": " And line-wise, operations just ignore horizontal columns entirely and operate on the whole row.", "tokens": [50680, 400, 1622, 12, 3711, 11, 7705, 445, 11200, 12750, 13766, 7696, 293, 9651, 322, 264, 1379, 5386, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 119274, "start": 1203.8, "end": 1204.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50918, 7587, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 119274, "start": 1204.38, "end": 1208.66, "text": " Now imagine trying to program those rules into a 3D character controller.", "tokens": [50947, 823, 3811, 1382, 281, 1461, 729, 4474, 666, 257, 805, 35, 2517, 10561, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 119274, "start": 1209.1, "end": 1209.66, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51183, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 119274, "start": 1209.82, "end": 1214.46, "text": " Checking collisions and animations for every possible combination of operators and motions.", "tokens": [51219, 6881, 278, 46537, 293, 22868, 337, 633, 1944, 6562, 295, 19077, 293, 27500, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 119274, "start": 1214.82, "end": 1217.0, "text": " It would be a spaghetti code disaster.", "tokens": [51469, 467, 576, 312, 257, 28556, 3089, 11293, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 119274, "start": 1217.38, "end": 1218.44, "text": " So how do they handle it?", "tokens": [51597, 407, 577, 360, 436, 4813, 309, 30, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144825821622796, "compression_ratio": 1.6357142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845690625048707e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 121844, "start": 1218.44, "end": 1224.54, "text": " Buffer World solves this by isolating all that logic in a central clamping function within the headless parser.", "tokens": [50365, 20254, 260, 3937, 39890, 341, 538, 48912, 439, 300, 9952, 294, 257, 5777, 17690, 278, 2445, 1951, 264, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 121844, "start": 1224.74, "end": 1224.96, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50680, 1033, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 121844, "start": 1225.0800000000002, "end": 1229.96, "text": " The parser calculates the exact start and end coordinates of the operation based on the motion type,", "tokens": [50697, 440, 21156, 260, 4322, 1024, 264, 1900, 722, 293, 917, 21056, 295, 264, 6916, 2361, 322, 264, 5394, 2010, 11, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 121844, "start": 1230.46, "end": 1233.26, "text": " clamps those coordinates to the boundaries of the text buffer,", "tokens": [50966, 44423, 729, 21056, 281, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 2487, 21762, 11, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 121844, "start": 1233.9, "end": 1238.94, "text": " executes the logic, and only then hands the final clean state to the renderer.", "tokens": [51138, 4454, 1819, 264, 9952, 11, 293, 787, 550, 2377, 264, 2572, 2541, 1785, 281, 264, 15529, 260, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 121844, "start": 1239.2, "end": 1243.6000000000001, "text": " It is insulating the presentation layer from the messy reality of the logic.", "tokens": [51403, 467, 307, 1028, 12162, 264, 5860, 4583, 490, 264, 16191, 4103, 295, 264, 9952, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 121844, "start": 1243.78, "end": 1244.3400000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51632, 48746, 736, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11445902895044398, "compression_ratio": 1.7364341085271318, "no_speech_prob": 1.97332037862874e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 124434, "start": 1244.34, "end": 1247.56, "text": " But what happens when that logic is intentionally inconsistent?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 300, 9952, 307, 22062, 36891, 30, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 124434, "start": 1248.48, "end": 1251.6, "text": " The spec calls out specific deliberate exceptions.", "tokens": [50572, 440, 1608, 5498, 484, 2685, 30515, 22847, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 124434, "start": 1251.98, "end": 1252.34, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50747, 2438, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 124434, "start": 1252.9199999999998, "end": 1261.4599999999998, "text": " The CW versus CE exception is fascinating to me because it shows how human intuition fundamentally broke the mathematical rules of the software.", "tokens": [50794, 440, 383, 54, 5717, 28109, 11183, 307, 10343, 281, 385, 570, 309, 3110, 577, 1952, 24002, 17879, 6902, 264, 18894, 4474, 295, 264, 4722, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 124434, "start": 1261.6399999999999, "end": 1262.54, "text": " It is a great example.", "tokens": [51230, 467, 307, 257, 869, 1365, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 124434, "start": 1262.82, "end": 1266.04, "text": " And now that broken rule has to be preserved as canonical truth.", "tokens": [51289, 400, 586, 300, 5463, 4978, 575, 281, 312, 22242, 382, 46491, 3494, 13, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 124434, "start": 1266.1799999999998, "end": 1268.48, "text": " It is a wonderful piece of software archaeology.", "tokens": [51457, 467, 307, 257, 3715, 2522, 295, 4722, 21894, 1793, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 124434, "start": 1268.84, "end": 1270.1, "text": " Let's look at the underlying logic.", "tokens": [51590, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 14217, 9952, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 124434, "start": 1270.1, "end": 1274.12, "text": " In standard Vim operation, DW means delete word.", "tokens": [51653, 682, 3832, 691, 332, 6916, 11, 45318, 1355, 12097, 1349, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18557664326259068, "compression_ratio": 1.6059602649006623, "no_speech_prob": 1.797182194729352e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 127434, "start": 1274.34, "end": 1278.9399999999998, "text": " If your cursor is on the word apple followed by a space and you type DW,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 428, 28169, 307, 322, 264, 1349, 10606, 6263, 538, 257, 1901, 293, 291, 2010, 45318, 11, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 127434, "start": 1279.72, "end": 1283.1, "text": " Vim deletes apple and it also deletes the trailing space.", "tokens": [50634, 691, 332, 1103, 37996, 10606, 293, 309, 611, 1103, 37996, 264, 944, 4883, 1901, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 127434, "start": 1283.1799999999998, "end": 1284.24, "text": " Which makes total sense.", "tokens": [50807, 3013, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 127434, "start": 1284.34, "end": 1288.5, "text": " You want the next word to slide over and sit flush without leaving a double space behind.", "tokens": [50865, 509, 528, 264, 958, 1349, 281, 4137, 670, 293, 1394, 19568, 1553, 5012, 257, 3834, 1901, 2261, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 127434, "start": 1288.6599999999999, "end": 1289.4599999999998, "text": " Perfectly logical.", "tokens": [51081, 10246, 356, 14978, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 127434, "start": 1290.0, "end": 1292.5, "text": " Now, the C operator stands for change.", "tokens": [51148, 823, 11, 264, 383, 12973, 7382, 337, 1319, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 127434, "start": 1292.62, "end": 1292.8, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51279, 865, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2020382992056913, "compression_ratio": 1.4927536231884058, "no_speech_prob": 2.08458445817572e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 129280, "start": 1292.8, "end": 1297.72, "text": " It deletes the target and immediately puts you into insert mode so you can type the replacement.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1103, 37996, 264, 3779, 293, 4258, 8137, 291, 666, 8969, 4391, 370, 291, 393, 2010, 264, 14419, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09841882614862352, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 2.1675883744159963e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 129280, "start": 1298.18, "end": 1304.3999999999999, "text": " So logic dictates that CW, change word, should behave exactly like DW.", "tokens": [50634, 407, 9952, 12569, 1024, 300, 383, 54, 11, 1319, 1349, 11, 820, 15158, 2293, 411, 45318, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09841882614862352, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 2.1675883744159963e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 129280, "start": 1304.74, "end": 1306.82, "text": " It should delete the word and the trailing space.", "tokens": [50962, 467, 820, 12097, 264, 1349, 293, 264, 944, 4883, 1901, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09841882614862352, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 2.1675883744159963e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 129280, "start": 1306.8999999999999, "end": 1312.3999999999999, "text": " But if it deletes the trailing space and drops me into insert mode, I'd be typing right up against the following word.", "tokens": [51070, 583, 498, 309, 1103, 37996, 264, 944, 4883, 1901, 293, 11438, 385, 666, 8969, 4391, 11, 286, 1116, 312, 18444, 558, 493, 1970, 264, 3480, 1349, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09841882614862352, "compression_ratio": 1.6551724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 2.1675883744159963e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 131240, "start": 1312.4, "end": 1312.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 131240, "start": 1313.0800000000002, "end": 1317.1200000000001, "text": " I would have to manually hit the space bar every single time I changed a word.", "tokens": [50399, 286, 576, 362, 281, 16945, 2045, 264, 1901, 2159, 633, 2167, 565, 286, 3105, 257, 1349, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 131240, "start": 1317.2800000000002, "end": 1318.16, "text": " That feels terrible.", "tokens": [50609, 663, 3417, 6237, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 131240, "start": 1318.3600000000001, "end": 1324.44, "text": " Bill Joy, the creator of Vim's predecessor, Vi, realized that felt terrible in the late 1970s.", "tokens": [50663, 5477, 15571, 11, 264, 14181, 295, 691, 332, 311, 34991, 11, 6626, 11, 5334, 300, 2762, 6237, 294, 264, 3469, 14577, 82, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 131240, "start": 1324.5600000000002, "end": 1326.3000000000002, "text": " So he hard-coded an exception.", "tokens": [50973, 407, 415, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 364, 11183, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 131240, "start": 1326.48, "end": 1327.5800000000002, "text": " He just broke his own rule.", "tokens": [51069, 634, 445, 6902, 702, 1065, 4978, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 131240, "start": 1327.8200000000002, "end": 1328.0800000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51136, 1079, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 131240, "start": 1328.3400000000001, "end": 1331.26, "text": " When you type CW, Vim breaks its own rules.", "tokens": [51162, 1133, 291, 2010, 383, 54, 11, 691, 332, 9857, 1080, 1065, 4474, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 131240, "start": 1331.7800000000002, "end": 1335.5800000000002, "text": " It silently changes the motion from W word to E end of word.", "tokens": [51334, 467, 40087, 2962, 264, 5394, 490, 343, 1349, 281, 462, 917, 295, 1349, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16316573684279984, "compression_ratio": 1.4820717131474104, "no_speech_prob": 1.681309497007788e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 133558, "start": 1335.58, "end": 1343.1, "text": " It deletes the word, but it deliberately leaves the trailing white space intact so your new typing has room to breathe.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1103, 37996, 264, 1349, 11, 457, 309, 23506, 5510, 264, 944, 4883, 2418, 1901, 23493, 370, 428, 777, 18444, 575, 1808, 281, 10192, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951158947414823, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683065077657046e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 133558, "start": 1343.52, "end": 1347.84, "text": " It abandons mathematical consistency to accommodate human ergonomics.", "tokens": [50762, 467, 410, 474, 892, 18894, 14416, 281, 21410, 1952, 42735, 29884, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951158947414823, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683065077657046e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 133558, "start": 1348.0, "end": 1348.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50986, 7587, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951158947414823, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683065077657046e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 133558, "start": 1349.04, "end": 1356.4399999999998, "text": " And because Buffer World is committed to absolute source fidelity, they cannot just write a clean, elegant parser.", "tokens": [51038, 400, 570, 20254, 260, 3937, 307, 7784, 281, 8236, 4009, 46404, 11, 436, 2644, 445, 2464, 257, 2541, 11, 21117, 21156, 260, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951158947414823, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683065077657046e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 133558, "start": 1357.1599999999999, "end": 1362.34, "text": " They have to explicitly program that exact same inconsistency into their game engine.", "tokens": [51444, 814, 362, 281, 20803, 1461, 300, 1900, 912, 22039, 468, 3020, 666, 641, 1216, 2848, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951158947414823, "compression_ratio": 1.5525291828793775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683065077657046e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 136234, "start": 1362.34, "end": 1366.24, "text": " They have to preserve the dents and scratches of the original artifact.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 362, 281, 15665, 264, 274, 791, 293, 33695, 295, 264, 3380, 34806, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 136234, "start": 1366.52, "end": 1368.6599999999999, "text": " You see this again with text object resolution, right?", "tokens": [50574, 509, 536, 341, 797, 365, 2487, 2657, 8669, 11, 558, 30, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 136234, "start": 1369.12, "end": 1369.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50704, 1079, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 136234, "start": 1369.48, "end": 1370.8999999999999, "text": " Text objects are another area.", "tokens": [50722, 18643, 6565, 366, 1071, 1859, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 136234, "start": 1371.1, "end": 1377.1, "text": " Text objects allow you to manipulate blocks of text based on structure, like brackets or quotes.", "tokens": [50803, 18643, 6565, 2089, 291, 281, 20459, 8474, 295, 2487, 2361, 322, 3877, 11, 411, 26179, 420, 19963, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 136234, "start": 1377.28, "end": 1377.4399999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51112, 1033, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 136234, "start": 1377.8, "end": 1389.06, "text": " If you are inside parentheses and type I, and then an open parentheses, meaning inner parentheses, Vim searches outward, traversing multiple lines if necessary to find the nearest enclosing brackets.", "tokens": [51138, 759, 291, 366, 1854, 34153, 293, 2010, 286, 11, 293, 550, 364, 1269, 34153, 11, 3620, 7284, 34153, 11, 691, 332, 26701, 26914, 11, 23149, 278, 3866, 3876, 498, 4818, 281, 915, 264, 23831, 20987, 6110, 26179, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 136234, "start": 1389.3, "end": 1390.6799999999998, "text": " So it looks up and down the document.", "tokens": [51713, 407, 309, 1542, 493, 293, 760, 264, 4166, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10910889253777972, "compression_ratio": 1.7108843537414966, "no_speech_prob": 1.6747648190137965e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 139068, "start": 1390.68, "end": 1396.8400000000001, "text": " If you add a count, like two I, open parentheses, it jumps out another layer to the next set of nested brackets.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 909, 257, 1207, 11, 411, 732, 286, 11, 1269, 34153, 11, 309, 16704, 484, 1071, 4583, 281, 264, 958, 992, 295, 15646, 292, 26179, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 139068, "start": 1397.14, "end": 1401.0, "text": " It treats brackets as structural nested containers spanning the whole document.", "tokens": [50688, 467, 19566, 26179, 382, 15067, 15646, 292, 17089, 47626, 264, 1379, 4166, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 139068, "start": 1401.5, "end": 1403.3400000000001, "text": " But quote marks don't work like that, do they?", "tokens": [50906, 583, 6513, 10640, 500, 380, 589, 411, 300, 11, 360, 436, 30, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 139068, "start": 1403.5600000000002, "end": 1404.3600000000001, "text": " No, they do not.", "tokens": [51009, 883, 11, 436, 360, 406, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 139068, "start": 1404.9, "end": 1408.9, "text": " Quote objects, like I and then a quote mark, have completely different parsing logic.", "tokens": [51076, 2326, 1370, 6565, 11, 411, 286, 293, 550, 257, 6513, 1491, 11, 362, 2584, 819, 21156, 278, 9952, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 139068, "start": 1409.1000000000001, "end": 1409.5, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51286, 1012, 370, 30, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 139068, "start": 1409.74, "end": 1412.3200000000002, "text": " Quotes cannot nest across lines in Vim.", "tokens": [51318, 2326, 17251, 2644, 15646, 2108, 3876, 294, 691, 332, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14230905388886073, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232395202292471e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 141232, "start": 1412.32, "end": 1422.48, "text": " If your cursor is sitting on a blank space at the beginning of a line, and you type inner quote, Vim does not search backward through the file to find where you last opened a quote.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 428, 28169, 307, 3798, 322, 257, 8247, 1901, 412, 264, 2863, 295, 257, 1622, 11, 293, 291, 2010, 7284, 6513, 11, 691, 332, 775, 406, 3164, 23897, 807, 264, 3991, 281, 915, 689, 291, 1036, 5625, 257, 6513, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196189087706727, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827772678252751e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 141232, "start": 1422.82, "end": 1423.74, "text": " What does it do instead?", "tokens": [50890, 708, 775, 309, 360, 2602, 30, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196189087706727, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827772678252751e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 141232, "start": 1424.0, "end": 1430.56, "text": " Instead, it scans strictly forward, only on the current line, and snaps to the first quoted string it finds.", "tokens": [50949, 7156, 11, 309, 35116, 20792, 2128, 11, 787, 322, 264, 2190, 1622, 11, 293, 19206, 281, 264, 700, 30047, 6798, 309, 10704, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196189087706727, "compression_ratio": 1.575, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827772678252751e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 143056, "start": 1430.56, "end": 1433.6, "text": " Computationally, that is a completely different search algorithm.", "tokens": [50365, 37804, 399, 379, 11, 300, 307, 257, 2584, 819, 3164, 9284, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14927800841953442, "compression_ratio": 1.6081632653061224, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954064462419092e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 143056, "start": 1433.78, "end": 1434.7, "text": " Completely different.", "tokens": [50526, 39978, 819, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14927800841953442, "compression_ratio": 1.6081632653061224, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954064462419092e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 143056, "start": 1434.82, "end": 1442.6599999999999, "text": " One uses a stack to track nesting across a global buffer, and the other is just a simple linear scan constrained by a line-brain delimiter.", "tokens": [50578, 1485, 4960, 257, 8630, 281, 2837, 297, 8714, 2108, 257, 4338, 21762, 11, 293, 264, 661, 307, 445, 257, 2199, 8213, 11049, 38901, 538, 257, 1622, 12, 6198, 259, 1103, 332, 1681, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14927800841953442, "compression_ratio": 1.6081632653061224, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954064462419092e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 143056, "start": 1442.84, "end": 1448.5, "text": " And buffer world must meticulously implement both, completely independent of the 3D graphics.", "tokens": [50979, 400, 21762, 1002, 1633, 41566, 25038, 4445, 1293, 11, 2584, 6695, 295, 264, 805, 35, 11837, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14927800841953442, "compression_ratio": 1.6081632653061224, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954064462419092e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 143056, "start": 1448.8999999999999, "end": 1452.1399999999999, "text": " Replicating these quirks is not about building a functional text editor.", "tokens": [51282, 1300, 4770, 990, 613, 35645, 1694, 307, 406, 466, 2390, 257, 11745, 2487, 9839, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14927800841953442, "compression_ratio": 1.6081632653061224, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954064462419092e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 145214, "start": 1452.14, "end": 1456.68, "text": " It is about a dogmatic, almost religious preservation of the source reality.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 466, 257, 3000, 25915, 11, 1920, 7185, 27257, 295, 264, 4009, 4103, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 145214, "start": 1456.92, "end": 1457.24, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50604, 1079, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 145214, "start": 1457.88, "end": 1461.42, "text": " The canonical source is not the abstract concept of text editing.", "tokens": [50652, 440, 46491, 4009, 307, 406, 264, 12649, 3410, 295, 2487, 10000, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 145214, "start": 1462.0, "end": 1466.72, "text": " The canonical source is Vim in all its idiosyncratic 1970s glory.", "tokens": [50858, 440, 46491, 4009, 307, 691, 332, 294, 439, 1080, 4496, 2717, 2534, 10757, 2399, 14577, 82, 11924, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 145214, "start": 1467.0, "end": 1469.66, "text": " This raises a massive structural question for me, though.", "tokens": [51108, 639, 19658, 257, 5994, 15067, 1168, 337, 385, 11, 1673, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 145214, "start": 1470.26, "end": 1477.1200000000001, "text": " Buffer world can define its absolute source state meticulously, because Vim is a finite, bounded piece of software.", "tokens": [51271, 20254, 260, 1002, 393, 6964, 1080, 8236, 4009, 1785, 41566, 25038, 11, 570, 691, 332, 307, 257, 19362, 11, 37498, 2522, 295, 4722, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 145214, "start": 1477.2800000000002, "end": 1478.3200000000002, "text": " It is a closed system.", "tokens": [51622, 467, 307, 257, 5395, 1185, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 145214, "start": 1478.3200000000002, "end": 1481.3000000000002, "text": " The rules are complex, but they are known.", "tokens": [51674, 440, 4474, 366, 3997, 11, 457, 436, 366, 2570, 13, 51823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14508050063560748, "compression_ratio": 1.635379061371841, "no_speech_prob": 1.811288749195561e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 148130, "start": 1481.3, "end": 1492.3, "text": " How on earth does Plenum Hub propose defining an absolute canonical source state for something as fluid, messy, and infinitely expanding as human knowledge and digital media?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 322, 4120, 775, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 17421, 17827, 364, 8236, 46491, 4009, 1785, 337, 746, 382, 9113, 11, 16191, 11, 293, 36227, 14702, 382, 1952, 3601, 293, 4562, 3021, 30, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1224829269959046, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627581232337324e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 148130, "start": 1492.52, "end": 1499.7, "text": " This is where we zoom out from the microscopic rules of a text editor parser, back to the macroscopic architecture of publishing.", "tokens": [50926, 639, 307, 689, 321, 8863, 484, 490, 264, 47897, 4474, 295, 257, 2487, 9839, 21156, 260, 11, 646, 281, 264, 7912, 38006, 299, 9482, 295, 17832, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1224829269959046, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627581232337324e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 148130, "start": 1499.82, "end": 1500.56, "text": " Okay, let's zoom out.", "tokens": [51291, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 8863, 484, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1224829269959046, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627581232337324e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 148130, "start": 1500.82, "end": 1506.1599999999999, "text": " To handle the messy reality of human knowledge, Plenum Hub shatters the concept of a version.", "tokens": [51341, 1407, 4813, 264, 16191, 4103, 295, 1952, 3601, 11, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 402, 37690, 264, 3410, 295, 257, 3037, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1224829269959046, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627581232337324e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 148130, "start": 1506.36, "end": 1511.02, "text": " Traditional media collapses all changes into a single, linear version history.", "tokens": [51618, 46738, 3021, 48765, 439, 2962, 666, 257, 2167, 11, 8213, 3037, 2503, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1224829269959046, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627581232337324e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 151130, "start": 1511.3, "end": 1513.02, "text": " Version 1, version 2, version 3.", "tokens": [50365, 35965, 502, 11, 3037, 568, 11, 3037, 805, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 151130, "start": 1513.18, "end": 1513.3799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50459, 1779, 13, 50469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 151130, "start": 1513.78, "end": 1516.7, "text": " Plenum Hub argues that this is fundamentally inadequate.", "tokens": [50489, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 38218, 300, 341, 307, 17879, 42107, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 151130, "start": 1517.34, "end": 1522.62, "text": " Instead, it proposes three entirely independent axes that map the dimensions of content.", "tokens": [50667, 7156, 11, 309, 2365, 4201, 1045, 7696, 6695, 35387, 300, 4471, 264, 12819, 295, 2701, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 151130, "start": 1522.8999999999999, "end": 1523.12, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50945, 1033, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 151130, "start": 1523.28, "end": 1525.86, "text": " Let's explore this 3D coordinate space for knowledge.", "tokens": [50964, 961, 311, 6839, 341, 805, 35, 15670, 1901, 337, 3601, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 151130, "start": 1525.98, "end": 1529.36, "text": " The first axis is lineage, but it's not a straight line, right?", "tokens": [51099, 440, 700, 10298, 307, 38257, 11, 457, 309, 311, 406, 257, 2997, 1622, 11, 558, 30, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 151130, "start": 1529.3999999999999, "end": 1529.68, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51270, 12753, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 151130, "start": 1529.8999999999999, "end": 1533.96, "text": " Lineage is a graph very similar to how Git tracks software development.", "tokens": [51295, 14670, 609, 307, 257, 4295, 588, 2531, 281, 577, 16939, 10218, 4722, 3250, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14932681518850974, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 2.1762661117641358e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 153396, "start": 1533.96, "end": 1539.44, "text": " It tracks the history of the content over time, but it formally distinguishes between revisions and branches.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 10218, 264, 2503, 295, 264, 2701, 670, 565, 11, 457, 309, 25983, 11365, 16423, 1296, 3698, 4252, 293, 14770, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 153396, "start": 1539.96, "end": 1542.22, "text": " A revision is a meaning-preserving correction.", "tokens": [50665, 316, 34218, 307, 257, 3620, 12, 14508, 20186, 19984, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 153396, "start": 1542.74, "end": 1544.88, "text": " It moves the state from N to N plus 1.", "tokens": [50804, 467, 6067, 264, 1785, 490, 426, 281, 426, 1804, 502, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 153396, "start": 1545.02, "end": 1549.64, "text": " Like fixing a typo, updating a broken link, clarifying a confusing sentence.", "tokens": [50918, 1743, 19442, 257, 2125, 78, 11, 25113, 257, 5463, 2113, 11, 6093, 5489, 257, 13181, 8174, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 153396, "start": 1549.9, "end": 1552.16, "text": " The core intent remains identical.", "tokens": [51162, 440, 4965, 8446, 7023, 14800, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 153396, "start": 1552.56, "end": 1552.96, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51295, 7587, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 153396, "start": 1553.52, "end": 1557.8600000000001, "text": " Revisions supersede the old version, but branches do not.", "tokens": [51343, 12127, 4252, 37906, 4858, 264, 1331, 3037, 11, 457, 14770, 360, 406, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 153396, "start": 1558.08, "end": 1559.6000000000001, "text": " Okay, so how do branches work?", "tokens": [51571, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 360, 14770, 589, 30, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15304473661026866, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552536251379646e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 155960, "start": 1559.6, "end": 1563.0, "text": " A branch is a divergent continuation from a common ancestor.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 9819, 307, 257, 18558, 6930, 29357, 490, 257, 2689, 40032, 13, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 155960, "start": 1563.8799999999999, "end": 1567.34, "text": " Imagine two authors collaborating on a political science essay.", "tokens": [50579, 11739, 732, 16552, 30188, 322, 257, 3905, 3497, 16238, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 155960, "start": 1567.58, "end": 1567.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50764, 1779, 13, 50774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 155960, "start": 1568.06, "end": 1572.74, "text": " They agree on the historical data, but midway through, they fundamentally disagree on the conclusion.", "tokens": [50788, 814, 3986, 322, 264, 8584, 1412, 11, 457, 2062, 676, 807, 11, 436, 17879, 14091, 322, 264, 10063, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 155960, "start": 1573.24, "end": 1576.2199999999998, "text": " In the Plenum Hub architecture, they simply branch the lineage.", "tokens": [51047, 682, 264, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 9482, 11, 436, 2935, 9819, 264, 38257, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 155960, "start": 1576.4199999999998, "end": 1577.08, "text": " They fork it.", "tokens": [51206, 814, 17716, 309, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 155960, "start": 1577.24, "end": 1583.76, "text": " Both conclusions exist simultaneously, sharing the exact same ancestral data, but neither invalidates the other.", "tokens": [51247, 6767, 22865, 2514, 16561, 11, 5414, 264, 1900, 912, 40049, 1412, 11, 457, 9662, 34702, 1024, 264, 661, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 155960, "start": 1583.8999999999999, "end": 1585.06, "text": " It is a multiverse of thought.", "tokens": [51580, 467, 307, 257, 2120, 5376, 295, 1194, 13, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 155960, "start": 1585.48, "end": 1587.1599999999999, "text": " So that is the x-axis, lineage.", "tokens": [51659, 407, 300, 307, 264, 2031, 12, 24633, 11, 38257, 13, 51743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 155960, "start": 1587.54, "end": 1588.9199999999998, "text": " The y-axis is depth.", "tokens": [51762, 440, 288, 12, 24633, 307, 7161, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16405482554998924, "compression_ratio": 1.727891156462585, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656457451305842e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 158892, "start": 1588.92, "end": 1592.68, "text": " Depth represents deliberately lossy compression of the material.", "tokens": [50365, 4056, 392, 8855, 23506, 4470, 88, 19355, 295, 264, 2527, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 158892, "start": 1593.14, "end": 1594.66, "text": " Think of it as semantic zoom.", "tokens": [50576, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 47982, 8863, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 158892, "start": 1594.8200000000002, "end": 1595.46, "text": " Semantic zoom.", "tokens": [50660, 14421, 7128, 8863, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 158892, "start": 1595.6000000000001, "end": 1596.0800000000002, "text": " I like that.", "tokens": [50699, 286, 411, 300, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 158892, "start": 1596.3000000000002, "end": 1601.3400000000001, "text": " You might have a full depth, which is the comprehensive, exhaustive exploration of the topic.", "tokens": [50734, 509, 1062, 362, 257, 1577, 7161, 11, 597, 307, 264, 13914, 11, 14687, 488, 16197, 295, 264, 4829, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 158892, "start": 1601.8400000000001, "end": 1604.8000000000002, "text": " Then you might have a medium depth, perhaps a five-minute overview.", "tokens": [51011, 1396, 291, 1062, 362, 257, 6399, 7161, 11, 4317, 257, 1732, 12, 18256, 12492, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 158892, "start": 1605.0, "end": 1605.24, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51169, 1033, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 158892, "start": 1605.46, "end": 1609.18, "text": " And finally, a short depth, a 30-second elevator pitch, or an abstract.", "tokens": [51192, 400, 2721, 11, 257, 2099, 7161, 11, 257, 2217, 12, 27375, 18782, 7293, 11, 420, 364, 12649, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 158892, "start": 1609.68, "end": 1613.38, "text": " So a full textbook chapter versus the flashcard summary.", "tokens": [51403, 407, 257, 1577, 25591, 7187, 5717, 264, 7319, 22259, 12691, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 158892, "start": 1614.1200000000001, "end": 1618.48, "text": " The crucial distinction here is that depth is completely decoupled from lineage.", "tokens": [51625, 440, 11462, 16844, 510, 307, 300, 7161, 307, 2584, 979, 263, 15551, 490, 38257, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1575421392917633, "compression_ratio": 1.644736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.950816244655762e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 161848, "start": 1618.48, "end": 1619.48, "text": " Completely decoupled.", "tokens": [50365, 39978, 979, 263, 15551, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17286260363081812, "compression_ratio": 1.5363128491620113, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279278051798852e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 161848, "start": 1620.16, "end": 1624.76, "text": " A shorter summary doesn't mean it is newer, and a newer revision isn't necessarily longer.", "tokens": [50449, 316, 11639, 12691, 1177, 380, 914, 309, 307, 17628, 11, 293, 257, 17628, 34218, 1943, 380, 4725, 2854, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17286260363081812, "compression_ratio": 1.5363128491620113, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279278051798852e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 161848, "start": 1625.42, "end": 1632.06, "text": " You can have a short depth rendering of a branch from three years ago, or a full depth rendering of a revision made five minutes ago.", "tokens": [50712, 509, 393, 362, 257, 2099, 7161, 22407, 295, 257, 9819, 490, 1045, 924, 2057, 11, 420, 257, 1577, 7161, 22407, 295, 257, 34218, 1027, 1732, 2077, 2057, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17286260363081812, "compression_ratio": 1.5363128491620113, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279278051798852e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 161848, "start": 1632.2, "end": 1633.1200000000001, "text": " That is exactly right.", "tokens": [51051, 663, 307, 2293, 558, 13, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17286260363081812, "compression_ratio": 1.5363128491620113, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279278051798852e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 161848, "start": 1633.22, "end": 1633.32, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51102, 865, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17286260363081812, "compression_ratio": 1.5363128491620113, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279278051798852e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 163332, "start": 1633.32, "end": 1637.48, "text": " And then we reach the z-axis, rendering, this is the output modality.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 321, 2524, 264, 710, 12, 24633, 11, 22407, 11, 341, 307, 264, 5598, 1072, 1860, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 163332, "start": 1637.58, "end": 1638.28, "text": " The actual format.", "tokens": [50578, 440, 3539, 7877, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 163332, "start": 1638.5, "end": 1644.96, "text": " Once you have selected your point in time, the lineage, and your level of detail, the depth, how do you want to consume it?", "tokens": [50624, 3443, 291, 362, 8209, 428, 935, 294, 565, 11, 264, 38257, 11, 293, 428, 1496, 295, 2607, 11, 264, 7161, 11, 577, 360, 291, 528, 281, 14732, 309, 30, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 163332, "start": 1645.12, "end": 1646.98, "text": " As a video, an audio podcast.", "tokens": [50955, 1018, 257, 960, 11, 364, 6278, 7367, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 163332, "start": 1647.2, "end": 1647.36, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51059, 865, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 163332, "start": 1647.4199999999998, "end": 1649.22, "text": " A text essay, an interactive comic.", "tokens": [51070, 316, 2487, 16238, 11, 364, 15141, 13900, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16113763832184205, "compression_ratio": 1.4564102564102563, "no_speech_prob": 1.7616347833607215e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 164922, "start": 1649.22, "end": 1649.58, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 164922, "start": 1649.78, "end": 1655.04, "text": " So in this architecture, you don't just click a URL and passively accept whatever video plays.", "tokens": [50393, 407, 294, 341, 9482, 11, 291, 500, 380, 445, 2052, 257, 12905, 293, 1320, 3413, 3241, 2035, 960, 5749, 13, 50656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 164922, "start": 1655.14, "end": 1656.84, "text": " You are making a specific request.", "tokens": [50661, 509, 366, 1455, 257, 2685, 5308, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 164922, "start": 1656.96, "end": 1659.6200000000001, "text": " A well-formed request is a specific coordinate query.", "tokens": [50752, 316, 731, 12, 22892, 5308, 307, 257, 2685, 15670, 14581, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 164922, "start": 1660.1200000000001, "end": 1667.42, "text": " You are asking the plenum hub substrate for, say, the short-depth audio rendering of branch B as of revision 12.", "tokens": [50910, 509, 366, 3365, 264, 499, 268, 449, 11838, 27585, 337, 11, 584, 11, 264, 2099, 12, 25478, 6278, 22407, 295, 9819, 363, 382, 295, 34218, 2272, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 164922, "start": 1667.72, "end": 1673.42, "text": " Infliction uses the educational sector as the ultimate proof of concept for this, which instantly made it quick for me.", "tokens": [51290, 682, 3423, 4105, 4960, 264, 10189, 6977, 382, 264, 9705, 8177, 295, 3410, 337, 341, 11, 597, 13518, 1027, 309, 1702, 337, 385, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 164922, "start": 1673.48, "end": 1674.96, "text": " It is the perfect use case.", "tokens": [51578, 467, 307, 264, 2176, 764, 1389, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11231531176650733, "compression_ratio": 1.5620689655172413, "no_speech_prob": 2.1339911174950155e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 167496, "start": 1674.96, "end": 1689.26, "text": " Think about a university biology course. In a traditional publishing model, the professor relies on a textbook, a deck of study flashcards, a recorded lecture series, and maybe an interactive lab simulation software.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 257, 5454, 14956, 1164, 13, 682, 257, 5164, 17832, 2316, 11, 264, 8304, 30910, 322, 257, 25591, 11, 257, 9341, 295, 2979, 7319, 40604, 11, 257, 8287, 7991, 2638, 11, 293, 1310, 364, 15141, 2715, 16575, 4722, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09872778979214755, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080406099906353e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 167496, "start": 1689.64, "end": 1693.08, "text": " Conventionally, those are four completely isolated artifacts.", "tokens": [51099, 26793, 379, 11, 729, 366, 1451, 2584, 14621, 24617, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09872778979214755, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080406099906353e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 167496, "start": 1693.26, "end": 1697.66, "text": " Right. Developed by different teams, living on different servers, and sold by different vendors.", "tokens": [51280, 1779, 13, 11442, 292, 538, 819, 5491, 11, 2647, 322, 819, 15909, 11, 293, 3718, 538, 819, 22056, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09872778979214755, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080406099906353e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 169766, "start": 1697.66, "end": 1705.18, "text": " And what happens when a new fossil is discovered that completely changes the timeline of a specific evolutionary branch?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 777, 18737, 307, 6941, 300, 2584, 2962, 264, 12933, 295, 257, 2685, 27567, 9819, 30, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09372370441754659, "compression_ratio": 1.601423487544484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614890445051158e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 169766, "start": 1705.3600000000001, "end": 1705.68, "text": " Chaos.", "tokens": [50750, 32644, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09372370441754659, "compression_ratio": 1.601423487544484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614890445051158e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 169766, "start": 1706.26, "end": 1719.3200000000002, "text": " The professor has to manually write an erratum for the textbook, record a supplementary video to append to the lecture, tell the students to throw out three specific flashcards, and hope the software vendor patches the simulation.", "tokens": [50795, 440, 8304, 575, 281, 16945, 2464, 364, 1189, 4481, 449, 337, 264, 25591, 11, 2136, 257, 15436, 822, 960, 281, 34116, 281, 264, 7991, 11, 980, 264, 1731, 281, 3507, 484, 1045, 2685, 7319, 40604, 11, 293, 1454, 264, 4722, 24321, 26531, 264, 16575, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09372370441754659, "compression_ratio": 1.601423487544484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614890445051158e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 169766, "start": 1719.6200000000001, "end": 1724.3200000000002, "text": " Which, let's be real, never happens perfectly. The artifacts immediately drift out of sync.", "tokens": [51463, 3013, 11, 718, 311, 312, 957, 11, 1128, 2314, 6239, 13, 440, 24617, 4258, 19699, 484, 295, 20271, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09372370441754659, "compression_ratio": 1.601423487544484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614890445051158e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 172432, "start": 1724.32, "end": 1729.1399999999999, "text": " A student studying the flashcards gets a different answer than a student watching the lecture.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 3107, 7601, 264, 7319, 40604, 2170, 257, 819, 1867, 813, 257, 3107, 1976, 264, 7991, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10665411562532992, "compression_ratio": 1.7854545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488013211690689e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 172432, "start": 1729.48, "end": 1736.8999999999999, "text": " But in the plenum hub architecture, those four things, the textbook, the flashcards, the lecture, the simulation, are not independent source artifacts.", "tokens": [50623, 583, 294, 264, 499, 268, 449, 11838, 9482, 11, 729, 1451, 721, 11, 264, 25591, 11, 264, 7319, 40604, 11, 264, 7991, 11, 264, 16575, 11, 366, 406, 6695, 4009, 24617, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10665411562532992, "compression_ratio": 1.7854545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488013211690689e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 172432, "start": 1737.04, "end": 1737.82, "text": " No, they are not.", "tokens": [51001, 883, 11, 436, 366, 406, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10665411562532992, "compression_ratio": 1.7854545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488013211690689e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 172432, "start": 1738.12, "end": 1745.9199999999998, "text": " They are simply four different renderings of a single, canonical source database, which Flixion designates mathematically as sigma.", "tokens": [51055, 814, 366, 2935, 1451, 819, 15529, 1109, 295, 257, 2167, 11, 46491, 4009, 8149, 11, 597, 3235, 970, 313, 1715, 1024, 44003, 382, 12771, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10665411562532992, "compression_ratio": 1.7854545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488013211690689e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 172432, "start": 1746.26, "end": 1752.46, "text": " If the underlying source sigma is updated with the new fossil discovery, that update cascades.", "tokens": [51462, 759, 264, 14217, 4009, 12771, 307, 10588, 365, 264, 777, 18737, 12114, 11, 300, 5623, 3058, 66, 2977, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10665411562532992, "compression_ratio": 1.7854545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488013211690689e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 175246, "start": 1752.46, "end": 1758.82, "text": " Because the renderings are disposable, IDO-generated views compiled from the source, they regenerate perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 15529, 1109, 366, 41578, 11, 7348, 46, 12, 21848, 770, 6809, 36548, 490, 264, 4009, 11, 436, 26358, 473, 6239, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 175246, "start": 1759.02, "end": 1766.3400000000001, "text": " The textbook PDF updates, the flashcard deck regenerates its short-depth text, the simulation adjusts its parameters.", "tokens": [50693, 440, 25591, 17752, 9205, 11, 264, 7319, 22259, 9341, 26358, 1024, 1080, 2099, 12, 25478, 2487, 11, 264, 16575, 4369, 82, 1080, 9834, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 175246, "start": 1766.66, "end": 1770.74, "text": " They can never drift out of sync because they do not contain the truth, they only reflect it.", "tokens": [51075, 814, 393, 1128, 19699, 484, 295, 20271, 570, 436, 360, 406, 5304, 264, 3494, 11, 436, 787, 5031, 309, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 175246, "start": 1770.8, "end": 1772.1200000000001, "text": " It is a beautiful system.", "tokens": [51282, 467, 307, 257, 2238, 1185, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 175246, "start": 1772.38, "end": 1775.88, "text": " But I do have to push back on this a little bit because it sounds almost entirely automated.", "tokens": [51361, 583, 286, 360, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 857, 570, 309, 3263, 1920, 7696, 18473, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 175246, "start": 1775.96, "end": 1777.04, "text": " Okay, what is your concern?", "tokens": [51540, 1033, 11, 437, 307, 428, 3136, 30, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10687906552205044, "compression_ratio": 1.598639455782313, "no_speech_prob": 1.5920922349574318e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 177704, "start": 1777.04, "end": 1784.8999999999999, "text": " If every rendering is just a disposable view pumped out by a compiler, doesn't that completely devalue the art of presentation?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 633, 22407, 307, 445, 257, 41578, 1910, 27774, 484, 538, 257, 31958, 11, 1177, 380, 300, 2584, 1905, 304, 622, 264, 1523, 295, 5860, 30, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 177704, "start": 1786.0, "end": 1791.6, "text": " Are we replacing brilliant video essayists and gifted writers with rendering pipelines?", "tokens": [50813, 2014, 321, 19139, 10248, 960, 16238, 1751, 293, 27104, 13491, 365, 22407, 40168, 30, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 177704, "start": 1792.0, "end": 1793.0, "text": " It is a fair question.", "tokens": [51113, 467, 307, 257, 3143, 1168, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 177704, "start": 1793.18, "end": 1797.02, "text": " What happens to the art of storytelling if the story is just a query result?", "tokens": [51172, 708, 2314, 281, 264, 1523, 295, 21479, 498, 264, 1657, 307, 445, 257, 14581, 1874, 30, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 177704, "start": 1797.56, "end": 1800.78, "text": " That is the most common critique of source-first architectures.", "tokens": [51391, 663, 307, 264, 881, 2689, 25673, 295, 4009, 12, 29581, 6331, 1303, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 177704, "start": 1801.1, "end": 1804.3999999999999, "text": " But Flixion argues the reality is the exact opposite.", "tokens": [51568, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 38218, 264, 4103, 307, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 177704, "start": 1804.6399999999999, "end": 1805.06, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51745, 1012, 370, 30, 51766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352120597407502, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881515716576923e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 180506, "start": 1805.06, "end": 1808.22, "text": " The art of the authored presentation doesn't lose its value.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1523, 295, 264, 6979, 2769, 5860, 1177, 380, 3624, 1080, 2158, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 180506, "start": 1808.54, "end": 1810.62, "text": " Its structural status simply changes.", "tokens": [50539, 6953, 15067, 6558, 2935, 2962, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 180506, "start": 1811.48, "end": 1817.94, "text": " A beautifully written essay or a masterfully edited video becomes what the essay calls a traversal of the source.", "tokens": [50686, 316, 16525, 3720, 16238, 420, 257, 4505, 2277, 23016, 960, 3643, 437, 264, 16238, 5498, 257, 23149, 304, 295, 264, 4009, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 180506, "start": 1818.1399999999999, "end": 1821.6, "text": " A traversal, like a curated path taken through a dense forest.", "tokens": [51019, 316, 23149, 304, 11, 411, 257, 47851, 3100, 2726, 807, 257, 18011, 6719, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 180506, "start": 1821.78, "end": 1822.04, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51201, 1079, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 180506, "start": 1822.56, "end": 1826.84, "text": " An author brings their unique perspective to navigate the space of possibilities.", "tokens": [51240, 1107, 3793, 5607, 641, 3845, 4585, 281, 12350, 264, 1901, 295, 12178, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 180506, "start": 1827.28, "end": 1828.52, "text": " So they are a guide.", "tokens": [51476, 407, 436, 366, 257, 5934, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15266435042671536, "compression_ratio": 1.5761316872427984, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442399942949274e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 182852, "start": 1828.52, "end": 1829.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791898293928665, "compression_ratio": 1.6593886462882097, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995396638474822e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 182852, "start": 1830.06, "end": 1839.16, "text": " Readers who want to experience the author's specific narrative tension, their pacing, their emotional beats, can follow that traversal and appreciate the art of the sequence.", "tokens": [50442, 1300, 15221, 567, 528, 281, 1752, 264, 3793, 311, 2685, 9977, 8980, 11, 641, 43285, 11, 641, 6863, 16447, 11, 393, 1524, 300, 23149, 304, 293, 4449, 264, 1523, 295, 264, 8310, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791898293928665, "compression_ratio": 1.6593886462882097, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995396638474822e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 182852, "start": 1839.3799999999999, "end": 1844.16, "text": " But, and this is the revolutionary part, readers who hit a point in the traversal and say,", "tokens": [50908, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 22687, 644, 11, 17147, 567, 2045, 257, 935, 294, 264, 23149, 304, 293, 584, 11, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791898293928665, "compression_ratio": 1.6593886462882097, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995396638474822e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 182852, "start": 1844.3799999999999, "end": 1850.56, "text": " wait, I want to see the counter arguments to this specific claim, are no longer trapped inside the video.", "tokens": [51158, 1699, 11, 286, 528, 281, 536, 264, 5682, 12869, 281, 341, 2685, 3932, 11, 366, 572, 2854, 14994, 1854, 264, 960, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14791898293928665, "compression_ratio": 1.6593886462882097, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995396638474822e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 185056, "start": 1850.56, "end": 1853.02, "text": " Because they can query the underlying source.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 436, 393, 14581, 264, 14217, 4009, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12665483259385632, "compression_ratio": 1.4715909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042334983149223e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 185056, "start": 1853.52, "end": 1858.28, "text": " The art of the presentation remains beautiful, but it no longer holds the underlying knowledge hostage.", "tokens": [50513, 440, 1523, 295, 264, 5860, 7023, 2238, 11, 457, 309, 572, 2854, 9190, 264, 14217, 3601, 38434, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12665483259385632, "compression_ratio": 1.4715909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042334983149223e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 185056, "start": 1858.72, "end": 1859.04, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50773, 3153, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12665483259385632, "compression_ratio": 1.4715909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042334983149223e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 185056, "start": 1859.26, "end": 1863.78, "text": " A rendering is an invitation to explore the source, not a prison cell locking you away from it.", "tokens": [50800, 316, 22407, 307, 364, 17890, 281, 6839, 264, 4009, 11, 406, 257, 6168, 2815, 23954, 291, 1314, 490, 309, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12665483259385632, "compression_ratio": 1.4715909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042334983149223e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 185056, "start": 1863.84, "end": 1864.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51029, 7587, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12665483259385632, "compression_ratio": 1.4715909090909092, "no_speech_prob": 1.9042334983149223e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 186432, "start": 1864.32, "end": 1870.6799999999998, "text": " But for this dynamic to function, the underlying system must have an absolute obsession with remembering the past.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 337, 341, 8546, 281, 2445, 11, 264, 14217, 1185, 1633, 362, 364, 8236, 30521, 365, 20719, 264, 1791, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 186432, "start": 1870.82, "end": 1871.4399999999998, "text": " Right, the history.", "tokens": [50690, 1779, 11, 264, 2503, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 186432, "start": 1871.6799999999998, "end": 1875.96, "text": " Both Buffer World and Plenum Hub rely heavily on retaining deep history.", "tokens": [50733, 6767, 20254, 260, 3937, 293, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 10687, 10950, 322, 34936, 2452, 2503, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 186432, "start": 1876.46, "end": 1879.76, "text": " Let's explore that history obsession, starting with Buffer World.", "tokens": [50972, 961, 311, 6839, 300, 2503, 30521, 11, 2891, 365, 20254, 260, 3937, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 186432, "start": 1880.4399999999998, "end": 1883.58, "text": " Standard text editors have a linear undo stack.", "tokens": [51171, 21298, 2487, 31446, 362, 257, 8213, 23779, 8630, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 186432, "start": 1883.82, "end": 1884.4399999999998, "text": " Very basic.", "tokens": [51340, 4372, 3875, 13, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 186432, "start": 1885.02, "end": 1892.3799999999999, "text": " If I type a paragraph, hit undo a few times to delete it, and then start typing something new, the original paragraph is gone forever.", "tokens": [51400, 759, 286, 2010, 257, 18865, 11, 2045, 23779, 257, 1326, 1413, 281, 12097, 309, 11, 293, 550, 722, 18444, 746, 777, 11, 264, 3380, 18865, 307, 2780, 5680, 13, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14234194025263056, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682400903397787e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 189238, "start": 1892.38, "end": 1896.42, "text": " My new typing overwrites the future of that undo stack.", "tokens": [50365, 1222, 777, 18444, 670, 86, 30931, 264, 2027, 295, 300, 23779, 8630, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 189238, "start": 1897.0600000000002, "end": 1898.3600000000001, "text": " But Vim doesn't do that.", "tokens": [50599, 583, 691, 332, 1177, 380, 360, 300, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 189238, "start": 1898.5, "end": 1901.24, "text": " No, Vim utilizes a tree-based undo system.", "tokens": [50671, 883, 11, 691, 332, 4976, 5660, 257, 4230, 12, 6032, 23779, 1185, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 189238, "start": 1901.74, "end": 1902.74, "text": " The undo spire.", "tokens": [50833, 440, 23779, 637, 621, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 189238, "start": 1903.0, "end": 1903.24, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50896, 1779, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 189238, "start": 1903.5200000000002, "end": 1909.4, "text": " If you undo changes and then branch off by making a new edit, Vim doesn't delete the redo branch you just abandoned.", "tokens": [50922, 759, 291, 23779, 2962, 293, 550, 9819, 766, 538, 1455, 257, 777, 8129, 11, 691, 332, 1177, 380, 12097, 264, 29956, 9819, 291, 445, 13732, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 189238, "start": 1909.5600000000002, "end": 1910.66, "text": " It forks the timeline.", "tokens": [51224, 467, 337, 1694, 264, 12933, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 189238, "start": 1910.8200000000002, "end": 1911.18, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51287, 467, 775, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 189238, "start": 1911.5400000000002, "end": 1916.7800000000002, "text": " Every single state the text buffer has ever occupied since the moment the file was opened is preserved.", "tokens": [51323, 2048, 2167, 1785, 264, 2487, 21762, 575, 1562, 19629, 1670, 264, 1623, 264, 3991, 390, 5625, 307, 22242, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 189238, "start": 1917.0, "end": 1921.5800000000002, "text": " You can literally time travel chronologically through every edit, regardless of which branch you are on,", "tokens": [51596, 509, 393, 3736, 565, 3147, 19393, 17157, 807, 633, 8129, 11, 10060, 295, 597, 9819, 291, 366, 322, 11, 51825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14402487698723287, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354643755742362e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 192158, "start": 1921.58, "end": 1923.72, "text": " using the G- and G- commands.", "tokens": [50365, 1228, 264, 460, 12, 293, 460, 12, 16901, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 192158, "start": 1923.8999999999999, "end": 1925.8, "text": " It is a multiverse of text editing.", "tokens": [50481, 467, 307, 257, 2120, 5376, 295, 2487, 10000, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 192158, "start": 1926.08, "end": 1931.82, "text": " I could be working on a piece of code, completely ruin it, undo back to yesterday, try a different approach, ruin that,", "tokens": [50590, 286, 727, 312, 1364, 322, 257, 2522, 295, 3089, 11, 2584, 15514, 309, 11, 23779, 646, 281, 5186, 11, 853, 257, 819, 3109, 11, 15514, 300, 11, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 192158, "start": 1931.9399999999998, "end": 1937.8, "text": " and then seamlessly time travel back to the exact state of my first failed attempt just to check a variable name.", "tokens": [50883, 293, 550, 38083, 565, 3147, 646, 281, 264, 1900, 1785, 295, 452, 700, 7612, 5217, 445, 281, 1520, 257, 7006, 1315, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 192158, "start": 1938.04, "end": 1939.58, "text": " It remembers everything.", "tokens": [51188, 467, 26228, 1203, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 192158, "start": 1940.28, "end": 1945.5, "text": " And Buffer World's phase zero specification demands that this complex branching data structure", "tokens": [51300, 400, 20254, 260, 3937, 311, 5574, 4018, 31256, 15107, 300, 341, 3997, 9819, 278, 1412, 3877, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 192158, "start": 1945.5, "end": 1949.04, "text": " be built as a foundational element of the headless parser from day one.", "tokens": [51561, 312, 3094, 382, 257, 32195, 4478, 295, 264, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 490, 786, 472, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 192158, "start": 1949.1, "end": 1950.48, "text": " It cannot be retrofitted.", "tokens": [51741, 467, 2644, 312, 18820, 69, 3944, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12314742058515549, "compression_ratio": 1.6105919003115265, "no_speech_prob": 1.5983075323314222e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 195048, "start": 1950.48, "end": 1954.18, "text": " And this brings us to how Plenum Hub handles the multiverse of human knowledge.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 577, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 18722, 264, 2120, 5376, 295, 1952, 3601, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 195048, "start": 1954.8, "end": 1964.0, "text": " Flickshion provides a formal mathematical argument in Proposition 6.2 for why any publishing substrate must keep histories, not snapshots.", "tokens": [50581, 3235, 618, 2716, 313, 6417, 257, 9860, 18894, 6770, 294, 21944, 5830, 1386, 13, 17, 337, 983, 604, 17832, 27585, 1633, 1066, 30631, 11, 406, 19206, 27495, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 195048, "start": 1964.26, "end": 1967.46, "text": " The core thesis is that snapshots underdetermine history.", "tokens": [51054, 440, 4965, 22288, 307, 300, 19206, 27495, 833, 49136, 533, 2503, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 195048, "start": 1967.74, "end": 1969.16, "text": " Okay, let's break down the math.", "tokens": [51228, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 760, 264, 5221, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 195048, "start": 1969.56, "end": 1972.46, "text": " What does underdetermine actually mean in this context?", "tokens": [51319, 708, 775, 833, 49136, 533, 767, 914, 294, 341, 4319, 30, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 195048, "start": 1972.72, "end": 1973.96, "text": " Flickshion defines a function.", "tokens": [51477, 3235, 618, 2716, 313, 23122, 257, 2445, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 195048, "start": 1974.58, "end": 1975.66, "text": " Pi of sigma equals m.", "tokens": [51570, 17741, 295, 12771, 6915, 275, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 195048, "start": 1975.82, "end": 1977.3600000000001, "text": " Okay, pi of sigma equals m.", "tokens": [51632, 1033, 11, 3895, 295, 12771, 6915, 275, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16367771665928726, "compression_ratio": 1.6336996336996337, "no_speech_prob": 1.8111179873533945e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 197736, "start": 1977.36, "end": 1984.0, "text": " In this equation, sigma is the canonical semantic object, the pure source containing the entire branching history of the text,", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 5367, 11, 12771, 307, 264, 46491, 47982, 2657, 11, 264, 6075, 4009, 19273, 264, 2302, 9819, 278, 2503, 295, 264, 2487, 11, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 197736, "start": 1984.1, "end": 1985.4599999999998, "text": " all the revisions, all the debates.", "tokens": [50702, 439, 264, 3698, 4252, 11, 439, 264, 24203, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 197736, "start": 1986.06, "end": 1987.9199999999998, "text": " The function pi acts as a flattener.", "tokens": [50800, 440, 2445, 3895, 10672, 382, 257, 24183, 260, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 197736, "start": 1988.08, "end": 1990.9599999999998, "text": " It strips away all the history and provenance outputting m.", "tokens": [50901, 467, 19842, 1314, 439, 264, 2503, 293, 12785, 719, 5598, 783, 275, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 197736, "start": 1991.02, "end": 1993.54, "text": " M being the populated content map, the current snapshot.", "tokens": [51048, 376, 885, 264, 32998, 2701, 4471, 11, 264, 2190, 30163, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 197736, "start": 1994.06, "end": 1994.9399999999998, "text": " Final batch cake.", "tokens": [51200, 13443, 15245, 5908, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 197736, "start": 1995.4399999999998, "end": 1996.6399999999999, "text": " The MP4 video file.", "tokens": [51269, 440, 14146, 19, 960, 3991, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18811856145444122, "compression_ratio": 1.5733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.972928981644473e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 199664, "start": 1996.64, "end": 1997.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 199664, "start": 1997.7, "end": 2002.0200000000002, "text": " The mathematical proof demonstrates that this flattening function pi is strictly non-injective.", "tokens": [50418, 440, 18894, 8177, 31034, 300, 341, 24183, 278, 2445, 3895, 307, 20792, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 199664, "start": 2002.26, "end": 2005.88, "text": " Non-injective, meaning you can't reverse engineer the input from the output.", "tokens": [50646, 8774, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 11, 3620, 291, 393, 380, 9943, 11403, 264, 4846, 490, 264, 5598, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 199664, "start": 2006.1000000000001, "end": 2010.3600000000001, "text": " In mapping terms, it means multiple different inputs can result in the exact same output.", "tokens": [50838, 682, 18350, 2115, 11, 309, 1355, 3866, 819, 15743, 393, 1874, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 5598, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 199664, "start": 2010.92, "end": 2012.6000000000001, "text": " Let's look at a practical scenario.", "tokens": [51079, 961, 311, 574, 412, 257, 8496, 9005, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 199664, "start": 2013.0800000000002, "end": 2013.3000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51187, 1779, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17942938019957724, "compression_ratio": 1.5242718446601942, "no_speech_prob": 1.803405623619636e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 201330, "start": 2013.3, "end": 2017.84, "text": " Imagine two different histories leading to the same sentence in a research paper.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 732, 819, 30631, 5775, 281, 264, 912, 8174, 294, 257, 2132, 3035, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11602908511494481, "compression_ratio": 1.6072874493927125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683225539578574e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 201330, "start": 2018.7, "end": 2024.06, "text": " In history A, two scientists spend a month vehemently debating a single claim.", "tokens": [50635, 682, 2503, 316, 11, 732, 7708, 3496, 257, 1618, 4221, 1712, 356, 40647, 257, 2167, 3932, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11602908511494481, "compression_ratio": 1.6072874493927125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683225539578574e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 201330, "start": 2025.12, "end": 2035.84, "text": " They write massive branching caveats, cite conflicting studies, and eventually compromise on a highly specific distilled sentence that they both agree is factually unassailable.", "tokens": [50956, 814, 2464, 5994, 9819, 278, 11730, 1720, 11, 37771, 43784, 5313, 11, 293, 4728, 18577, 322, 257, 5405, 2685, 1483, 6261, 8174, 300, 436, 1293, 3986, 307, 1186, 671, 517, 640, 32699, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11602908511494481, "compression_ratio": 1.6072874493927125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683225539578574e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 201330, "start": 2036.04, "end": 2039.44, "text": " So that is a dense, rich history of intellectual friction.", "tokens": [51502, 407, 300, 307, 257, 18011, 11, 4593, 2503, 295, 12576, 17710, 13, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11602908511494481, "compression_ratio": 1.6072874493927125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683225539578574e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 203944, "start": 2039.44, "end": 2044.5, "text": " Now imagine history B, so a single researcher who hasn't done much reading on the topic just guesses.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 3811, 2503, 363, 11, 370, 257, 2167, 21751, 567, 6132, 380, 1096, 709, 3760, 322, 264, 4829, 445, 42703, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 203944, "start": 2044.8400000000001, "end": 2045.04, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50635, 1033, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 203944, "start": 2045.3200000000002, "end": 2049.06, "text": " They type out that exact same distilled sentence purely by chance.", "tokens": [50659, 814, 2010, 484, 300, 1900, 912, 1483, 6261, 8174, 17491, 538, 2931, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 203944, "start": 2049.18, "end": 2049.5, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50852, 3153, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 203944, "start": 2050.12, "end": 2058.88, "text": " If you apply the flattening function pi to both histories, the output m, the final snapshot printed in the journal, is character for character identical.", "tokens": [50899, 759, 291, 3079, 264, 24183, 278, 2445, 3895, 281, 1293, 30631, 11, 264, 5598, 275, 11, 264, 2572, 30163, 13567, 294, 264, 6708, 11, 307, 2517, 337, 2517, 14800, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 203944, "start": 2059.12, "end": 2061.38, "text": " The snapshot is completely non-injective.", "tokens": [51349, 440, 30163, 307, 2584, 2107, 12, 259, 1020, 488, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 203944, "start": 2061.44, "end": 2063.36, "text": " And that is a catastrophe for human knowledge.", "tokens": [51465, 400, 300, 307, 257, 36043, 337, 1952, 3601, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 203944, "start": 2063.48, "end": 2069.4, "text": " The snapshot of what currently exists cannot, even in principle, tell you how it became this.", "tokens": [51567, 440, 30163, 295, 437, 4362, 8198, 2644, 11, 754, 294, 8665, 11, 980, 291, 577, 309, 3062, 341, 13, 51863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12077944840842146, "compression_ratio": 1.6226415094339623, "no_speech_prob": 1.7830402952723201e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 206944, "start": 2069.7200000000003, "end": 2079.66, "text": " By only saving the final snapshot, traditional media permanently erases the context, the discarded alternatives, and the rigorous debate that justifies the conclusion.", "tokens": [50379, 3146, 787, 6816, 264, 2572, 30163, 11, 5164, 3021, 24042, 1189, 1957, 264, 4319, 11, 264, 45469, 20478, 11, 293, 264, 29882, 7958, 300, 445, 11221, 264, 10063, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1050410691429587, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040560365029101e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 206944, "start": 2080.18, "end": 2084.82, "text": " It is like looking at the answer four on a math test, but the student erased all their scratch work.", "tokens": [50902, 467, 307, 411, 1237, 412, 264, 1867, 1451, 322, 257, 5221, 1500, 11, 457, 264, 3107, 38359, 439, 641, 8459, 589, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1050410691429587, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040560365029101e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 206944, "start": 2084.9, "end": 2086.4, "text": " You have no idea how they got there.", "tokens": [51138, 509, 362, 572, 1558, 577, 436, 658, 456, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1050410691429587, "compression_ratio": 1.5326633165829147, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040560365029101e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 208640, "start": 2086.4, "end": 2096.1600000000003, "text": " You have no idea if they logically deduced that two plus two is four, or if they made two massive errors that happened to cancel each other out, or if they just copied off the person next to them.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 572, 1558, 498, 436, 38887, 4172, 41209, 300, 732, 1804, 732, 307, 1451, 11, 420, 498, 436, 1027, 732, 5994, 13603, 300, 2011, 281, 10373, 1184, 661, 484, 11, 420, 498, 436, 445, 25365, 766, 264, 954, 958, 281, 552, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11429895852741442, "compression_ratio": 1.5523809523809524, "no_speech_prob": 2.2364081073145137e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 208640, "start": 2096.34, "end": 2103.9, "text": " This is exactly why Plenum Hub insists that the entire provenance graph must remain a first-class component of the source object.", "tokens": [50862, 639, 307, 2293, 983, 2149, 268, 449, 18986, 50137, 300, 264, 2302, 12785, 719, 4295, 1633, 6222, 257, 700, 12, 11665, 6542, 295, 264, 4009, 2657, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11429895852741442, "compression_ratio": 1.5523809523809524, "no_speech_prob": 2.2364081073145137e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 210390, "start": 2103.9, "end": 2112.7000000000003, "text": " Forgetting a debate should be a reversible, deliberate choice by the reader, not a permanent structural deletion by the platform.", "tokens": [50365, 18675, 783, 257, 7958, 820, 312, 257, 44788, 11, 30515, 3922, 538, 264, 15149, 11, 406, 257, 10996, 15067, 1103, 302, 313, 538, 264, 3663, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11138668488920404, "compression_ratio": 1.6171003717472119, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722144944107063e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 210390, "start": 2112.7000000000003, "end": 2124.32, "text": " This distinction between the history of how something happened versus the final state of what happened is perfectly illustrated by another technical quirk in Buffer World, the difference between macros and the dot command.", "tokens": [50805, 639, 16844, 1296, 264, 2503, 295, 577, 746, 2011, 5717, 264, 2572, 1785, 295, 437, 2011, 307, 6239, 33875, 538, 1071, 6191, 421, 18610, 294, 20254, 260, 3937, 11, 264, 2649, 1296, 7912, 2635, 293, 264, 5893, 5622, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11138668488920404, "compression_ratio": 1.6171003717472119, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722144944107063e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 210390, "start": 2124.48, "end": 2128.06, "text": " Oh, this blew my mind when I realized what was actually happening computationally.", "tokens": [51394, 876, 11, 341, 19075, 452, 1575, 562, 286, 5334, 437, 390, 767, 2737, 24903, 379, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11138668488920404, "compression_ratio": 1.6171003717472119, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722144944107063e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 212806, "start": 2128.06, "end": 2129.08, "text": " It is so subtle.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 370, 13743, 13, 50416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 212806, "start": 2129.42, "end": 2135.2999999999997, "text": " To a casual user, recording a macro and using the dot command seem to do the exact same thing.", "tokens": [50433, 1407, 257, 13052, 4195, 11, 6613, 257, 18887, 293, 1228, 264, 5893, 5622, 1643, 281, 360, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 212806, "start": 2135.58, "end": 2136.48, "text": " They repeat an action.", "tokens": [50741, 814, 7149, 364, 3069, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 212806, "start": 2136.68, "end": 2139.2799999999997, "text": " But they operate at completely different conceptual levels.", "tokens": [50796, 583, 436, 9651, 412, 2584, 819, 24106, 4358, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 212806, "start": 2139.42, "end": 2139.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50933, 1779, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 212806, "start": 2139.92, "end": 2141.08, "text": " Let's start with the dot command.", "tokens": [50958, 961, 311, 722, 365, 264, 5893, 5622, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 212806, "start": 2141.2, "end": 2143.6, "text": " The dot command replays a resolved command.", "tokens": [51022, 440, 5893, 5622, 23836, 82, 257, 20772, 5622, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 212806, "start": 2144.2799999999997, "end": 2146.68, "text": " It represents the meaning, the intent of the edit.", "tokens": [51176, 467, 8855, 264, 3620, 11, 264, 8446, 295, 264, 8129, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 212806, "start": 2146.86, "end": 2147.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51305, 1779, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 212806, "start": 2147.1, "end": 2156.7999999999997, "text": " If I type 3D2W, we established earlier that the parser builds an abstract syntax tree and resolves that to delete six words.", "tokens": [51317, 759, 286, 2010, 805, 35, 17, 54, 11, 321, 7545, 3071, 300, 264, 21156, 260, 15182, 364, 12649, 28431, 4230, 293, 7923, 977, 300, 281, 12097, 2309, 2283, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15309997496566152, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 3.0567046289953215e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 215680, "start": 2156.8, "end": 2159.1600000000003, "text": " The dot command caches that result intent.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5893, 5622, 269, 13272, 300, 1874, 8446, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 215680, "start": 2159.3, "end": 2165.26, "text": " If I move my cursor to a new caragraph and press dot, the engine executes delete six words.", "tokens": [50490, 759, 286, 1286, 452, 28169, 281, 257, 777, 1032, 559, 2662, 293, 1886, 5893, 11, 264, 2848, 4454, 1819, 12097, 2309, 2283, 13, 50788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 215680, "start": 2165.6000000000004, "end": 2167.6000000000004, "text": " It doesn't care what buttons I press to get there.", "tokens": [50805, 467, 1177, 380, 1127, 437, 9905, 286, 1886, 281, 483, 456, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 215680, "start": 2167.78, "end": 2170.3, "text": " It only cares about the finalized semantic meaning.", "tokens": [50914, 467, 787, 12310, 466, 264, 2572, 1602, 47982, 3620, 13, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 215680, "start": 2170.76, "end": 2172.36, "text": " But a macro is entirely different.", "tokens": [51063, 583, 257, 18887, 307, 7696, 819, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 215680, "start": 2172.48, "end": 2176.1800000000003, "text": " A macro records the literal history of your physical fingers on the keyboard.", "tokens": [51149, 316, 18887, 7724, 264, 20411, 2503, 295, 428, 4001, 7350, 322, 264, 10186, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 215680, "start": 2176.32, "end": 2177.54, "text": " It is a raw keylogger.", "tokens": [51341, 467, 307, 257, 8936, 2141, 4987, 1321, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 215680, "start": 2177.6200000000003, "end": 2178.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51406, 7587, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 215680, "start": 2178.5, "end": 2183.1800000000003, "text": " When you replay a macro, it doesn't remember that your intent was to delete six words.", "tokens": [51450, 1133, 291, 23836, 257, 18887, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1604, 300, 428, 8446, 390, 281, 12097, 2309, 2283, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13370800018310547, "compression_ratio": 1.657243816254417, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980380619264107e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 218318, "start": 2183.18, "end": 2193.7, "text": " It just blindly refeeds the literal keystrokes, 3D2W, back into the parser's input buffer, forcing the parser to recalculate the entire meaning from scratch.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 445, 47744, 1895, 5033, 82, 264, 20411, 2141, 27616, 5993, 11, 805, 35, 17, 54, 11, 646, 666, 264, 21156, 260, 311, 4846, 21762, 11, 19030, 264, 21156, 260, 281, 850, 304, 2444, 473, 264, 2302, 3620, 490, 8459, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05039137500827595, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493903039564104e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 218318, "start": 2193.8199999999997, "end": 2204.3399999999997, "text": " And conflating those two things, replaying the semantic intent of a snapshot versus replaying the literal historical keystrokes, is a guaranteed way to introduce catastrophic bugs when building a Vim clone.", "tokens": [50897, 400, 1497, 75, 990, 729, 732, 721, 11, 23836, 278, 264, 47982, 8446, 295, 257, 30163, 5717, 23836, 278, 264, 20411, 8584, 2141, 27616, 5993, 11, 307, 257, 18031, 636, 281, 5366, 34915, 15120, 562, 2390, 257, 691, 332, 26506, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05039137500827595, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493903039564104e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 218318, "start": 2204.62, "end": 2211.12, "text": " Just like conflating a document's current snapshot with its provenance history causes bugs in human knowledge.", "tokens": [51437, 1449, 411, 1497, 75, 990, 257, 4166, 311, 2190, 30163, 365, 1080, 12785, 719, 2503, 7700, 15120, 294, 1952, 3601, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05039137500827595, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493903039564104e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 218318, "start": 2211.3999999999996, "end": 2212.52, "text": " The exact same problem.", "tokens": [51776, 440, 1900, 912, 1154, 13, 51832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05039137500827595, "compression_ratio": 1.6801346801346801, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493903039564104e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 221252, "start": 2212.52, "end": 2221.52, "text": " If you treat the final, flattened PDF of a scientific paper as the whole truth, you lose the macro-level history of how those ideas were formed.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 2387, 264, 2572, 11, 24183, 292, 17752, 295, 257, 8134, 3035, 382, 264, 1379, 3494, 11, 291, 3624, 264, 18887, 12, 12418, 2503, 295, 577, 729, 3487, 645, 8693, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 221252, "start": 2221.92, "end": 2223.66, "text": " You lose the keystrokes of the debate.", "tokens": [50835, 509, 3624, 264, 2141, 27616, 5993, 295, 264, 7958, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 221252, "start": 2224.22, "end": 2227.38, "text": " But this introduces an enormous practical challenge.", "tokens": [50950, 583, 341, 31472, 364, 11322, 8496, 3430, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 221252, "start": 2227.56, "end": 2228.12, "text": " What is that?", "tokens": [51117, 708, 307, 300, 30, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 221252, "start": 2228.48, "end": 2235.66, "text": " If your system allows for infinite branching histories and supports multiple rendering depths from short summaries to full textbooks,", "tokens": [51163, 759, 428, 1185, 4045, 337, 13785, 9819, 278, 30631, 293, 9346, 3866, 22407, 28439, 490, 2099, 8367, 4889, 281, 1577, 33587, 11, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 221252, "start": 2236.18, "end": 2239.54, "text": " how do you guarantee that the system isn't lying to the user?", "tokens": [51548, 577, 360, 291, 10815, 300, 264, 1185, 1943, 380, 8493, 281, 264, 4195, 30, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 221252, "start": 2240.14, "end": 2241.48, "text": " Ah, verification.", "tokens": [51746, 2438, 11, 30206, 13, 51813], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12408085736361417, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6173055733190167e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 224148, "start": 2241.48, "end": 2248.04, "text": " How do you mathematically prove that a 30-second TikTok summary isn't completely misrepresenting the underlying source text?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 360, 291, 44003, 7081, 300, 257, 2217, 12, 27375, 20211, 12691, 1943, 380, 2584, 3346, 19919, 11662, 278, 264, 14217, 4009, 2487, 30, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 224148, "start": 2248.32, "end": 2254.2400000000002, "text": " Or, returning to our game, how do you prove that the 3D graphics aren't lying about how Vim actually works?", "tokens": [50707, 1610, 11, 12678, 281, 527, 1216, 11, 577, 360, 291, 7081, 300, 264, 805, 35, 11837, 3212, 380, 8493, 466, 577, 691, 332, 767, 1985, 30, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 224148, "start": 2254.36, "end": 2255.9, "text": " This brings us to section 6.", "tokens": [51009, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 3541, 1386, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 224148, "start": 2256.44, "end": 2258.38, "text": " Entropy, drift, and oracle testing.", "tokens": [51113, 3951, 27514, 11, 19699, 11, 293, 420, 7041, 4997, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 224148, "start": 2258.7400000000002, "end": 2261.56, "text": " Let's look at how Buffer World solves the truth problem first.", "tokens": [51228, 961, 311, 574, 412, 577, 20254, 260, 3937, 39890, 264, 3494, 1154, 700, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 224148, "start": 2261.72, "end": 2264.02, "text": " They employ a methodology called oracle testing.", "tokens": [51377, 814, 3188, 257, 24850, 1219, 420, 7041, 4997, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 224148, "start": 2264.14, "end": 2265.32, "text": " Okay, what is oracle testing?", "tokens": [51498, 1033, 11, 437, 307, 420, 7041, 4997, 30, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11150633661370528, "compression_ratio": 1.5734767025089607, "no_speech_prob": 3.4908315387632838e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 226532, "start": 2265.32, "end": 2271.46, "text": " When developers write unit tests for software, they usually write the input, and then they write the expected output.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 8849, 2464, 4985, 6921, 337, 4722, 11, 436, 2673, 2464, 264, 4846, 11, 293, 550, 436, 2464, 264, 5176, 5598, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390169461568196, "compression_ratio": 1.5904255319148937, "no_speech_prob": 1.714481096155851e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 226532, "start": 2271.6600000000003, "end": 2273.46, "text": " If I put in 2 plus 2, expect 4.", "tokens": [50682, 759, 286, 829, 294, 568, 1804, 568, 11, 2066, 1017, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390169461568196, "compression_ratio": 1.5904255319148937, "no_speech_prob": 1.714481096155851e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 226532, "start": 2273.6600000000003, "end": 2274.7200000000003, "text": " Sure, standard testing.", "tokens": [50782, 4894, 11, 3832, 4997, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390169461568196, "compression_ratio": 1.5904255319148937, "no_speech_prob": 1.714481096155851e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 226532, "start": 2275.02, "end": 2283.52, "text": " But the developers of Buffer World realize that handwriting expected outputs for a system as complex as Vim is deeply flawed.", "tokens": [50850, 583, 264, 8849, 295, 20254, 260, 3937, 4325, 300, 39179, 5176, 23930, 337, 257, 1185, 382, 3997, 382, 691, 332, 307, 8760, 38823, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390169461568196, "compression_ratio": 1.5904255319148937, "no_speech_prob": 1.714481096155851e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 228352, "start": 2283.52, "end": 2287.06, "text": " Because the person writing the test is the same person writing the code.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 954, 3579, 264, 1500, 307, 264, 912, 954, 3579, 264, 3089, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10282846500999049, "compression_ratio": 1.6507177033492824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813209895508163e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 228352, "start": 2287.2599999999998, "end": 2287.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50552, 7587, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10282846500999049, "compression_ratio": 1.6507177033492824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813209895508163e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 228352, "start": 2288.12, "end": 2295.66, "text": " If a developer fundamentally misunderstands how the CW command works, they will write a test that expects the wrong outcome.", "tokens": [50595, 759, 257, 10754, 17879, 35736, 82, 577, 264, 383, 54, 5622, 1985, 11, 436, 486, 2464, 257, 1500, 300, 33280, 264, 2085, 9700, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10282846500999049, "compression_ratio": 1.6507177033492824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813209895508163e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 228352, "start": 2295.74, "end": 2303.06, "text": " And the parser will behave incorrectly, pass the incorrect test perfectly, and the developer will deploy broken code with 100% confidence.", "tokens": [50976, 400, 264, 21156, 260, 486, 15158, 42892, 11, 1320, 264, 18424, 1500, 6239, 11, 293, 264, 10754, 486, 7274, 5463, 3089, 365, 2319, 4, 6687, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10282846500999049, "compression_ratio": 1.6507177033492824, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813209895508163e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 230306, "start": 2303.06, "end": 2310.52, "text": " So to break that cycle of confirmation bias, the specification demands an external, incorruptible oracle.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 281, 1821, 300, 6586, 295, 21871, 12577, 11, 264, 31256, 15107, 364, 8320, 11, 7121, 5428, 964, 420, 7041, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 230306, "start": 2310.7, "end": 2311.06, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50747, 1079, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 230306, "start": 2311.34, "end": 2312.48, "text": " And what serves as the oracle?", "tokens": [50779, 400, 437, 13451, 382, 264, 420, 7041, 30, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 230306, "start": 2312.56, "end": 2313.0, "text": " Real Vim.", "tokens": [50840, 8467, 691, 332, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 230306, "start": 2313.5, "end": 2317.6, "text": " Specifically, they utilize a headless instance of NeoVim running in the background.", "tokens": [50887, 26058, 11, 436, 16117, 257, 1378, 1832, 5197, 295, 24458, 53, 332, 2614, 294, 264, 3678, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 230306, "start": 2317.82, "end": 2318.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51103, 1033, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 230306, "start": 2318.2799999999997, "end": 2325.54, "text": " The testing suite pipes a sequence of keystrokes into real NeoVim via an RPC, a remote procedure call API.", "tokens": [51126, 440, 4997, 14205, 21882, 257, 8310, 295, 2141, 27616, 5993, 666, 957, 24458, 53, 332, 5766, 364, 497, 12986, 11, 257, 8607, 10747, 818, 9362, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699533462524414, "compression_ratio": 1.4935622317596566, "no_speech_prob": 2.4370668243872684e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 232554, "start": 2325.54, "end": 2336.72, "text": " NeoVim processes the keystrokes and returns a massive JSON payload containing the exact mathematically perfect state of the buffer, the cursor coordinates, and the mode.", "tokens": [50365, 24458, 53, 332, 7555, 264, 2141, 27616, 5993, 293, 11247, 257, 5994, 31828, 30918, 19273, 264, 1900, 44003, 2176, 1785, 295, 264, 21762, 11, 264, 28169, 21056, 11, 293, 264, 4391, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 232554, "start": 2337.06, "end": 2339.96, "text": " So the test suite asks the real world for the truth.", "tokens": [50941, 407, 264, 1500, 14205, 8962, 264, 957, 1002, 337, 264, 3494, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 232554, "start": 2340.06, "end": 2340.38, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51091, 1079, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 232554, "start": 2340.86, "end": 2346.8, "text": " Then it feeds those exact same keystrokes into Buffer World's internal headless parser.", "tokens": [51131, 1396, 309, 23712, 729, 1900, 912, 2141, 27616, 5993, 666, 20254, 260, 3937, 311, 6920, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 232554, "start": 2346.92, "end": 2347.8, "text": " And compares them.", "tokens": [51434, 400, 38334, 552, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 232554, "start": 2347.98, "end": 2353.98, "text": " It takes the resulting state from Buffer World and asserts it against the JSON payload from the NeoVim oracle.", "tokens": [51487, 467, 2516, 264, 16505, 1785, 490, 20254, 260, 3937, 293, 19810, 82, 309, 1970, 264, 31828, 30918, 490, 264, 24458, 53, 332, 420, 7041, 13, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12218557585270033, "compression_ratio": 1.6984732824427482, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 235398, "start": 2353.98, "end": 2362.8, "text": " If there is a single byte out of place, if the cursor is one column off, if a white space was deleted when it shouldn't have been, the test fails.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 456, 307, 257, 2167, 40846, 484, 295, 1081, 11, 498, 264, 28169, 307, 472, 7738, 766, 11, 498, 257, 2418, 1901, 390, 22981, 562, 309, 4659, 380, 362, 668, 11, 264, 1500, 18199, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08156116122291202, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.9122123589426776e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 235398, "start": 2362.9, "end": 2365.68, "text": " It is an automated, unyielding truth checker.", "tokens": [50811, 467, 307, 364, 18473, 11, 517, 88, 1789, 278, 3494, 1520, 260, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08156116122291202, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.9122123589426776e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 235398, "start": 2366.22, "end": 2375.52, "text": " Any mismatch means either there is a genuine bug in Buffer World's code, or the developers have made a documented, deliberate choice to not support a specific edge case feature.", "tokens": [50977, 2639, 23220, 852, 1355, 2139, 456, 307, 257, 16699, 7426, 294, 20254, 260, 3937, 311, 3089, 11, 420, 264, 8849, 362, 1027, 257, 23007, 11, 30515, 3922, 281, 406, 1406, 257, 2685, 4691, 1389, 4111, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08156116122291202, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.9122123589426776e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 235398, "start": 2375.64, "end": 2378.48, "text": " And this oracle testing is a phase zero requirement.", "tokens": [51448, 400, 341, 420, 7041, 4997, 307, 257, 5574, 4018, 11695, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08156116122291202, "compression_ratio": 1.6022727272727273, "no_speech_prob": 1.9122123589426776e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 237848, "start": 2378.48, "end": 2385.14, "text": " They are strictly forbidden from building the 3D glowing polygons until this automated verification against reality passes completely.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 20792, 25990, 490, 2390, 264, 805, 35, 27064, 6754, 70, 892, 1826, 341, 18473, 30206, 1970, 4103, 11335, 2584, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09410719124667616, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 2.455806608417377e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 237848, "start": 2385.4, "end": 2389.72, "text": " So that is how a video game algorithmically guarantees truth against a software benchmark.", "tokens": [50711, 407, 300, 307, 577, 257, 960, 1216, 9284, 984, 32567, 3494, 1970, 257, 4722, 18927, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09410719124667616, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 2.455806608417377e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 237848, "start": 2389.98, "end": 2392.34, "text": " But PlenumHub faces a much harder problem.", "tokens": [50940, 583, 2149, 268, 449, 21150, 8475, 257, 709, 6081, 1154, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09410719124667616, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 2.455806608417377e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 237848, "start": 2393.18, "end": 2402.14, "text": " How do you algorithmically guarantee truth against the abstract concepts of human knowledge when transforming a long source into a short video?", "tokens": [51100, 1012, 360, 291, 9284, 984, 10815, 3494, 1970, 264, 12649, 10392, 295, 1952, 3601, 562, 27210, 257, 938, 4009, 666, 257, 2099, 960, 30, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09410719124667616, "compression_ratio": 1.5907335907335907, "no_speech_prob": 2.455806608417377e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 240214, "start": 2402.14, "end": 2407.98, "text": " Fliction attempts to solve this by introducing a formal calculus for what they call semantic entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 15257, 281, 5039, 341, 538, 15424, 257, 9860, 33400, 337, 437, 436, 818, 47982, 30867, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 240214, "start": 2408.2999999999997, "end": 2409.06, "text": " Semantic entropy.", "tokens": [50673, 14421, 7128, 30867, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 240214, "start": 2409.24, "end": 2412.3799999999997, "text": " This is outlined in definition 12.9 of the essay.", "tokens": [50720, 639, 307, 27412, 294, 7123, 2272, 13, 24, 295, 264, 16238, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 240214, "start": 2412.8799999999997, "end": 2417.3399999999997, "text": " The explicit goal is to place mathematical boundaries on semantic drift.", "tokens": [50902, 440, 13691, 3387, 307, 281, 1081, 18894, 13180, 322, 47982, 19699, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 240214, "start": 2417.52, "end": 2423.3199999999997, "text": " Semantic drift is the phenomenon where meaning degrades or mutates as it passes through translation layers.", "tokens": [51134, 14421, 7128, 19699, 307, 264, 14029, 689, 3620, 368, 22626, 420, 5839, 1024, 382, 309, 11335, 807, 12853, 7914, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 240214, "start": 2423.54, "end": 2425.06, "text": " It is the game of telephone effect.", "tokens": [51435, 467, 307, 264, 1216, 295, 19800, 1802, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13794942335648971, "compression_ratio": 1.670995670995671, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612992669555847e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 242506, "start": 2425.06, "end": 2425.36, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 242506, "start": 2425.48, "end": 2432.46, "text": " When a dense 50-page sociological study is summarized by a university PR department into a two-page press release.", "tokens": [50386, 1133, 257, 18011, 2625, 12, 15161, 3075, 4383, 2979, 307, 14611, 1602, 538, 257, 5454, 11568, 5882, 666, 257, 732, 12, 15161, 1886, 4374, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 242506, "start": 2432.74, "end": 2436.02, "text": " And then summarized again by a tech blogger into a short social media post.", "tokens": [50749, 400, 550, 14611, 1602, 797, 538, 257, 7553, 6968, 1321, 666, 257, 2099, 2093, 3021, 2183, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 242506, "start": 2436.06, "end": 2436.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50915, 7587, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 242506, "start": 2436.74, "end": 2440.22, "text": " The final rendering often actively contradicts the original source.", "tokens": [50949, 440, 2572, 22407, 2049, 13022, 28900, 82, 264, 3380, 4009, 13, 51123], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 242506, "start": 2440.32, "end": 2441.82, "text": " So how does the math prevent that?", "tokens": [51128, 407, 577, 775, 264, 5221, 4871, 300, 30, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 242506, "start": 2442.12, "end": 2451.86, "text": " Well, the formula for semantic entropy calculates the baseline entropy of a specific rendering, essentially how much raw information is contained within that specific video or summary.", "tokens": [51218, 1042, 11, 264, 8513, 337, 47982, 30867, 4322, 1024, 264, 20518, 30867, 295, 257, 2685, 22407, 11, 4476, 577, 709, 8936, 1589, 307, 16212, 1951, 300, 2685, 960, 420, 12691, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11248665196555001, "compression_ratio": 1.6411960132890366, "no_speech_prob": 2.092920888679961e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 245186, "start": 2451.86, "end": 2456.6200000000003, "text": " But the critical innovation is that the formula then subtracts a mutual information term.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 4924, 8504, 307, 300, 264, 8513, 550, 16390, 82, 257, 16917, 1589, 1433, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 245186, "start": 2457.06, "end": 2460.06, "text": " Why subtract mutual information? What does that accomplish?", "tokens": [50625, 1545, 16390, 16917, 1589, 30, 708, 775, 300, 9021, 30, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 245186, "start": 2460.6800000000003, "end": 2464.9, "text": " It mathematically penalizes redundancy and rewards structural alignment.", "tokens": [50806, 467, 44003, 13661, 5660, 27830, 6717, 293, 17203, 15067, 18515, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 245186, "start": 2465.4, "end": 2466.1200000000003, "text": " Give me an example.", "tokens": [51042, 5303, 385, 364, 1365, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 245186, "start": 2466.6800000000003, "end": 2470.6, "text": " Imagine you have two renderings compiled from the exact same source coordinate.", "tokens": [51106, 11739, 291, 362, 732, 15529, 1109, 36548, 490, 264, 1900, 912, 4009, 15670, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 245186, "start": 2471.54, "end": 2478.1800000000003, "text": " A 10-page text essay and an hour-long audio recording of someone reading that exact essay.", "tokens": [51349, 316, 1266, 12, 15161, 2487, 16238, 293, 364, 1773, 12, 13025, 6278, 6613, 295, 1580, 3760, 300, 1900, 16238, 13, 51681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 245186, "start": 2478.46, "end": 2480.84, "text": " They contain the exact same semantic arguments.", "tokens": [51695, 814, 5304, 264, 1900, 912, 47982, 12869, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.188355712890625, "compression_ratio": 1.6824817518248176, "no_speech_prob": 1.898032295569174e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 248084, "start": 2480.84, "end": 2484.46, "text": " Exactly. The mutual information between them is incredibly high.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 16917, 1589, 1296, 552, 307, 6252, 1090, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09549812648607336, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756263903130233e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 248084, "start": 2485.0, "end": 2490.54, "text": " Therefore, subtracting that high mutual information keeps the overall semantic entropy of the system low.", "tokens": [50573, 7504, 11, 16390, 278, 300, 1090, 16917, 1589, 5965, 264, 4787, 47982, 30867, 295, 264, 1185, 2295, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09549812648607336, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756263903130233e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 248084, "start": 2491.06, "end": 2491.7400000000002, "text": " They are coherent.", "tokens": [50876, 814, 366, 36239, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09549812648607336, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756263903130233e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 248084, "start": 2492.08, "end": 2497.58, "text": " But what if a rogue AI summarizer pipeline creates a rendering that hallucinates facts?", "tokens": [50927, 583, 437, 498, 257, 39100, 7318, 14611, 6545, 15517, 7829, 257, 22407, 300, 35212, 259, 1024, 9130, 30, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09549812648607336, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756263903130233e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 248084, "start": 2497.8, "end": 2505.0, "text": " Right. If you have two renderings, a long one and a short one, that are individually coherent internally but have very low mutual information.", "tokens": [51213, 1779, 13, 759, 291, 362, 732, 15529, 1109, 11, 257, 938, 472, 293, 257, 2099, 472, 11, 300, 366, 16652, 36239, 19501, 457, 362, 588, 2295, 16917, 1589, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09549812648607336, "compression_ratio": 1.7004048582995952, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756263903130233e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 250500, "start": 2505.0, "end": 2511.18, "text": " Meaning they share almost no core concepts or they actively contradict each other on the points they do share.", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 436, 2073, 1920, 572, 4965, 10392, 420, 436, 13022, 28900, 1184, 661, 322, 264, 2793, 436, 360, 2073, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10448102674622467, "compression_ratio": 1.61244019138756, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744107185842627e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 250500, "start": 2511.34, "end": 2515.88, "text": " That low mutual information subtraction results in a massive spike in system entropy.", "tokens": [50682, 663, 2295, 16917, 1589, 16390, 313, 3542, 294, 257, 5994, 21053, 294, 1185, 30867, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10448102674622467, "compression_ratio": 1.61244019138756, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744107185842627e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 250500, "start": 2516.36, "end": 2523.08, "text": " And that entropy spike is mathematical evidence that at least one of the renderings has structurally drifted away from the canonical source.", "tokens": [50933, 400, 300, 30867, 21053, 307, 18894, 4467, 300, 412, 1935, 472, 295, 264, 15529, 1109, 575, 6594, 6512, 19699, 292, 1314, 490, 264, 46491, 4009, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10448102674622467, "compression_ratio": 1.61244019138756, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744107185842627e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 252308, "start": 2523.08, "end": 2534.2999999999997, "text": " So every programmatic rule that transforms the source database into a rendering, like a summarization algorithm or an automated video generator, must declare an entropy budget.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 633, 1461, 25915, 4978, 300, 35592, 264, 4009, 8149, 666, 257, 22407, 11, 411, 257, 14611, 2144, 9284, 420, 364, 18473, 960, 19265, 11, 1633, 19710, 364, 30867, 4706, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1017989090510777, "compression_ratio": 1.353846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 2.361748817347742e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 253430, "start": 2534.3, "end": 2537.0600000000004, "text": " That is formalized in theorem 12.10.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 9860, 1602, 294, 20904, 2272, 13, 3279, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21061257755055146, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439513796766118e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 253430, "start": 2537.0600000000004, "end": 2547.7000000000003, "text": " It mathematically proves that the semantic drift, after a long chain of successive rendering transformations, is strictly bounded by the sum of those declared entropy costs.", "tokens": [50503, 467, 44003, 25019, 300, 264, 47982, 19699, 11, 934, 257, 938, 5021, 295, 48043, 22407, 34852, 11, 307, 20792, 37498, 538, 264, 2408, 295, 729, 15489, 30867, 5497, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21061257755055146, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439513796766118e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 253430, "start": 2548.1800000000003, "end": 2552.44, "text": " You cannot silently accumulate errors the way human aggregators do.", "tokens": [51059, 509, 2644, 40087, 33384, 13603, 264, 636, 1952, 16743, 3391, 360, 13, 51272], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21061257755055146, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439513796766118e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 253430, "start": 2552.88, "end": 2555.6000000000004, "text": " The system dynamically tracks the divergence.", "tokens": [51294, 440, 1185, 43492, 10218, 264, 47387, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21061257755055146, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439513796766118e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 255560, "start": 2555.6, "end": 2559.08, "text": " And this enforces what fiction calls the coherence condition.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 25495, 887, 437, 13266, 5498, 264, 26528, 655, 4188, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08763525221082899, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 2.044504105944145e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 255560, "start": 2559.2799999999997, "end": 2559.74, "text": " Which means?", "tokens": [50549, 3013, 1355, 30, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08763525221082899, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 2.044504105944145e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 255560, "start": 2559.92, "end": 2569.4, "text": " If a short depth video and a full depth essay compiled from the exact same source coordinate contradict each other on the parts they both cover, it proves one of two things must be true.", "tokens": [50581, 759, 257, 2099, 7161, 960, 293, 257, 1577, 7161, 16238, 36548, 490, 264, 1900, 912, 4009, 15670, 28900, 1184, 661, 322, 264, 3166, 436, 1293, 2060, 11, 309, 25019, 472, 295, 732, 721, 1633, 312, 2074, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08763525221082899, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 2.044504105944145e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 255560, "start": 2569.58, "end": 2569.8199999999997, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51064, 1033, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08763525221082899, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 2.044504105944145e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 255560, "start": 2570.16, "end": 2582.8199999999997, "text": " Either the rendering pipeline that generated the short video is mathematically defective, or one of the files is not a legitimate rendering at all, but rather an unauthorized forged fork masquerading as the truth.", "tokens": [51093, 13746, 264, 22407, 15517, 300, 10833, 264, 2099, 960, 307, 44003, 16445, 488, 11, 420, 472, 295, 264, 7098, 307, 406, 257, 17956, 22407, 412, 439, 11, 457, 2831, 364, 517, 34224, 1602, 40226, 17716, 2300, 8035, 8166, 382, 264, 3494, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08763525221082899, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 2.044504105944145e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 258282, "start": 2582.82, "end": 2586.6000000000004, "text": " It acts as an automated cryptographic alarm system for truth.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 10672, 382, 364, 18473, 9844, 12295, 14183, 1185, 337, 3494, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 258282, "start": 2586.7000000000003, "end": 2587.54, "text": " It is brilliant.", "tokens": [50559, 467, 307, 10248, 13, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 258282, "start": 2588.1000000000004, "end": 2592.96, "text": " But I do have to push back here again, because this sounds like it's promising something physically impossible.", "tokens": [50629, 583, 286, 360, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 510, 797, 11, 570, 341, 3263, 411, 309, 311, 20257, 746, 9762, 6243, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 258282, "start": 2593.32, "end": 2602.4, "text": " Doesn't the paper itself explicitly prove that NO rendering can be fully 100% faithful to an unboundedly long history?", "tokens": [50890, 12955, 380, 264, 3035, 2564, 20803, 7081, 300, 9146, 22407, 393, 312, 4498, 2319, 4, 17808, 281, 364, 517, 18767, 13516, 938, 2503, 30, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 258282, "start": 2602.8, "end": 2604.1800000000003, "text": " What about the pigeonhole principle?", "tokens": [51364, 708, 466, 264, 37886, 14094, 8665, 30, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 258282, "start": 2604.52, "end": 2610.28, "text": " You're bringing up theorem 12.22, the no faithful rendering theorem, and you are entirely correct to push back.", "tokens": [51450, 509, 434, 5062, 493, 20904, 2272, 13, 7490, 11, 264, 572, 17808, 22407, 20904, 11, 293, 291, 366, 7696, 3006, 281, 2944, 646, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 258282, "start": 2610.48, "end": 2611.06, "text": " Okay, good.", "tokens": [51748, 1033, 11, 665, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1436988115310669, "compression_ratio": 1.5614617940199336, "no_speech_prob": 1.5613005679981917e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 261106, "start": 2611.06, "end": 2612.96, "text": " Fluidiction is not claiming magic.", "tokens": [50365, 33612, 327, 4105, 307, 406, 19232, 5585, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 261106, "start": 2613.34, "end": 2616.7999999999997, "text": " The essay freely admits a fundamental physical limit to any rendering.", "tokens": [50479, 440, 16238, 16433, 46682, 257, 8088, 4001, 4948, 281, 604, 22407, 13, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 261106, "start": 2617.42, "end": 2618.92, "text": " A video has a finite runtime.", "tokens": [50683, 316, 960, 575, 257, 19362, 34474, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 261106, "start": 2619.5, "end": 2621.46, "text": " A summary has a finite token count.", "tokens": [50787, 316, 12691, 575, 257, 19362, 14862, 1207, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 261106, "start": 2621.58, "end": 2629.9, "text": " But the provenance graph of the canonical source, the endless revisions, the debates, the branching counter arguments can grow infinitely large.", "tokens": [50891, 583, 264, 12785, 719, 4295, 295, 264, 46491, 4009, 11, 264, 16144, 3698, 4252, 11, 264, 24203, 11, 264, 9819, 278, 5682, 12869, 393, 1852, 36227, 2416, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 261106, "start": 2630.14, "end": 2634.6, "text": " You physically cannot fit an infinite amount of history into a 10-minute YouTube video.", "tokens": [51319, 509, 9762, 2644, 3318, 364, 13785, 2372, 295, 2503, 666, 257, 1266, 12, 18256, 3088, 960, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14512114829205452, "compression_ratio": 1.6290322580645162, "no_speech_prob": 1.361292263808711e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 263460, "start": 2634.6, "end": 2641.7599999999998, "text": " Right. The pigeonhole principle states that if you have more pigeons than you have pigeonholes, at least one hole must contain more than one pigeon.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 440, 37886, 14094, 8665, 4368, 300, 498, 291, 362, 544, 48297, 813, 291, 362, 37886, 37894, 11, 412, 1935, 472, 5458, 1633, 5304, 544, 813, 472, 37886, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09709530432247421, "compression_ratio": 1.713768115942029, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179320895872486e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 263460, "start": 2641.96, "end": 2651.24, "text": " Apply here, it means that multiple highly nuanced historical debates must inevitably be flattened and compressed into the exact same simplified sentence in the final video.", "tokens": [50733, 25264, 510, 11, 309, 1355, 300, 3866, 5405, 45115, 8584, 24203, 1633, 28171, 312, 24183, 292, 293, 30353, 666, 264, 1900, 912, 26335, 8174, 294, 264, 2572, 960, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09709530432247421, "compression_ratio": 1.713768115942029, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179320895872486e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 263460, "start": 2651.3399999999997, "end": 2653.1, "text": " Laws of detail is a physical certainty.", "tokens": [51202, 7744, 82, 295, 2607, 307, 257, 4001, 27022, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09709530432247421, "compression_ratio": 1.713768115942029, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179320895872486e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 263460, "start": 2653.2599999999998, "end": 2654.8399999999997, "text": " That is mathematically undeniable.", "tokens": [51298, 663, 307, 44003, 674, 268, 9364, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09709530432247421, "compression_ratio": 1.713768115942029, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179320895872486e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 263460, "start": 2655.38, "end": 2658.7599999999998, "text": " Nuance must be lost in any rendering that is shorter than the source itself.", "tokens": [51404, 13612, 719, 1633, 312, 2731, 294, 604, 22407, 300, 307, 11639, 813, 264, 4009, 2564, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09709530432247421, "compression_ratio": 1.713768115942029, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179320895872486e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 265876, "start": 2658.76, "end": 2661.0400000000004, "text": " So how is this better than what we have now?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 577, 307, 341, 1101, 813, 437, 321, 362, 586, 30, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16491939710534137, "compression_ratio": 1.4947916666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736678413434966e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 265876, "start": 2661.0400000000004, "end": 2664.5400000000004, "text": " Here is the critical, paradigm-shifting difference.", "tokens": [50479, 1692, 307, 264, 4924, 11, 24709, 12, 2716, 10106, 2649, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16491939710534137, "compression_ratio": 1.4947916666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736678413434966e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 265876, "start": 2665.2000000000003, "end": 2670.7400000000002, "text": " In traditional media, that loss of nuance is permanent because the video is the only copy.", "tokens": [50687, 682, 5164, 3021, 11, 300, 4470, 295, 42625, 307, 10996, 570, 264, 960, 307, 264, 787, 5055, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16491939710534137, "compression_ratio": 1.4947916666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736678413434966e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 265876, "start": 2671.26, "end": 2676.78, "text": " In the plenum hub architecture, the loss of fidelity is strictly temporary and entirely reversible.", "tokens": [50990, 682, 264, 499, 268, 449, 11838, 9482, 11, 264, 4470, 295, 46404, 307, 20792, 13413, 293, 7696, 44788, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16491939710534137, "compression_ratio": 1.4947916666666667, "no_speech_prob": 2.5736678413434966e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 267678, "start": 2676.78, "end": 2681.2200000000003, "text": " Because the canonical source is always retained and remains globally addressable.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 46491, 4009, 307, 1009, 33438, 293, 7023, 18958, 2985, 712, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 267678, "start": 2681.34, "end": 2685.0600000000004, "text": " Precisely. Through a mechanism called progressive disclosure.", "tokens": [50593, 48746, 736, 13, 8927, 257, 7513, 1219, 16131, 30392, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 267678, "start": 2685.5800000000004, "end": 2686.8, "text": " How does that work in practice?", "tokens": [50805, 1012, 775, 300, 589, 294, 3124, 30, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 267678, "start": 2687.1200000000003, "end": 2696.32, "text": " If a reader finishes watching a short, heavily compressed video rendering and feels dissatisfied with a specific claim, they don't have to go search the internet for an alternative.", "tokens": [50882, 759, 257, 15149, 23615, 1976, 257, 2099, 11, 10950, 30353, 960, 22407, 293, 3417, 7802, 38502, 365, 257, 2685, 3932, 11, 436, 500, 380, 362, 281, 352, 3164, 264, 4705, 337, 364, 8535, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 267678, "start": 2696.5800000000004, "end": 2697.86, "text": " They just ask for more depth.", "tokens": [51355, 814, 445, 1029, 337, 544, 7161, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 267678, "start": 2698.0, "end": 2701.76, "text": " They simply ask the system for a deeper rendering of that specific coordinate.", "tokens": [51426, 814, 2935, 1029, 264, 1185, 337, 257, 7731, 22407, 295, 300, 2685, 15670, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1354700627953115, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.9129140545887102e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 270176, "start": 2701.76, "end": 2710.6400000000003, "text": " Because the canonical source sigma is intact beneath the video, the system instantly compiles and serves a medium or full-depth rendering.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 264, 46491, 4009, 12771, 307, 23493, 17149, 264, 960, 11, 264, 1185, 13518, 715, 4680, 293, 13451, 257, 6399, 420, 1577, 12, 25478, 22407, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 270176, "start": 2710.86, "end": 2714.32, "text": " And the deeper rendering doesn't invalidate or contradict the shallow one.", "tokens": [50820, 400, 264, 7731, 22407, 1177, 380, 34702, 473, 420, 28900, 264, 20488, 472, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 270176, "start": 2714.5600000000004, "end": 2716.6000000000004, "text": " It flawlessly expands upon it.", "tokens": [51005, 467, 13717, 12048, 33706, 3564, 309, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 270176, "start": 2716.7000000000003, "end": 2718.98, "text": " The truth is never destroyed to save time.", "tokens": [51112, 440, 3494, 307, 1128, 8937, 281, 3155, 565, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 270176, "start": 2719.32, "end": 2723.0, "text": " It is merely hidden for convenience, ready to be expanded on demand.", "tokens": [51243, 467, 307, 17003, 7633, 337, 19283, 11, 1919, 281, 312, 14342, 322, 4733, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 270176, "start": 2723.4, "end": 2726.5200000000004, "text": " Which leads us perfectly into the final section of our deep dive.", "tokens": [51447, 3013, 6689, 505, 6239, 666, 264, 2572, 3541, 295, 527, 2452, 9192, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 270176, "start": 2727.44, "end": 2728.5600000000004, "text": " Empowering the user.", "tokens": [51649, 8599, 968, 278, 264, 4195, 13, 51705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 270176, "start": 2728.7400000000002, "end": 2731.6400000000003, "text": " We have talked a lot about the architecture and the math.", "tokens": [51714, 492, 362, 2825, 257, 688, 466, 264, 9482, 293, 264, 5221, 13, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15044062016373974, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.524501874906493e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 273176, "start": 2731.76, "end": 2738.96, "text": " But what does a source-first reality actually mean for you, the listener, the everyday consumer of this media?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 437, 775, 257, 4009, 12, 29581, 4103, 767, 914, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 264, 7429, 9711, 295, 341, 3021, 30, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 273176, "start": 2739.5400000000004, "end": 2747.6400000000003, "text": " It dictates a total psychological transition from being a passive reader of frozen artifacts to being an active querier of streaks.", "tokens": [50754, 467, 12569, 1024, 257, 3217, 14346, 6034, 490, 885, 257, 14975, 15149, 295, 12496, 24617, 281, 885, 364, 4967, 7083, 811, 295, 2242, 5461, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 273176, "start": 2747.8, "end": 2748.5400000000004, "text": " Active querier?", "tokens": [51167, 26635, 7083, 811, 30, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 273176, "start": 2748.78, "end": 2755.0800000000004, "text": " In this paradigm, you, the user, are explicitly granted what Fliction calls reader rights.", "tokens": [51216, 682, 341, 24709, 11, 291, 11, 264, 4195, 11, 366, 20803, 12344, 437, 3235, 4105, 5498, 15149, 4601, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 273176, "start": 2755.1800000000003, "end": 2755.6800000000003, "text": " Reader rights.", "tokens": [51536, 1300, 8312, 4601, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 273176, "start": 2755.7400000000002, "end": 2757.34, "text": " I love how that frames the dynamic.", "tokens": [51564, 286, 959, 577, 300, 12083, 264, 8546, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 273176, "start": 2757.9, "end": 2759.5800000000004, "text": " What exactly do I have the right to do?", "tokens": [51672, 708, 2293, 360, 286, 362, 264, 558, 281, 360, 30, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13585626094713124, "compression_ratio": 1.673003802281369, "no_speech_prob": 2.5242722408863605e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 275958, "start": 2759.58, "end": 2763.18, "text": " You have the right to demand the provenance of any claim you encounter.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 264, 558, 281, 4733, 264, 12785, 719, 295, 604, 3932, 291, 8593, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0885809888743391, "compression_ratio": 1.7768240343347639, "no_speech_prob": 3.0809805661585754e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 275958, "start": 2763.42, "end": 2768.62, "text": " If you see a chart in a video, you have the right to click it and see exactly which data set it was compiled from.", "tokens": [50557, 759, 291, 536, 257, 6927, 294, 257, 960, 11, 291, 362, 264, 558, 281, 2052, 309, 293, 536, 2293, 597, 1412, 992, 309, 390, 36548, 490, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0885809888743391, "compression_ratio": 1.7768240343347639, "no_speech_prob": 3.0809805661585754e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 275958, "start": 2768.7799999999997, "end": 2769.62, "text": " That is powerful.", "tokens": [50825, 663, 307, 4005, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0885809888743391, "compression_ratio": 1.7768240343347639, "no_speech_prob": 3.0809805661585754e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 275958, "start": 2769.84, "end": 2772.7799999999997, "text": " You have the right to request alternatives to the current branch.", "tokens": [50878, 509, 362, 264, 558, 281, 5308, 20478, 281, 264, 2190, 9819, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0885809888743391, "compression_ratio": 1.7768240343347639, "no_speech_prob": 3.0809805661585754e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 275958, "start": 2773.12, "end": 2780.06, "text": " If an author states a conclusion, you have the right to instantly ask the system who branched off from this data and argued the exact opposite.", "tokens": [51042, 759, 364, 3793, 4368, 257, 10063, 11, 291, 362, 264, 558, 281, 13518, 1029, 264, 1185, 567, 9819, 292, 766, 490, 341, 1412, 293, 20219, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0885809888743391, "compression_ratio": 1.7768240343347639, "no_speech_prob": 3.0809805661585754e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 278006, "start": 2780.06, "end": 2788.2999999999997, "text": " You have the right to inspect the raw canonical source, the algorithmic logic of the rendering pipeline that created the video you're watching.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 264, 558, 281, 15018, 264, 8936, 46491, 4009, 11, 264, 9284, 299, 9952, 295, 264, 22407, 15517, 300, 2942, 264, 960, 291, 434, 1976, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099959427455687, "compression_ratio": 1.5512820512820513, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504581547618137e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 278006, "start": 2788.7, "end": 2794.2, "text": " And most importantly, the right to view any context that a shorter rendering omitted to save time.", "tokens": [50797, 400, 881, 8906, 11, 264, 558, 281, 1910, 604, 4319, 300, 257, 11639, 22407, 3406, 3944, 281, 3155, 565, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09099959427455687, "compression_ratio": 1.5512820512820513, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504581547618137e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 279420, "start": 2794.2, "end": 2796.74, "text": " You're no longer just absorbing information.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 434, 572, 2854, 445, 38720, 1589, 13, 50492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16683234029741428, "compression_ratio": 1.4759358288770053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897498804167467e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 279420, "start": 2796.96, "end": 2798.12, "text": " You are interrogating it.", "tokens": [50503, 509, 366, 24871, 990, 309, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16683234029741428, "compression_ratio": 1.4759358288770053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897498804167467e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 279420, "start": 2798.58, "end": 2800.16, "text": " You are cross-examining the media.", "tokens": [50584, 509, 366, 3278, 12, 3121, 335, 1760, 264, 3021, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16683234029741428, "compression_ratio": 1.4759358288770053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897498804167467e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 279420, "start": 2800.72, "end": 2811.2999999999997, "text": " And both of our sources today propose a way to make this interrogation not just a solitary academic exercise, but a public, highly competitive, gamified community effort.", "tokens": [50691, 400, 1293, 295, 527, 7139, 965, 17421, 257, 636, 281, 652, 341, 24871, 399, 406, 445, 257, 44155, 7778, 5380, 11, 457, 257, 1908, 11, 5405, 10043, 11, 8019, 2587, 1768, 4630, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16683234029741428, "compression_ratio": 1.4759358288770053, "no_speech_prob": 1.7897498804167467e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 281130, "start": 2811.3, "end": 2814.46, "text": " Klenum Hub proposes a concept they call Pipeline Golf.", "tokens": [50365, 591, 6698, 449, 18986, 2365, 4201, 257, 3410, 436, 818, 35396, 5440, 30176, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 281130, "start": 2814.5800000000004, "end": 2815.3, "text": " Pipeline Golf.", "tokens": [50529, 35396, 5440, 30176, 13, 50565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 281130, "start": 2815.86, "end": 2816.6800000000003, "text": " Like Code Golf.", "tokens": [50593, 1743, 15549, 30176, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 281130, "start": 2817.3, "end": 2825.42, "text": " It borrows heavily from the programming concept of Code Golf, where developers compete to solve a complex algorithm using the fewest possible characters of code.", "tokens": [50665, 467, 14828, 28251, 10950, 490, 264, 9410, 3410, 295, 15549, 30176, 11, 689, 8849, 11831, 281, 5039, 257, 3997, 9284, 1228, 264, 1326, 377, 1944, 4342, 295, 3089, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 281130, "start": 2825.5800000000004, "end": 2827.38, "text": " Okay, so how does Pipeline Golf work?", "tokens": [51079, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 775, 35396, 5440, 30176, 589, 30, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 281130, "start": 2827.5600000000004, "end": 2832.9, "text": " In Pipeline Golf, a community of users is given a fixed, highly complex canonical source text.", "tokens": [51178, 682, 35396, 5440, 30176, 11, 257, 1768, 295, 5022, 307, 2212, 257, 6806, 11, 5405, 3997, 46491, 4009, 2487, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 281130, "start": 2833.1400000000003, "end": 2836.7400000000002, "text": " They then compete against each other to architect the best rendering pipeline.", "tokens": [51457, 814, 550, 11831, 1970, 1184, 661, 281, 6331, 264, 1151, 22407, 15517, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15577983856201172, "compression_ratio": 1.6813186813186813, "no_speech_prob": 1.935623970134026e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 283674, "start": 2836.74, "end": 2842.8799999999997, "text": " The rule set that translates that dense text into an accessible image, an animation, or a short audio track.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4978, 992, 300, 28468, 300, 18011, 2487, 666, 364, 9515, 3256, 11, 364, 9603, 11, 420, 257, 2099, 6278, 2837, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 283674, "start": 2843.2599999999998, "end": 2845.54, "text": " And how do you judge who built the best pipeline?", "tokens": [50691, 400, 577, 360, 291, 6995, 567, 3094, 264, 1151, 15517, 30, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 283674, "start": 2845.9199999999996, "end": 2847.7999999999997, "text": " It cannot just be about making it short.", "tokens": [50824, 467, 2644, 445, 312, 466, 1455, 309, 2099, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 283674, "start": 2848.04, "end": 2850.8999999999996, "text": " They're judged on a multidimensional matrix, fidelity.", "tokens": [50930, 814, 434, 27485, 322, 257, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 8141, 11, 46404, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 283674, "start": 2851.66, "end": 2856.72, "text": " Mathematically, how much of the source structure survives a transformation without semantic drift?", "tokens": [51111, 15776, 40197, 11, 577, 709, 295, 264, 4009, 3877, 46231, 257, 9887, 1553, 47982, 19699, 30, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 283674, "start": 2857.14, "end": 2857.58, "text": " Economy.", "tokens": [51385, 48223, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 283674, "start": 2858.3199999999997, "end": 2861.9199999999996, "text": " How few computational steps or tokens does the pipeline require?", "tokens": [51444, 1012, 1326, 28270, 4439, 420, 22667, 775, 264, 15517, 3651, 30, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 283674, "start": 2862.68, "end": 2863.24, "text": " Explainability.", "tokens": [51662, 39574, 2310, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17906466892787387, "compression_ratio": 1.5543859649122806, "no_speech_prob": 2.1509161639288177e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 286324, "start": 2863.24, "end": 2868.3199999999997, "text": " Can another user easily read and understand the logic of the transformation rules?", "tokens": [50365, 1664, 1071, 4195, 3612, 1401, 293, 1223, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 9887, 4474, 30, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 286324, "start": 2868.52, "end": 2869.72, "text": " And finally, surprise.", "tokens": [50629, 400, 2721, 11, 6365, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 286324, "start": 2870.2799999999997, "end": 2875.4399999999996, "text": " Is the resulting visual rendering actually interesting, elegant, or entertaining to consume?", "tokens": [50717, 1119, 264, 16505, 5056, 22407, 767, 1880, 11, 21117, 11, 420, 20402, 281, 14732, 30, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 286324, "start": 2875.7999999999997, "end": 2881.0, "text": " It turns the act of rendering information into a verifiable, community-driven puzzle.", "tokens": [50993, 467, 4523, 264, 605, 295, 22407, 1589, 666, 257, 1306, 30876, 11, 1768, 12, 25456, 12805, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 286324, "start": 2881.4599999999996, "end": 2887.54, "text": " It incentivizes the crowd to constantly iterate and improve how we visualize complex data.", "tokens": [51276, 467, 35328, 5660, 264, 6919, 281, 6460, 44497, 293, 3470, 577, 321, 23273, 3997, 1412, 13, 51580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 286324, "start": 2887.7599999999998, "end": 2892.7999999999997, "text": " And Buffer World has independently developed the exact same philosophy with its user-generated levels.", "tokens": [51591, 400, 20254, 260, 3937, 575, 21761, 4743, 264, 1900, 912, 10675, 365, 1080, 4195, 12, 21848, 770, 4358, 13, 51843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13201298713684081, "compression_ratio": 1.6482758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 2.2017344544766893e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 289280, "start": 2892.8, "end": 2895.7200000000003, "text": " Section 13 of the Buffer World spec details this.", "tokens": [50365, 21804, 3705, 295, 264, 20254, 260, 3937, 1608, 4365, 341, 13, 50511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 289280, "start": 2896.3, "end": 2898.38, "text": " They don't just want players solving pre-made puzzles.", "tokens": [50540, 814, 500, 380, 445, 528, 4150, 12606, 659, 12, 10341, 24138, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 289280, "start": 2898.78, "end": 2902.6800000000003, "text": " They want players actively importing their real-world problems into the game engine.", "tokens": [50664, 814, 528, 4150, 13022, 43866, 641, 957, 12, 13217, 2740, 666, 264, 1216, 2848, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 289280, "start": 2902.9, "end": 2907.92, "text": " Let's say a programmer has a massive, messy, 10,000-line server log file.", "tokens": [50870, 961, 311, 584, 257, 32116, 575, 257, 5994, 11, 16191, 11, 1266, 11, 1360, 12, 1889, 7154, 3565, 3991, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 289280, "start": 2908.04, "end": 2908.2400000000002, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51127, 1033, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 289280, "start": 2908.5600000000004, "end": 2915.5800000000004, "text": " They need to reformat all the timestamps, fix a repeated typo that occurs randomly, and rename a variable everywhere it appears.", "tokens": [51153, 814, 643, 281, 8290, 267, 439, 264, 49108, 23150, 11, 3191, 257, 10477, 2125, 78, 300, 11843, 16979, 11, 293, 36741, 257, 7006, 5315, 309, 7038, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747358341028194, "compression_ratio": 1.5190839694656488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6292441571211236e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 291558, "start": 2915.58, "end": 2920.7, "text": " They can import that starting text and their desired final text and turn it into a custom level.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 393, 974, 300, 2891, 2487, 293, 641, 14721, 2572, 2487, 293, 1261, 309, 666, 257, 2375, 1496, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10695073237785926, "compression_ratio": 1.6776556776556777, "no_speech_prob": 2.5424668880641432e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 291558, "start": 2921.2599999999998, "end": 2923.64, "text": " The game calculates the diff between the two files.", "tokens": [50649, 440, 1216, 4322, 1024, 264, 7593, 1296, 264, 732, 7098, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10695073237785926, "compression_ratio": 1.6776556776556777, "no_speech_prob": 2.5424668880641432e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 291558, "start": 2924.02, "end": 2927.36, "text": " But how does the game leaderboard know what the parse score is?", "tokens": [50787, 583, 577, 775, 264, 1216, 5263, 3787, 458, 437, 264, 48377, 6175, 307, 30, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10695073237785926, "compression_ratio": 1.6776556776556777, "no_speech_prob": 2.5424668880641432e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 291558, "start": 2927.7999999999997, "end": 2934.2999999999997, "text": " How does it know the absolute minimum number of Vim keystrokes required to get from state A to state B?", "tokens": [50976, 1012, 775, 309, 458, 264, 8236, 7285, 1230, 295, 691, 332, 2141, 27616, 5993, 4739, 281, 483, 490, 1785, 316, 281, 1785, 363, 30, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10695073237785926, "compression_ratio": 1.6776556776556777, "no_speech_prob": 2.5424668880641432e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 291558, "start": 2934.7999999999997, "end": 2943.2, "text": " Computing the mathematically perfect minimum keystroke sequence for a complex text transformation is known to be computationally intractable.", "tokens": [51326, 37804, 278, 264, 44003, 2176, 7285, 2141, 42706, 8310, 337, 257, 3997, 2487, 9887, 307, 2570, 281, 312, 24903, 379, 560, 1897, 712, 13, 51746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10695073237785926, "compression_ratio": 1.6776556776556777, "no_speech_prob": 2.5424668880641432e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 294320, "start": 2943.2, "end": 2948.2799999999997, "text": " It would take a supercomputer years to brute force all possible Vim combinations.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 747, 257, 36708, 924, 281, 47909, 3464, 439, 1944, 691, 332, 21267, 13, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 294320, "start": 2949.16, "end": 2954.14, "text": " So Buffer World sidesteps the math by using AuthorPlay's first parse seeding.", "tokens": [50663, 407, 20254, 260, 3937, 20822, 377, 10653, 264, 5221, 538, 1228, 20216, 24262, 311, 700, 48377, 8871, 278, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 294320, "start": 2954.2999999999997, "end": 2956.54, "text": " Ah, so the author has to eat their own cooking?", "tokens": [50920, 2438, 11, 370, 264, 3793, 575, 281, 1862, 641, 1065, 6361, 30, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 294320, "start": 2956.74, "end": 2957.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51042, 7587, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 294320, "start": 2957.54, "end": 2963.72, "text": " To prove that the imported level is actually solvable, the author must solve it themselves inside the engine at the moment of import.", "tokens": [51082, 1407, 7081, 300, 264, 25524, 1496, 307, 767, 1404, 17915, 11, 264, 3793, 1633, 5039, 309, 2969, 1854, 264, 2848, 412, 264, 1623, 295, 974, 13, 51391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 294320, "start": 2963.8999999999996, "end": 2968.48, "text": " The number of keystrokes the author used becomes the initial parse score for the global leaderboard.", "tokens": [51400, 440, 1230, 295, 2141, 27616, 5993, 264, 3793, 1143, 3643, 264, 5883, 48377, 6175, 337, 264, 4338, 5263, 3787, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11409955554538304, "compression_ratio": 1.6223021582733812, "no_speech_prob": 1.681322182173206e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 296848, "start": 2968.48, "end": 2977.3, "text": " And then the global community descends on the level, utilizing obscure Vim commands to shave off one or two keystrokes, constantly pushing the parse score down.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 264, 4338, 1768, 7471, 2581, 322, 264, 1496, 11, 26775, 34443, 691, 332, 16901, 281, 25544, 766, 472, 420, 732, 2141, 27616, 5993, 11, 6460, 7380, 264, 48377, 6175, 760, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07949626992601867, "compression_ratio": 1.6308724832214765, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591404879284237e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 296848, "start": 2977.4, "end": 2980.02, "text": " But with a global leaderboard, people will always try to cheat.", "tokens": [50811, 583, 365, 257, 4338, 5263, 3787, 11, 561, 486, 1009, 853, 281, 17470, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07949626992601867, "compression_ratio": 1.6308724832214765, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591404879284237e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 296848, "start": 2980.82, "end": 2985.28, "text": " How do you stop someone from just hacking the client and submitting a score of one keystroke?", "tokens": [50982, 1012, 360, 291, 1590, 1580, 490, 445, 31422, 264, 6423, 293, 31836, 257, 6175, 295, 472, 2141, 42706, 30, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07949626992601867, "compression_ratio": 1.6308724832214765, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591404879284237e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 296848, "start": 2985.56, "end": 2989.72, "text": " Here is where the strict architectural adherence to the truth becomes critical again.", "tokens": [51219, 1692, 307, 689, 264, 10910, 26621, 30106, 655, 281, 264, 3494, 3643, 4924, 797, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07949626992601867, "compression_ratio": 1.6308724832214765, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591404879284237e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 296848, "start": 2990.36, "end": 2995.36, "text": " To prevent cheating, Buffer World leaderboards rely entirely on verified replays.", "tokens": [51459, 1407, 4871, 18309, 11, 20254, 260, 3937, 5263, 17228, 10687, 7696, 322, 31197, 23836, 82, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07949626992601867, "compression_ratio": 1.6308724832214765, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591404879284237e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 299536, "start": 2995.36, "end": 2999.44, "text": " A player cannot just submit an integer score of 15 keystrokes to the server.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 4256, 2644, 445, 10315, 364, 24922, 6175, 295, 2119, 2141, 27616, 5993, 281, 264, 7154, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545392068584314, "compression_ratio": 1.645320197044335, "no_speech_prob": 3.1661192764764756e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 299536, "start": 2999.6800000000003, "end": 2999.94, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50581, 883, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545392068584314, "compression_ratio": 1.645320197044335, "no_speech_prob": 3.1661192764764756e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 299536, "start": 3000.6400000000003, "end": 3006.86, "text": " The client must submit the actual, literal sequence of those 15 keystrokes as a data payload.", "tokens": [50629, 440, 6423, 1633, 10315, 264, 3539, 11, 20411, 8310, 295, 729, 2119, 2141, 27616, 5993, 382, 257, 1412, 30918, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545392068584314, "compression_ratio": 1.645320197044335, "no_speech_prob": 3.1661192764764756e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 299536, "start": 3007.2400000000002, "end": 3008.34, "text": " And the server checks it.", "tokens": [50959, 400, 264, 7154, 13834, 309, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545392068584314, "compression_ratio": 1.645320197044335, "no_speech_prob": 3.1661192764764756e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 299536, "start": 3008.54, "end": 3016.5, "text": " The master server then spins up its own instance of the headless parser, the incorruptible oracle, feeds those 15 keystrokes into it,", "tokens": [51024, 440, 4505, 7154, 550, 31587, 493, 1080, 1065, 5197, 295, 264, 1378, 1832, 21156, 260, 11, 264, 7121, 5428, 964, 420, 7041, 11, 23712, 729, 2119, 2141, 27616, 5993, 666, 309, 11, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545392068584314, "compression_ratio": 1.645320197044335, "no_speech_prob": 3.1661192764764756e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 301650, "start": 3016.5, "end": 3021.48, "text": " and strictly verifies that the resulting state matches the required win state of the level.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 20792, 1306, 11221, 300, 264, 16505, 1785, 10676, 264, 4739, 1942, 1785, 295, 264, 1496, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 301650, "start": 3021.78, "end": 3027.04, "text": " The mechanism used to verify the leaderboards is identical to the mechanism used to run the unit tests.", "tokens": [50629, 440, 7513, 1143, 281, 16888, 264, 5263, 17228, 307, 14800, 281, 264, 7513, 1143, 281, 1190, 264, 4985, 6921, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 301650, "start": 3027.28, "end": 3028.8, "text": " It is a closed loop of truth.", "tokens": [50904, 467, 307, 257, 5395, 6367, 295, 3494, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 301650, "start": 3029.04, "end": 3031.9, "text": " The truth is verifiable at every single step of the stack.", "tokens": [50992, 440, 3494, 307, 1306, 30876, 412, 633, 2167, 1823, 295, 264, 8630, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 301650, "start": 3032.44, "end": 3039.92, "text": " And engaging with this system actively trains the user to think in the same structural, transformational ways that the architecture requires.", "tokens": [51162, 400, 11268, 365, 341, 1185, 13022, 16329, 264, 4195, 281, 519, 294, 264, 912, 15067, 11, 4088, 1478, 2098, 300, 264, 9482, 7029, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 301650, "start": 3040.18, "end": 3044.86, "text": " This is perfectly highlighted by Buffer World's final training phase, which they call SearchWorks.", "tokens": [51549, 639, 307, 6239, 17173, 538, 20254, 260, 3937, 311, 2572, 3097, 5574, 11, 597, 436, 818, 17180, 28846, 82, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11567552336331072, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.2716325348559607e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 304486, "start": 3044.86, "end": 3052.88, "text": " SearchWorks covers the most advanced Vim mechanics, global commands, denoted by colon G, and substitute commands, denoted by colon S.", "tokens": [50365, 17180, 28846, 82, 10538, 264, 881, 7339, 691, 332, 12939, 11, 4338, 16901, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 8255, 460, 11, 293, 15802, 16901, 11, 1441, 23325, 538, 8255, 318, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11549679438273112, "compression_ratio": 1.6273764258555132, "no_speech_prob": 2.3899571557906008e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 304486, "start": 3053.4, "end": 3057.96, "text": " Mastering these forces, a complete paradigm shift in the player's mental model.", "tokens": [50792, 6140, 278, 613, 5874, 11, 257, 3566, 24709, 5513, 294, 264, 4256, 311, 4973, 2316, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11549679438273112, "compression_ratio": 1.6273764258555132, "no_speech_prob": 2.3899571557906008e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 304486, "start": 3058.7400000000002, "end": 3064.94, "text": " In the early levels of the game, you are taught to move your character to a word, delete it, move to the next word, change it.", "tokens": [51059, 682, 264, 2440, 4358, 295, 264, 1216, 11, 291, 366, 5928, 281, 1286, 428, 2517, 281, 257, 1349, 11, 12097, 309, 11, 1286, 281, 264, 958, 1349, 11, 1319, 309, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11549679438273112, "compression_ratio": 1.6273764258555132, "no_speech_prob": 2.3899571557906008e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 304486, "start": 3065.58, "end": 3068.1600000000003, "text": " You are acting on one discrete object at a time.", "tokens": [51401, 509, 366, 6577, 322, 472, 27706, 2657, 412, 257, 565, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11549679438273112, "compression_ratio": 1.6273764258555132, "no_speech_prob": 2.3899571557906008e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 304486, "start": 3068.6, "end": 3071.1600000000003, "text": " It is very localized, linear thinking.", "tokens": [51552, 467, 307, 588, 44574, 11, 8213, 1953, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11549679438273112, "compression_ratio": 1.6273764258555132, "no_speech_prob": 2.3899571557906008e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 307116, "start": 3071.16, "end": 3074.6, "text": " But SearchWorks teaches you to abandon the cursor entirely.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 17180, 28846, 82, 16876, 291, 281, 9072, 264, 28169, 7696, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13784453743382505, "compression_ratio": 1.7363636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491480711074535e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 307116, "start": 3075.08, "end": 3076.04, "text": " Abandon the cursor.", "tokens": [50561, 2847, 8518, 264, 28169, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13784453743382505, "compression_ratio": 1.7363636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491480711074535e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 307116, "start": 3076.22, "end": 3086.2999999999997, "text": " It teaches you to write a command that instantly selects an entire population, say, highlighting every single instance of word error across thousands of lines of text simultaneously,", "tokens": [50618, 467, 16876, 291, 281, 2464, 257, 5622, 300, 13518, 3048, 82, 364, 2302, 4415, 11, 584, 11, 26551, 633, 2167, 5197, 295, 1349, 6713, 2108, 5383, 295, 3876, 295, 2487, 16561, 11, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13784453743382505, "compression_ratio": 1.7363636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491480711074535e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 307116, "start": 3086.2999999999997, "end": 3094.12, "text": " and then applying a systematic transformation to that entire population in one single coordinated instantaneous motion.", "tokens": [51122, 293, 550, 9275, 257, 27249, 9887, 281, 300, 2302, 4415, 294, 472, 2167, 29591, 45596, 5394, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13784453743382505, "compression_ratio": 1.7363636363636363, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491480711074535e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 309412, "start": 3094.12, "end": 3100.12, "text": " Which, if you think about it, is the exact computational logic required to manage a plenum hub database.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 11, 498, 291, 519, 466, 309, 11, 307, 264, 1900, 28270, 9952, 4739, 281, 3067, 257, 499, 268, 449, 11838, 8149, 13, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873140180433118, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.789744784666536e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 309412, "start": 3100.2999999999997, "end": 3100.7599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50674, 7587, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873140180433118, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.789744784666536e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 309412, "start": 3100.88, "end": 3107.38, "text": " When that biology professor updates the date of the fossil discovery, the underlying system acts like a global Vim command.", "tokens": [50703, 1133, 300, 14956, 8304, 9205, 264, 4002, 295, 264, 18737, 12114, 11, 264, 14217, 1185, 10672, 411, 257, 4338, 691, 332, 5622, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873140180433118, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.789744784666536e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 309412, "start": 3107.7, "end": 3113.12, "text": " It selects the population of all link renderings, the textbook, the flashcards, the video, and transforms them systematically.", "tokens": [51044, 467, 3048, 82, 264, 4415, 295, 439, 2113, 15529, 1109, 11, 264, 25591, 11, 264, 7319, 40604, 11, 264, 960, 11, 293, 35592, 552, 39531, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873140180433118, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.789744784666536e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 309412, "start": 3113.9, "end": 3121.7599999999998, "text": " By playing this 3D game, you are literally training your brain to intuitively grasp the mechanics of source-first data transformation.", "tokens": [51354, 3146, 2433, 341, 805, 35, 1216, 11, 291, 366, 3736, 3097, 428, 3567, 281, 46506, 21743, 264, 12939, 295, 4009, 12, 29581, 1412, 9887, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09873140180433118, "compression_ratio": 1.6360655737704919, "no_speech_prob": 1.789744784666536e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 312176, "start": 3121.76, "end": 3127.92, "text": " It is a profound synchronization of the tool, the architecture, and the human mental model.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 19331, 2144, 295, 264, 2290, 11, 264, 9482, 11, 293, 264, 1952, 4973, 2316, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136833054678781, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 2.271268026085571e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 312176, "start": 3128.1200000000003, "end": 3130.88, "text": " Okay, let's pull all this together and recap this massive journey.", "tokens": [50683, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 2235, 439, 341, 1214, 293, 20928, 341, 5994, 4671, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136833054678781, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 2.271268026085571e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 312176, "start": 3131.7400000000002, "end": 3137.1600000000003, "text": " We started with the very human frustration of spotting permanent errors in baked-in videos.", "tokens": [50864, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 588, 1952, 20491, 295, 4008, 783, 10996, 13603, 294, 19453, 12, 259, 2145, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136833054678781, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 2.271268026085571e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 312176, "start": 3137.2400000000002, "end": 3143.5, "text": " Diagnosing the conflation problem, where modern media tragically fuses the underlying truth with its temporary presentation.", "tokens": [51139, 8789, 4535, 6110, 264, 1497, 24278, 1154, 11, 689, 4363, 3021, 38282, 984, 283, 8355, 264, 14217, 3494, 365, 1080, 13413, 5860, 13, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136833054678781, "compression_ratio": 1.5625, "no_speech_prob": 2.271268026085571e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 314350, "start": 3143.5, "end": 3156.2, "text": " We then looked at Buffer World, a video game that solves this by strictly separating the brain, the headless, mathematically rigorous Vim parser, from the glowing 3D polygons of the rendering engine.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 550, 2956, 412, 20254, 260, 3937, 11, 257, 960, 1216, 300, 39890, 341, 538, 20792, 29279, 264, 3567, 11, 264, 1378, 1832, 11, 44003, 29882, 691, 332, 21156, 260, 11, 490, 264, 27064, 805, 35, 6754, 70, 892, 295, 264, 22407, 2848, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697675108909607, "compression_ratio": 1.519650655021834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888142781948615e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 314350, "start": 3156.36, "end": 3164.24, "text": " And we saw how the plenum hub theoretical architecture takes that exact same decoupled philosophy and applies it to the totality of human knowledge.", "tokens": [51008, 400, 321, 1866, 577, 264, 499, 268, 449, 11838, 20864, 9482, 2516, 300, 1900, 912, 979, 263, 15551, 10675, 293, 13165, 309, 281, 264, 1993, 1860, 295, 1952, 3601, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0697675108909607, "compression_ratio": 1.519650655021834, "no_speech_prob": 1.9888142781948615e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 316424, "start": 3164.24, "end": 3173.66, "text": " We explored how it shatters the linear version into three dimensions, a branching lineage of history, variable depths of lossy compression, and diverse output modalities.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 24016, 577, 309, 402, 37690, 264, 8213, 3037, 666, 1045, 12819, 11, 257, 9819, 278, 38257, 295, 2503, 11, 7006, 28439, 295, 4470, 88, 19355, 11, 293, 9521, 5598, 1072, 16110, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0912185279271936, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.4948524149359663e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 316424, "start": 3174.0, "end": 3182.9399999999996, "text": " We examined the mathematical necessity of retaining deep provenance, because flattening histories into snapshots fundamentally erases the why behind any conclusion.", "tokens": [50853, 492, 30972, 264, 18894, 24217, 295, 34936, 2452, 12785, 719, 11, 570, 24183, 278, 30631, 666, 19206, 27495, 17879, 1189, 1957, 264, 983, 2261, 604, 10063, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0912185279271936, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.4948524149359663e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 316424, "start": 3183.3799999999997, "end": 3189.9599999999996, "text": " We looked at how systems can guarantee this truth, using automated NeoVim oracles and semantic entropy calculus to bound drift.", "tokens": [51322, 492, 2956, 412, 577, 3652, 393, 10815, 341, 3494, 11, 1228, 18473, 24458, 53, 332, 420, 9918, 293, 47982, 30867, 33400, 281, 5472, 19699, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0912185279271936, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 2.4948524149359663e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 318996, "start": 3189.96, "end": 3196.68, "text": " And finally, we saw how separating the source from the rendering empowers you with reader rights.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 1866, 577, 29279, 264, 4009, 490, 264, 22407, 4012, 23054, 291, 365, 15149, 4601, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566128308259988, "compression_ratio": 1.6196581196581197, "no_speech_prob": 2.446255437799083e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 318996, "start": 3196.86, "end": 3202.2400000000002, "text": " Turning passive consumption into a verifiable, competitive, community-driven interrogation of knowledge.", "tokens": [50710, 39660, 14975, 12126, 666, 257, 1306, 30876, 11, 10043, 11, 1768, 12, 25456, 24871, 399, 295, 3601, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566128308259988, "compression_ratio": 1.6196581196581197, "no_speech_prob": 2.446255437799083e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 318996, "start": 3202.6, "end": 3207.14, "text": " The future of digital media demands that we stop confusing the presentation with the truth.", "tokens": [50997, 440, 2027, 295, 4562, 3021, 15107, 300, 321, 1590, 13181, 264, 5860, 365, 264, 3494, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566128308259988, "compression_ratio": 1.6196581196581197, "no_speech_prob": 2.446255437799083e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 318996, "start": 3207.56, "end": 3212.92, "text": " The canonical source must remain sacred, globally addressable, and totally headless.", "tokens": [51245, 440, 46491, 4009, 1633, 6222, 15757, 11, 18958, 2985, 712, 11, 293, 3879, 1378, 1832, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566128308259988, "compression_ratio": 1.6196581196581197, "no_speech_prob": 2.446255437799083e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 321292, "start": 3212.92, "end": 3221.12, "text": " Renderings, whether they're YouTube videos, textbooks, or 3D games, are just disposable, beautiful, temporary views of that deeper truth.", "tokens": [50365, 497, 3216, 1109, 11, 1968, 436, 434, 3088, 2145, 11, 33587, 11, 420, 805, 35, 2813, 11, 366, 445, 41578, 11, 2238, 11, 13413, 6809, 295, 300, 7731, 3494, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 321292, "start": 3221.4, "end": 3226.6, "text": " I want to leave you, the listener, with a final thought to mull over as you close out this deep dive.", "tokens": [50789, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 281, 275, 858, 670, 382, 291, 1998, 484, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 321292, "start": 3226.76, "end": 3227.08, "text": " Go ahead.", "tokens": [51057, 1037, 2286, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 321292, "start": 3227.56, "end": 3233.12, "text": " Turn this lens away from theoretical architecture and look at your own personal digital footprint.", "tokens": [51097, 7956, 341, 6765, 1314, 490, 20864, 9482, 293, 574, 412, 428, 1065, 2973, 4562, 24222, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 321292, "start": 3233.76, "end": 3239.54, "text": " Think about your thousands of emails, your sprawling notes apps, your decade of social media posts.", "tokens": [51407, 6557, 466, 428, 5383, 295, 12524, 11, 428, 22734, 1688, 5570, 7733, 11, 428, 10378, 295, 2093, 3021, 12300, 13, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 321292, "start": 3239.66, "end": 3240.38, "text": " Oh, wow, yeah.", "tokens": [51702, 876, 11, 6076, 11, 1338, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1128523726212351, "compression_ratio": 1.5589225589225588, "no_speech_prob": 2.1846099148431497e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 324038, "start": 3240.38, "end": 3245.38, "text": " How much of what you create and store is currently trapped as a frozen snapshot rendering?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 709, 295, 437, 291, 1884, 293, 3531, 307, 4362, 14994, 382, 257, 12496, 30163, 22407, 30, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07206095470471328, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.004709115724368e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 324038, "start": 3246.42, "end": 3263.34, "text": " And more importantly, how much of your actual provenance, the history of how you arrived at your core beliefs, the intense debates you had in draft folders, the nuanced alternatives you ultimately threw away, has been permanently overwritten and lost to time because your tools didn't care to remember.", "tokens": [50667, 400, 544, 8906, 11, 577, 709, 295, 428, 3539, 12785, 719, 11, 264, 2503, 295, 577, 291, 6678, 412, 428, 4965, 13585, 11, 264, 9447, 24203, 291, 632, 294, 11206, 31082, 11, 264, 45115, 20478, 291, 6284, 11918, 1314, 11, 575, 668, 24042, 670, 26859, 293, 2731, 281, 565, 570, 428, 3873, 994, 380, 1127, 281, 1604, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07206095470471328, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.004709115724368e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 324038, "start": 3263.54, "end": 3264.82, "text": " That is a chilling thought.", "tokens": [51523, 663, 307, 257, 31047, 1194, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07206095470471328, "compression_ratio": 1.6317829457364341, "no_speech_prob": 2.004709115724368e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 326482, "start": 3264.82, "end": 3277.7400000000002, "text": " If a video game can mathematically guarantee the preservation of every single keystroke history of a typo in VIM, shouldn't we demand that our publishing systems possess the same respect for the history of our ideas?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 960, 1216, 393, 44003, 10815, 264, 27257, 295, 633, 2167, 2141, 42706, 2503, 295, 257, 2125, 78, 294, 691, 6324, 11, 4659, 380, 321, 4733, 300, 527, 17832, 3652, 17490, 264, 912, 3104, 337, 264, 2503, 295, 527, 3487, 30, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09135442166715055, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834421869340368e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 326482, "start": 3277.9, "end": 3280.7200000000003, "text": " Just like that swapped access chart we talked about at the very beginning.", "tokens": [51019, 1449, 411, 300, 50011, 2105, 6927, 321, 2825, 466, 412, 264, 588, 2863, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09135442166715055, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834421869340368e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 326482, "start": 3280.88, "end": 3281.06, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51168, 865, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09135442166715055, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834421869340368e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 326482, "start": 3281.2200000000003, "end": 3292.94, "text": " We need to stop building systems that only show us the broken chart and start building systems that remember exactly how it got broken, allowing us to rewind the tape, fix the source, and instantly regenerate the world.", "tokens": [51185, 492, 643, 281, 1590, 2390, 3652, 300, 787, 855, 505, 264, 5463, 6927, 293, 722, 2390, 3652, 300, 1604, 2293, 577, 309, 658, 5463, 11, 8293, 505, 281, 41458, 264, 7314, 11, 3191, 264, 4009, 11, 293, 13518, 26358, 473, 264, 1002, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09135442166715055, "compression_ratio": 1.717607973421927, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834421869340368e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 329294, "start": 3292.94, "end": 3293.46, "text": " Absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 7021, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22835073665696748, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.897746933557376e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 329294, "start": 3294.02, "end": 3295.7000000000003, "text": " Thanks for joining us on this deep dive.", "tokens": [50419, 2561, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22835073665696748, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.897746933557376e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 329294, "start": 3296.08, "end": 3296.78, "text": " Keep exploring.", "tokens": [50522, 5527, 12736, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22835073665696748, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.897746933557376e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 329294, "start": 3297.14, "end": 3299.12, "text": " Keep demanding the providence of what you read.", "tokens": [50575, 5527, 19960, 264, 1439, 2778, 295, 437, 291, 1401, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22835073665696748, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.897746933557376e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 329294, "start": 3299.38, "end": 3302.82, "text": " And keep questioning the structures beneath the surfaces you see every day.", "tokens": [50687, 400, 1066, 21257, 264, 9227, 17149, 264, 16130, 291, 536, 633, 786, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22835073665696748, "compression_ratio": 1.391304347826087, "no_speech_prob": 1.897746933557376e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 330282, "start": 3302.82, "end": 3303.0800000000004, "text": " Hey.", "tokens": [50365, 1911, 13, 50378], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 809, "seek": 330282, "start": 3303.0800000000004, "end": 3303.38, "text": " Hey.", "tokens": [50378, 1911, 13, 50393], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 810, "seek": 330282, "start": 3303.38, "end": 3303.54, "text": " Bye.", "tokens": [50393, 4621, 13, 50401], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 811, "seek": 330282, "start": 3303.54, "end": 3303.7000000000003, "text": " Bye.", "tokens": [50401, 4621, 13, 50409], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 812, "seek": 330282, "start": 3303.7000000000003, "end": 3303.88, "text": " Bye.", "tokens": [50409, 4621, 13, 50418], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 813, "seek": 330282, "start": 3303.88, "end": 3304.76, "text": " Bye.", "tokens": [50418, 4621, 13, 50462], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob": -1.603666716930913, "compression_ratio": 6.2, "no_speech_prob": 3.035650203431217e-11}, {"id": 814, "seek": 330282, "start": 3305.34, "end": 3306.42, "text": " Bye.", "tokens": [50491, 4621, 13, 50545], "temperature": 1.0, "avg_logprob":